// ============================================================================
//  ops1q.ks  --  the ascent (OPS 1) of the SOCK on Sol: liftoff to MECO, the ET separation, the OMS-2 plan
//  Usage: on the pad, RUN ops1q. (flown and logged: it starts ascent_log.ks itself; SET ASC_LOG TO FALSE. first flies
//  it unlogged; RUN ascent_log("ops1q.ks"). works too), then launch: it waits for liftoff.
//  Stage 1 (FSSR 4.2.3 / 4.2.4): the vertical rise to the tower clear, then pitch, heading and roll from the I-load tables
//  on VREL_AERO_REF, the constant pitch rate from T_CNS_PITCH_RATE, the SRB separation at burnout.
//  Stage 2 (FSSR 4.8.1 / 4.8.3 / 4.8.5): UPFG every DTGD s, the 3 g limit, the fine count to MECO; the ET separation; then
//  the OMS-2 plan for ops2q. The I-loads: lib/lib_ascent_iload.ks (generated by the offline tools).
//  The displays (lib/lib_ascdisp.ks): ASCENT TRAJ 1 / 2 and OMS/MPS in GUI windows, the events in the MESSAGES; under
//  TRAJ: Mode [the modes open] ABORT, TAL site [the sites in reach] and "!" (the FAILURES window: OFF / TIME /
//  RAND, timed rows MET + SSME, FAIL NOW L / C / R); a first SSME out with no abort selected selects the best mode open
//  by itself (asc_auto_1eo); the console stays empty. Without asc_bg/ the console instead (lib/lib_ascent_con.ks: the
//  state every 0.5 s, the events below it).
//  The aborts: TAL (FSSR 4.8.1 PEG subtask 15a): PEG flies to the site's MECO target (Zaragoza; Moron when the propellant
//  check falls short), the OMS dump (ASC_TAL_DUMP t) from ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY s after a stage-1 selection, after a stage-2
//  one only when the ET falls short (asc_tal_need), then the ET separation and no OMS-2 (the entry to the site is not
//  in ops1q). RTLS (FSSR 4.6, lib/lib_ascent_rtls.ks): the fuel dissipation, the pitcharound, the flyback on PEG's RTLS
//  mode to the launch site's runway (ASC_RTLS_SITE: the SLF from KSC, Vandenberg from SLC-6), the powered pitchdown,
//  MECO on the MECO line; the OMS dump (ASC_RTLS_DUMP_T t, ASC_RTLS_DUMP_T_LO t when it starts below
//  ASC_RTLS_V_DUMP_SW); then the ET separation (the glide to the runway is not in ops1q). ATO (FSSR 4.5.2; one ATO
//  button: PRESS TO ORBIT or COME BACK, the AOA, chosen after OMS-1): PEG's MECO speed to the ATO target's (an apogee
//  at ASC_ATO_H), no dump; after the ET separation OMS-1 to that apogee when it is short (ops2q flies it, asks,
//  plans OMS-2: the ATO's circle at ASC_ATO_H with ASC_ATO_DV_DEORBIT kept, or the AOA's entry perigee), else the
//  question and the OMS-2 plan here. A failure at a set time: SET ASC_EO TO "C 120". before the run (the centre SSME
//  at MET 120 s; pairs, e.g. "C 120 L 200"; "ANY": a random running SSME; they fill the FAILURES window's rows,
//  TIME on); an abort at a set time: SET ASC_AB TO "TAL 125". (or "RTLS 170", "ATO 130"). The logs:
//  An SSME that fails from outside our script (shut down by hand, an action group, a failure mod; flamed out, gone, no
//  thrust) is found by lib/lib_ascent_eo.ks and flown as our own failure (asc_fail): SET ASC_EO_EXT TO FALSE. before the run
//  turns that off. The logs:
//  0:/logs/ascent_peg_<ut>.csv (every PEG pass and the events), and ascent_log.ks's 0:/logs/ascent_<n>.csv (+ .txt).
//  After an SSME fails (in stage 2) the roll on the centre SSME only (else one other; with one SSME left on the RCS,
//  roll only); the ascent DAP (lib/lib_ascent_dap.ks) steers from the failure to MECO in place of kOS's steering. SET
//  ASC_EO_DAP TO FALSE. before the run: kOS's steering with the roll / yaw slower (SET ASC_EO_TS TO 6. sets its
//  settling time; default 4 s, 2 s before the failure).
//  The guidance attitude's own rate is fed forward to the DAP (asc["wff"], low-passed); an RTLS's slews and the roll
//  to heads up feed their own (rate asc["wff"], acceleration asc["aff"]; asc["eff"] stays 0 for the slews); on a TAL the logger waits end 10 s after the ET separation at the latest
//  (asc["lg_wait"]), then OPS 6. From SRB sep to MECO the steering attitude keeps q x |alpha| at most lib_hudg's
//  HDG_QA_LIM (40 kPa deg, the HUD cue's limit; asc_qa_limit): PEG's, an RTLS's and the droop's commands alike,
//  not the 2EO contingency's. An RTLS flies the DAP too (offline, on the MECO line its cut matches an ideal
//  follower's); SET ASC_RTLS_DAP TO FALSE. flies it on kOS's steering.
//  At the ET separation the RCS translates the orbiter up (away from the ET) for 5 s and right for 1.5 s (an RTLS: 5 s),
//  both from the separation; SET ASC_SEP_UP TO x. / SET ASC_SEP_RT TO x. before the run sets the times (0: none).
//  After a TAL's ET separation ops1q runs OPS 6 itself as its last action: RUNPATH("0:/ops6q.ks", "TAL", site), site
//  "ZZA", "MRN" or "SNN". After an RTLS's ET separation likewise: RUNPATH("0:/ops6q.ks", "RTLS", site), site the RTLS
//  runway's name, "SLF" or "VBG".
//  Every hand-off to OPS 6 (TAL, RTLS, CONT, SPLITS) has the RCS on: a TAL's, an RTLS's or a contingency's from the ET
//  separation on (the end of its translation leaves the RCS on), each one at the main loop's end and at its RUNPATH.
//  ASC_HO["eo3"] tells OPS 6 a stage-2 3EO picked the mode (asc_3eo_go): ops6q burns a 3EO TAL's dump on for
//  dump_left t only then.
//  A 3EO's TAL from VI 2750 m/s (offline, 2686 / 2724 lost). In an RTLS's fuel dissipation and pitcharound a second
//  failure flies the contingency's mode 2 (YELLOW, asc_rtls_m2_go); with ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 FALSE the pages' 2EO line
//  there is BLUE (offline: 122 of 122 short of TAEM) and the bailout is OPS 6's.
//  The messages: ABORT: THROTTLE UP, SPLIT-S CONFIRMED, BAILOUT CONFIRMED, RTLS 3EO <COLOR>; some events go to the log
//  only; THROTTLE DOWN in an RTLS (the first step, the floor: asc_rtls_kdn); a 3EO's word in an RTLS GREEN in the
//  powered pitchdown, else BLUE (asc_rtls_3eo_word). The console stays blank (the INITIATING lines to the log),
//  except the RUN refusals and the failed hand-offs.
//  ASC_HO["meco_ut"], MECO's UT for OPS 6's reach test (-1: no MECO).
//  ASC_HO["eo2"], the locked 2EO word (asc["eo2_ln"]; "" without one): BLUE makes ops6q bail out at once (an RTLS
//  whose second SSME failed in the fuel dissipation / pitcharound with the cut).
//  The hand-off: HOPREP's hold goes straight to the entry alpha (ASC_HO_RATE 0: kOS's steering slews), the dump's
//  relight once the OMS thrust line no longer points toward the ET (asc_ho_clear: the ET's BOUNDS box against the
//  dump's path), then OPS 6; a dump the hold could not light goes to OPS 6 (ASC_HO dump_wait, dump_go, dump_clr),
//  which lights it once clear.
//  The pad searches' cache: their result kept in 0:/logs/padc/ under a key of their inputs; the same inputs and code on
//  the next pad: no search, no hold (lib/lib_ascent_padc.ks, asc_padc_work). A miss searches faster: while the count
//  holds the searches run ASC_PAD_SLICE s of units a pass (asc_pad_full); E TAL from the nominal's states and seeded
//  by the tables' mark (lib_ascent_etl).
//  The launch countdown (lib/lib_ascent_cd.ks) from T-30 s: the arms still out retracted (the count holds at T-30
//  until they are in), T-10 the sparklers, T-6.6 the SSMEs 3-2-1 120 ms apart to 100 %, T-0 the SRBs' stage; 104 %
//  from liftoff; MET from T-0. SET ASC_CD TO FALSE. before the run: no countdown (the crew stages).
//  A 3EO IN STAGE 2 (FSSR 4.10.2's need test, this vehicle's numbers; in stage 1 the split-S): at the cutoff
//  asc_3eo_go picks the ATO when the OMS on board covers the ATO plan's OMS-1 + OMS-2 (and the coast's apogee is above
//  ASC_3EO_HA_MIN) or from VI ASC_3EO_VI_ATO, else the TAL from VI ASC_3EO_VI_TAL (the site nearest the plane; the OMS
//  it needs, by its MECO target, from the hand-off once ops6q runs a dump on), else the contingency: GREEN to the ELS
//  of the 3EO footprint (lib_ascent_bgl's bgl_point3), else BLUE, the OMS to empty; an RTLS or a contingency already
//  flying goes on. The pages' 3EO line shows the same pick live (asc_3eo_work). SET ASC_3EO_ON TO FALSE.: MECO, then
//  the abort's hand-off.
//  After OPS1Q COMPLETE: RUN ops2q. flies the plan written last: OMS-2 (prograde, centred at the apoapsis). After
//  an ATO with OMS-1 the same: ops2q flies OMS-1, asks PRESS TO ORBIT or COME BACK (lib_aoa.ks's aoaAsk) and
//  plans OMS-2; RUN ops2q. again flies OMS-2 (then, for COME BACK, fam_build and ops3q's AOA).
//  THE ARD (lib/lib_ascent_ard.ks): all the abort boundaries computed from the current state: from a PEG pass's state
//  it flies the path ahead and each abort on it fast, and puts the pages' marks ATO and PRESS (1EO) and 2EO TAL, ATO
//  and PRESS where each abort starts to work (the tables until its first values; E TAL stays the tables'; the droop's
//  2EO bound kept: a 2EO's MECO not below 67 km), and NEG RTN where an RTLS selected could no longer turn around in
//  time (the RTLS's own turnaround test on the path's states). After an SSME out or a selection it starts again on the
//  SSMEs left and the selected mode; the top-left 1EO line then holds the abort selected (else the line at the
//  failure), and a second failure later than CREW_DELAY flies the 2EO line too once the ARD has refreshed on two
//  SSMEs, or before that the line at the first failure where that one opened a mode already (else MODE SEL). Its work
//  fills the main loop's passes with the pages (ASC_ARD_MAXU units a pass); SET ASC_ARD TO FALSE. before the run flies
//  the tables' marks. The log: #ardr (a restart), #ardl (a mark found), #ard (a refresh done), #ardo (off near MECO).
//  THE SPLIT-S (NOT FSSR: the 1987 scheme, AIAA 87-2398, never certified; it replaces the bailout for the stage-1 2EOs
//  and 3EOs, with a loft from the start). A second (or third) SSME out in stage 1 selects SPLITS (asc_s1c_arm; no
//  other abort from then): the 7 control surfaces on (their pitch / yaw / roll fields, not AG9), the loft
//  (lib_ascent_s1's asc_s1c_pitch: the table's pitch raised to gamma + ASC_LOFT deg, heads down: the orbiter's alpha
//  negative, its wing lifting), the OMS dump from the failure + 5 s, paused at MET 78 s, and from MET 74 s the nose
//  onto the relative wind (alpha and sideslip 0 at the sep). At the SRB burnout the separation: the throttle 0, ABORT
//  (the craft's Abort group: the ET off with the SRBs on it, the SSMEs off and their gimbals locked, the surfaces on),
//  the staging to the OMS's stage; the RCS up (away from the ET; on already from MET 78 s, before the sep) and back;
//  alpha up from the sep at 5 deg/s to 38 deg (without striking the ET with the body flap), Nz at most 2.5 g (at the
//  sep's q alpha 45 would pull 4-13 g); above 17.84 deg (the OMS thrust line on every launch craft) the OMS dump on to
//  empty, the back RCS off, the up RCS 5 s more; then OPS 6's split-S (RUNPATH("0:/ops6q.ks", "SPLITS", site)) once
//  ops6q flies it, else the controls are the crew's (SAS on). The free orbiter pitches toward the ET after the sep
//  before kOS's pitch steering (2 s response time) pushes back (4 deg measured; with alpha held 0 for 1 s, or the up
//  RCS only from the sep, it recontacted the ET), so the up RCS starts before the sep, the alpha command starts at +3
//  deg and the pitch steering's response time is 0.5 s until DONE. Settings before the run: SET ASC_SPLITS TO FALSE.
//  (a 2EO then armed at the SRB sep: asc_2eo_arm),
//  ASC_LOFT (deg, 15; 0: the table's pitch), ASC_LOFT_QA (kPa deg; 0: none), ASC_LOFT_SURF (TRUE: the surfaces on),
//  ASC_LOFT_GUARD (TRUE: the loft's alpha lowered while the SRBs' pitch gimbal stays saturated), ASC_SPLITS_DAP (TRUE:
//  the C# DAP flies the loft in AUTO; FALSE: kOS's steering; CSS either way, on through the sep), ASC_SPLITS_ALPHA /
//  ASC_SPLITS_NZ / ASC_SPLITS_HOLD / ASC_SPLITS_RATE / ASC_SPLITS_UP_T / ASC_SPLITS_A0 / ASC_SPLITS_TS (38 deg, 2.5 g,
//  0 s, 5 deg/s, MET 78 s (< 0: the up RCS at the sep), 3 deg, 0.5 s (<= 0: the steering as it is)). The log: #s1c
//  (10 Hz to the sep), #s1cq (10 Hz after it), #s1c,arm / surf / eo / up / sep / end.
//  The crew chooses between a bailout and the split-S in a stage 1 2EO (the split-S by default): with the pages up a
//  2EO arms the split-S at once, as above, and opens the crew's window, ASC_SPLITS_WAIT s (5; 0: none): the Mode list
//  SPLITS / BAILOUT, ABORT flies the pick; at the window's end or the SRB burnout the list's pick flies (SPLITS unless
//  the crew moved it), a 3EO keeps the split-S. BAILOUT undoes the arm (the loft off, the dump not lit, the surfaces'
//  fields back) and flies the 2EO response at the SRB sep (asc_2eo_arm); the split-S's dump and up RCS only after the
//  window. The log: #s1c,win / lock / bail.
// ============================================================================
@LAZYGLOBAL OFF.
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_progreset.ks").  progReset().   // No hook of an earlier program outlives it (lib_progreset)
CLEARSCREEN.                    // the console clear first
SET CONFIG:IPU TO 10000.        // the patched kOS's IPU ceiling; set before the libraries load
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_logsw.ks").                  // SOCK_LOG: the logs on or off (0:/logging.txt)
// The ascent's logs (0:/logs: ascent_peg_<ut>.csv, ascent_<n>.csv / .txt, asccss_<t>.csv and the addon's
// hohold_<ut>.csv) are written when SOCK_LOG is on, or under RUN ascent_log("ops1q.ks"). (its own logger running);
// SET ASC_LOG TO TRUE. or FALSE. before the run overrides both. The pad searches' cache (0:/logs/padc) and the
// OMS plans are written either way.
GLOBAL ASC_LGON IS SOCK_LOG.
IF DEFINED LG_DONE { IF NOT LG_DONE { SET ASC_LGON TO TRUE. } }
IF DEFINED ASC_LOG { SET ASC_LGON TO ASC_LOG. }
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_iload.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_s1.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_peg.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_s2.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_rtls.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_con.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascdisp.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_dap.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_css.ks").   // CSS in the ascent (the TRAJ page's PITCH / ROLL/YAW toggles)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_hud.ks").   // the HUD in the ascent (the OMS/MPS page's HUD | HUD CAM)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_hudg.ks").   // the FD square, the guidance diamond, the yaw line
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_guistyle.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_far.ks").   // FAR control surfaces (asc_s1c_surf) when FAR is installed
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_gui.ks").
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_abr.ks").   // the abort marks' predictor
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_cnt.ks").   // the 2EO contingency (FSSR 4.9)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_ard.ks").   // the ARD (the abort marks from the state)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_etl.ks").   // E TAL live: the earliest TAL from the pad (lib_ascent_ard's TAL flights)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_bgl.ks").   // the live BLUE / GREEN: the footprint over the ARD's path (asc_bgl_work)
IF DEFINED ASC_ARD { SET ASC_ARD_ON TO ASC_ARD. }   // SET ASC_ARD TO FALSE. before the run: the tables' marks
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_padc.ks").   // the pad searches' cache (asc_padc_work)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_padcs.ks").   // the pad searches in C# (asc_pad_cs_go / _work)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_ardcs.ks").   // the in-flight refreshes in C# (asc_live_cs_go / _work)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_oms_plan.ks").   // the OMS plans' one writer (omsPlanWrite)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_cd.ks").   // the launch countdown (asc_cd_new / asc_cd_tick)
IF DEFINED ASC_CD { SET ASC_CD_ON TO ASC_CD. }   // SET ASC_CD TO FALSE. before the run: the crew stages
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_failui.ks").                  // the FAILURES window and the failure state under it
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_ascent_eo.ks").   // the SSME-out detector (asc_eo_watch / asc_eo_why): a failure from outside our script
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_cwui.ks").   // the caution & warning panel (lib_cw: the state and the lamp API, lib_cwui: the window and the tone)
RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_cwchk.ks").   // the checks' pure parts (the debounce, the Pc test)
IF DEFINED ASC_EO_EXT { SET ASC_EO_EXT_ON TO ASC_EO_EXT. }   // SET ASC_EO_EXT TO FALSE. before the run: no detector
LOCAL asc_o2_ho IS EXISTS("0:/ops2q.ks") AND EXISTS("0:/lib/lib_o2ato.ks").   // an ATO hands over to ops2q's ATO / AOA TGT page (the pick asked there, before OMS-1)
LOCAL asc_aoa_lib IS EXISTS("0:/lib/lib_aoa.ks").   // lib_aoa's aoaAsk / aoaPlanOms2 (without it: PRESS TO ORBIT)
IF asc_aoa_lib { RUNONCEPATH("0:/lib/lib_aoa.ks"). }

// The hand-off's gap (3.5-7.5 s measured) is kOS compiling ops6q.ks and the libraries this program has not loaded
// (~1 MB), so they are compiled here, on the pad, to 0:/ksm/ (fresh each run, so never stale); asc_o6_path runs
// 0:/ksm/ops6q.ksm with O6_KSM_GO TRUE, and their loads take the .ksm (each a CHOOSE on O6_KSM_GO; ops6q clears it at
// its end). ASC_O6_PRE FALSE before the run: the sources.
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_O6_PRE) { GLOBAL ASC_O6_PRE IS TRUE. }
IF DEFINED O6_KSM_GO { SET O6_KSM_GO TO FALSE. } ELSE { GLOBAL O6_KSM_GO IS FALSE. }
GLOBAL ASC_O6_KSM_FILES IS LIST("ops6q", "lib/lib_entdisp", "lib/lib_land", "lib/lib_taemdisp", "lib/lib_coast", "lib/lib_dap", "lib/taemg_const", "lib/fcs_pitch", "lib/alg", "lib/alg_const", "lib/taemg", "lib/lib_solq_atm", "lib/solq_atm_data", "lib/lib_grdap", "lib/lib_grtls", "lib/lib_tal", "lib/lib_kepler", "lib/traj_display", "lib/lib_fam", "lib/lib_plan", "lib/lib_guide", "lib/lib_vehicle", "lib/display", "lib/flightlogger").
GLOBAL ASC_O6_KSM IS FALSE.
GLOBAL ASC_O6_NOTE IS "".             // the precompile's outcome, logged at liftoff (the terminal stays blank)
// ops1q's own steering lock, released by the libraries that take the controls (lib_grdap, lib_land, lib_ascent_css):
// kOS's UNLOCK STEERING removes only the lock of the file it is compiled in, and a lock left running sets STEERING each
// tick, which turns the cooked steering back on
FUNCTION asc_unlock_steer { UNLOCK STEERING. }
IF NOT (DEFINED STEER_UNLOCKS) { GLOBAL STEER_UNLOCKS IS LIST(). }
STEER_UNLOCKS:ADD(asc_unlock_steer@).
// the same for its throttle lock (left on when the hand-off's dump burns on into OPS 6: ops6q's hoDumpEnd)
FUNCTION asc_unlock_thr { UNLOCK THROTTLE. }
IF NOT (DEFINED THROTTLE_UNLOCKS) { GLOBAL THROTTLE_UNLOCKS IS LIST(). }
THROTTLE_UNLOCKS:ADD(asc_unlock_thr@).
IF ASC_O6_PRE AND EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") {
  LOCAL o6t0 IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL o6ok IS TRUE.
  FOR o6f IN ASC_O6_KSM_FILES {
    IF EXISTS("0:/" + o6f + ".ks") {
      COMPILE "0:/" + o6f + ".ks" TO "0:/ksm/" + o6f + ".ksm".
      IF NOT EXISTS("0:/ksm/" + o6f + ".ksm") { SET o6ok TO FALSE. }
    } ELSE { SET o6ok TO FALSE. }
  }
  SET ASC_O6_KSM TO o6ok.
  SET ASC_O6_NOTE TO "OPS 6 PRECOMPILED " + (CHOOSE "" IF o6ok ELSE "(INCOMPLETE: THE SOURCES AT THE HAND-OFF) ")
    + "IN " + ROUND(TIME:SECONDS - o6t0, 1) + " S (" + ASC_O6_KSM_FILES:LENGTH + " FILES)".
}
FUNCTION asc_o6_path {                 // ops6q to run (and its libraries' loads with it)
  SET O6_KSM_GO TO ASC_O6_KSM.
  asc_ho_hold().
  RETURN CHOOSE "0:/ksm/ops6q.ksm" IF ASC_O6_KSM ELSE "0:/ops6q.ks".
}
// At the RUNPATH the addon's hand-off hold (KalsAddon.HoHold.cs) keeps CSS and the hand-off attitude flying through the
// gap: it is armed on the hand-off's attitude (asc_ho_dir) and the crew's CSS axes (asc["css_c"]): lib_ascent_css's
// Law A, in the fly-by-wire handler every physics tick, while kOS loads ops6q; lib_grdap's grdStart (or the first FBW3)
// releases it, ASC_HO_CS_TMAX s at most. ASC_HO_CS_FLY TRUE (the default): the hold commands the axes (its log,
// logs/hohold_<ut>.csv, either way); FALSE: the SHADOW, computed and logged only, kOS's steering lock flying the gap.
// ASC_HO_CS FALSE or an older DLL: none.
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_HO_CS) { GLOBAL ASC_HO_CS IS TRUE. }
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_HO_CS_FLY) { GLOBAL ASC_HO_CS_FLY IS TRUE. }
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_HO_CS_TMAX) { GLOBAL ASC_HO_CS_TMAX IS 60. }
// the HUD kept live through the gap by the addon (KalsAddon.HoHud.cs: lib_hud's update in C# on hdCsIn's reads, the
// vessel's and the camera's refreshed), until OPS 6's first HUD update. ASC_HO_CS_HUD FALSE or an older DLL: the HUD
// stays up frozen.
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_HO_CS_HUD) { GLOBAL ASC_HO_CS_HUD IS TRUE. }
FUNCTION asc_ho_hud {
  IF NOT ASC_HO_CS_HUD OR NOT asc["hud"] OR NOT ADDONS:HASSUFFIX("KALS") { RETURN. }
  IF NOT ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("HOHUD") { RETURN. }
  IF NOT (hdOK AND hdShown AND hdCsOn) { RETURN. }
  LOCAL hoGeo IS LIST().
  LOCAL hoHt IS LIST().
  IF hdRwyOn AND hdRwyIx >= 0 {
    SET hoGeo TO LIST(hdThr, hdPts[0], hdPts[1], hdPts[2], hdPts[3], hdPts[4], hdPts[5]).
    SET hoHt TO LIST(hdElev, hdElev, hdElev, hdElevFar, hdElevFar, hdElev, hdElev).
  }
  LOCAL hoHr IS ADDONS:KALS:HOHUD(LIST(CHOOSE hdCam IF hdCamOK ELSE 0, hdCsIn(), hoGeo, hoHt, HD_MAX_HZ, ASC_HO_CS_TMAX,
    CHOOSE hdCsG IF asc["hudg"] ELSE FALSE)).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" {
    LOG "#ho," + asc_met() + ",C# HUD COAST" + (CHOOSE "" IF hoHr = "" ELSE ": " + hoHr) TO asc["log"].
  }
}
FUNCTION asc_ho_hold {
  asc_ho_hud().
  IF NOT ASC_HO_CS OR asc["ho"]:LENGTH = 0 OR NOT ADDONS:HASSUFFIX("KALS") { RETURN. }
  IF NOT ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("HOHOLD") { RETURN. }
  LOCAL hoTg IS asc_ho_dir().
  LOCAL hoFc IS SHIP:FACING.
  LOCAL hoCc IS asc["css_c"].
  LOCAL hoLg IS ASC_LGON.
  LOCAL hoRs IS ADDONS:KALS:HOHOLD(LIST(ASC_HO_CS_FLY, hoTg, hoCc[0], hoCc[1], ADDONS:KALS:FBWCTRL(),
    LIST(ASC_CSS_QMAX, ASC_CSS_YMAX, ASC_CSS_RMAX, ASC_CSS_T, ASC_CSS_KA, ASC_CSS_WAUTO, ASC_CSS_AMIN, ASC_CSS_AUTH_K,
         ASC_CSS_WARP_KT, ASC_CSS_TI, ASC_CSS_IMAX, ASC_CSS_RHC, ASC_CSS_DB, ASC_CSS_EXP, ASC_CSS_CAP_W, ASC_CSS_CAP_T,
         ASC_CSS_AUTH_N, ASC_HO_CS_TMAX),
    ascCssErr(hoFc:FOREVECTOR, hoFc:TOPVECTOR, hoFc:STARVECTOR, hoTg), SHIP:ANGULARVEL * 57.2958, hoLg)).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" {
    LOG "#ho," + asc_met() + ",C# HAND-OFF HOLD " + (CHOOSE "FLYING" IF ASC_HO_CS_FLY ELSE "SHADOW") + " (CSS "
      + (CHOOSE "PITCH " IF hoCc[0] ELSE "") + (CHOOSE "ROLL/YAW " IF hoCc[1] ELSE "") + (CHOOSE "" IF hoCc[0] OR hoCc[1] ELSE "OFF ")
      + ")" + (CHOOSE "" IF hoRs = "" ELSE ": " + hoRs) TO asc["log"].
  }
}

// THE LAUNCH SITE, before the box: the RTLS returns to wherever the launch site is (there are no West Coast 2EO
// sites): the site whose RTLS runway lies nearest the pad (lib_ascent_gui's asc_site_pick: the SLF from KSC,
// Vandenberg from SLC-6) is the RTLS's, NEG RTN's and OPS 6's (ASC_RTLS_SITE), and its own I-loads fly (asc_site_set;
// Vandenberg: 98 deg south by default), so the box opens on them; the console says which.
LOCAL asc_site IS asc_site_pick(SHIP:LATITUDE, SHIP:LONGITUDE).
asc_site_set(asc_site[0]).
// ASC_ABR_CONT's static 2EO window (Bermuda, from the tables) is KSC's: from any other site none (Vandenberg: no West
// Coast 2EO site), BLUE until a live BLUE / GREEN sweep finds one
IF asc_site[0]["name"] <> "KSC" { SET ASC_ABR_CONT[0] TO LIST(). }

// THE LAUNCH-TARGET BOX FIRST, before anything else runs: the target altitude (km; the apoapsis at MECO), the
// inclination and a selector for the launch azimuth (north / south): ACCEPT sets ASC_VDMAG + ASC_TGT_AP, ASC_TGT_INC,
// ASC_LAUNCH_DIR, ASC_HDG_DELTA (lib_ascent_gui); CANCEL flies nothing. SET ASC_GUI TO FALSE. before the run skips it.
LOCAL asc_gui_on IS TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_GUI { SET asc_gui_on TO ASC_GUI. }
LOCAL asc_gui_ok IS TRUE.
IF asc_gui_on { SET asc_gui_ok TO asc_gui_target(). }

// the run's state: the phase, the liftoff UT (-1 on the pad), the first stage, the lit SRBs; from liftoff the inertial
// frame, PEG's plane, the SSMEs and the ET's burnable load; the second stage, the MECO time and cause, the roll's start
// (MET; -1 = heads down), the PEG log; the commanded throttle (PL %), the console's events and next update, and the pass
// flag (a tick with a PEG pass leaves the console to the next one)
LOCAL asc IS LEXICON("phase", "PAD", "t_lo", -1, "s1", asc_s1_new(), "srbs", LIST(), "fr", asc_frame_new(TIME:SECONDS),
  "iyd", V(0, 0, 0), "et_full", 0, "s2_on", FALSE, "g", LEXICON(), "ssme", LIST(), "ssme_ok", FALSE, "t_meco", -1, "why", "",
  "t_roll", -1, "log", "", "kcmd", 0, "ev", LIST(), "con_next", 0, "busy", FALSE).
// what the locks fly: the attitude (the pad's until the tower clear) and the KSP throttle
LOCAL asc_dir IS SHIP:FACING.
LOCAL asc_thr IS 0.
// the caution & warning panel. asc_event hands every fault line to cwFromAsc (lib_cw's CW_MAP_ASC); the SSME-out detector's own
// "SSME k FAIL" lights MPS red. The one check here: a lit SSME under CW_PC_LOW x its expected thrust for CW_PC_LOW_S s (a degraded
// engine the detector, which calls it out at 30 %, still flies on) = MPS CAUTION "SSME k PC LOW"; it steps back when the thrust does.
FUNCTION ascCwMet { RETURN asc_met_of(asc). }
LOCAL ascCwDeb IS LEXICON().
LOCAL ascCwPc IS FALSE.
FUNCTION ascCwChk {
  PARAMETER ut.
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 OR asc["t_meco"] >= 0 OR NOT asc:HASKEY("eo") { RETURN. }
  LOCAL es IS LIST().
  LIST ENGINES IN es.
  LOCAL alive IS LEXICON().
  FOR en IN es { SET alive[en:UID] TO TRUE. }
  LOCAL who IS "".
  FOR rc IN asc["eo"]["recs"] {
    IF NOT rc["done"] AND alive:HASKEY(rc["uid"]) AND NOT adOut:HASKEY(rc["k"]) {
      LOCAL en IS rc["en"].
      IF cwDeb(ascCwDeb, rc["k"], cwPcLow(en:IGNITION, asc_thr, en:AVAILABLETHRUST, en:THRUST), ut, CW_PC_LOW_S) { SET who TO rc["k"]. }
    }
  }
  IF who <> "" {
    IF cwLampCls("MPS") <> "W" { cwSet("MPS", "C", "SSME " + who + " PC LOW"). SET ascCwPc TO TRUE. }
  } ELSE IF ascCwPc {
    SET ascCwPc TO FALSE.
    IF cwLampCls("MPS") = "C" { cwClear("MPS"). }
  }
}
// FLT CNTL = a lit, unlocked SSME gimbal on its stop (cwGmbApply, the fraction of its range as asc_s1c_gmb reads the SRBs'); GUID = PEG's count of
// unconverged passes in a row over CW_PEG_UNCONV (cwPegApply). Both end at MECO (the lamps they lit go dark).
LOCAL ascCwFc IS LEXICON().
LOCAL ascCwGd IS LEXICON().
FUNCTION ascCwChk2 {
  PARAMETER ut.
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL fr IS -1.
  LOCAL un IS 0.
  IF asc["t_meco"] < 0 {
    FOR eg IN asc["ssme"] {
      IF eg:IGNITION AND NOT eg:FLAMEOUT AND eg:HASGIMBAL { IF NOT eg:GIMBAL:LOCK {
        SET fr TO MAX(fr, MAX(ABS(eg:GIMBAL:PITCHANGLE), ABS(eg:GIMBAL:YAWANGLE))).
      } }
    }
    IF asc["s2_on"] AND asc["g"]:HASKEY("peg") { SET un TO asc["g"]["peg"]["unconv"]. }
  }
  cwGmbApply(ascCwFc, ut, fr).
  cwPegApply(ascCwGd, un).
}
cwInit(ascCwMet@).
cwListen().
cwCheck("MPS", ascCwChk@, 0.5).
cwCheck("FCS", ascCwChk2@, 0.5).
cwuiStart().
// the OMS-2 plan's file; an ATO's OMS-1 plan's (ops2q's latest-plan pick reads both)
LOCAL asc_oms2_file IS "0:/oms2_plan.txt".
LOCAL asc_oms1_file IS "0:/oms1_plan.txt".
// THE THRUST AXIS: stage 2 puts the SSMEs' thrust axis, not the nose, on PEG's command, so the heads-up roll turns
// about that axis (about the nose it leaves a yaw offset). The axis in the body frame (x star, y top, z nose) is each
// pass's sensed dv, taken below TB_Q_ON kPa (aero spoils it above) and outside the roll, filtered with TB_GAIN from
// the prior (two flights measured 11.7 / 11.9 deg toward the belly); the compensation ramps in from TB_Q_OFF to
// TB_Q_ON kPa. Stage 1's command turns at most S1_RATE deg/s per axis (a liftoff roll to the azimuth at 36 deg/s set
// off a +-12 deg/s yaw swing).
LOCAL asc_tb_prior IS V(0, -SIN(12), COS(12)).
LOCAL asc_tb_q_off IS 4.
LOCAL asc_tb_q_on IS 1.
LOCAL asc_tb_gain IS 0.5.
LOCAL asc_tb_max IS 20.
// the 2EO TAL's alpha floor (asc_af_hold): PEG would pitch a 2EO TAL to negative alpha; below asc_af_alt alpha is
// held at asc_af_alpha or above, m and deg
LOCAL asc_af_alt IS 80000.
LOCAL asc_af_alpha IS -2.
LOCAL asc_s1_rate IS 10.
// with the C# DAP (asc["csd"]) the turn's rate ramps up at asc_s1_racc deg/s2 to asc_s1_rate and is braked to a stop
// (sqrt(2 a left)): the roll program a smooth roll the DAP follows (offline: the nose within 0.6 deg through the roll)
LOCAL asc_s1_racc IS 2.5.
// the C# DAP's target rate (asc_dir's turn since the last pass) above asc_csd_wmax deg/s is a jump, not a turn: none fed
LOCAL asc_csd_wmax IS 15.
// the estimate, its samples, the attitude at the last pass (and whether there was one), the last stage-1 tick
SET asc["tb"] TO asc_tb_prior.
SET asc["tb_n"] TO 0.
SET asc["tbe"] TO V(0, 0, 1).          // the thrust axis asc_dir is built on (stage 2; lib_ascent_css's stick roll axis)
SET asc["f_prev"] TO SHIP:FACING.
SET asc["f_ok"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["t_att"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
// the pages up (else the console), stage 1's command still turning to the tables' (the pages' ROLL PGM), the fuel cell
SET asc["pg"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["slew"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["fc"] TO FALSE.
// the abort: its mode ("" = none, "TAL", "RTLS", "ATO"; no "AOA"), the TAL's site (its index in ASC_TAL_SITES), the
// selection's MET (-1: none yet; a stage-1 selection waits for PEG's start), the propellant check done; the OMS dump:
// its state (0 none, 1 waiting for its start, 2 burning, 3 over), its start (MET), the OMS engines lit, the OMS
// propellant at its start (t)
SET asc["abort"] TO "".
SET asc["abr"] TO asc_abr_new().   // the pages' abort marks, computed in flight
SET asc["tal_k"] TO 0.
SET asc["t_sel"] TO -1.
SET asc["tal_chk"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["tal_hand"] TO FALSE.             // the TAL's site picked by hand (the propellant check keeps it)
SET asc["oms_need"] TO FALSE.              // a stage-2 TAL's dump waits for asc_tal_need's test
SET asc["tal_nd"] TO 0.                    // its state (0 to test, 1 no dump, 2 lit, 3 lit later)
SET asc["tal_m0"] TO -1.                   // the OMS on board (t) at the first such TAL (-1: none)
SET asc["s2_t0"] TO -1.                    // stage 2's start (MET; -1: not yet)
SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0.
SET asc["oms_t0"] TO -1.
SET asc["oms"] TO LIST().
SET asc["oms_m0"] TO 0.
// the OMS tanks / the ET's (asc_oms_parts), the oxidizer transfer into the ET and whether one was made, and whether
// the orbiter's LF / OX still need balancing
SET asc["oms_tk"] TO LIST().
SET asc["oms_tr"] TO 0.
SET asc["oms_tro"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE.
// the fuel cell's LF / OX locked while the AJ10s dump (asc_oms_lock): LIST(resource, ENABLED before)
SET asc["oms_lk"] TO LIST().
SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 0.                  // t the dump still had to go when it stopped (99 = to empty)
SET asc["oms_ct"] TO FALSE.                // the cut trigger armed (after the ET sep; asc_oms_cut_arm)
SET asc["ho"] TO LEXICON().                // the hand-off's hold (asc_ho_init)
SET asc["cd"] TO LEXICON().                // the countdown's state (asc_cd_new, on the pad's first pass)
SET asc["cd_txt"] TO "".                   // its text for the pages (adGuid: in place of READY)
// whether the engine-out steering is on, the roll / yaw torque loops' settling times before it, and the one after it
// (s; SET ASC_EO_TS TO 6. before the run tries another)
SET asc["eo_st"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["eo_ts0"] TO LIST(2, 2).
SET asc["eo_ts"] TO 4.
IF DEFINED ASC_EO_TS { SET asc["eo_ts"] TO ASC_EO_TS. }
// after an SSME failure in stage 2 the ascent DAP steers (SET ASC_EO_DAP TO FALSE. before the run: kOS's steering);
// relock = the main loop locks the steering again (MECO); the next #dap log line's time
SET asc["eo_dap"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_EO_DAP { SET asc["eo_dap"] TO ASC_EO_DAP. }
// whether an RTLS flies the DAP too (default yes)
SET asc["rtls_dap"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_RTLS_DAP { SET asc["rtls_dap"] TO ASC_RTLS_DAP. }
SET asc["relock"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["dap_log"] TO 0.
SET asc["rpy_log"] TO 0.
// the ascent DAP in C# (KalsAddon.AscDap.cs) flies liftoff to MECO in place of kOS's steering (SET ASC_DAP_CS TO
// FALSE. before the run: kOS's steering as before): the addon has it (csd_ok), it flies (csd), it failed (csd_bad: kOS's
// steering to MECO), the stage-2 set armed (csd_s2), the target at the last pass and its time, its rate fed; stage 1's
// turn rate (asc_s1_racc)
SET asc["csd_on"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_DAP_CS { SET asc["csd_on"] TO ASC_DAP_CS. }
SET asc["csd_ok"] TO ADDONS:AVAILABLE("KALS").
IF asc["csd_ok"] { SET asc["csd_ok"] TO ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("ASCDAP"). }
SET asc["am_ok"] TO ADDONS:AVAILABLE("KALS").      // The AG4 manual MECO press + the backup 3 g limiter (the DLL's ASCMECO)
IF asc["am_ok"] { SET asc["am_ok"] TO ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("ASCMECO"). }
// lib_ascent_dap's I-hat: the vessel's live tensor where the addon has ASCIHAT (the polynomials otherwise); the last
// one logged ("#ihat,kos,...")
SET ascDap["ihk"] TO ADDONS:AVAILABLE("KALS").
IF ascDap["ihk"] { SET ascDap["ihk"] TO ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("ASCIHAT"). }
SET asc["ihs"] TO "".
SET asc["csd"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["csd_bad"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["csd_s2"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["csd_dir"] TO SHIP:FACING.
SET asc["csd_t"] TO 0.
SET asc["csd_wff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
SET asc["s1r"] TO 0.
// the DAP's feed-forward (raw, rad/s; asc["wf"]: the guidance attitude's filtered rate, asc_dir at its last pass);
// the TAL's deadline for the logger waits (-1: none)
SET asc["wff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
SET asc["wf"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
SET asc["wf_dir"] TO SHIP:FACING.
SET asc["wf_t"] TO -1.
// the q x alpha limit: whether it turned asc_dir this tick, the MET of its last #qa line (-1: none)
SET asc["qa_on"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["qa_t"] TO -1.
SET asc["eff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
SET asc["aff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
SET asc["lg_wait"] TO -1.
// at a 2EO the RCS parts with their pitch / yaw / roll switches before it, and the RCS group before it
SET asc["eo_rcs"] TO LIST().
SET asc["eo_rcs0"] TO FALSE.
// the ET separation's clearing translation on the RCS (s from the separation; up = away from the ET, right =
// starboard), the RCS group before it, the separation's MET, the ET at its first sight (asc_et_rel)
SET asc["sep_up"] TO 5.
IF DEFINED ASC_SEP_UP { SET asc["sep_up"] TO ASC_SEP_UP. }
SET asc["sep_rt"] TO 1.5.
SET asc["sep_rt_rtls"] TO 5.        // an RTLS's
IF DEFINED ASC_SEP_RT { SET asc["sep_rt"] TO ASC_SEP_RT. SET asc["sep_rt_rtls"] TO ASC_SEP_RT. }
SET asc["sep_rcs0"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["t_sep"] TO 0.
SET asc["sep_v0"] TO LIST().
// the dump's size (t: ASC_TAL_DUMP, or the RTLS's two-level rule); the RTLS's state (lib_ascent_rtls.ks; empty:
// none)
SET asc["oms_dump"] TO 0.
// the OMS assist's state (asc_ast_chk: 0 before its check, 1 none then, 2 lit, 3 over, 4 off for good), the re-check
// made, its t, the OMS / the orbiter / PEG's MASS_MIN at its first light (-1: not lit), its stop (MET); asc_oms's
// console label and the stop line's reason
SET asc["ast_st"] TO 0.
SET asc["ast_rc"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["ast_x"] TO 0.
SET asc["ast_m0"] TO -1.
SET asc["ast_mo"] TO 0.
SET asc["ast_mm0"] TO 0.
SET asc["ast_toff"] TO -1.
SET asc["oms_lbl"] TO "OMS DUMP".
SET asc["oms_why"] TO "".
SET asc["rl"] TO LEXICON().
SET asc["cn"] TO LEXICON().   // the 2EO contingency's state (lib_ascent_cnt; empty: not armed)
SET asc["o2ho"] TO FALSE.      // an ATO wrote its hand-off to ops2q (asc_ato_ho)
SET asc["eo3"] TO FALSE.       // a 3EO in stage 2 picked its mode (asc_3eo_go)
SET asc["eo3_ln"] TO "".       // the pages' 3EO line (asc_3eo_work; "": lib_ascdisp's own)
SET asc["eo3_t"] TO -1.        // its last update (TIME:SECONDS)
SET asc["eo3_mg"] TO -100000.  // Its 3EO footprint margin (km; asc_3eo_work, the contingency's pick: CONT / GREEN / BLUE)
SET asc["eo3_sk"] TO 0.        // its tries without room
SET asc["rl2_ln"] TO "".       // the pages' 2EO line in an RTLS (asc_rtls_step; "": lib_ascdisp's own)
SET asc["rkdn"] TO 0.          // the RTLS's THROTTLE DOWN messages said (asc_rtls_kdn)
SET asc["drp"] TO asc_drp_new().   // the droop's state (lib_ascent_cnt: FSSR 4.3.4)
SET asc["ard"] TO ard_srch_new().   // the ARD's search (lib_ascent_ard; off until stage 2)
SET asc["etl"] TO LEXICON().        // E TAL live: the search from the pad (lib_ascent_etl; asc_etl_work)
SET asc["etl_lg"] TO FALSE.        // its #etl line in the PEG log written (the result, NOT DONE or NOT STARTED)
SET asc["etl_t0"] TO 0.            // its start (TIME:SECONDS): the PAD TAL SEARCH COMPLETE message's time
// the SRBs measured live on the pad for the E TAL (asc_srb_meas): one SRB's dry mass (t; -1 = not measured yet) and
// all the SRBs' over the I-load's (t: lib_ascent_abr's stage-1 delta leaves it out, that mass separates with them;
// 0 = the I-load flown)
SET asc["srb_dry"] TO -1.
SET asc["srb_dd"] TO 0.
SET asc["bgl"] TO bgl_new().        // the live BLUE / GREEN's sweep (lib_ascent_bgl; asc_bgl_work)
// whether the abort flown came from the 1EO automatic (the crew may then still switch: ATO <-> TAL, or RTLS while
// open), the automatic's state (0 not armed, 1 armed by a first SSME out, 3 its pick shown, 2 over) and its wait for
// the crew's own pick while TAL is open (s from the failure), the lists' next update (UT), RAND's last MET second,
// the droop's pitch last said (deg), the sites' E TAL from the pad search
SET asc["ab_auto"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["auto_st"] TO 0.
LOCAL asc_auto_wait IS 15.
SET asc["ui_next"] TO 0.
SET asc["rand_s"] TO -1.
SET asc["drp_pa"] TO -999.
SET asc["drp_said"] TO FALSE.   // the DROOP ENGAGED line shown for this engagement
SET asc["st_et"] TO LEXICON().
// the pad search (asc_ard_pad): its state, predictor, start, plane, refresh count, the hold's start, the hold given
// up, its log lines (written at liftoff, with the BLUE / GREEN sweep's if it ends on the pad)
SET asc["ardp"] TO 0.
SET asc["ardp_s1"] TO LEXICON().
SET asc["ardp_t0"] TO -1.
SET asc["ardp_iy"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
SET asc["ardp_nr"] TO 0.
SET asc["ardp_h0"] TO -1.
SET asc["ardp_to"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["ardp_log"] TO LIST().
SET asc["padc"] TO 0.               // the cache: 0 not tried, 1 a miss (a save to come), 2 a hit, 3 saved / none
SET asc["padc_key"] TO "".
SET asc["eo2_s1"] TO FALSE.            // the second SSME out came in stage 1 (armed at stage 2's start)
SET asc["oms_ind"] TO FALSE.           // the OMS engines on their own throttle (asc_oms_full)
SET asc["ei_ok"] TO -1.                // ADDONS:KALS:ENGIND there (1) or not (0); -1 unchecked
SET asc["core_ok"] TO FALSE.         // the core weighed on the pad (asc_core_meas): its t over the I-load, the ET at liftoff
SET asc["core_dm"] TO 0.
SET asc["et_lo"] TO ASC_S1P_ET.
SET asc["padcs"] TO 0.              // the C# pad search (asc_pad_cs_work: its states)
SET asc["padcs_h"] TO 0.
SET asc["padcs_in"] TO LEXICON().
SET asc["padcs_ard"] TO LEXICON().
SET asc["padcs_t0"] TO 0.
SET asc["ardcs"] TO 0.             // the C# refresh in flight (asc_live_cs_work: its states)
SET asc["ardcs_h"] TO 0.
SET asc["ardcs_t0"] TO 0.
SET asc["ardcs_t"] TO -1.
SET asc["ardcs_l0"] TO LIST().
SET asc["ardcs_bgl"] TO FALSE.
SET asc["ardcs_n"] TO 0.            // its refreshes since the last start (the event once)
SET asc["s1l"] TO 0.               // the stage-1 refreshes in C# (asc_s1l_work: 0 idle, 1 a job out, 9 over)
SET asc["s1l_h"] TO 0.
SET asc["s1l_t0"] TO -1E9.         // the last job's start (TIME:SECONDS)
SET asc["s1l_cx"] TO LEXICON().    // the last job's context (its MET, VI, masses, sites, seeds: the write-back's)
SET asc["s1l_bgl"] TO FALSE.       // the last job has the sweep
SET asc["s1l_j"] TO 0.             // jobs started
SET asc["s1l_n"] TO 0.             // results applied
SET asc["s1l_etp"] TO FALSE.       // E TAL passed (no more E TAL in the jobs)
SET asc["s1l_le"] TO FALSE.        // a refresh's E TAL on the pages (asc_etl_apply, asc_site_etal: no mass shift)
SET asc["s1l_la"] TO FALSE.        // a refresh's levels on the pages (asc_ard_apply, asc_ard_sh: no mass shift)
SET ASC_ARD_W TO asc["fr"]["w"] * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD.   // the planet's rotation for its drag (rad/s)
// THE SPLIT-S (the header): on or off, its I-loads (lib_ascent_s1's asc_s1c_cfg) with the settings before the run
// over them, the surfaces on, the saturation guard; its state (empty: not armed); the liftoff SSMEs (the OMS dump's
// propellants after a 3EO: asc_oms_parts)
SET asc["s1c_on"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS { SET asc["s1c_on"] TO ASC_SPLITS. }
SET asc["s1cfg"] TO asc_s1c_cfg().
IF DEFINED ASC_LOFT { SET asc["s1cfg"]["amax"] TO ASC_LOFT. }
IF DEFINED ASC_LOFT_QA { SET asc["s1cfg"]["qa"] TO ASC_LOFT_QA. }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_ALPHA { SET asc["s1cfg"]["alpha"] TO MIN(80, MAX(0, ASC_SPLITS_ALPHA)). }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_NZ { SET asc["s1cfg"]["nz"] TO ASC_SPLITS_NZ. }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_HOLD { SET asc["s1cfg"]["hold"] TO ASC_SPLITS_HOLD. }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_RATE { SET asc["s1cfg"]["rate"] TO ASC_SPLITS_RATE. }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_UP_T { SET asc["s1cfg"]["up_t"] TO ASC_SPLITS_UP_T. }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_A0 { SET asc["s1cfg"]["a0"] TO MIN(80, MAX(0, ASC_SPLITS_A0)). }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_TS { SET asc["s1cfg"]["ts"] TO ASC_SPLITS_TS. }
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_WAIT { SET asc["s1cfg"]["wait"] TO MAX(0, ASC_SPLITS_WAIT). }   // the crew's window, s
SET asc["s1c_surf"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_LOFT_SURF { SET asc["s1c_surf"] TO ASC_LOFT_SURF. }
SET asc["s1c_guard"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_LOFT_GUARD { SET asc["s1c_guard"] TO ASC_LOFT_GUARD. }
SET asc["s1c_dap"] TO TRUE.
IF DEFINED ASC_SPLITS_DAP { SET asc["s1c_dap"] TO ASC_SPLITS_DAP. }
SET asc["s1c"] TO LEXICON().
SET asc["s1w"] TO -1.               // the crew's window's end (MET s; -1: none open)
SET asc["ssme0"] TO LIST().

// "A 1 B 2 ..." -> LIST(LIST("A", 1, FALSE), ...): the word upper case, the MET (-1 when not a number), not done yet
FUNCTION asc_pairs {
  PARAMETER txt.
  LOCAL w IS LIST().
  LOCAL out IS LIST().
  FOR s IN ("" + txt):SPLIT(" ") { IF s <> "" { w:ADD(s). } }
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i + 1 >= w:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 2. } DO {
    out:ADD(LIST(w[i]:TOUPPER, w[i + 1]:TONUMBER(-1), FALSE)).
  }
  RETURN out.
}

// the failures (ASC_EO: LIST(SSME, MET, done)) and the abort (ASC_AB: LIST(mode, MET, done)) set before the run
// the lists have their own names: kOS names are case-insensitive, so a LOCAL asc_eo would be ASC_EO itself and hide
// the string set before the run (asc_pairs would get the empty list: no failure ever due)
LOCAL asc_eo_due IS LIST().
IF DEFINED ASC_EO { SET asc_eo_due TO asc_pairs(ASC_EO). }
LOCAL asc_ab_due IS LIST().
IF DEFINED ASC_AB { SET asc_ab_due TO asc_pairs(ASC_AB). }

FUNCTION asc_met {
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 { RETURN 0. }
  RETURN TIME:SECONDS - asc["t_lo"].
}

// The I-loads were made for this planet: its MU and radius within 1e-4, or nothing flies.
FUNCTION asc_body_ok {
  LOCAL dmu IS ABS(BODY:MU / ASC_MU - 1).
  LOCAL drr IS ABS(BODY:RADIUS / ASC_R - 1).
  IF dmu > 1e-4 OR drr > 1e-4 {
    PRINT "ops1: the I-loads are for MU " + ASC_MU + " and R " + ASC_R + ".".
    PRINT "       " + BODY:NAME + " has MU " + BODY:MU + " and R " + BODY:RADIUS + ": not flown.".
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  RETURN TRUE.
}

// The target plane must pass over the pad northbound (southbound: ASC_LAUNCH_DIR -1; the pad's latitude below the
// inclination).
FUNCTION asc_plane_ok {
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL fr IS asc_frame_new(ut).
  IF asc_iyd(asc_sample(fr, ut)[1], ASC_TGT_INC, ASC_PLANE_DLNG):MAG = 0 {
    PRINT "ops1: no " + (CHOOSE "northbound" IF ASC_LAUNCH_DIR > 0 ELSE "southbound") + " pass over the pad at "
      + "inclination " + ASC_TGT_INC + " deg: not flown.".
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  RETURN TRUE.
}

// The attitude command d0 turned toward d1 by at most st deg per axis: the nose by a slerp step, then the roll about the
// new nose.
FUNCTION asc_turn {
  PARAMETER d0, d1, st.
  LOCAL f0 IS d0:FOREVECTOR.
  LOCAL f1 IS d1:FOREVECTOR.
  LOCAL fa IS VANG(f0, f1).
  LOCAL fn IS f1.
  IF fa > st AND fa < 179.9 { SET fn TO ((f0 * SIN(fa - st) + f1 * SIN(st)) / SIN(fa)):NORMALIZED. }
  LOCAL ua IS VXCL(fn, d0:TOPVECTOR):NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL ub IS VXCL(fn, d1:TOPVECTOR):NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL un IS ub.
  IF VANG(ua, ub) > st {
    IF VDOT(VCRS(ua, ub), fn) >= 0 { SET un TO ANGLEAXIS(st, fn) * ua. } ELSE { SET un TO ANGLEAXIS(-st, fn) * ua. }
  }
  RETURN LOOKDIRUP(fn, un).
}

// The SSMEs' variant by their full vacuum thrust (RMM's Cotopaxi configs, ASC_SSME_VARIANTS: FOCF 522 kN = the rated
// 100 % PL, Block I 546 = 104.6 %, Block II 570 = 109.2 % (the late Shuttle's), Block III 626 (the SLS-like)): the PL ->
// KSP throttle from it and every PL command capped at the engines' full thrust (Block I: its abort level 104.6 %), so
// the SSMEs fly 104 % of the rated thrust and up to 109 % in an abort on every variant.
// The engines not throttle-locked above half the rated thrust (the SSMEs; not the SRBs, not the OMS): FALSE until found.
// The variant's line is kept in asc["ssme_txt"]: it runs before the PEG log opens (liftoff, or an RSLS abort), which
// writes it.
FUNCTION asc_ssme_detect {
  PARAMETER engs.
  LOCAL f IS 0.
  FOR en IN engs {
    IF NOT en:THROTTLELOCK {
      LOCAL a IS en:POSSIBLETHRUSTAT(0).
      IF a > ASC_SSME_RPL / 2 AND (f = 0 OR a < f) { SET f TO a. }
    }
  }
  IF f = 0 { RETURN FALSE. }
  LOCAL pl IS 100 * f / ASC_SSME_RPL.
  SET ASC_PL_TO_KSP TO 100 / pl.
  SET ASC_K_STAGE1 TO MIN(ASC_K_STAGE1, pl).
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= ASC_THROT:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
    SET ASC_THROT[i] TO MIN(ASC_THROT[i], pl).
  }
  SET ASC_KMAX TO MIN(ASC_KMAX, pl).
  SET ASC_KMAX_ABORT TO MIN(ASC_KMAX_ABORT, pl).
  // The first-stage state was built at load with k_cmd = the uncapped ASC_K_STAGE1 (104): until the first
  // throttle step (V_rel 18 m/s) stage 1 flew 104 on a 100 % FOCF vehicle, "THROTTLE UP 104" then "THROTTLE DOWN
  // 100" at T+3. Capped here too (before any step: j = 0), so no throttle-up past the variant's full thrust.
  IF asc["s1"]["j"] = 0 { SET asc["s1"]["k_cmd"] TO MIN(asc["s1"]["k_cmd"], pl). }
  LOCAL nm IS "UNKNOWN".
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= ASC_SSME_VARIANTS:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 2. } DO {
    IF ABS(f - ASC_SSME_VARIANTS[i + 1]) < 3 { SET nm TO ASC_SSME_VARIANTS[i]. }
  }
  SET asc["ssme_txt"] TO "SSMES " + nm + " (" + ROUND(f) + " KN VAC = " + ROUND(pl, 1) + " %): " + ROUND(ASC_KMAX, 1)
    + " % NOMINAL, " + ROUND(ASC_KMAX_ABORT, 1) + " % IN AN ABORT".
  asc_note(asc, asc["ssme_txt"]).
  RETURN TRUE.
}

// KMAX to the abort level (ASC_KMAX_ABORT) at an SSME out or an abort's start, once; the running stage-2 K command with
// it (not under G-LIM, which moves K itself up to KMAX, nor past the fine count); stage 1 takes KMAX itself with an
// SSME out, the RTLS reads it at its start (asc_rtls_init). The message leaves out why.
FUNCTION asc_kabort {
  PARAMETER why.
  asc_ast_off(why).                          // an abort or an SSME out ends the OMS assist first
  IF ASC_KMAX >= ASC_KMAX_ABORT { RETURN. }
  SET ASC_KMAX TO ASC_KMAX_ABORT.
  IF asc["s2_on"] {
    LOCAL g IS asc["g"].
    IF NOT g["glim_on"] AND NOT g["S_MECO"] { SET g["K_CMD"] TO ASC_KMAX. }
  }
  asc_event(asc, "ABORT: THROTTLE UP " + ROUND(ASC_KMAX, 1)).
}

// The throttle messages show only at the max-q bucket, an abort and an RTLS's throttle-down: in an RTLS, THROTTLE
// DOWN <k> once at the first step down (PEG's flyback throttle, a 3-engine RTLS's start at 70) and once at the floor
// ASC_KMIN (the pitchdown's too); k = stage 2's K_CMD this tick, asc["kcmd"] the last tick's; asc["rkdn"] 0, 1 (the
// first said), 2 (the floor said)
FUNCTION asc_rtls_kdn {
  PARAMETER k.
  IF asc["abort"] <> "RTLS" OR k > asc["kcmd"] - 0.05 OR asc["rkdn"] = 2 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL lo IS k <= ASC_KMIN + 0.05.
  IF asc["rkdn"] = 0 OR lo {
    asc_event(asc, "THROTTLE DOWN " + ROUND(k)).
    SET asc["rkdn"] TO CHOOSE 2 IF lo ELSE 1.
  }
}

// The gimbals centred until liftoff: on the pad the locked steering would drive the clamped stack's gimbals. At the
// pad's first tick every gimbal is set to the craft's VAB state, whatever a stopped run left (its locks: the pad's,
// MECO's, an engine out's, the RSLS's; the EO's roll assignment): the SSMEs' and SRBs' pitch, yaw and roll on, limit
// 100 %, all in the list asc["gl_pad"] (locked = centred until liftoff: KSP centres a locked gimbal; free when
// ASC_PAD_GLOCK_ON is FALSE); the OMS's locked (css_dap unlocks its own). asc_pad unlocks the lit ones at liftoff. An
// event says how many were not in that state.
GLOBAL ASC_PAD_GLOCK_ON IS TRUE.          // FALSE: the gimbals free on the pad
FUNCTION asc_pad_glock {
  LOCAL es IS LIST().
  LIST ENGINES IN es.
  LOCAL L IS LIST().
  LOCAL nf IS 0.
  FOR en IN es {
    IF en:HASGIMBAL {
      LOCAL gm IS en:GIMBAL.
      IF en:NAME:CONTAINS("AJ10") {
        IF NOT gm:LOCK { SET gm:LOCK TO TRUE. SET nf TO nf + 1. }
      } ELSE {
        IF gm:LOCK OR NOT gm:PITCH OR NOT gm:YAW OR NOT gm:ROLL OR gm:LIMIT < 100 { SET nf TO nf + 1. }
        SET gm:PITCH TO TRUE. SET gm:YAW TO TRUE. SET gm:ROLL TO TRUE. SET gm:LIMIT TO 100.
        SET gm:LOCK TO ASC_PAD_GLOCK_ON.
        IF ASC_PAD_GLOCK_ON { L:ADD(en). }
      }
    }
  }
  SET asc["gl_pad"] TO L.
  IF nf > 0 { asc_event(asc, "PAD: " + nf + " GIMBALS RESET"). }
}

// Every C# switch logged: the events say once that PEG flies in the KAL/S coprocessor (lib_ascent_peg's ASC_PEG_CS_N >
// 0), and once when PEG (ASC_PEG_CS_ERR), the abort searches' flights (lib_ascent_ard's ASC_ARD_CS_ERR) or the HUD's
// inputs (ASC_HUD_CS_ERR) fell back to kOS. The pad search and the in-flight refreshes say their own ("PAD SEARCH IN C#" / "ABORT REFRESH IN C#" ...).
GLOBAL ASC_CS_SAID IS LEXICON().
FUNCTION asc_cs_say {
  IF (DEFINED ASC_PEG_CS_N) AND NOT ASC_CS_SAID:HASKEY("peg") { IF ASC_PEG_CS_N > 0 {
    SET ASC_CS_SAID["peg"] TO 1.
    asc_note(asc, "PEG IN C#").
  } }
  IF (DEFINED ASC_PEG_CS_ERR) AND NOT ASC_CS_SAID:HASKEY("pegx") { IF ASC_PEG_CS_ERR <> "" {
    SET ASC_CS_SAID["pegx"] TO 1.
    asc_event(asc, "PEG: KOS (" + ASC_PEG_CS_ERR + ")").
  } }
  IF (DEFINED ASC_ARD_CS_ERR) AND NOT ASC_CS_SAID:HASKEY("ardx") { IF ASC_ARD_CS_ERR <> "" {
    SET ASC_CS_SAID["ardx"] TO 1.
    asc_event(asc, "ABORT FLIGHTS: KOS (" + ASC_ARD_CS_ERR + ")").
  } }
  IF (DEFINED ASC_HUD_CS_ERR) AND NOT ASC_CS_SAID:HASKEY("hudx") { IF ASC_HUD_CS_ERR <> "" {
    SET ASC_CS_SAID["hudx"] TO 1.
    asc_event(asc, "HUD: KOS (" + ASC_HUD_CS_ERR + ")").
  } }
}

// RSLS (lib_ascent_cd asc_cd_watch): the count stopped on the pad, every SSME shut down, the SRBs not lit. The throttle 0;
// once: the event and the count's lines in their own log (logs/ascent_peg_<t>.csv: no liftoff); the run ends
// ASC_CD_RSLS_HOLD s later (the end: the throttle 0, the controls released).
FUNCTION asc_pad_rsls {
  PARAMETER cdst.
  SET asc["kcmd"] TO 0.
  SET asc_thr TO 0.
  IF NOT cdst:HASKEY("t_rsls") {
    SET cdst["t_rsls"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
    LOCAL k IS "?".
    LOCAL idp IS adEngIds(cdst["eng"]).
    // adEngIds' map also holds "rt" (a vector: no UID suffix) and the SRBs: only the three SSMEs' letters
    FOR kk IN LIST("L", "C", "R") { IF idp:HASKEY(kk) { IF idp[kk]:UID = cdst["rsls_uid"] { SET k TO kk. } } }
    LOCAL w IS "OUT".
    IF cdst["rsls_k"] = "no start" { SET w TO "FAILED TO START". }
    ELSE IF cdst["rsls_k"]:STARTSWITH("low") { SET w TO "BELOW 90 % (" + cdst["rsls_k"]:SUBSTRING(4, cdst["rsls_k"]:LENGTH - 4) + " %)". }
    IF ASC_LGON { SET asc["log"] TO "0:/logs/ascent_peg_" + logFreeTag(ROUND(TIME:SECONDS), LIST("0:/logs/ascent_peg_", "0:/logs/ascdap_"), ".csv") + ".csv". }   // One id per flight, never a reused file
    SET FL_LOG TO asc["log"].                 // The failures' lines go to this flight's log ("" = no log)
    FOR cdl IN cdst["log"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG cdl TO asc["log"]. } }
    IF asc:HASKEY("ssme_txt") { asc_note(asc, asc["ssme_txt"]). }   // the SSMEs' variant, found before the log opened
    asc_event(asc, "RSLS ABORT: SSME " + k + " " + w + " AT T-" + ROUND(MAX(0, cdst["t0"] - TIME:SECONDS), 1)
                   + ". SSMES SHUT DOWN, SRBS NOT LIT").
  }
  IF TIME:SECONDS >= cdst["t_rsls"] + ASC_CD_RSLS_HOLD { RETURN "DONE". }
  RETURN "PAD".
}

// ---- the phases: each runs one tick and returns the next phase
FUNCTION asc_pad {
  // the pad attitude held; the countdown flies the engines' start and the SRBs' stage (lib_ascent_cd: the throttle 0
  // until main engine start, then its ramp to 100 %); without it (ASC_CD FALSE, or an SSME already lit) the throttle at
  // K_STAGE1 before the crew starts the engines; liftoff when the vessel leaves the pad: the frame starts, PEG's plane
  // is set through the pad (launch when ready), the SSMEs and the ET's load are read; MET from T-0 when the count fired
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("gl_pad") { asc_pad_glock(). }   // the gimbals centred until liftoff, set as built
  IF NOT asc["ssme_ok"] {
    LOCAL es IS LIST().
    LIST ENGINES IN es.
    SET asc["ssme_ok"] TO asc_ssme_detect(es).
  }
  IF asc["cd"]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["cd"] TO asc_cd_new(ASC_CD_ON). }
  LOCAL cdst IS asc["cd"].                  // (not cd: CD is a kOS command)
  IF cdst["st"] = "OFF" {
    SET asc["kcmd"] TO ASC_K_STAGE1.
  } ELSE {
    IF cdst["st"] = "HOLD" { SET cdst["hold_x"] TO asc_pad_hold(). }   // the searches hold the count at T-30
    asc_cd_tick(cdst).
    IF cdst["t_mes"] > 0 AND NOT asc:HASKEY("mes_ev") {   // the first SSME started
      SET asc["mes_ev"] TO TRUE.
      asc_event(asc, "SSME START").
    }
    SET asc["kcmd"] TO cdst["k"].
    SET asc["cd_txt"] TO cdst["txt"].
    IF cdst["st"] = "RSLS" { RETURN asc_pad_rsls(cdst). }   // RSLS: the count stopped, the SSMEs shut down
  }
  SET asc_thr TO asc["kcmd"] / 100 * ASC_PL_TO_KSP.
  IF SHIP:STATUS = "FLYING" OR SHIP:VERTICALSPEED > 1 {
    LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
    SET asc["t_lo"] TO ut.
    IF cdst["t_fire"] > 0 { SET asc["t_lo"] TO cdst["t_fire"]. }   // MET from T-0 (the SRBs' stage)
    SET asc["cd_txt"] TO "".
    IF EXISTS("1:/abort_mode.txt") { DELETEPATH("1:/abort_mode.txt"). }   // lib_aoa's AOA flag, an earlier flight's
    IF EXISTS("1:/ops2q_ho.txt") { DELETEPATH("1:/ops2q_ho.txt"). }       // an earlier flight's ATO hand-off to ops2q
    IF asc:HASKEY("gl_pad") {                  // the pad's locks off for the engines still lit (a failed one stays)
      LOCAL n IS 0.
      FOR en IN asc["gl_pad"] { IF en:IGNITION AND NOT en:FLAMEOUT { SET en:GIMBAL:LOCK TO FALSE. SET n TO n + 1. } }
      SET asc["gl_n"] TO n.
    }
    SET asc["fr"] TO asc_frame_new(ut).
    SET asc["iyd"] TO asc_iyd(asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut)[1], ASC_TGT_INC, ASC_PLANE_DLNG).
    SET asc["ssme"] TO asc_eo_lift(cdst, asc_liquids()).
    SET asc["ssme0"] TO asc["ssme"]:COPY.     // the liftoff SSMEs (asc_oms_parts after a 3EO)
    IF NOT asc["ssme_ok"] { SET asc["ssme_ok"] TO asc_ssme_detect(asc["ssme"]). }
    SET asc["et_full"] TO asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]).
    IF ASC_LGON { SET asc["log"] TO "0:/logs/ascent_peg_" + logFreeTag(ROUND(ut), LIST("0:/logs/ascent_peg_", "0:/logs/ascdap_"), ".csv") + ".csv". }   // One id per flight, never a reused file
    SET FL_LOG TO asc["log"].                 // The failures' lines go to this flight's log ("" = no log)
    IF cdst:LENGTH > 0 {                       // the count's lines, then the liftoff's delay after T-0
      FOR cdl IN cdst["log"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG cdl TO asc["log"]. } }
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cd,liftoff," + (CHOOSE ROUND(ut - cdst["t_fire"], 3) IF cdst["t_fire"] > 0 ELSE -1) + "," + cdst["st"] TO asc["log"]. }
    }
    FOR apl IN asc["ardp_log"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG apl TO asc["log"]. } }   // the pad search's lines
    IF asc:HASKEY("ssme_txt") { asc_note(asc, asc["ssme_txt"]). }   // the SSMEs' variant, found before the log opened
    IF ASC_O6_NOTE <> "" { asc_note(asc, ASC_O6_NOTE). }
    IF ASC_AST_PRE_LOG <> "" {                 // the launch box's assist estimate
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#astpre,x,e0,lim,cap,e_cap,ms,prop,vgo,vd,inc,mo,om,mse,F,cs,mds" TO asc["log"]. }
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG ASC_AST_PRE_LOG TO asc["log"]. }
    }
    IF asc:HASKEY("gl_pad") { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#glock,liftoff," + asc["gl_pad"]:LENGTH + "," + asc["gl_n"] TO asc["log"]. } }
    asc["ardp_log"]:CLEAR().
    RETURN "STAGE1".
  }
  RETURN "PAD".
}

FUNCTION asc_stage1 {
  // the vertical rise, the tables, the tail-off rate, the throttle steps; SRBSEP once every lit SRB has flamed out,
  // or at the time backup (ASC_SRB_SEP_BKUP)
  IF asc["srbs"]:LENGTH = 0 {
    FOR en IN asc_srbs() { IF en:IGNITION { asc["srbs"]:ADD(en). } }
  }
  LOCAL vrel IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG.
  LOCAL att IS asc_s1_att(asc["s1"], asc_met(), vrel, SHIP:ALTITUDE).
  LOCAL dt IS MIN(MAX(TIME:SECONDS - asc["t_att"], 0), 0.2).
  SET asc["t_att"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  IF att:LENGTH = 3 {
    LOCAL tgt IS HEADING(att[1], att[0], att[2]).
    IF asc["s1c"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET tgt TO asc_s1c_dir(att). }   // the split-S's loft, then the nose to the wind
    LOCAL st IS asc_s1_rate * dt.
    IF asc["csd"] {
      LOCAL rem IS MAX(VANG(asc_dir:FOREVECTOR, tgt:FOREVECTOR), VANG(asc_dir:TOPVECTOR, tgt:TOPVECTOR)).
      SET asc["s1r"] TO MIN(asc_s1_rate, MIN(asc["s1r"] + asc_s1_racc * dt, SQRT(2 * asc_s1_racc * rem))).
      SET st TO asc["s1r"] * dt.
    }
    SET asc_dir TO asc_turn(asc_dir, tgt, st).
    SET asc["slew"] TO VANG(asc_dir:TOPVECTOR, tgt:TOPVECTOR) > 1.
  }
  LOCAL k0 IS asc["kcmd"].
  SET asc["kcmd"] TO asc_s1_thr(asc["s1"], vrel).
  // the max-q bucket's steps as messages (THROTTLE DOWN / THROTTLE UP <% rated thrust>, PL %), on three SSMEs (else
  // KMAX below)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 3 {
    IF asc["kcmd"] < k0 - 0.05 { asc_event(asc, "THROTTLE DOWN " + ROUND(asc["kcmd"])). }
    ELSE IF asc["kcmd"] > k0 + 0.05 { asc_event(asc, "THROTTLE UP " + ROUND(asc["kcmd"])). }
  }
  // with an SSME out the boost throttle steps stop and KMAX flies to SRB sep (FSSR 4.8.9, the SSME-out safing task;
  // 4.2.4 skips its throttling after a failure): no 72 % bucket on two SSMEs (offline: max q within 0.4 % of the
  // nominal's)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 3 { SET asc["kcmd"] TO ASC_KMAX. }
  SET asc_thr TO asc["kcmd"] / 100 * ASC_PL_TO_KSP.
  IF asc["s1c"]:LENGTH > 0 { asc_s1c_tick(dt). }   // the split-S's OMS dump, its guard, its log
  LOCAL bo IS asc_srb_out(asc["srbs"]).
  IF NOT bo AND asc_met() >= ASC_SRB_SEP_BKUP {   // the time backup: no burnout cue by now
    asc_event(asc, "SRB SEP BACKUP").
    SET bo TO TRUE.
  }
  IF asc["s1w"] >= 0 { asc_s1c_win(bo). }     // the crew's window: the pick at its end or the burnout
  IF bo {
    IF asc["s1c"]:LENGTH > 0 { RETURN "S1CSEP". }
    RETURN "SRBSEP".
  }
  RETURN "STAGE1".
}

FUNCTION asc_srbsep {
  // the separation (the craft's next stage, or the next ones: asc_sep_more); the attitude stays at the last stage-1
  // command (the FSSR's EV25E freeze)
  IF NOT STAGE:READY { RETURN "SRBSEP". }
  LOCAL n0 IS STAGE:NUMBER.
  LOCAL want IS asc_sep_in(asc["srbs"]).
  STAGE.
  IF asc_sep_more(n0, want) {
    asc_event(asc, "SRB SEP: STAGE " + (n0 - 1) + ", STAGING ON").
    RETURN "SRBSEP".
  }
  RETURN "STAGE2".
}

// A separation's STAGE can find its stage empty: a part lost in flight (a rudder taking the drag chute, the craft's
// only stage-0 part) empties a stage, the game drops it and shifts the stages above it down by one, while the current
// stage stays. So the separation stages on, one STAGE a pass, until the stage that holds the separated part's
// decoupler has fired. asc_sep_in: the latest stage any of the parts ps decouples in (Part:DECOUPLEDIN, the stage of
// its nearest decoupler, read live; -1 without one); asc_sep_more: another STAGE is due after this one (n0 = the stage
// number before it); with no decoupler known, one STAGE as before.
FUNCTION asc_sep_in {
  PARAMETER ps.
  LOCAL w IS -1.
  FOR p IN ps { SET w TO MAX(w, p:DECOUPLEDIN). }
  RETURN w.
}

FUNCTION asc_sep_more {
  PARAMETER n0, want.
  RETURN want >= 0 AND n0 - 1 > want.
}

// ---- THE SPLIT-S (the header). NOT FSSR (never certified). The laws: lib_ascent_s1's asc_s1c_*.

// A second (or third) SSME out in stage 1 (asc_fail): SPLITS selected (asc_abort refuses any other from now), the loft
// (asc_s1c_dir), the control surfaces on, the OMS dump from the failure + OMS_DLY s to TA1 (asc_s1c_tick), the 2EO line
// the mode flown; the logger kept on past the SSMEs' stop (ascent_log.ks stops LG_END_S s after it: a 3EO at 40 s would
// end the log before the sep), its end at the sequence's end; what it changes saved for a BAILOUT in the crew's
// window (asc_s1c_bail), the window opened after a 2EO with the pages up
FUNCTION asc_s1c_arm {
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL c IS asc["s1cfg"]:COPY.
  SET c["t_eo"] TO met.
  SET c["n"] TO asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
  SET c["amax0"] TO c["amax"].
  SET c["th_tab"] TO 90.
  SET c["th_cmd"] TO 90.
  SET c["wind"] TO 0.
  SET c["sat0"] TO -1.
  SET c["sat_said"] TO FALSE.
  SET c["log_t"] TO 0.
  SET c["t_sep"] TO -1.
  SET c["acmd"] TO 0.
  SET c["nzf"] TO 0.
  SET c["v0"] TO SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT.
  SET c["u0"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  SET c["t_oms"] TO -1.
  SET c["up_on"] TO FALSE.
  SET c["rp"] TO FALSE.               // the steering PIDs' second reset due (asc_s1c_seq)
  SET c["ts0"] TO STEERINGMANAGER:PITCHTS.
  SET c["ab0"] TO asc["abort"].      // the state before, for asc_s1c_bail
  SET c["ln0"] TO "".
  IF asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") { SET c["ln0"] TO asc["eo2_ln"]. }
  SET c["od0"] TO asc["oms_dump"].
  SET c["lg0"] TO -1.
  IF DEFINED LG_END_S { SET c["lg0"] TO LG_END_S. }
  SET c["surf0"] TO LIST().          // the surfaces' fields as they were (asc_s1c_surf)
  SET asc["s1c"] TO c.
  SET asc["abort"] TO "SPLITS".
  SET asc["ab_auto"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["auto_st"] TO 2.
  SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "SPLITS".
  SET adSel TO "SPLITS".
  asc_event(asc, (3 - c["n"]) + "EO: SPLIT-S  LOFT ALPHA " + ROUND(c["amax"], 1)).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1ch,met,alt,q,mref,gam,th_tab,th_cmd,th_fly,alpha,beta,qa,nz,amax,wind,aerr,perr,yerr,rerr,gp,gy,gr,thr,oms_st,"
    + "oms_t" TO asc["log"]. }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,arm," + met + "," + c["n"] + "," + c["amax"] + "," + c["qa"] + "," + c["th"] + "," + c["ta0"] + "," + c["ta1"]
    + "," + asc["s1c_surf"] + "," + asc["s1c_guard"] + "," + c["alpha"] + "," + c["nz"] TO asc["log"]. }
  IF asc["s1c_surf"] { asc_s1c_surf(). }
  IF met + c["oms_dly"] < c["ta1"] {
    SET asc["oms_dump"] TO 99.
    SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met + c["oms_dly"].
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
  }
  IF DEFINED LG_END_S { SET LG_END_S TO 600. }
  // after a 2EO with the pages up the crew's window, WAIT s, to pick a bailout instead (the split-S by default); the
  // split-S flies meanwhile (armed 5 s later, the offline model's turn back lost up to 3.5 km of margin for 2EOs at
  // 40-65 s), its dump and up RCS not before the window's end (asc_s1c_tick); BAILOUT + ABORT in it undoes this
  IF c["n"] = 1 AND c["wait"] > 0 AND asc["pg"] {
    SET asc["s1w"] TO met + c["wait"].
    SET asc["ui_next"] TO 0.
    IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_t0"] TO MAX(asc["oms_t0"], asc["s1w"]). }
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,win," + met + "," + asc["s1w"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  // a 2EO from MET c["bail"] on has no runway in reach -> BAILOUT by default (the real Shuttle's rule: no
  // site in reach, bail out): the window's pick starts at BAILOUT (the crew may move it to SPLITS); no window: at once
  IF c["n"] = 1 AND c["bail"] > 0 AND met >= c["bail"] {
    asc_event(asc, "SPLIT-S NO REACH: BAILOUT").
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,reach," + met + "," + c["bail"] TO asc["log"]. }
    IF asc["s1w"] >= 0 { SET adSel TO "BAILOUT". SET asc["ui_next"] TO 0. } ELSE { asc_s1c_bail(). }
  }
}

// the crew's window each stage-1 tick (asc["s1w"] its end, MET s): at its end or the SRB burnout (bo) the Mode
// list's pick flies -- BAILOUT if the crew moved it there (asc_s1c_bail), else the split-S stays (asc_s1c_lock)
FUNCTION asc_s1c_win {
  PARAMETER bo.
  IF NOT (bo OR asc_met() >= asc["s1w"]) { RETURN. }
  IF adSel = "BAILOUT" { asc_s1c_bail(). } ELSE { asc_s1c_lock(" (AUTO)"). }
}

// the split-S kept -- ABORT with SPLITS picked (tag ""), the window's end or the burnout (" (AUTO)"), a 3EO
// (" (3EO)"): the window closed, the Mode list SPLITS alone again
FUNCTION asc_s1c_lock {
  PARAMETER tag.
  SET asc["s1w"] TO -1.
  SET adSel TO "SPLITS".
  SET asc["ui_next"] TO 0.
  asc_event(asc, "SPLIT-S CONFIRMED").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,lock," + asc_met() + "," + tag:TRIM TO asc["log"]. }
}

// BAILOUT in the crew's window: asc_s1c_arm undone (its saves: the abort, the 2EO line, the dump not lit, the
// surfaces' fields, the logger's end; the up RCS is never on in the window) and no split-S for the rest of the
// flight (s1c_on FALSE): at the SRB sep asc_s2_start arms the 2EO response (asc_2eo_arm: the 2EO contingency, or the
// RTLS's 2EO in an RTLS), a 3EO later the 3EO's MECO at stage 2's start; with the loft off asc_stage1 flies the FSSR
// table's attitude again
FUNCTION asc_s1c_bail {
  LOCAL c IS asc["s1c"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  SET asc["s1w"] TO -1.
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms_off(met). } ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0. }
  SET asc["oms_dump"] TO c["od0"].
  FOR sv IN c["surf0"] { IF modLive(sv[0]) { sv[0]:SETFIELD(sv[1], sv[2]). } }
  IF c["lg0"] >= 0 { IF DEFINED LG_END_S { SET LG_END_S TO c["lg0"]. } }
  SET asc["abort"] TO c["ab0"].
  IF c["ln0"] <> "" { SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO c["ln0"]. } ELSE IF asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") { asc:REMOVE("eo2_ln"). }
  SET adSel TO c["ab0"].
  SET asc["s1c"] TO LEXICON().
  SET asc["s1c_on"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["ui_next"] TO 0.
  asc_event(asc, "BAILOUT CONFIRMED").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,bail," + met + "," + asc["abort"] TO asc["log"]. }
}

// the control surfaces on, for extra authority: every ModuleControlSurface's pitch / yaw / roll fields FALSE (TRUE =
// that axis ignored: lib_dap's lockAxis), as the Abort group's ActivateAllControls does at the sep
FUNCTION asc_s1c_surf {
  LOCAL n IS 0.
  LOCAL sv IS asc["s1c"]["surf0"].   // each field as it was, for asc_s1c_bail
  FOR m IN SHIP:MODULESNAMED(SURF_MN) {
    modReg(m).
    FOR fd IN LIST("pitch", "yaw", "roll") {
      IF FAR_ON { IF m:HASFIELD(fd + " %") { sv:ADD(LIST(m, fd + " %", m:GETFIELD(fd + " %"))). surfSetLock(m, fd, FALSE). } }
      ELSE IF m:HASFIELD(fd) { sv:ADD(LIST(m, fd, m:GETFIELD(fd))). m:SETFIELD(fd, FALSE). }
    }
    SET n TO n + 1.
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,surf," + asc_met() + "," + n TO asc["log"]. }
}

// the loft's attitude (stage 1, armed): the table's heading and roll, its pitch raised (asc_s1c_pitch); from TA0 the nose
// turned onto the relative wind (asc_s1c_wind; alpha and sideslip 0 at TA1), the top kept
FUNCTION asc_s1c_dir {
  PARAMETER att.
  LOCAL c IS asc["s1c"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL gam IS 90 - VANG(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, vs).
  LOCAL th IS asc_s1c_pitch(att[0], gam, SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA, met, c).
  SET c["th_tab"] TO att[0].
  SET c["th_cmd"] TO th.
  LOCAL d IS HEADING(att[1], th, att[2]).
  LOCAL s IS asc_s1c_wind(met, c).
  SET c["wind"] TO s.
  IF s <= 0 OR vs:MAG < 1 { RETURN d. }
  LOCAL f0 IS d:FOREVECTOR.
  LOCAL f1 IS vs:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL a IS VANG(f0, f1).
  LOCAL f IS f1.
  IF s < 1 AND a > 0.01 AND a < 179 { SET f TO ((f0 * SIN((1 - s) * a) + f1 * SIN(s * a)) / SIN(a)):NORMALIZED. }
  RETURN LOOKDIRUP(f, d:TOPVECTOR).
}

// each stage-1 tick once armed: the Nz; the OMS dump to TA1, then paused (the OMS off before the sep; the oxidizer's
// balance into the ET goes on); THE GUARD (the alpha the stack holds is not known before flight): while the SRBs'
// pitch gimbal stays at SAT of its range for SAT_T s, before the turn onto the wind, the loft's alpha down at BACK
// deg/s; from UP_T (MET s) the up RCS, before the sep (< 0: at the sep); the #s1c line at 10 Hz
FUNCTION asc_s1c_tick {
  PARAMETER dt.
  LOCAL c IS asc["s1c"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  asc_s1c_nzm(c).
  IF met >= c["ta1"] {
    IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms_off(met). } ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0. }
    IF asc["oms_bal"] { asc_oms_bal(). }
  } ELSE { asc_oms(asc["g"], met). }
  IF NOT c["up_on"] AND c["up_t"] >= 0 AND met >= c["up_t"] AND asc["s1w"] < 0 {   // not in the window
    SET c["up_on"] TO TRUE.
    SET asc["sep_rcs0"] TO RCS.
    RCS ON.
    SET SHIP:CONTROL:TOP TO 1.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,up," + met TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  LOCAL gm IS asc_s1c_gmb().
  IF asc["s1c_guard"] AND c["amax"] > 0 AND c["wind"] <= 0 {
    IF ABS(gm[0]) >= c["sat"] {
      IF c["sat0"] < 0 { SET c["sat0"] TO met. }
      IF met - c["sat0"] >= c["sat_t"] {
        SET c["amax"] TO MAX(0, c["amax"] - c["back"] * dt).
        IF NOT c["sat_said"] {
          SET c["sat_said"] TO TRUE.
          IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,sat," + met + "," + c["amax"] + "," + SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA TO asc["log"]. }
        }
      }
    } ELSE { SET c["sat0"] TO -1. }
  }
  IF TIME:SECONDS >= c["log_t"] {
    SET c["log_t"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 0.1.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c," + asc_s1c_row(c, gm) TO asc["log"]. }
  }
}

// Nz (g): the acceleration less gravity along the orbiter's top (+ = the lift at a positive alpha; the thrust's part
// with it), from one tick's velocity change, filtered over 0.25 s
// (not asc_s1c_nz: kOS names are case-insensitive and a bare name that matches a function compiles as its call;
// lib_ascent_s1's GLOBAL ASC_S1C_NZ would call it with no argument)
FUNCTION asc_s1c_nzm {
  PARAMETER c.
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL du IS ut - c["u0"].
  IF du < 0.01 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL vv IS SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT.
  LOCAL rr IS -BODY:POSITION.
  LOCAL ac IS (vv - c["v0"]) / du + rr:NORMALIZED * BODY:MU / rr:SQRMAGNITUDE.
  LOCAL nz IS VDOT(ac, SHIP:FACING:TOPVECTOR) / CONSTANT:G0.
  SET c["nzf"] TO c["nzf"] + MIN(1, du / 0.25) * (nz - c["nzf"]).
  SET c["v0"] TO vv.
  SET c["u0"] TO ut.
}

// the SRBs' gimbal (the first with its gimbal unlocked): LIST(pitch, yaw, roll) as fractions of its range (-1..1); zeros
// without one
FUNCTION asc_s1c_gmb {
  FOR en IN asc["srbs"] {
    IF en:HASGIMBAL { IF NOT en:GIMBAL:LOCK {
      RETURN LIST(en:GIMBAL:PITCHANGLE, en:GIMBAL:YAWANGLE, en:GIMBAL:ROLLANGLE).
    } }
  }
  RETURN LIST(0, 0, 0).
}

// LIST(alpha, beta) (deg) of the orbiter's facing in the relative wind vs: alpha + = the wind on the belly side (heads
// down: the nose below the wind), beta + = the wind from the right
FUNCTION asc_s1c_ab {
  PARAMETER vs.
  IF vs:MAG < 1 { RETURN LIST(0, 0). }
  LOCAL u IS vs:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL f IS SHIP:FACING.
  RETURN LIST(ARCTAN2(-VDOT(u, f:TOPVECTOR), VDOT(u, f:FOREVECTOR)), ARCSIN(MIN(1, MAX(-1, VDOT(u, f:STARVECTOR))))).
}

// the #s1c line (the #s1ch header's columns): MET, alt m, q kPa, VREL_AERO_REF / the sea-level speed of sound, gamma,
// the table's pitch, the command's, the nose's, alpha, beta, q alpha, Nz, the loft's alpha, the turn onto the wind,
// kOS's steering errors (angle, pitch, yaw, roll), the SRBs' gimbal (pitch, yaw, roll), the throttle, the dump's state,
// the OMS propellant (t)
FUNCTION asc_s1c_row {
  PARAMETER c, gm.
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL ab IS asc_s1c_ab(vs).
  LOCAL qk IS SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA.
  RETURN LIST(ROUND(asc_met(), 2), ROUND(SHIP:ALTITUDE), ROUND(qk, 2), ROUND(asc_vref(vs:MAG, SHIP:ALTITUDE) / ASC_SSSL, 3),
    ROUND(90 - VANG(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, vs), 2), ROUND(c["th_tab"], 2), ROUND(c["th_cmd"], 2),
    ROUND(90 - VANG(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, SHIP:FACING:FOREVECTOR), 2), ROUND(ab[0], 2), ROUND(ab[1], 2), ROUND(qk * ab[0], 1),
    ROUND(c["nzf"], 3), ROUND(c["amax"], 2), ROUND(c["wind"], 3), ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:ANGLEERROR, 2),
    ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:PITCHERROR, 2), ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:YAWERROR, 2), ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:ROLLERROR, 2),
    ROUND(gm[0], 3), ROUND(gm[1], 3), ROUND(gm[2], 3), ROUND(asc_thr, 3), asc["oms_st"], ROUND(asc_oms_mass(), 3)):JOIN(",").
}

// THE SEPARATION at the SRB burnout: the OMS off (a dump still waiting dropped), the throttle 0, the attitude as flown
// (alpha and sideslip ~0: asc_s1c_dir), ABORT (the craft's Abort group: the ET decoupled with the SRBs on it, the
// SSMEs off and their gimbals locked, the surfaces on); then the RCS up (away from the ET; on already from UP_T:
// asc_s1c_tick) and back, on until asc_s1c_seq stops them; the alpha command from A0, the pitch steering's response
// time TS until DONE (the free orbiter's pitch toward the ET). The C# DAP (it steers with the engines' gimbals only)
// ends here: the sep and the sequence fly CSS's Law A (lib_ascent_css's ascCssMode starts it this pass: the RCS, the
// surfaces, the OMS gimbals at ASC_CSS_OMS_LIM %), the crew's CSS axes from the stick, the AUTO axes on the sequence's
// attitude; without the KAL/S addon's FBW3, kOS's steering (PITCHTS TS), locked again by the main loop's relock
FUNCTION asc_s1c_sep {
  LOCAL c IS asc["s1c"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  // Law A flying the loft: its integrators hold the stack's trim (the SRBs', the last SSME's), zeroed for the orbiter
  IF ascCss["on"] { SET ascCss["i"] TO LIST(0, 0, 0). }
  IF asc["csd"] {
    asc_csd_off().
    SET asc["relock"] TO TRUE.
  }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms_off(met). } ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0. }
  SET asc_thr TO 0.
  SET asc["kcmd"] TO 0.
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL ab IS asc_s1c_ab(vs).
  LOCAL qk IS SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA.
  ABORT ON.
  // the cooked steering's integrators hold the stack's trim against the off-centre last SSME (L out: yaw -0.11 /
  // roll +0.02, R out the signs flipped; pitch -0.20; the steering errors ~0) and would put it on the free orbiter
  // (measured: a roll error of -12 / -17 / +6 deg in 5 s, beta 4.5 deg; C out: none): a roll wiggle at the sep. Zeroed
  // here, and once more at the sequence's first pass (c["rp"])
  STEERINGMANAGER:RESETPIDS().
  SET c["rp"] TO TRUE.
  SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["oms_tro"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["t_sep"] TO met.
  SET c["t_sep"] TO met.
  SET c["acmd"] TO c["a0"].
  SET c["ts0"] TO STEERINGMANAGER:PITCHTS.
  IF c["ts"] > 0 { SET STEERINGMANAGER:PITCHTS TO c["ts"]. }
  SET c["log_t"] TO 0.
  IF NOT c["up_on"] { SET asc["sep_rcs0"] TO RCS. }
  SET c["up_on"] TO TRUE.
  RCS ON.
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:TOP TO 1.
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:FORE TO -1.
  asc_event(asc, "SPLIT-S SEP  Q " + ROUND(qk, 1) + " KPA  ALPHA " + ROUND(ab[0], 1) + "  BETA " + ROUND(ab[1], 1) + "  H "
    + ROUND(SHIP:ALTITUDE / 1000, 1) + "K").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,sep," + met + "," + qk + "," + ab[0] + "," + ab[1] + "," + SHIP:ALTITUDE + "," + vs:MAG + ","
    + (90 - VANG(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, vs)) + "," + c["amax"] + "," + STAGE:NUMBER + "," + c["a0"] + "," + c["ts"]
    TO asc["log"]. }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1qh,met,ts,alt,q,mref,gam,alpha,beta,acmd,nz,aerr,perr,yerr,rerr,thr,oms_st,oms_t,et_d,et_top,et_fore,et_star,"
    + "et_vtop,et_vfore,stage,wp,wq,wr" TO asc["log"]. }
  RETURN "S1CSEQ".
}

// THE SEQUENCE after the sep: the staging stepped to the OMS's stage (STAGE:NUMBER 1, as after a normal ET sep; the
// chute's stays); alpha A0 for HOLD s, then up at RATE deg/s to ALPHA under the Nz limit (asc_s1c_acmd; the attitude
// about the relative wind, sideslip 0, the top kept); once alpha > EPS (the OMS thrust line) the OMS dump on
// (throttle 1, to empty; no tank locked, cut by the aft's mass) and the back RCS off, the up RCS UP_MORE s more;
// then DONE (the logger ends; OPS 6 or the crew's controls after the main loop). SEQ_MAX s without the OMS line: DONE.
FUNCTION asc_s1c_seq {
  LOCAL c IS asc["s1c"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL ts IS met - c["t_sep"].
  LOCAL dt IS MIN(MAX(TIME:SECONDS - asc["t_att"], 0), 0.2).
  SET asc["t_att"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  IF c["rp"] {                         // the steering PIDs zeroed once more, the orbiter free (asc_s1c_sep)
    STEERINGMANAGER:RESETPIDS().
    SET c["rp"] TO FALSE.
  }
  IF STAGE:NUMBER > 1 AND STAGE:READY { STAGE. }
  asc_s1c_nzm(c).
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL ab IS asc_s1c_ab(vs).
  SET c["acmd"] TO asc_s1c_acmd(c["acmd"], ts, dt, c["nzf"], c).
  IF vs:MAG > 1 {
    LOCAL u IS vs:NORMALIZED.
    LOCAL tp IS VXCL(u, asc_dir:TOPVECTOR):NORMALIZED.
    LOCAL a IS c["acmd"].
    SET asc_dir TO LOOKDIRUP(u * COS(a) + tp * SIN(a), tp * COS(a) - u * SIN(a)).
  }
  IF c["t_oms"] < 0 AND ab[0] > c["eps"] {
    SET c["t_oms"] TO met.
    SET SHIP:CONTROL:FORE TO 0.
    SET asc_thr TO 1.
    SET asc["oms_dump"] TO 99.
    SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met.
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,oms," + met + "," + ab[0] + "," + c["nzf"] TO asc["log"]. }   // no message: the log only
  }
  asc_oms(asc["g"], met).
  LOCAL fin IS c["t_oms"] >= 0 AND met >= c["t_oms"] + c["up_more"].
  IF fin { SET SHIP:CONTROL:TOP TO 0. }
  IF TIME:SECONDS >= c["log_t"] {
    SET c["log_t"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 0.1.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1cq," + asc_s1c_qrow(c, ts, ab) TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  IF NOT fin AND ts < c["seq_max"] { RETURN "S1CSEQ". }
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:TOP TO 0.
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:FORE TO 0.
  SET STEERINGMANAGER:PITCHTS TO c["ts0"].
  // the dump runs on into OPS 6 (on every hand-off, to empty) when ops6q.ks reads ASC_HO; the hold keeps alpha and
  // the top
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 AND NOT asc_ho_knows() { asc_oms_off(met). }
  ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0. }
  LOCAL a1 IS CHOOSE ab[0] IF ascCss["on"] AND ascCss["cp"] ELSE c["acmd"].   // the hold's alpha: the crew's in CSS pitch
  asc_ho_init(a1, a1, 0, TRUE).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,end," + met + "," + fin + "," + ab[0] + "," + c["nzf"] + "," + c["t_oms"] + "," + asc_oms_mass()
    TO asc["log"]. }
  IF DEFINED LG_END_S { SET LG_END_S TO 0. }
  SET asc["lg_wait"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 10.
  RETURN "DONE".
}

// the #s1cq line (the #s1qh header's columns): MET, s since the sep, alt m, q kPa, VREL_AERO_REF / the sea-level speed of
// sound, gamma, alpha, beta, the alpha command, Nz, kOS's steering errors, the throttle, the dump's state, the OMS
// propellant (t), the ET (asc_s1c_et), STAGE:NUMBER, the body rates (asc_s1c_w)
FUNCTION asc_s1c_qrow {
  PARAMETER c, ts, ab.
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  RETURN LIST(ROUND(asc_met(), 2), ROUND(ts, 2), ROUND(SHIP:ALTITUDE), ROUND(SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA, 2),
    ROUND(asc_vref(vs:MAG, SHIP:ALTITUDE) / ASC_SSSL, 3), ROUND(90 - VANG(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, vs), 2), ROUND(ab[0], 2),
    ROUND(ab[1], 2), ROUND(c["acmd"], 2), ROUND(c["nzf"], 3), ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:ANGLEERROR, 2),
    ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:PITCHERROR, 2), ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:YAWERROR, 2), ROUND(STEERINGMANAGER:ROLLERROR, 2),
    ROUND(asc_thr, 3), asc["oms_st"], ROUND(asc_oms_mass(), 3)):JOIN(",") + "," + asc_s1c_et():JOIN(",") + ","
    + STAGE:NUMBER + "," + asc_s1c_w():JOIN(",").
}

// the body rates, deg/s (lib_dap's signs; kOS's ANGULARVEL is left-handed): roll + right, pitch + nose up, yaw +
// nose right
FUNCTION asc_s1c_w {
  LOCAL w IS SHIP:ANGULARVEL * CONSTANT:RADTODEG.
  LOCAL f IS SHIP:FACING.
  RETURN LIST(ROUND(-VDOT(w, f:FOREVECTOR), 2), ROUND(-VDOT(w, f:STARVECTOR), 2), ROUND(VDOT(w, f:TOPVECTOR), 2)).
}

// the ET (with the SRBs) after the sep: the nearest other vessel within 2 km: LIST(its distance m (to its centre of
// mass), its position from the orbiter along the orbiter's top / fore / starboard m, its velocity relative to the
// orbiter along top / fore m/s); -1 and zeros without one
FUNCTION asc_s1c_et {
  LOCAL tl IS LIST().
  LIST TARGETS IN tl.
  LOCAL best IS SHIP.
  LOCAL dmin IS 2000.
  FOR ve IN tl { IF ve:DISTANCE < dmin { SET dmin TO ve:DISTANCE. SET best TO ve. } }
  IF dmin >= 2000 { RETURN LIST(-1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0). }
  LOCAL f IS SHIP:FACING.
  LOCAL p IS best:POSITION.
  LOCAL rv IS best:VELOCITY:ORBIT - SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT.
  RETURN LIST(ROUND(dmin, 2), ROUND(VDOT(p, f:TOPVECTOR), 2), ROUND(VDOT(p, f:FOREVECTOR), 2), ROUND(VDOT(p, f:STARVECTOR), 2),
    ROUND(VDOT(rv, f:TOPVECTOR), 3), ROUND(VDOT(rv, f:FOREVECTOR), 3)).
}

// The second stage starts: PEG's state (the MECO target, the plane, MASS_MIN = the core with the ET empty), the hold
// direction (the zero-alpha one now), the SSMEs, the PEG log's first lines.
FUNCTION asc_s2_start {
  PARAMETER ut, met.
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut).
  SET asc["ssme"] TO asc_liquids().
  LOCAL peg IS asc_peg_new(ASC_R + ASC_MECO_H, ASC_GAMD, ASC_VDMAG, asc["iyd"],
    SHIP:MASS - asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]), ASC_MU).
  SET asc["g"] TO asc_s2_new(peg, met, sm[1], sm[2], asc_to_i(sm[0], SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE):NORMALIZED).
  SET asc["s2_on"] TO TRUE.
  asc_am_set(1).                             // AG4 manual MECO + the 3 g backup armed (after the SRB sep)
  SET asc["s2_t0"] TO met.                   // a TAL declared now was declared in stage 1
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG asc_peg_init(peg) TO asc["log"]. }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG asc_peg_head() TO asc["log"]. }
  IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" { asc_tal_go(met). }
  IF asc["abort"] = "RTLS" { asc_rtls_go(ut, met). }
  IF asc["abort"] = "ATO" { asc_ato_go(met). }
  asc_eo_steer().                             // an SSME failed in stage 1
  // a second SSME out in stage 1 with no split-S flown: what one in stage 2 arms (asc_2eo_arm)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 1 AND asc["cn"]:LENGTH = 0 AND asc["s1c"]:LENGTH = 0 AND asc["t_meco"] < 0 {
    SET asc["eo2_s1"] TO TRUE.
    asc_2eo_arm().
  }
  asc_ard_reset().                            // the ARD from PEG's first passes
}

// ---- TAL (FSSR 4.8.1 PEG subtask 15a)
// A site's target for asc_peg_tal: its I-loads (ASC_TAL) with its position at liftoff in the inertial frame (x on the
// prime meridian at liftoff, so lat / lng as they are; R = the I-loads') and the body's rotation (deg/s).
FUNCTION asc_tal_lex {
  PARAMETER k.
  LOCAL il IS ASC_TAL[k].
  LOCAL rm IS ASC_R + il["alt"].
  LOCAL lw IS asc_tal_low(il).               // the 2EO low-energy set (lib_ascent_iload ASC_TAL_LOW_ON)
  RETURN LEXICON("ef", rm * V(COS(il["lat"]) * COS(il["lng"]), COS(il["lat"]) * SIN(il["lng"]), SIN(il["lat"])),
    "w", asc["fr"]["w"], "A", CHOOSE il["A_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["A"], "VMIN", CHOOSE il["VMIN_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["VMIN"],
    "VMAX", il["VMAX"], "CRMAX", CHOOSE il["CRMAX_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["CRMAX"],
    "RDMAG", CHOOSE il["RDMAG_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["RDMAG"], "GAMD", CHOOSE il["GAMD_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["GAMD"],
    "name", il["name"]).
}

// The FSSR's S_DROOP_TARGETS, picked here by the SSMEs left (A deviation): a TAL flies the site's low-energy set
// (lib_ascent_iload) once one SSME is left after liftoff -- a 2EO TAL, whichever way it was declared (asc_2eo_go
// re-targets one already flying)
FUNCTION asc_tal_low {
  PARAMETER il.
  RETURN ASC_TAL_LOW_ON AND il:HASKEY("A_LOW") AND asc["t_lo"] >= 0 AND asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 1.
}

// A TAL dumps only the OMS it needs, when it needs it (more left for a 2EO GREEN): one declared in stage 2 dumps only
// when the ET falls short (asc_tal_need); one declared in stage 1 (at PEG's start: its margin still falls for ~60 s)
// dumps ASC_TAL_DUMP t from ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY s after PEG's start
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_DUMP_NEED IS TRUE.   // FALSE: every TAL dumps ASC_TAL_DUMP t from ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY s after the selection
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_NEED_DT IS 10.      // s after a stage-2 selection: the margin's test (offline: flat from +9 s)
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_NEED_FREE IS 0.     // m/s: no dump while the ET's margin is this or more (asc_tal_check's ASC_TAL_MARGIN)
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_NEED_RE IS -50.     // m/s: a TAL without its dump lights it (once) when the margin falls under this
// THE LANDING WEIGHT. A stage-2 TAL whose ET margin needs no dump
// still dumps, in powered flight, the OMS that would land it over its site's limit (the real Shuttle's TAL OMS dump is a
// pre-MECO weight / c.g. dump). Flight C kept 4.15 t of OMS, came to TAEM at
// 25.46 t and stopped 31 m past MRN20's end. The limits from the A/L sim: MRN20
// (1249 m) 25.1 t -> 60 m left; ZZA30 / SNN23 (2378 m) 26.5 t -> 276 m, touchdown alpha 11.8 under the 12 deg tail cap.
// The dump takes the predicted landing mass (asc_tal_land_m) to the limit less ASC_TAL_LAND_PAD (asc_tal_land_x), tested
// with the margin (asc_tal_need: state 4); no relight by the margin after it (its thrust only adds dV).
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_LAND_ON IS TRUE.     // FALSE: the dump by the ET's margin only
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_LAND_MAX IS LEXICON("ZZA", 26.5, "MRN", 25.1, "SNN", 26.5).   // t: the landing mass over which a TAL dumps
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_LAND_PAD IS 0.3.     // t: the dump's target is the limit less this
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_MONO_KEEP IS 222.5.  // units: what ops6q's pre-entry monoprop dump keeps (MONO_PEAK_UNITS + MONO_PRE_FRAC x MONO_USED_EST)

// TAL in stage 2 (at the selection, or at PEG's start for a stage-1 selection): PEG's target to the site from its
// next pass, the OMS dump OMS_DELAY s later (after a stage-2 selection, asc_tal_need's)
FUNCTION asc_tal_go {
  PARAMETER met.
  asc_kabort("TAL").
  LOCAL tl IS asc_tal_lex(ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]).
  asc_peg_tal(asc["g"]["peg"], tl).
  SET asc["t_sel"] TO met.
  SET asc["oms_dump"] TO ASC_TAL_DUMP.
  SET asc["tal_nd"] TO 0.
  SET asc["oms_need"] TO ASC_TAL_DUMP_NEED AND ASC_TAL_DUMP > 0 AND asc["s2_t0"] >= 0 AND met > asc["s2_t0"] + 1e-6.
  IF asc["oms_need"] {                      // no dump yet (asc_tal_need tests at ASC_TAL_NEED_DT s)
    IF asc["tal_m0"] < 0 {
      IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH < 4 { SET asc["oms_tk"] TO asc_oms_parts(). }
      SET asc["tal_m0"] TO asc_oms_mass().
    }
  } ELSE IF ASC_TAL_DUMP > 0 { SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met + ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY. SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1. }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#tal," + met + "," + ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]] + "," + tl["RDMAG"] + "," + tl["GAMD"] + asc_csv_v(tl["ef"]) + ","
    + tl["w"] TO asc["log"]. }
}

// ---- ATO (FSSR 4.5.2; the AOA is chosen after OMS-1)
// At the selection in stage 2 (or at PEG's start for a stage-1 selection): PEG's MECO speed to the ATO target's from its
// next pass (FSSR 4.5.2: VDMAG for an apogee at R + ATO_H; the nominal RDMAG and GAMD kept), the AOA's too (the orbiter
// chose an AOA after MECO; A deviation: here it shares the ATO's MECO target); no OMS dump. Past the fine count PEG
// keeps its target.
FUNCTION asc_ato_go {
  PARAMETER met.
  asc_kabort(asc["abort"]).
  SET asc["t_sel"] TO met.
  IF asc["g"]["S_MECO"] { RETURN. }
  SET asc["g"]["peg"]["VDMAG"] TO ASC_ATO_VDMAG.
  LOCAL kp IS asc_kep(ASC_R + ASC_MECO_H, ASC_ATO_VDMAG, ASC_GAMD).   // the target's orbit: its perigee too
  LOCAL hp IS "".
  IF kp:LENGTH > 0 { SET hp TO " HP " + ROUND((kp[0] * (1 - kp[1]) - ASC_R) / 1000) + "K". }
  asc_event(asc, asc["abort"] + ": MECO TARGET VI " + ROUND(ASC_ATO_VDMAG) + "  HA " + ROUND(ASC_ATO_H / 1000)
    + "K" + hp).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ato," + met + "," + asc["abort"] + "," + ASC_ATO_VDMAG TO asc["log"]. }
}

// ---- RTLS (FSSR 4.6)
// At the selection in stage 2 (or at PEG's start for a stage-1 selection): the RTLS's state
// (asc_rtls_init: the fuel dissipation attitude, the OMS dump, PEG's RTLS mode); the pitchdown's nose by the measured
// thrust axis (its angle below the nose in the pitch plane).
FUNCTION asc_rtls_go {
  PARAMETER ut, met.
  asc_kabort("RTLS").
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut).
  SET asc["t_sel"] TO met.
  LOCAL rl IS asc_rtls_init(asc, met, sm[1], sm[2]).
  SET rl["toff"] TO ARCTAN2(-asc["tb"]:Y, asc["tb"]:Z).
  SET asc["rl"] TO rl.
  LOCAL pr IS asc["g"]["peg"]["RTLS"].
  asc_event(asc, "RTLS FUEL DISSIPATION  PITCH " + ROUND(rl["THETA_C"]) + "  DUMP " + ROUND(asc["oms_dump"], 1)
    + " T  MBO " + ROUND(pr["MBO"], 1) + " T").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#rtlsgo," + met + "," + rl["neng"] + "," + rl["V_FD"] + "," + rl["THETA_C"] + "," + asc["oms_dump"] + "," + pr["MBO"]
    + "," + rl["line"][0] + "," + rl["line"][1] + "," + rl["DT_TURN"] + "," + rl["toff"] + "," + asc["g"]["K_CMD"]
    TO asc["log"]. }
}

// An RTLS step on the sample (lib_ascent_rtls.ks's tasks): the PEG log's RTLS line; the phase changes and the MECO
// command in the MESSAGES
FUNCTION asc_rtls_step {
  PARAMETER met, sm, ft.
  LOCAL rl IS asc["rl"].
  LOCAL g IS asc["g"].
  LOCAL md IS rl["mode"].
  LOCAL tm IS g["T_MECO"].
  asc_rtls_tasks(asc, rl, met, sm[1], sm[2], SHIP:MASS, ft[1], ft[0]).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG asc_rtls_line(asc, rl, met) TO asc["log"]. }
  // the pages' 2EO line in the RTLS, the colour of what a second SSME out would fly now (asc_rtls_2eo_word)
  SET asc["rl2_ln"] TO asc_rtls_2eo_word(rl["mode"], asc_rtls_vhh(rl, met, sm[1], sm[2])).
  IF rl["mode"] <> md {
    LOCAL nm IS LEXICON("fd", "FUEL DISSIPATION", "turn", "PITCHAROUND", "fb", "FLYBACK", "fc", "FINE COUNT",
      "ppd", "POWERED PITCHDOWN", "m5", "MODE 5").
    asc_event(asc, "RTLS " + nm[rl["mode"]] + "  VREL " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG) + "  H "
      + adFx(SHIP:ALTITUDE / 1000, 1) + "K").
  }
  IF rl["mode"] <> md AND rl["mode"] = "turn" { fuiSimPt("PPA", 0). }   // SimSup's PPA point = the powered pitch-around starts
  IF tm < 0 AND g["T_MECO"] >= 0 { asc_event(asc, "RTLS TGO " + ROUND(g["T_MECO"] - met, 2) + " S"). }
}

// m/s, the speed over the ground toward the RTLS site (< 0: still flying away) at MET met, rr (m) / vv (m/s) inertial
FUNCTION asc_rtls_vhh {
  PARAMETER rl, met, rr, vv.
  LOCAL rt IS asc_rotz(rl["ef"], rl["w"] * met).
  RETURN VDOT(vv - asc_rtls_wxr(rl, rr), VXCL(rr:NORMALIZED, rt - rr):NORMALIZED).
}

// The FSSR 4.9.2 RTLS colour of what asc_rtls_2eo flies from RTLS mode md at vhh m/s toward the site: YELLOW in the
// fuel dissipation and the pitcharound (the FSSR's RTLS mode 2: the contingency's mode 2, asc_rtls_m2_go; GREEN once
// its law cuts for a runway end, BLUE when it never does; ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 FALSE: BLUE, the pitchdown and MECO at once,
// as the bailout: offline, 122 of 122 short of TAEM; the FSSR's BLUE / YELLOW there), ORANGE PEG on one SSME (on toward
// the site, then the cut: as mode 3), RED mode 5, RTLS the fine count or the pitchdown going on (the FSSR's region 0,
// no contingency). A deviation from the FSSR: ORANGE for PEG, the bound ASC_RTLS_M5_VH
FUNCTION asc_rtls_2eo_word {
  PARAMETER md, vhh.
  IF md = "m5" { RETURN "RED". }
  IF md = "fc" OR md = "ppd" { RETURN "RTLS". }
  IF md = "fb" { RETURN CHOOSE "RED" IF vhh >= ASC_RTLS_M5_VH ELSE "ORANGE". }
  IF ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 { RETURN "YELLOW". }   // the fuel dissipation and the pitcharound
  RETURN "BLUE".                         // the same with ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 FALSE
}
// a 2EO colour word in its colour (RED the pages' alert red, ORANGE lib_guistyle's warning orange, GREEN the pages'
// green, BLUE a blue of its own); another word as it is
FUNCTION asc_col_word {
  PARAMETER w.
  IF w = "RED" { RETURN asc_col(w, "#ff2929"). }
  IF w = "ORANGE" { RETURN asc_col(w, UI_WARN). }
  IF w = "GREEN" { RETURN asc_col(w, "#3ce03c"). }
  IF w = "BLUE" { RETURN asc_col(w, "#5c9cff"). }
  IF w = "YELLOW" { RETURN asc_col(w, AD_YELLOW). }
  RETURN w.
}

// A second SSME out in an RTLS. On the flyback at ASC_RTLS_M5_VH m/s toward the site or more, FSSR 4.9.7's mode 5
// (lib_ascent_rtls' asc_rtls_m5: offline it lands from MECO - 49..65 s where PEG on one SSME lands from MECO - 10..25 s);
// on the flyback below it PEG flies on (one SSME, to the ET's low level: offline it reaches TAEM there where mode 5 and
// the cut at once crash, both ascents); in the fuel dissipation and the pitcharound the contingency's mode 2 instead of
// the cut (asc_rtls_m2_go; ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 FALSE: the pitchdown and MECO at once, which reaches TAEM there where PEG
// and mode 5 do not); a second failure in stage 1 (armed at the SRB sep: asc["eo2_s1"], outside the offline grid)
// keeps the cut; in the fine count or the pitchdown, as they are. The hand-off: OPS 6 RTLS (CONT after mode 2).
GLOBAL ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 IS TRUE.          // FALSE: the pitchdown and MECO at once (BLUE)
FUNCTION asc_rtls_2eo {
  LOCAL rl IS asc["rl"].
  LOCAL g IS asc["g"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], TIME:SECONDS).
  LOCAL rr IS sm[1].
  LOCAL vv IS sm[2].
  LOCAL vhh IS asc_rtls_vhh(rl, met, rr, vv).
  SET rl["neng"] TO 1.                    // not rl["N"]: the same key as the plane normal rl["n"] (kOS keys ignore
                                          // case): a scalar there stops ops1q at the top vector
  SET rl["m5_tgo"] TO -1.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#rtls2eo," + met + "," + rl["mode"] + "," + vhh TO asc["log"]. }
  SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO asc_rtls_2eo_word(rl["mode"], vhh).   // the 2EO line's lock, the colour of the response
  IF rl["mode"] = "fc" OR rl["mode"] = "ppd" {
    asc_note(asc, "2EO IN AN RTLS: THE PITCHDOWN FLIES ON  VHH " + ROUND(vhh)).
  } ELSE IF rl["mode"] = "fb" AND vhh >= ASC_RTLS_M5_VH {
    SET rl["mode"] TO "m5".
    SET g["K_CMD"] TO ASC_KMAX.
    asc_event(asc, "RTLS 2EO " + asc_col_word(asc["eo2_ln"]) + "  VHH " + ROUND(vhh)).
  } ELSE IF rl["mode"] = "fb" {
    asc_event(asc, "RTLS 2EO " + asc_col_word(asc["eo2_ln"]) + "  VHH " + ROUND(vhh)).
  } ELSE IF ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 AND NOT asc["eo2_s1"] {
    asc_rtls_m2_go(met, sm, vhh).
  } ELSE {
    SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "BLUE".
    asc_rtls_ppd_start(asc, rl, met, rr, vv).
    SET g["T_MECO"] TO rl["ppd_ready_t"].
    asc_event(asc, "RTLS 2EO " + asc_col_word(asc["eo2_ln"]) + "  VHH " + ROUND(vhh)).
  }
}

// A deviation (the real Shuttle's crew picks mode 1 BLUE or mode 2 YELLOW by the sink rate after a crew delay; this
// vehicle always flies mode 2, at once): the contingency (lib_ascent_cnt) from the RTLS state now, as asc_cnt_arm's
// start -- the RTLS's thrust direction the start's, heads up (the DAP rolls; one SSME: the RCS), MODE SEL's mode 2
// forced with its hold, cap, cut law and yaw (asc_cnt_m2), the load gate (cn["rtls"]), the SSMEs at KMAX, the dump to
// empty, the abort "CONT" (its MECO, fast sep and OPS 6 hand-off; the RTLS record stays for the pages). The site is the
// law's end at its cut (GREEN); no cut: the FSSR's pitchdown, site NONE, OPS 6's BLUE bailout
FUNCTION asc_rtls_m2_go {
  PARAMETER met, sm, vhh.
  LOCAL g IS asc["g"].
  LOCAL cn IS asc_cnt_new(met, SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).
  SET cn["sel"] TO 2.
  SET cn["rtls"] TO TRUE.
  SET asc["cn"] TO cn.
  SET g["T_MECO"] TO -1.
  asc_cnt_start(cn, met, asc_rtls_dir(asc["rl"], g["peg"], met, g["hold"]), 2, TRUE).
  asc_cnt_m2in(cn, sm).
  asc_cnt_cycle(cn, met, sm[1], sm[2], asc_to_i(sm[0], SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE),
    SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA * 1000).
  SET g["K_CMD"] TO ASC_KMAX.
  SET asc["abort"] TO "CONT".
  asc_oms_empty(met).                      // the full dump for ECALs (a running RTLS dump goes on to empty)
  asc_oms_now(met).
  IF ascDap["on"] { SET ascDap["roll1"] TO TRUE. }
  SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "YELLOW".
  asc_event(asc, "RTLS 2EO " + asc_col_word("YELLOW") + "  VHH " + ROUND(vhh) + ": CONT MODE 2").
  asc_cnt_law_say(met).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt,start," + met + ",2,rtls," + cn["ph"] + "," + vhh TO asc["log"]. }
}

// The OMS propellant in the orbiter (t): by part, its OMS tanks' LF + OX (a ship-wide OMS-only sum misses the
// oxidizer the ET shares), the aft fuselage's: not the mid fuselage's, the fuel cell's
FUNCTION asc_oms_mass {                    // t of OMS propellant in the orbiter's OMS tanks (LF + OX)
  LOCAL m IS 0.
  LOCAL tk IS asc["oms_tk"].
  IF tk:LENGTH >= 4 {
    FOR pt IN tk[0] {
      FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES {
        IF tk[2]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) OR tk[3]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) { SET m TO m + rs:AMOUNT * rs:DENSITY. }
      }
    }
  }
  RETURN m.
}

// LIST(the orbiter's OMS tanks, the ET's tanks, the OMS-only propellants, the shared ones, the fuel cell's tanks), at
// the dump's start: the SSMEs burn LqdHydrogen + Oxidizer, the AJ10s LiquidFuel + Oxidizer; a part holding an OMS-only
// propellant is an OMS tank (the aft fuselage) unless it has a ModuleResourceConverter (the mid fuselage: its LF / OX
// feed the fuel cell, never the dump), one holding an SSME-only propellant (and none of the OMS's) is the ET's; a part
// beyond a decoupler (a payload's tank: lib_ascent_gui's asc_gui_beyond) is no OMS tank
FUNCTION asc_oms_parts {
  LOCAL sn IS LIST().
  LOCAL se IS asc["ssme"].
  IF se:LENGTH = 0 { SET se TO asc["ssme0"]. }   // after a 3EO the liftoff SSMEs (the split-S's dump)
  IF se:LENGTH > 0 { FOR cr IN se[0]:CONSUMEDRESOURCES:VALUES { sn:ADD(cr:NAME). } }
  IF sn:LENGTH = 0 OR asc["oms"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN LIST(LIST(), LIST(), LIST(), LIST(), LIST()). }
  LOCAL onm IS LIST().
  LOCAL sh IS LIST().
  FOR cr IN asc["oms"][0]:CONSUMEDRESOURCES:VALUES {
    IF sn:CONTAINS(cr:NAME) { sh:ADD(cr:NAME). } ELSE { onm:ADD(cr:NAME). }
  }
  LOCAL op IS LIST().
  LOCAL ep IS LIST().
  LOCAL fp IS LIST().
  FOR pt IN SHIP:PARTS {
    LOCAL ko IS FALSE.
    LOCAL ke IS FALSE.
    FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES {
      IF rs:CAPACITY > 0 AND onm:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) { SET ko TO TRUE. }
      IF rs:CAPACITY > 0 AND sn:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) AND NOT sh:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) { SET ke TO TRUE. }
    }
    IF ko AND asc_gui_beyond(pt) { SET ko TO FALSE. }   // a payload's own tank (beyond a decoupler), not the orbiter's
    IF ko { IF pt:HASMODULE("ModuleResourceConverter") { fp:ADD(pt). } ELSE { op:ADD(pt). } }
    ELSE IF ke { ep:ADD(pt). }
  }
  RETURN LIST(op, ep, onm, sh, fp).
}

// By KSP's crossfeed the AJ10s draw the shared propellant (Oxidizer) from the ET, so the orbiter's OX would stay full
// while its LF drains. Each shared propellant's surplus in the OMS tanks over the LF's fraction goes into the ET
// (kOS TRANSFER, one at a time; under 0.5 units left alone); after the dump's stop, until balanced.
FUNCTION asc_oms_bal {
  LOCAL tk IS asc["oms_tk"].
  IF tk:LENGTH < 4 { SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE. RETURN. }
  IF tk[0]:LENGTH = 0 OR tk[1]:LENGTH = 0 OR tk[3]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE. RETURN. }
  IF asc["oms_tro"] { IF asc["oms_tr"]:STATUS = "Transferring" { RETURN. } }
  LOCAL fa IS 0.
  LOCAL fc IS 0.
  LOCAL am IS LEXICON().
  LOCAL ca IS LEXICON().
  FOR nm IN tk[3] { SET am[nm] TO 0. SET ca[nm] TO 0. }
  FOR pt IN tk[0] {
    FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES {
      IF tk[2]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) { SET fa TO fa + rs:AMOUNT. SET fc TO fc + rs:CAPACITY. }
      ELSE IF am:HASKEY(rs:NAME) {
        SET am[rs:NAME] TO am[rs:NAME] + rs:AMOUNT.
        SET ca[rs:NAME] TO ca[rs:NAME] + rs:CAPACITY.
      }
    }
  }
  IF fc <= 0 { SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE. RETURN. }
  FOR nm IN tk[3] {
    LOCAL dx IS am[nm] - ca[nm] * fa / fc.
    IF dx > 0.5 {
      LOCAL tr IS TRANSFER(nm, tk[0], tk[1], dx).
      SET tr:ACTIVE TO TRUE.
      SET asc["oms_tr"] TO tr.
      SET asc["oms_tro"] TO TRUE.
      RETURN.
    }
  }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 3 { SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE. }
}

// The OMS dump drains the aft fuselage only, never the mid fuselage (its LF / OX feed the fuel cell): KSP's crossfeed
// lets the AJ10s draw from every LF / OX tank, so the fuel cell's (asc_oms_parts' 5th list) are locked (ENABLED FALSE)
// before the AJ10s light and set back as they were after their shutdown (asc_oms_off). The fuel cell (AutoShutdown
// false) may pause while they are locked. After the ET sep the mid LFO must feed the fuel cell, and the fuel priority
// drains it last (all 14 craft: the mid fuselage resPri -10, the aft 0): nothing is locked; a trigger cuts the AJ10s
// (asc_oms_cut_arm).
FUNCTION asc_oms_lock {
  PARAMETER met.
  IF asc["t_sep"] > 0 {                    // after the ET sep the mid LFO feeds the fuel cell
    asc_oms_unlock(met).
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,nolock," + met + "," + asc_oms_fc() TO asc["log"]. }
    RETURN.
  }
  asc["oms_lk"]:CLEAR().
  LOCAL tk IS asc["oms_tk"].
  IF tk:LENGTH < 5 { RETURN. }
  FOR pt IN tk[4] {
    FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES {
      IF tk[2]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) OR tk[3]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) {
        IF rs:TOGGLEABLE {
          asc["oms_lk"]:ADD(LIST(rs, rs:ENABLED)).
          SET rs:ENABLED TO FALSE.
        }
      }
    }
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,lock," + met + "," + tk[4]:LENGTH + "," + asc["oms_lk"]:LENGTH + "," + asc_oms_fc() TO asc["log"]. }
}

FUNCTION asc_oms_unlock {
  PARAMETER met.
  IF asc["oms_lk"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }
  FOR lk IN asc["oms_lk"] { SET lk[0]:ENABLED TO lk[1]. }
  asc["oms_lk"]:CLEAR().
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,unlock," + met + "," + asc_oms_fc() TO asc["log"]. }
}

// the fuel cell's tanks: "LF units,OX units" (the OMS-only propellants, the shared ones; for the log)
FUNCTION asc_oms_fc {
  LOCAL lf IS 0.
  LOCAL ox IS 0.
  LOCAL tk IS asc["oms_tk"].
  IF tk:LENGTH < 5 { RETURN "0,0". }
  FOR pt IN tk[4] {
    FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES {
      IF tk[2]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) { SET lf TO lf + rs:AMOUNT. }
      ELSE IF tk[3]:CONTAINS(rs:NAME) { SET ox TO ox + rs:AMOUNT. }
    }
  }
  RETURN "" + lf + "," + ox.
}

// The OMS dump: the OMS engines lit at oms_t0; they follow the main throttle and PEG counts their thrust (asc_engs).
// It stops once the dump's t are burned (asc["oms_dump"]), once the OMS tanks are dry (OMS_DRY t left, or every OMS
// engine flamed out), for a TAL at PEG's TGO OMS_TGO_OFF (before the fine count), for an RTLS at its fine countdown
// (S_MECO), or at MECO.
GLOBAL ASC_OMS_DRY IS 0.005.   // t: the OMS tanks dry (asc_oms_bal leaves under 0.5 units of a shared propellant)
FUNCTION asc_oms {
  PARAMETER g, met.
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 AND met >= asc["oms_t0"] {
    asc["oms"]:CLEAR().
    FOR en IN SHIP:ENGINES { IF en:NAME:CONTAINS("AJ10") { asc["oms"]:ADD(en). } }
    IF asc["oms"]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["oms_st"] TO 3. asc_event(asc, asc["oms_lbl"] + ": NO OMS ENGINES"). RETURN. }
    SET asc["oms_tk"] TO asc_oms_parts().
    asc_oms_lock(met).                       // the aft fuselage only, never the mid
    FOR en IN asc["oms"] { IF NOT en:IGNITION { en:ACTIVATE(). } }
    SET asc["oms_m0"] TO asc_oms_mass().
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 2.
    IF asc["t_sep"] > 0 { asc_oms_cut_arm(). }   // after the ET sep the cut by the aft's mass, every tick
    SET asc["oms_bal"] TO TRUE.
    IF asc["oms_lbl"] = "OMS DUMP" { asc_event(asc, "OMS DUMP " + ROUND(asc["oms_m0"], 2) + " T"). }
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,start," + met + "," + asc["oms_m0"] + "," + asc["oms_tk"][0]:LENGTH + "," + asc["oms_tk"][1]:LENGTH
      TO asc["log"]. }
  } ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 {
    asc_oms_bal().
    LOCAL mo IS asc_oms_mass().
    LOCAL burned IS asc["oms_m0"] - mo.
    LOCAL mdry IS ASC_OMS_DRY.
    IF asc["t_sep"] > 0 { SET mdry TO mdry + ASC_OMS_CUT_M. }   // after the sep the mid LFO next (no flameout)
    LOCAL dry IS mo <= mdry OR asc_all_out(asc["oms"]).
    LOCAL stop IS burned >= asc["oms_dump"] OR dry.
    IF g:HASKEY("S_MECO") { IF g["S_MECO"] { SET stop TO TRUE. } }   // the split-S's dump flies without PEG (g empty)
    IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" AND g:HASKEY("peg") {
      LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
      IF NOT p["S_INIT"] { IF p["TGO"] < ASC_TAL_OMS_TGO_OFF { SET stop TO TRUE. } }
    }
    IF stop {
      IF dry { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,dry," + met + "," + mo + "," + asc["oms_dump"] TO asc["log"]. } }
      asc_oms_off(met).
    }
  } ELSE IF asc["oms_bal"] { asc_oms_bal(). }
}

// The dump's t still to burn: its target's rest, at most what the OMS tanks hold (the aft's: the fuel cell's tanks are
// not in the dump); before its start the target (at most the tanks' once they are known); none once it is over
FUNCTION asc_oms_left {
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 {
    IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH >= 4 { RETURN MIN(asc["oms_dump"], asc_oms_mass()). }
    RETURN asc["oms_dump"].
  }
  IF asc["oms_st"] <> 2 { RETURN 0. }
  LOCAL mo IS asc_oms_mass().
  RETURN MAX(0, MIN(asc["oms_dump"] - (asc["oms_m0"] - mo), mo)).
}

FUNCTION asc_oms_off {
  PARAMETER met.
  IF asc["oms_st"] <> 2 { RETURN. }        // the cut trigger may have stopped it this tick
  LOCAL left IS asc_oms_mass().             // the stop line shows what is left
  LOCAL burned IS asc["oms_m0"] - left.
  SET asc["oms_rest"] TO MAX(0, asc["oms_dump"] - burned).   // what a hand-off starts again after the sep
  FOR en IN asc["oms"] { IF en:IGNITION { en:SHUTDOWN(). } }
  asc_oms_unlock(met).                     // after the AJ10s' shutdown: the fuel cell's tanks as they were
  asc["oms"]:CLEAR().
  asc_oms_bal().
  SET asc["oms_st"] TO 3.
  asc_event(asc, asc["oms_lbl"] + " STOP " + ROUND(left, 2) + " T").
  IF asc["oms_lbl"] <> "OMS DUMP" { asc_ast_fin(met). }   // the assist's
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,stop," + met + "," + burned TO asc["log"]. }
}

// After the ET sep the AJ10s would go on into the mid LFO once the aft is dry (no flameout to stop them), so a
// trigger checks the aft's mass every physics tick and cuts them at ASC_OMS_DRY + ASC_OMS_CUT_M or once the dump's t
// are burned; it runs on into OPS 6 (ops1q's scope lives through the RUNPATH): there the cut is quiet (no console
// text over ops6q's screen; ASC_HO["oms_cut"] TRUE tells ops6q)
GLOBAL ASC_OMS_CUT_M IS 0.01.   // t left in the aft at the cut after the sep (~0.5 s of both AJ10s)
FUNCTION asc_oms_cut_arm {
  IF asc["oms_ct"] { RETURN. }
  SET asc["oms_ct"] TO TRUE.
  SET asc["oms_ta"] TO TIME:SECONDS.     // the arm (= the relight) time
  WHEN asc_oms_cut_due() THEN {
    SET asc["oms_ct"] TO FALSE.
    IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { IF ASC_HO:LENGTH > 0 { asc_oms_cut(). } ELSE { asc_oms_off(asc_met()). } }
  }
}

FUNCTION asc_oms_cut_due {             // the trigger's test: the dump over, the aft at the cut, or its t burned
  IF asc["oms_st"] <> 2 { RETURN TRUE. }
  LOCAL lit IS FALSE.                  // none lit 1 s after the relight = ops6q shut them
  FOR en IN asc["oms"] { IF en:IGNITION { SET lit TO TRUE. } }   // down itself: disarm (else this polls all entry)
  IF NOT lit AND TIME:SECONDS > asc["oms_ta"] + 1 { RETURN TRUE. }
  LOCAL mo IS asc_oms_mass().
  RETURN mo <= ASC_OMS_DRY + ASC_OMS_CUT_M OR asc["oms_m0"] - mo >= asc["oms_dump"].
}

FUNCTION asc_oms_cut {                 // in OPS 6: the AJ10s off by part (the list kept), no console text
  LOCAL mo IS asc_oms_mass().
  LOCAL n IS 0.                        // how many it shut down (0: ops6q had)
  FOR en IN asc["oms"] { IF en:IGNITION { en:SHUTDOWN(). SET n TO n + 1. } }
  SET asc["oms_st"] TO 3.
  SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 0.
  SET asc_thr TO 0.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms,cut," + asc_met() + "," + mo + "," + (asc["oms_m0"] - mo) + "," + n TO asc["log"]. }
}

// The OMS engines in a burn fire at 100 % thrust independent of the SSME throttle, and the throttle shows the SSMEs':
// while an OMS burn runs (a dump or the assist: asc["oms"] lit) with the SSMEs lit, the OMS engines fly KSP's
// independent throttle at 100 % (ADDONS:KALS:ENGIND, called each tick: the addon puts them back on the vessel's throttle
// 0.5 s after the last call, so a stopped script leaves no OMS burning); the vessel's throttle stays asc_thr, the SSMEs'
// command. Back on the vessel's throttle at MECO, when the burn ends and after the loop. The ARD's flights
// (lib_ascent_ard ASC_ARD_FOMS, Fts.cs) and the offline model fly the OMS at full thrust too. Without the addon's ENGIND
// (an older DLL) the OMS follow the SSME throttle.
GLOBAL ASC_OMS_ON IS TRUE.                 // FALSE: the OMS engines follow the SSME throttle. (Not
                                           // ASC_OMS_FULL: kOS names ignore case, and a bare name that is also a
                                           // function is a call: asc_oms_full() with no argument)
FUNCTION asc_oms_full {
  PARAMETER live.
  IF asc["ei_ok"] < 0 {
    SET asc["ei_ok"] TO 0.
    IF ADDONS:HASSUFFIX("KALS") { IF ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("ENGIND") { SET asc["ei_ok"] TO 1. } }
  }
  LOCAL fu IS live AND ASC_OMS_ON AND asc["ei_ok"] = 1 AND asc["oms"]:LENGTH > 0 AND asc["t_meco"] < 0 AND asc_thr > 0.
  IF fu {
    LOCAL n IS ADDONS:KALS:ENGIND("AJ10", 100).
    IF NOT asc["oms_ind"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#omsfull," + asc_met() + ",100," + n TO asc["log"]. } SET asc["oms_ind"] TO TRUE. }
  } ELSE IF asc["oms_ind"] {
    LOCAL n IS ADDONS:KALS:ENGIND("AJ10", -1).
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#omsfull," + asc_met() + ",off," + n TO asc["log"]. }
    SET asc["oms_ind"] TO FALSE.
  }
}

// PEG's FMAX and VEX (asc_s2_tasks's, the RTLS's and the droop's ft) at the SSMEs' throttle kf: with the OMS at full the
// FMAX whose kf share is the thrust (kf FMAX = kf Fs + Fo) and the VEX of that thrust's flow; else asc_thrust's
FUNCTION asc_ft_oms {                      // not asc_ft (= ASC_FT, m per ft, called bare in the aborts)
  PARAMETER kf.
  IF NOT asc["oms_ind"] OR asc["oms"]:LENGTH = 0 OR kf <= 0 { RETURN asc_thrust(asc_engs()). }
  LOCAL fs IS asc_thrust(asc["ssme"]).
  LOCAL fo IS asc_thrust(asc["oms"]).
  LOCAL f IS kf * fs[0] + fo[0].
  LOCAL md IS 0.
  IF fs[1] > 0 { SET md TO kf * fs[0] / fs[1]. }
  IF fo[1] > 0 { SET md TO md + fo[0] / fo[1]. }
  IF md <= 0 { RETURN LIST(f / kf, 0). }
  RETURN LIST(f / kf, f / md).
}

// the engines PEG counts: the SSMEs, and the OMS engines while they dump
FUNCTION asc_engs {
  IF asc["oms"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN asc["ssme"]. }
  LOCAL es IS asc["ssme"]:COPY.
  FOR en IN asc["oms"] { es:ADD(en). }
  RETURN es.
}

// The propellant check: on PEG's first converged pass DT_SITE s after the selection, the ET's delta-V (the SSMEs'
// vacuum exhaust speed; the burnable load less the reserve; the OMS left out) against PEG's VGO; another site, once,
// when it falls MARGIN short -- the best-ranked other site in reach (asc_tal_next_site), and none when the crew picked
// the site by hand (asc["tal_hand"]: the site kept, an event).
FUNCTION asc_tal_check {
  PARAMETER g, met.
  IF asc["abort"] <> "TAL" OR asc["tal_chk"] OR asc["t_sel"] < 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL nx IS asc_tal_next_site(ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]).
  IF nx = "" AND NOT asc["tal_hand"] { RETURN. }
  LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
  IF p["S_INIT"] OR NOT p["SCONV"] OR met < asc["t_sel"] + ASC_TAL_DT_SITE - 1e-9 { RETURN. }
  SET asc["tal_chk"] TO TRUE.
  LOCAL ms IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL prop IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]) - ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"].
  LOCAL vex IS 0.
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET vex TO asc["ssme"][0]:VISP * CONSTANT:G0. }
  LOCAL dv IS 0.
  IF prop > 0 AND prop < ms { SET dv TO vex * LN(ms / (ms - prop)). }
  LOCAL vgo IS p["vgo"]:MAG.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#talchk," + met + "," + dv + "," + vgo + "," + prop + "," + ms TO asc["log"]. }
  IF dv - vgo < ASC_TAL_MARGIN AND asc["tal_hand"] {
    asc_event(asc, asc_col("TAL PROP LOW " + ROUND(dv) + "/" + ROUND(vgo), "#ff2929")).
  } ELSE IF dv - vgo < ASC_TAL_MARGIN AND nx <> "" {
    SET asc["tal_k"] TO ASC_TAL_SITES:INDEXOF(nx).
    SET adSite TO nx.
    LOCAL tl IS asc_tal_lex(ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]).
    asc_peg_tal(p, tl).
    asc_event(asc, "TAL SITE " + tl["name"]:TOUPPER + ": DV " + ROUND(dv) + " < VGO " + ROUND(vgo)).
    asc_ard_reset().                          // the 2EO TAL mark for the new site
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#tal," + met + "," + ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]] + "," + tl["RDMAG"] + "," + tl["GAMD"] + asc_csv_v(tl["ef"])
      + "," + tl["w"] TO asc["log"]. }
  } ELSE {
    asc_note(asc, "TAL PROP GO " + ROUND(dv) + "/" + ROUND(vgo)).   // the log alone
  }
}

// a stage-2 TAL's dump by need: at the first converged pass ASC_TAL_NEED_DT s after the selection, asc_tal_check's
// margin (the ET's dV less VGO, the OMS left out): ASC_TAL_NEED_FREE or more, no dump; less, the dump (ASC_TAL_DUMP
// t) from now; with no dump, a margin under ASC_TAL_NEED_RE later (TGO over ASC_TAL_OMS_TGO_OFF + 20 s) lights what
// is left of it, once. The dump ends as any other (its t, dry, TGO, MECO).
FUNCTION asc_tal_need_do {                // the state after nd (0 to test, 1 no dump, 2 lit, 3 lit later, 4 lit for the landing weight)
  PARAMETER nd, mg, left, tgo, wx IS 0.     // wx: t of OMS over the landing limit (asc_tal_land_x)
  IF nd = 0 { IF mg >= ASC_TAL_NEED_FREE { RETURN CHOOSE 4 IF wx > 0 ELSE 1. } RETURN 2. }
  IF nd = 1 AND mg < ASC_TAL_NEED_RE AND left > ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN AND tgo > ASC_TAL_OMS_TGO_OFF + 20 { RETURN 3. }
  RETURN nd.
}

// The landing mass (t) predicted now: the parts that stay on after the ET sep (DECOUPLEDIN below the ET tanks'),
// less the monoprop ops6q dumps before the entry (over ASC_TAL_MONO_KEEP units); -1 when the ET is not known
FUNCTION asc_tal_land_m {
  IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH < 4 { SET asc["oms_tk"] TO asc_oms_parts(). }
  IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH < 4 OR asc["oms_tk"][1]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN -1. }
  LOCAL et IS asc_sep_in(asc["oms_tk"][1]).
  LOCAL m IS 0.
  LOCAL mu IS 0.
  LOCAL md IS 0.004.
  FOR pt IN SHIP:PARTS {
    IF pt:DECOUPLEDIN < et {
      SET m TO m + pt:MASS.
      FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES { IF rs:NAME = "MonoPropellant" { SET mu TO mu + rs:AMOUNT. SET md TO rs:DENSITY. } }
    }
  }
  RETURN m - MAX(0, mu - ASC_TAL_MONO_KEEP) * md.
}
// t of OMS a TAL dumps for its landing weight at site: over the site's limit, the excess plus ASC_TAL_LAND_PAD, at
// most ASC_TAL_DUMP and the OMS tanks' load; 0 at or under the limit, under ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN or with no landing mass (ml < 0)
FUNCTION asc_tal_land_x {
  PARAMETER site, ml.
  IF NOT ASC_TAL_LAND_ON OR ml < 0 OR NOT ASC_TAL_LAND_MAX:HASKEY(site) { RETURN 0. }
  IF ml <= ASC_TAL_LAND_MAX[site] { RETURN 0. }
  LOCAL x IS MIN(ml - ASC_TAL_LAND_MAX[site] + ASC_TAL_LAND_PAD, MIN(ASC_TAL_DUMP, asc_oms_mass())).
  RETURN CHOOSE x IF x > ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN ELSE 0.
}

FUNCTION asc_tal_need {
  PARAMETER g, met.
  IF NOT asc["oms_need"] OR asc["abort"] <> "TAL" OR asc["t_sel"] < 0 OR asc["tal_nd"] >= 2 { RETURN. }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 OR asc["oms_st"] = 2 OR asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
  IF p["S_INIT"] OR NOT p["SCONV"] OR met < asc["t_sel"] + ASC_TAL_NEED_DT - 1e-9 { RETURN. }
  IF p["TGO"] < ASC_TAL_OMS_TGO_OFF { RETURN. }
  LOCAL ms IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL prop IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]) - ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"].
  IF prop <= 0 OR prop >= ms { RETURN. }
  LOCAL mg IS asc["ssme"][0]:VISP * CONSTANT:G0 * LN(ms / (ms - prop)) - p["vgo"]:MAG.
  LOCAL left IS MAX(0, ASC_TAL_DUMP - (asc["tal_m0"] - asc_oms_mass())).
  LOCAL ml IS -1.
  LOCAL wx IS 0.
  IF asc["tal_nd"] = 0 {                    // The landing weight, at the first test
    SET ml TO asc_tal_land_m().
    SET wx TO asc_tal_land_x(ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]], ml).
  }
  LOCAL nd IS asc_tal_need_do(asc["tal_nd"], mg, left, p["TGO"], wx).
  IF nd = asc["tal_nd"] { RETURN. }
  SET asc["tal_nd"] TO nd.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#talneed," + met + "," + nd + "," + mg + "," + left + "," + p["TGO"] + "," + ml + "," + wx TO asc["log"]. }
  IF nd = 1 { asc_note(asc, "TAL OMS DUMP NOT NEEDED  MARGIN " + ROUND(mg) + " M/S" + (CHOOSE "  LANDING " + ROUND(ml, 2) + " T" IF ml >= 0 ELSE "")). RETURN. }
  IF nd = 4 { SET left TO wx. }             // the dump for the landing weight (#talneed above logs ml and wx)
  SET asc["oms_dump"] TO left.
  SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met.
  SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
}

// ---- THE OMS ASSIST, active only when the mass exceeds the limits without it: both AJ10s burn with the SSMEs from
// just after SRB sep when the ET would fall short of its 1 % reserve at MECO; PEG counts their thrust (asc_engs) and
// its MASS_MIN drops by the assist; the OMS dump's machinery flies it (asc_oms: the fuel cell's tanks locked, the
// oxidizer balanced into the ET; the label OMS ASSIST). The test (calibrated offline): the ET's margin (asc_tal_need's:
// the SSMEs' vacuum exhaust speed on the burnable load less the reserve, less PEG's VGO) against the margin of the
// heaviest flight that makes it without (4.35 t of payload) at the same time after the sep (ASC_AST_TDT / _TE: it
// falls ~12 m/s over stage 2 as the steering losses come in). At the first converged pass ASC_AST_DT s after the sep:
// short of that + ASC_AST_PAD with the assist counted (asc_ast_est: the joint burn, then the SSMEs alone) -> the
// assist sized to it (asc_ast_size) times ASC_AST_G0 + ASC_AST_G1 X (the joint burn's smaller gravity loss, which the
// estimate leaves out), at most what the OMS rule leaves (asc_ast_cap; all of it when short). Not re-sized while lit
// (PEG then reads high: a closed loop burned 0.07-0.2 t too little). Once, at the first converged pass ASC_AST_DT2 s
// after the sep and ASC_AST_WAIT s after the stop: under the line + ASC_AST_RC -> a top-up sized the same. An abort or
// an SSME out ends it (asc_kabort -> asc_ast_off); the rest is the abort's, its dump started from none. Offline: 28 of
// 28 on target from 4.36 to 7.84 t with the first check's margin off by -3 to +6 m/s, 0.03-0.17 t over the reserve;
// the game's margin within -0.4 / +2.6 m/s of the offline model's 5.8 s after the sep (three nominal flights).
FUNCTION asc_ast_crit {                   // m/s: ASC_AST_TE at dt s after the sep (linear between, held at the ends)
  PARAMETER dt.
  LOCAL ts IS ASC_AST_TDT.
  LOCAL es IS ASC_AST_TE.
  IF dt <= ts[0] { RETURN es[0]. }
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 1. } UNTIL i >= ts:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
    IF dt <= ts[i] { RETURN es[i - 1] + (es[i] - es[i - 1]) * (dt - ts[i - 1]) / (ts[i] - ts[i - 1]). }
  }
  RETURN es[es:LENGTH - 1].
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_est {                    // m/s: the ET's margin with xr t of OMS burned (ms t now, prop t of the ET to
  PARAMETER ms, prop, vgo, xr, rq, cs, co.   // its reserve, PEG's |VGO|; rq the SSMEs' / the AJ10s' mass flow, cs / co
  IF prop <= 0 OR prop >= ms { RETURN -vgo. }   // their exhaust speeds): the joint burn, then the SSMEs alone
  IF xr <= 0 { RETURN cs * LN(ms / (ms - prop)) - vgo. }
  LOCAL used IS rq * xr.
  LOCAL xb IS xr.
  IF used >= prop { SET used TO prop. SET xb TO prop / rq. }   // the ET's end first: that much of the joint burn
  LOCAL m1 IS ms - used - xb.
  LOCAL dv IS (rq * cs + co) / (rq + 1) * LN(ms / m1).
  IF prop - used > 1e-9 { SET dv TO dv + cs * LN(m1 / (m1 - (prop - used))). }
  RETURN dv - vgo.
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_size {                   // t of OMS for the margin tgt (0: met without; cap: not met with all of it)
  PARAMETER ms, prop, vgo, tgt, rq, cs, co, cap.
  IF asc_ast_est(ms, prop, vgo, 0, rq, cs, co) >= tgt { RETURN 0. }
  IF cap <= 0 { RETURN 0. }
  IF asc_ast_est(ms, prop, vgo, cap, rq, cs, co) < tgt { RETURN cap. }
  LOCAL lo IS 0.
  LOCAL hi IS cap.
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= 24 STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
    LOCAL md IS (lo + hi) / 2.
    IF asc_ast_est(ms, prop, vgo, md, rq, cs, co) >= tgt { SET hi TO md. } ELSE { SET lo TO md. }
  }
  RETURN hi.
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_keep {                   // m/s the OMS rule keeps after MECO (the launch box's sum): OMS-2 to the
  LOCAL ra IS ASC_R + ASC_TGT_AP.         // circle at ASC_TGT_AP + its deorbit + the on-orbit allowance + the margin
  LOCAL d2 IS MAX(0, SQRT(ASC_MU / ra) - (ASC_R + ASC_MECO_H) * ASC_VDMAG * COS(ASC_GAMD) / ra).
  RETURN d2 + asc_deorbit_dv(ASC_TGT_AP) + ASC_OMS_ONORB + ASC_OMS_EMERG.
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_cap {                    // t of OMS the assist may burn: the aft OMS less what keeps asc_ast_keep on
  PARAMETER tk.                           // the orbiter after the sep, itself lighter by the assist (asc_3eo_tanks' tk)
  IF tk[0]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN 0. }
  LOCAL f IS CONSTANT:E ^ (-asc_ast_keep() / (ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0)).
  RETURN MAX(0, (asc_oms_mass() - asc_3eo_morb(tk) * (1 - f)) / f).
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_chk {                    // at a new PEG pass in stage 2 (no RTLS, no contingency): the check, the
  PARAMETER g, met.                       // re-check
  LOCAL st IS asc["ast_st"].
  IF NOT ASC_AST_ON OR st = 2 OR st >= 4 OR asc["abort"] <> "" OR asc:HASKEY("t_eo1") OR asc["s2_t0"] < 0 { RETURN. }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 OR asc["oms_st"] = 2 OR asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
  IF p["S_INIT"] OR NOT p["SCONV"] { RETURN. }
  LOCAL dt IS met - asc["s2_t0"].
  IF st = 0 { IF dt < ASC_AST_DT - 1e-9 { RETURN. } }
  ELSE IF asc["ast_rc"] OR dt < ASC_AST_DT2 - 1e-9 { RETURN. }
  ELSE IF st = 3 AND met < asc["ast_toff"] + ASC_AST_WAIT - 1e-9 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL ms IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL prop IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]) - ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"].
  LOCAL vgo IS p["vgo"]:MAG.
  LOCAL cs IS asc["ssme"][0]:VISP * CONSTANT:G0.
  LOCAL co IS ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0.
  LOCAL mds IS 0.
  FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { SET mds TO mds + en:MAXMASSFLOW. }
  LOCAL rq IS mds / (ASC_OMS_F / co).
  LOCAL e0 IS asc_ast_est(ms, prop, vgo, 0, rq, cs, co).
  LOCAL cr IS asc_ast_crit(dt).
  LOCAL top IS st <> 0.
  LOCAL lim IS cr + ASC_AST_PAD.
  IF top { SET asc["ast_rc"] TO TRUE. SET lim TO cr + ASC_AST_RC. } ELSE { SET asc["ast_st"] TO 1. }
  LOCAL x IS 0.
  LOCAL cap IS -1.
  IF e0 < lim {
    SET cap TO asc_ast_cap(asc_3eo_tanks()).
    SET x TO asc_ast_size(ms, prop, vgo, cr + ASC_AST_PAD, rq, cs, co, cap).
    IF x < cap - 1e-6 { SET x TO MIN(cap, x * (ASC_AST_G0 + ASC_AST_G1 * x)). }
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ast," + met + "," + top + "," + dt + "," + e0 + "," + cr + "," + x + "," + cap + "," + ms + "," + prop + "," + vgo
    + "," + rq TO asc["log"]. }
  IF e0 >= lim { RETURN. }
  IF x < ASC_AST_MIN {
    IF cap < ASC_AST_MIN {
      // on the pages (yellow) as well as the log: the ET is short and no OMS is left to assist
      asc_event(asc, "OMS ASSIST: NO SPARE OMS  ET MARGIN " + ROUND(e0 / 0.3048) + " FT/S").
      SET asc["ast_st"] TO 4.
    }
    RETURN.
  }
  asc_ast_light(g, met, x, e0, top, x >= cap - 1e-6).
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_light {                  // the assist (or its top-up) lit through the dump's machinery: x t from now
  PARAMETER g, met, x, e0, top, capped.
  IF asc["ast_m0"] < 0 {
    SET asc["ast_m0"] TO asc_oms_mass().
    SET asc["ast_mo"] TO asc_3eo_morb(asc["oms_tk"]).
    SET asc["ast_mm0"] TO g["peg"]["MASS_MIN"].
  }
  SET asc["ast_x"] TO asc["ast_m0"] - asc_oms_mass() + x.
  SET g["peg"]["MASS_MIN"] TO asc["ast_mm0"] - asc["ast_x"].
  SET asc["oms_dump"] TO x.
  SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met.
  SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
  SET asc["oms_lbl"] TO "OMS ASSIST".
  SET asc["oms_why"] TO "".
  SET asc["ast_st"] TO 2.
  asc_event(asc, "OMS ASSIST " + ROUND(asc_oms_mass(), 2) + " T").   // the OMS on board
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_tick {                   // each stage-2 tick while lit / over: no engines found -> over; over and its
  PARAMETER met.                          // oxidizer balanced -> the dump's state back to none (the aborts' dumps test
  IF asc["ast_st"] = 2 AND asc["oms_st"] = 3 { asc_ast_fin(met). }   // 0 = none yet, 3 = theirs made)
  IF asc["ast_st"] = 3 AND asc["oms_st"] = 3 AND NOT asc["oms_bal"] {
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0.
    SET asc["oms_dump"] TO 0.
  }
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_fin {                    // the assist's stop (asc_oms_off): PEG's MASS_MIN on what it burned, the OMS
  PARAMETER met.                          // dV left after the sep (ASC_OMS_DV_NOW: the abort search's ATO), the label
  LOCAL b IS MAX(0, asc["ast_m0"] - asc_oms_mass()).
  IF asc["s2_on"] AND asc["ast_m0"] >= 0 { SET asc["g"]["peg"]["MASS_MIN"] TO asc["ast_mm0"] - b. }
  LOCAL m9 IS asc["ast_mo"] - asc["ast_m0"].   // the orbiter with no aft OMS
  IF asc["ast_m0"] >= 0 AND m9 > 0 AND asc["ast_mo"] - b > m9 {
    SET ASC_OMS_DV_NOW TO ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0 * LN((asc["ast_mo"] - b) / m9).
  }
  SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 0.
  SET asc["oms_lbl"] TO "OMS DUMP".
  SET asc["oms_why"] TO "".
  SET asc["ast_st"] TO 3.
  SET asc["ast_toff"] TO met.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ast,stop," + met + "," + b + "," + ASC_OMS_DV_NOW TO asc["log"]. }
}

FUNCTION asc_ast_off {                    // an abort or an SSME out (asc_kabort, before the abort's own dump): the
  PARAMETER why.                          // assist off for good; lit: the AJ10s off now, the stop line with the reason;
  LOCAL st IS asc["ast_st"].              // the dump's state back to none
  IF st >= 4 { RETURN. }
  IF st = 2 AND asc["oms_st"] = 2 { SET asc["oms_why"] TO "  " + why. asc_oms_off(asc_met()). }
  ELSE IF st = 2 { asc_ast_fin(asc_met()). asc_event(asc, "OMS ASSIST OFF"). }
  IF (st = 2 OR st = 3) AND (asc["oms_st"] = 1 OR asc["oms_st"] = 3) {
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0.
    SET asc["oms_dump"] TO 0.
    SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 0.
  }
  SET asc["ast_st"] TO 4.
}

// The thrust axis from a PEG pass: the pass's sensed dv (inertial) in the body frame at both ends of the pass, taken
// below TB_Q_ON kPa, outside the heads-up roll (+ 4 s), above 5 m/s2 and within TB_MAX deg of the nose; the estimate
// moves TB_GAIN toward it. The first sample's angle goes on the console; each pass logs "#tb".
FUNCTION asc_tb_sample {
  PARAMETER g, met, ax.
  LOCAL fprev IS asc["f_prev"].
  LOCAL fok IS asc["f_ok"].
  SET asc["f_prev"] TO SHIP:FACING.
  SET asc["f_ok"] TO TRUE.
  LOCAL dvs IS g["dvs_last"].
  LOCAL qk IS SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA.
  LOCAL take IS fok AND dvs:MAG > 5 * ASC_DTGD AND qk < asc_tb_q_on.
  IF asc["t_roll"] >= 0 AND met < asc["t_roll"] + 180 / ASC_ROLL_RATE + 4 { SET take TO FALSE. }
  LOCAL sb IS V(0, 0, 1).
  IF take {
    LOCAL dr IS asc_to_raw(ax, dvs).
    SET sb TO ((fprev:INVERSE * dr):NORMALIZED + (SHIP:FACING:INVERSE * dr):NORMALIZED):NORMALIZED.
    IF VANG(sb, V(0, 0, 1)) > asc_tb_max { SET take TO FALSE. }
  }
  IF take {
    SET asc["tb"] TO (asc["tb"] * (1 - asc_tb_gain) + sb * asc_tb_gain):NORMALIZED.
    SET asc["tb_n"] TO asc["tb_n"] + 1.
    IF asc["tb_n"] = 1 { asc_note(asc, "THRUST AXIS " + ROUND(VANG(V(0, 0, 1), asc["tb"]), 1) + " DEG"). }
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#tb," + met + "," + qk + "," + take + "," + sb:X + "," + sb:Y + "," + sb:Z + "," + asc["tb"]:X + ","
    + asc["tb"]:Y + "," + asc["tb"]:Z TO asc["log"]. }
}

// THE 2EO TAL'S ALPHA FLOOR: PEG would pitch a 2EO TAL to negative alpha; below asc_af_alt asc_dir's body X is held at
// asc_af_alpha or above in the vertical plane of the surface velocity (the alpha of lib_ascent_cnt's asc_cnt_cut): the
// whole attitude turned up about that plane's normal by the shortfall (ROTATEFROMTO(w, w turned up): the body X's
// alpha then asc_af_alpha exactly, the roll kept); a #af line a second (the alpha after read back from asc_dir; no
// message). Offline, on the 2EO droop flights: the floor in 4 of 30 pairs, no TAL's outcome changed; in the flight
// that showed it, PEG -10.6 deg there, the floor 76 s, MECO 3.4 km higher
FUNCTION asc_af_hold {
  PARAMETER met.
  LOCAL wv IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL upv IS SHIP:UP:VECTOR.
  LOCAL fx IS asc_af_fix(asc_dir:FOREVECTOR, wv, upv).
  IF fx:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }
  SET asc_dir TO ROTATEFROMTO(fx[0], fx[1]) * asc_dir.
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("af_t") {
    SET asc["af_t"] TO -1.
  }
  IF met - asc["af_t"] >= 1 {
    LOCAL xb IS asc_dir:FOREVECTOR.
    LOCAL nw IS (upv - VDOT(upv, fx[0]) * fx[0]):NORMALIZED.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#af," + met + "," + fx[2] + "," + ARCTAN2(VDOT(xb, nw), VDOT(xb, fx[0])) + "," + ALTITUDE TO asc["log"]. }
    SET asc["af_t"] TO met.
  }
}

// the floor's turn for the body X xb in the vertical plane of wv (upv up): LIST(w, w turned up by the shortfall, the alpha
// before, xb so turned) when its alpha is below asc_af_alpha, else LIST() (also for wv about 0); ROTATEFROMTO(w, that)
// turns every vector so (about the plane's normal), the body X to the fourth
FUNCTION asc_af_fix {
  PARAMETER xb, wv, upv.
  IF wv:MAG < 1 { RETURN LIST(). }
  LOCAL w IS wv:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL nw IS (upv - VDOT(upv, w) * w):NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL al IS ARCTAN2(VDOT(xb, nw), VDOT(xb, w)).
  IF al >= asc_af_alpha { RETURN LIST(). }
  LOCAL d IS asc_af_alpha - al.
  RETURN LIST(w, COS(d) * w + SIN(d) * nw, al, asc_af_turn(xb, w, nw, d)).
}

FUNCTION asc_af_turn {                    // x turned ang deg in the plane (w, nw), from w toward nw; its part off the plane kept
  PARAMETER x, w, nw, ang.
  LOCAL a IS VDOT(x, w).
  LOCAL b IS VDOT(x, nw).
  LOCAL s IS x - a * w - b * nw.
  RETURN ((a * COS(ang) - b * SIN(ang)) * w + (a * SIN(ang) + b * COS(ang)) * nw + s):NORMALIZED.
}

// THE q x ALPHA LIMIT (RTLS SRB sep follows it, and so does every other abort and the
// nominal ascent): this stack drops its SRBs at ~10.6 kPa (the real one at ~2), so a stage-2 command far off the wind meets a
// load the engine-out DAP cannot fly against (PEG's TAL loft stepped 29.6 deg at 7.5 kPa). asc_dir is turned about
// its own pitch axis so that |alpha| in its pitch plane (the HUD cue's reading, lib_ascent_s2 asc_qa_alpha) is at most
// HDG_QA_LIM / q: one number for AUTO, the needles and the cue's demanded pointer. The limit opens as q falls (L q' / q2,
// 0.3 - 2 deg/s on the flights), so a step becomes a few deg and a ramp; it leaves nothing above lim / 180 kPa. A #qa
// line a second while it turns (no message). Offline on flight C's TAL, two RTLS and a nominal (tests/asc_qa_selftest):
// the command's q x alpha 215 / 139 / 135 / 49 -> 40; the nominal's limited 5 s (MET 82 - 87, the DAP 5 deg behind PEG)
FUNCTION asc_qa_limit {
  PARAMETER met, qk.
  SET asc["qa_on"] TO FALSE.
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  IF vs:MAG < 1 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL w IS vs:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL fx IS asc_qa_fix(asc_dir, w, qk, HDG_QA_LIM).
  IF fx:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }
  SET asc_dir TO ROTATEFROMTO(asc_dir:FOREVECTOR, fx[2]) * asc_dir.
  SET asc["qa_on"] TO TRUE.
  IF met - asc["qa_t"] >= 1 {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#qa," + met + "," + qk + "," + fx[0] + "," + fx[1] + "," + asc_qa_alpha(asc_dir, w) + ","
      + ALTITUDE TO asc["log"]. }
    SET asc["qa_t"] TO met.
  }
}

// The
// DLL (KalsAddon.AscMeco.cs) watches AG4 and holds the accel at 3 g on the final throttle; it armed at the stage-2 start (after the
// SRB sep), off at MECO. A press with an SSME lit is latched there; asc_am_poll (main loop) takes it into asc_am_man, which
// asc_stage2 reads FIRST of its MECO tests (why "man"): the unchanged asc_meco then shuts the SSMEs, ET SEP follows as for a cut.
// A press before the SRB sep only gets a message. Without the DLL / an older one nothing here does anything.
LOCAL asc_am_man IS FALSE.
GLOBAL ASC_AM_DBL IS 1.5.            // s after the AG4 press that cued the MECO in which another AG4 press is a double click, ignored
LOCAL asc_am_t IS -1000000.          // The time of the AG4 press that cued the MECO (UT s)
LOCAL asc_am_on IS FALSE.            // kOS watches AG4 itself from MECO on (the DLL stops latching presses at MECO)
LOCAL asc_am_ag IS FALSE.            // AG4's last state
LOCAL asc_am_force IS FALSE.         // A press (not a double click) since the last read: it forces the hand-off's CSS wait over
// The DLL's limiter cuts the final throttle ONLY
// with its gate set, and asc_am_poll sets the gate while the ascent guidance is down (asc_gdl: SW 02 GUIDANCE LOST, or a DPS 04 / DPS 05 hold with the BFS
// not engaged), pushed on change only (ASCMECO(LIST(4, 1 / 0))). Healthy guidance throttles by itself (asc_glim, 2.97 g): the backup never touches it.
LOCAL asc_am_gd IS FALSE.            // T1001: the gate as last sent to the DLL (every asc_am_set clears it, the DLL clears its own on a reset / arm / done)
FUNCTION asc_am_set { PARAMETER m. SET asc_am_gd TO FALSE. IF asc["am_ok"] { ADDONS:KALS:ASCMECO(LIST(m)). } }    // 3 reset, 1 arm, 0 done
FUNCTION asc_am_poll {
  IF NOT asc["am_ok"] { RETURN. }
  LOCAL gdn IS asc_gdl().                // T1001: the limiter's gate = the ascent guidance has failed
  IF gdn <> asc_am_gd {
    SET asc_am_gd TO gdn.
    ADDONS:KALS:ASCMECO(LIST(4, CHOOSE 1 IF gdn ELSE 0)).
  }
  LOCAL amr IS ADDONS:KALS:ASCMECOTAKE.
  IF amr = 1 {
    IF NOT asc_am_man { SET asc_am_t TO TIME:SECONDS. }
    SET asc_am_man TO TRUE.
    asc_event(asc, "AG4: MANUAL MECO").
  }
  ELSE IF amr = 2 { asc_event(asc, "AG4: MANUAL MECO ONLY AFTER SRB SEP"). }
}
// After MECO the DLL no longer latches AG4, so kOS reads it (a CHANGE is a press, as ops2q does). A press within
// ASC_AM_DBL s of the one that cued the MECO is a double click and is ignored; any other sets asc_am_force, which the hand-off's CSS
// wait (asc_ho_css_wait) takes: OPS 6 at once.
FUNCTION asc_ag4 { RETURN AG4. }
FUNCTION asc_am_trk {
  IF NOT asc_am_on { RETURN. }
  LOCAL a IS asc_ag4().
  IF a = asc_am_ag { RETURN. }
  SET asc_am_ag TO a.
  IF TIME:SECONDS - asc_am_t < ASC_AM_DBL { RETURN. }
  SET asc_am_force TO TRUE.
}
// The ET's low level for MECO "res": the burnable
// propellant at ASC_ET_MECO_FRAC of the load (~0.4 t, 0.55-0.9 s of 3 SSMEs at the end), or that floor within
// ASC_ET_MECO_PASSES passes of the last pass's burn (asc["et_b"]: the burnable one pass ago), so the cutoff
// asc_meco commands one pass later always comes before the dry tank's flame-out. The abort planners keep
// ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC as their guard. sim/ascent/fly.py's 'res' event: the floor (its 0.1 s step burns 0.07 t).
FUNCTION asc_et_low {
  LOCAL b IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]).
  LOCAL db IS 0.
  IF asc:HASKEY("et_b") { SET db TO MAX(0, asc["et_b"] - b). }
  SET asc["et_b"] TO b.
  RETURN b <= ASC_ET_MECO_FRAC * asc["et_full"] + ASC_ET_MECO_PASSES * db.
}
FUNCTION asc_stage2 {
  // the passes and the fine count when due (a sample in this tick), the steering every tick, the throttle at K_CMD;
  // MECO at T_MECO, at the ET's low level (asc_et_low: ET_MECO_FRAC of its load, T1008) or when the SSMEs are out
  // every SSME out (RAND's three, or three FAILs): MECO now, before a PEG pass on no thrust (a 3EO flies on by hand)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["why"] TO "out". RETURN "MECO". }
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL met IS ut - asc["t_lo"].
  IF NOT asc["s2_on"] { asc_s2_start(ut, met). }
  LOCAL g IS asc["g"].
  LOCAL tb_due IS FALSE.
  IF asc["ast_st"] = 2 OR asc["ast_st"] = 3 { asc_ast_tick(met). }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 OR asc["oms_st"] = 2 OR asc["oms_bal"] { asc_oms(g, met). }
  // an RTLS flies lib_ascent_rtls.ks's tasks (no fine count, no thrust axis samples, no heads-up roll)
  LOCAL rtl IS asc["rl"]:LENGTH > 0.
  // the 2EO contingency once started flies its own passes (lib_ascent_cnt), no PEG
  LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
  LOCAL con IS FALSE.
  IF cn:LENGTH > 0 { SET con TO cn["on"]. }
  LOCAL due IS FALSE.
  IF con { SET due TO met >= cn["t_next"] - 0.001. }
  ELSE IF rtl { SET due TO asc_rtls_due(asc["rl"], g, met). } ELSE { SET due TO asc_s2_due(g, met). }
  IF due {
    SET asc["busy"] TO TRUE.
    LOCAL mk IS asc_opc_mark().
    LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut).
    LOCAL ft IS asc_ft_oms(g["K_CMD"] / 100 * ASC_PL_TO_KSP).   // the OMS at full in a burn
    LOCAL np IS g["peg"]["npass"].
    IF con { asc_cnt_pass(met, sm). }
    ELSE IF rtl { asc_rtls_step(met, sm, ft). } ELSE { asc_s2_tasks(g, met, sm[1], sm[2], SHIP:MASS, ft[1], ft[0]). }
    IF g["peg"]["npass"] > np {
      SET tb_due TO NOT rtl.
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG asc_peg_line(g["peg"], met, sm[1], sm[2], g["dvs_last"], g["M_last"], g["VEX_last"], g["ATR_last"],
        asc_opc_since(mk)) TO asc["log"]. }
      IF asc["t_sel"] >= 0 AND NOT rtl {
        LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
        IF p:HASKEY("tal_rth") {
          IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#talp," + met + "," + p["VDMAG"] + "," + p["tal_rth"] + "," + p["tal_cr"] + "," + p["tal_tca"] + ","
            + asc["oms_st"] TO asc["log"]. }
        }
        asc_tal_check(g, met).
        asc_tal_need(g, met).
      }
      IF NOT rtl AND NOT con { asc_ast_chk(g, met). }   // the OMS assist's check / re-check
      // the roll to heads up at a pass past V_RHO_PHI (the relative speed): the console line first
      IF asc["t_roll"] < 0 AND SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG > ASC_V_RHO_PHI AND NOT rtl {
        asc_event(asc, "ROLL TO HEADS UP  VREL " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG)).
        IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#roll," + met + "," + SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG TO asc["log"]. }
        SET asc["t_roll"] TO met.
      }
      IF NOT rtl AND NOT con AND ASC_DRP_ON { asc_drp_go(g, met, sm, ft). }   // the droop task
      IF cn:LENGTH > 0 AND NOT rtl { asc_cnt_arm(g, met, sm). }   // MODE SEL, the start
      IF NOT rtl AND NOT con { asc_ard_snap(g, met, sm). }   // the ARD's next snapshot (when it waits for one)
    }
  }
  // a second failure's response on the first tick after it, not at the next PEG pass (ASC_DTGD 1.92 s): MODE SEL and
  // the pick on the state now, so a mode with no crew decision (a 2EO GREEN: the yaw, pitch, roll and OMS dump
  // together) starts at once; PEG passes go on; the verdict's line likewise on the first tick after the verdict is in
  IF NOT due AND cn:LENGTH > 0 AND NOT rtl AND NOT con {
    IF cn["now"] OR (cn["vd"] = "RUN" AND asc["ard"]["ph"] <> 4) {
      SET asc["busy"] TO TRUE.
      asc_cnt_arm(g, met, asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut)).
    }
  }
  IF cn:LENGTH > 0 { SET con TO cn["on"]. }
  // the thrust direction from PEG (an RTLS's: its command, slewed); the top toward the ground (heads down), turning
  // about the thrust axis at ROLL_RATE from the roll's start to heads up; an RTLS's top = u x n (n at its selection: heads
  // down at the start, turning with the thrust through the vertical to heads up on the flyback)
  LOCAL ax IS asc_frame_axes(asc["fr"], ut).
  IF tb_due { asc_tb_sample(g, met, ax). }
  LOCAL ui IS asc_peg_dir(g["peg"], met, g["hold"]).
  IF asc["drp"]["cmd_on"] { SET ui TO asc["drp"]["cmd"]. }   // the droop steers (until S_MIN_ALT hands back to PEG)
  IF rtl { SET ui TO asc_rtls_dir(asc["rl"], g["peg"], met, g["hold"]). }
  IF con {                                  // the contingency's thrust direction and its roll attitude
    asc_cnt_phi(cn, met, asc_cnt_roll_now(cn, ax)).
    SET ui TO asc_cnt_dir(cn, met).
  }
  LOCAL fwd IS asc_to_raw(ax, ui).
  LOCAL top IS -SHIP:UP:VECTOR.
  IF con { SET top TO asc_to_raw(ax, asc_cnt_top(cn, ui)). }
  ELSE IF rtl { SET top TO asc_to_raw(ax, VCRS(ui, asc["rl"]["n"])). }
  ELSE IF asc["t_roll"] >= 0 { SET top TO ANGLEAXIS(MIN(180, ASC_ROLL_RATE * (met - asc["t_roll"])), fwd) * top. }
  // the sampled thrust axis put on fwd, ramped in as q falls from TB_Q_OFF to TB_Q_ON kPa
  LOCAL qk IS SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA.
  LOCAL tbc IS MIN(MAX((asc_tb_q_off - qk) / (asc_tb_q_off - asc_tb_q_on), 0), 1).
  LOCAL tbe IS (V(0, 0, 1) * (1 - tbc) + asc["tb"] * tbc):NORMALIZED.
  SET asc["tbe"] TO tbe.
  SET asc_dir TO LOOKDIRUP(fwd, top) * ROTATEFROMTO(V(0, 0, 1), tbe):INVERSE.
  // the 2EO TAL's alpha floor (-2 deg below 80 km): a TAL on one SSME before MECO below asc_af_alt (without it PEG
  // pitched a 2EO TAL to -31.7 deg of alpha at 73 km before MECO)
  IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" AND asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 1 AND asc["t_meco"] < 0 AND NOT con AND NOT rtl
    AND ALTITUDE < asc_af_alt { asc_af_hold(met). }
  // the q x alpha limit (after the floor: lim / q >= 2 deg below 20 kPa, so the two never cross); not the contingency's
  IF con { SET asc["qa_on"] TO FALSE. } ELSE { asc_qa_limit(met, qk). }
  // the guidance attitude's own rate for the ascent DAP, fed forward (raw, rad/s; VCRS's sense, the DAP's): asc_dir's
  // turn since the last pass, low-passed over ASC_WFF_TAU s; a pass turning more than ASC_WFF_STEP deg (a step) adds
  // none. PEG's command turns within each pass and steps back at the next (up to ~0.4 deg on an RTLS flyback); the
  // filter carries the mean of both. Without it the DAP trails a turning command by its rate / ka (ka = wn / (2 zeta)):
  // offline, on an RTLS flyback's PEG passes, 0.45 deg nose low at 0.28 deg/s; with it 0.01. The contingency gets none
  // (its manoeuvres' rates would be carried past their ends).
  LOCAL tn IS TIME:SECONDS.
  IF asc["wf_t"] < 0 { SET asc["wf_dir"] TO asc_dir. SET asc["wf_t"] TO tn. }
  LOCAL dw IS tn - asc["wf_t"].
  IF dw > 0.001 {
    LOCAL o IS asc["wf_dir"].
    LOCAL wr IS (VCRS(o:STARVECTOR, asc_dir:STARVECTOR) + VCRS(o:FOREVECTOR, asc_dir:FOREVECTOR)
      + VCRS(o:TOPVECTOR, asc_dir:TOPVECTOR)) * (0.5 / dw).
    IF wr:MAG * dw > ASC_WFF_STEP * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD { SET wr TO V(0, 0, 0). }
    SET asc["wf"] TO asc["wf"] + (wr - asc["wf"]) * (dw / (ASC_WFF_TAU + dw)).
    SET asc["wf_dir"] TO asc_dir.
    SET asc["wf_t"] TO tn.
  }
  SET asc["wff"] TO CHOOSE V(0, 0, 0) IF con ELSE asc["wf"].
  SET asc["eff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
  SET asc["aff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
  // an RTLS slew's rate and acceleration in its place (raw, rad/s and rad/s2): u0 x u1 taken in the raw frame (VCRS:
  // the DAP's own sense of a turn); the slew itself accelerates and brakes (asc_rtls_slew_at), so the command has no
  // rate step to lag behind and the stack's rate peaks at the slew's. The filter follows these feeds (asc["wf"] set
  // to them), so it takes over at their ends from their rate, not the turn they carried. Neither while the q x alpha
  // limit turns asc_dir: the slew's or the roll's rate would carry the DAP past the limit; the filter's is the limited one.
  IF rtl AND NOT con AND ascDap["on"] AND NOT asc["qa_on"] {   // the contingency steers after an RTLS's 2EO
    LOCAL sl IS asc["rl"]["slew"].
    IF sl:LENGTH > 0 {
      LOCAL cx IS VCRS(asc_to_raw(ax, sl[1]), asc_to_raw(ax, sl[2])).
      IF met >= sl[0] AND met < sl[4] AND cx:MAG > 0.000001 {
        LOCAL axr IS cx:NORMALIZED.
        LOCAL sa IS asc_rtls_slew_at(sl, met).
        SET asc["wff"] TO axr * (sa[1] * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD).
        SET asc["aff"] TO axr * (sa[2] * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD).
        SET asc["wf"] TO asc["wff"].
      }
    }
  } ELSE IF ascDap["on"] AND asc["t_roll"] >= 0 AND NOT asc["qa_on"] {
    // the roll to heads up's rate fed forward the same way, about fwd in VCRS's sense of ANGLEAXIS's turn (the
    // DAP's), ramped down over ASC_ROLL_RAMP s centred on the roll's end (offline: heads up in 36 s, the thrust
    // within 0.7 deg of fwd; without it the DAP chased the roll at its 2 deg/s clip: 87 s, the thrust up to 23 deg
    // off fwd); one SSME: none (the roll free)
    IF NOT ascDap["one"] {
      LOCAL t1 IS asc["t_roll"] + 180 / ASC_ROLL_RATE.
      LOCAL tr IS ASC_ROLL_RAMP.
      LOCAL fr IS MIN(MAX((t1 + 0.5 * tr - met) / tr, 0), 1).
      LOCAL p0 IS VCRS(fwd, SHIP:UP:VECTOR).
      IF fr > 0 AND p0:MAG > 0.01 {
        LOCAL axr IS VCRS(p0, ANGLEAXIS(90, fwd) * p0):NORMALIZED.
        SET asc["wff"] TO axr * (ASC_ROLL_RATE * fr * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD).
        SET asc["wf"] TO asc["wff"].
        LOCAL tq IS met - (t1 - 0.5 * tr).
        IF tq > 0 AND tq < tr {
          LOCAL dq IS MIN(tq, tr - tq).
          SET asc["eff"] TO axr * (ASC_ROLL_RATE * dq * dq / (2 * tr) * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD).
          SET asc["aff"] TO axr * (-ASC_ROLL_RATE / tr * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD).
        }
      }
    }
  }
  asc_rtls_kdn(g["K_CMD"]).          // an RTLS's THROTTLE DOWN messages
  SET asc["kcmd"] TO g["K_CMD"].
  SET asc_thr TO g["K_CMD"] / 100 * ASC_PL_TO_KSP.
  IF asc_am_man { SET asc["why"] TO "man". }     // The AG4 press (the pilot's MECO, whatever the PEG says)
  ELSE IF g["T_MECO"] >= 0 AND met >= g["T_MECO"] - 0.01 { SET asc["why"] TO "cut". }
  ELSE IF asc_et_low() { SET asc["why"] TO "res". }     // T1008: the ET's floor, no 1 % reserve
  ELSE IF asc_all_dead(asc["ssme"]) { SET asc["why"] TO "out". }
  IF asc["why"] <> "" { RETURN "MECO". }
  RETURN "STAGE2".
}

// ---- A 3EO IN STAGE 2, with the OMS making up the underspeed where it can (for a TAL coordinated with OPS 6: the OMS
// fired through the hand-off and early entry). FSSR 4.10.2 at MECO confirm: no contingency (region 0) when the
// vehicle can still make it, else the contingency's separation and entry. Here, in that order: the ATO when the OMS dV
// on board (the OMS propellant on the orbiter after the sep, ASC_OMS_ISP) covers the ATO plan's need from the state
// now (asc_ato_plan's Kepler: OMS-1 at ASC_ABT_OMS1_LEAD, OMS-2, ASC_ATO_DV_DEORBIT kept) and the coast's apogee is
// ASC_3EO_HA_MIN up, and from VI ASC_3EO_VI_ATO in any case (offline on the nominal: the TAL overshoots from 3565 /
// 3609 m/s, the ATO's two burns fit from 3494 / 3565; the AOA is the crew's after OMS-1 as an ATO's); else the TAL
// from VI ASC_3EO_VI_TAL (offline: the OMS along the velocity takes a 3EO on the nominal to Moron (36.25 deg) /
// Zaragoza (51.6) from VI 2686 / 2724 m/s with all of it), to the TAL site nearest the orbit's plane (a TAL flown
// keeps its own), the OMS it needs (asc_3eo_tal_dv: the energy of the site's MECO target, the line that puts the site
// at 67.5 deg of bank, less the cutoff's, + ASC_3EO_TAL_PAD; offline, the OMS along the velocity at the cutoff: with
// the pad -250 .. -350 every 3EO reaches its site within 15 km from 244 to 272 s on 51.6 and from 240 to 268 s on
// 36.25, the OMS to empty overshoots from 252 / 248 s) from the hand-off (HOPREP, once ops6q.ks runs a dump on); else
// the contingency (CONT): GREEN to the 3EO footprint's best ELS (lib_ascent_bgl's bgl_point3: the offline footprint
// maps, the full dump), else BLUE (the bailout), the OMS to empty from the hand-off as a 2EO's. An RTLS (its GRTLS)
// and a contingency already flying go on unchanged.
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_ON IS TRUE.               // FALSE: a 3EO in stage 2 only cuts (MECO, the abort's hand-off)
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_HA_MIN IS 80000.          // m: the ATO by its need only with the coast's apogee this high (offline)
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_VI_ATO IS 3500.           // m/s: the ATO from this VI whatever its need (above it the TAL overshoots)
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_TAL_PAD IS -300.          // m/s: on the TAL's OMS dV by its target (offline: -250 .. -350 all reach)
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_VI_TAL IS 2750.           // m/s: the TAL from this VI (offline, an impulsive OMS:
// 2593 / 2631 m/s fail, 2686 / 2724 reach; the dump burned from the hand-off at the TAL's alpha:
// 2686 / 2724 miss ~215 km, 2785 / 2825 reach TAEM ~3 km low, the rest high)
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_LN_DT IS 2.               // s: the pages' 3EO line at most this often
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_ROOM IS 6000.             // opcodes left in the tick for an update of the line
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_SKIP IS 4.                // tries: an update anyway after this many without room
GLOBAL ASC_3EO_M_ORB IS 25.808.          // t: the orbiter after the sep when the ET's tanks are not found (offline)

FUNCTION asc_3eo_tanks {                 // asc_oms_parts once (it needs the AJ10s in asc["oms"]: as they were after it);
  IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH >= 4 { RETURN asc["oms_tk"]. }   // kept only when it found the OMS tanks
  LOCAL e0 IS asc["oms"]:LENGTH = 0.
  IF e0 { FOR en IN SHIP:ENGINES { IF en:NAME:CONTAINS("AJ10") { asc["oms"]:ADD(en). } } }
  LOCAL tk IS asc_oms_parts().
  IF e0 { asc["oms"]:CLEAR(). }
  IF tk[0]:LENGTH > 0 { SET asc["oms_tk"] TO tk. }
  RETURN tk.
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_morb {                  // t: the orbiter after the ET sep = the vessel less the ET's tanks (asc_oms_parts'
  PARAMETER tk.                          // second list); ASC_3EO_M_ORB when they are not found; after the sep the vessel
  IF asc["t_sep"] > 0 { RETURN SHIP:MASS. }
  IF tk[1]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN ASC_3EO_M_ORB. }
  LOCAL m IS SHIP:MASS.
  FOR pt IN tk[1] { SET m TO m - pt:MASS. }
  RETURN m.
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_need {                  // the OMS dV (m/s) the ATO plan needs from the state at rm (m), vm (m/s), gm (deg)
  PARAMETER rm, vm, gm, ms, ve.          // with ms t and ve m/s (asc_ato_plan's): LIST(need, the coast's apogee radius m);
  LOCAL k0 IS asc_kep(rm, vm, gm).       // not an ellipse: LIST(-1, 0)
  IF k0:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN LIST(-1, 0). }
  LOCAL ra0 IS k0[0] * (1 + k0[1]).
  LOCAL dv1 IS 0.
  LOCAL k2 IS k0.
  IF ra0 < ASC_R + ASC_ATO_H {
    LOCAL tb IS 0.
    LOCAL s1 IS LIST().
    FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= 4 STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
      SET s1 TO asc_kep_at(k0, ASC_ABT_OMS1_LEAD + tb / 2).
      SET dv1 TO asc_v_apo(s1[0], s1[2], ASC_R + ASC_ATO_H) - s1[1].
      SET tb TO ms * (1 - CONSTANT:E ^ (-dv1 / ve)) * ve / ASC_OMS_F.
    }
    SET k2 TO asc_kep(s1[0], s1[1] + dv1, s1[2]).
  }
  IF k2:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN LIST(-1, ra0). }
  LOCAL ra IS k2[0] * (1 + k2[1]).
  LOCAL rt IS MIN(ASC_R + ASC_ATO_H, ra).
  LOCAL dv2 IS SQRT(ASC_MU * (2 / ra - 2 / (ra + rt))) - SQRT(ASC_MU * (2 / ra - 1 / k2[0])).
  RETURN LIST(dv1 + ABS(dv2) + ASC_ATO_DV_DEORBIT, ra0).
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_pick {                  // the mode after a 3EO: ab the abort flown, vi m/s, need the ATO's OMS dV (m/s;
  PARAMETER ab, vi, need, dvo, ra0, mg, tal.   // < 0: none), dvo the OMS dV on board, ra0 the coast's apogee radius (m),
  IF ab = "CONT" OR ab = "RTLS" { RETURN ab. }   // mg the 3EO footprint's best margin (km), tal: the launch has a TAL
  IF vi >= ASC_3EO_VI_ATO OR (need >= 0 AND need <= dvo AND ra0 >= ASC_R + ASC_3EO_HA_MIN) { RETURN "ATO". }   // site
  IF vi >= ASC_3EO_VI_TAL AND tal { RETURN "TAL". }   // no TAL site (a VBG launch): no 3EO TAL
  IF mg >= 0 { RETURN "GREEN". }
  RETURN "BLUE".
}

// the launch has a TAL site: a TAL flown, or a site whose own E TAL (asc_site_etal) or 2EO TAL mark (the ARD's
// TAL_2EO_<site>) is on the scale (a VBG launch: both NEVER for ZZA and MRN, so no 3EO TAL)
FUNCTION asc_3eo_tal_any {
  IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" { RETURN TRUE. }
  FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES {
    IF asc_site_etal(st) < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 { RETURN TRUE. }
    FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] {
      IF x["key"] = "TAL_2EO_" + st AND x["vb"] >= 0 AND x["vb"] < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 { RETURN TRUE. }
    }
  }
  RETURN FALSE.
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_eval {                  // LIST(the pick, the ATO's need m/s, the OMS dV on board m/s, the coast's apogee
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], TIME:SECONDS).   // km, the footprint's best margin km, its ELS); the ATO's need only
  LOCAL rm IS sm[1]:MAG.                 // from VI ASC_3EO_VI_TAL, the footprint only below it
  LOCAL vm IS sm[2]:MAG.
  LOCAL nd IS LIST(-1, 0).
  LOCAL dvo IS 0.
  IF vm >= ASC_3EO_VI_TAL {
    LOCAL tk IS asc_3eo_tanks().
    LOCAL mo IS asc_oms_mass().
    LOCAL ms IS asc_3eo_morb(tk).
    LOCAL ve IS ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0.
    IF mo > 0 AND mo < ms { SET dvo TO ve * LN(ms / (ms - mo)). }
    SET nd TO asc_3eo_need(rm, vm, ARCSIN(MAX(-1, MIN(1, VDOT(sm[1], sm[2]) / (rm * vm)))), ms, ve).
  }
  LOCAL pt IS LIST(ASC_BGL_NONE, "NONE").
  LOCAL tal IS asc_3eo_tal_any().         // without a TAL site the footprint above ASC_3EO_VI_TAL too
  IF vm < ASC_3EO_VI_TAL OR NOT tal {   // + the cut's flight-path angle (the 3EO footprint's two sets)
    SET pt TO bgl_point3(SHIP:GEOPOSITION:LAT, SHIP:GEOPOSITION:LNG, asc_ho_az(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE), vm,
      ARCSIN(MAX(-1, MIN(1, VDOT(sm[1], sm[2]) / (rm * vm))))).
  }
  RETURN LIST(asc_3eo_pick(asc["abort"], vm, nd[0], dvo, nd[1], pt[0], tal), nd[0], dvo, (nd[1] - ASC_R) / 1000, pt[0], pt[1]).
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_line {                  // the pick's word on the pages' 3EO line: a contingency flying, its own GREEN /
  PARAMETER md.                          // BLUE; an RTLS, asc_rtls_3eo_word
  IF md = "RTLS" { RETURN asc_rtls_3eo_word(). }
  IF md = "CONT" { RETURN CHOOSE "BLUE" IF asc["cn"]["site"] = "NONE" ELSE "GREEN". }
  RETURN md.
}

// a 3EO's colour in an RTLS (its GRTLS from the cutoff): GREEN in the powered pitchdown, else BLUE: offline, the cut
// at once stops on the SLF in 35 of 35 pitchdowns and in 0 of 440 before (fuel dissipation 95, pitcharound 27, flyback
// 305, fine count 13); OPS 6's reach test decides at the hand-off
FUNCTION asc_rtls_3eo_word {
  IF asc["rl"]:HASKEY("mode") { IF asc["rl"]["mode"] = "ppd" { RETURN "GREEN". } }
  RETURN "BLUE".
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_tal_k {                 // the TAL site (its index in ASC_TAL_SITES) nearest the orbit's plane now
  LOCAL nv IS VCRS(-BODY:POSITION, SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT):NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL k IS 0.
  LOCAL best IS 2.
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= ASC_TAL_SITES:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
    LOCAL s IS ASC_TAL[ASC_TAL_SITES[i]].
    LOCAL x IS ABS(VDOT((LATLNG(s["lat"], s["lng"]):POSITION - BODY:POSITION):NORMALIZED, nv)).
    IF x < best { SET best TO x. SET k TO i. }
  }
  RETURN k.
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_tal_dv {                // m/s: the OMS dV a 3EO's TAL to site k needs (< 0: none): the energy of its MECO
  PARAMETER k, rr, vv, met.              // target (VDMAG by the range now, asc_tal_vel's line, at RDMAG) less the cutoff's
  LOCAL tl IS asc_tal_lex(ASC_TAL_SITES[k]).   // at rr (m), vv (m/s) inertial (asc_sample), MET met s
  LOCAL rt IS asc_rotz(tl["ef"], tl["w"] * met).
  LOCAL rth IS tl["ef"]:MAG * ARCCOS(MAX(-1, MIN(1, VDOT(rr:NORMALIZED, rt:NORMALIZED)))) * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD.
  LOCAL ca IS tl["A"].
  LOCAL vd IS asc_mid(tl["VMIN"], ca[0] + rth * (ca[1] + rth * (ca[2] + rth * ca[3])), tl["VMAX"]).
  RETURN SQRT(MAX(0, vd * vd + 2 * ASC_MU * (1 / rr:MAG - 1 / tl["RDMAG"]))) - vv:MAG.
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_work {                  // the pages' 3EO line from the state now: in stage 2 before MECO, at most every
  IF NOT ASC_3EO_ON OR NOT asc["s2_on"] OR asc["t_meco"] >= 0 OR asc["eo3"] { RETURN. }   // ASC_3EO_LN_DT s, with room
  IF TIME:SECONDS < asc["eo3_t"] + ASC_3EO_LN_DT { RETURN. }
  IF OPCODESLEFT < ASC_3EO_ROOM AND asc["eo3_sk"] < ASC_3EO_SKIP { SET asc["eo3_sk"] TO asc["eo3_sk"] + 1. RETURN. }
  SET asc["eo3_sk"] TO 0.
  SET asc["eo3_t"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL ev IS asc_3eo_eval().
  SET asc["eo3_ln"] TO asc_3eo_line(ev[0]).
  // The 3EO footprint's margin (km) when the pick is the contingency: "CONT" (one flies already) or its
  // GREEN / BLUE (asc_3eo_pick on any other ascent; S2c fed only "CONT", so GREEN3_OPEN never fired)
  SET asc["eo3_mg"] TO CHOOSE ev[4] IF (ev[0] = "CONT" OR ev[0] = "GREEN" OR ev[0] = "BLUE") ELSE ASC_BGL_NONE.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" {                  // #eo3,met,vi,pick,line,margin km,ELS,lit SSMEs
    LOCAL nlit IS 0.
    FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { IF en:IGNITION AND NOT en:FLAMEOUT { SET nlit TO nlit + 1. } }
    LOG "#eo3," + ROUND(asc_met(), 2) + "," + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG, 1) + "," + ev[0] + "," + asc["eo3_ln"] + ","
      + ROUND(asc["eo3_mg"], 1) + "," + ev[5] + "," + nlit TO asc["log"].
  }
}

// THE PASS'S OPCODE COST BY BLOCK, to plan the moves to C#. OFF unless AOP_ON is TRUE before the run (a job file: GLOBAL AOP_ON IS TRUE.); off it costs one
// IF per checkpoint. A checkpoint charges the opcodes since the last one (+ CONFIG:IPU per tick crossed, 0.02 s each) to its
// block; its own bookkeeping is charged to none. Every AOP_DT s one line: #opc,MET,IPU,ticks, then per block 1..21
// sum:calls:max. The blocks (aop_k's numbers in the main loop): 1 the phase's work on a page pass, 2 the phase change +
// asc_cs_say, 3 the DAP target + #dap / #rpy lines, 4 CSS, 5 the HUD, 6 the C# DAP feed + relock, 7 asc_view_dir +
// asc_req, 8 the SRB / core weighing, 9 asc_padc_work, 10 asc_abr_tick, 11 asc_etl_apply, 12 asc_ard_apply, 13
// asc_ban_b, 14 adTick, 15 asc_ard_work, 16 asc_bgl_work, 17 asc_etl_work, 18 asc_3eo_work, 19 asc_con, 20 asc_oms_full,
// 21 the phase's work on a PEG pass (asc["busy"]); 0 (S0b) = CONFIG:IPU - OPCODESLEFT at the pass's start, a fresh tick after
// WAIT 0 = the tick's triggers (WHEN TRUE: lib_ascent_css, lib_ascent_dap, lib_cwui; LOCK STEERING) + the loop head.
// The first window is not logged (its start is not a checkpoint).
// THE DISPLAYS' UPDATE INTERVALS: each update's real time (the HUD when hdNextUpd moves, a page window when adCyc moves,
// read before the call); per window one line #opi,MET, then per display (hud, top = TRAJ, bot = ENG) nominal ms:updates:
// mean ms:min ms:max ms:late (a gap over 1.5 x nominal). The few opcodes of these reads land in blocks 5 / 14.
IF NOT (DEFINED AOP_ON) { GLOBAL AOP_ON IS FALSE. }
IF NOT (DEFINED AOP_DT) { GLOBAL AOP_DT IS 2. }
GLOBAL AOP_S IS aop_z().                 // opcodes per block in this window
GLOBAL AOP_N IS aop_z().                 // calls per block
GLOBAL AOP_M IS aop_z().                 // the largest single call per block
GLOBAL AOP_O IS 0.                       // OPCODESLEFT at the last checkpoint
GLOBAL AOP_T IS 0.                       // TIME:SECONDS at the last checkpoint
GLOBAL AOP_L IS 0.                       // the window's start (0: none yet)
GLOBAL AOP_I IS LIST(aop_i0(-1), aop_i0(-1), aop_i0(-1)).   // hud, top, bot: last, n, sum, min, max, late, nominal
GLOBAL AOP_HN IS 0.                      // hdNextUpd before the HUD's pass
GLOBAL AOP_HT IS 0.                      // its real time
GLOBAL AOP_AC IS 0.                      // adCyc before adTick
GLOBAL AOP_AT IS 0.                      // its real time

FUNCTION aop_i0 {
  PARAMETER t.
  RETURN LIST(t, 0, 0, 999, 0, 0, 0).
}

FUNCTION aop_iv {                        // display d updated at real time t (nominal interval nom s)
  PARAMETER d, t, nom.
  LOCAL ivr IS AOP_I[d].
  SET ivr[6] TO nom.
  IF ivr[0] >= 0 {
    LOCAL g IS t - ivr[0].
    SET ivr[1] TO ivr[1] + 1.
    SET ivr[2] TO ivr[2] + g.
    IF g < ivr[3] { SET ivr[3] TO g. }
    IF g > ivr[4] { SET ivr[4] TO g. }
    IF g > 1.5 * nom { SET ivr[5] TO ivr[5] + 1. }
  }
  SET ivr[0] TO t.
  SET AOP_O TO OPCODESLEFT.
  SET AOP_T TO TIME:SECONDS.
}

FUNCTION aop_z {
  LOCAL l IS LIST().
  FROM { LOCAL k IS 0. } UNTIL k > 21 STEP { SET k TO k + 1. } DO { l:ADD(0). }
  RETURN l.
}

FUNCTION aop_k {
  PARAMETER k.
  LOCAL c IS AOP_O - OPCODESLEFT + ROUND((TIME:SECONDS - AOP_T) / 0.02) * CONFIG:IPU.
  SET AOP_S[k] TO AOP_S[k] + c.
  SET AOP_N[k] TO AOP_N[k] + 1.
  IF c > AOP_M[k] { SET AOP_M[k] TO c. }
  SET AOP_O TO OPCODESLEFT.
  SET AOP_T TO TIME:SECONDS.
}

FUNCTION aop_log {                       // at the pass's end: the window's line every AOP_DT s, then a new window
  IF TIME:SECONDS < AOP_L + AOP_DT { RETURN. }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" {
    IF AOP_L > 0 {
      LOCAL s IS "#opc," + ROUND(asc_met(), 2) + "," + CONFIG:IPU + "," + ROUND((TIME:SECONDS - AOP_L) / 0.02).
      FROM { LOCAL k IS 0. } UNTIL k > 21 STEP { SET k TO k + 1. } DO { SET s TO s + "," + AOP_S[k] + ":" + AOP_N[k] + ":" + AOP_M[k]. }
      LOG s TO asc["log"].
      SET s TO "#opi," + ROUND(asc_met(), 2).
      FOR ivr IN AOP_I {
        SET s TO s + "," + ROUND(ivr[6] * 1000) + ":" + ivr[1] + ":" + ROUND(ivr[2] / MAX(1, ivr[1]) * 1000, 1) + ":"
          + (CHOOSE ROUND(ivr[3] * 1000, 1) IF ivr[1] > 0 ELSE 0) + ":" + ROUND(ivr[4] * 1000, 1) + ":" + ivr[5].
      }
      LOG s TO asc["log"].
    } ELSE {
      LOG "#opch,met,ipu,ticks,trig,phase,cssay,dap,css,hud,csd,view,meas,padc,abr,etla,arda,ban,adtick,ardw,bglw,etlw,3eow,con,oms,peg" TO asc["log"].
    }
  }
  SET AOP_S TO aop_z().
  SET AOP_N TO aop_z().
  SET AOP_M TO aop_z().
  FROM { LOCAL d IS 0. } UNTIL d > 2 STEP { SET d TO d + 1. } DO { SET AOP_I[d] TO aop_i0(AOP_I[d][0]). }
  SET AOP_L TO TIME:SECONDS.
}

FUNCTION asc_3eo_go {                    // at the 3EO's MECO (asc_meco): the mode, its events, the OMS to go
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL ev IS asc_3eo_eval().
  LOCAL md IS ev[0].
  SET asc["eo3"] TO TRUE.
  SET asc["eo3_ln"] TO asc_3eo_line(md).
  LOCAL dvt IS -1.
  IF md = "TAL" {
    IF asc["abort"] <> "TAL" { SET asc["tal_k"] TO asc_3eo_tal_k(). }
    LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], TIME:SECONDS).
    SET dvt TO MAX(0, MIN(ev[2], asc_3eo_tal_dv(asc["tal_k"], sm[1], sm[2], met) + ASC_3EO_TAL_PAD)).
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#3eo," + met + "," + md + "," + asc["abort"] + "," + SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG + "," + ev[1] + "," + ev[2] + ","
    + ev[3] + "," + ev[4] + "," + ev[5] + "," + dvt TO asc["log"]. }
  IF md = "RTLS" { asc_event(asc, "RTLS 3EO " + asc_3eo_line(md)). RETURN. }
  IF md = "CONT" {
    // a 2EO contingency that found no site (NONE) and a 3EO footprint that reaches one: take it, as a 2EO GREEN does
    IF asc["cn"]["site"] = "NONE" AND ev[4] >= 0 {
      SET asc["cn"]["site"] TO ev[5].
      SET asc["eo3_ln"] TO "GREEN".
      asc_event(asc, "3EO CONT GREEN (" + ev[5] + ")").
    }
    RETURN.
  }
  IF md = "ATO" {
    SET asc["abort"] TO "ATO".
    asc_event(asc, "3EO ATO: OMS DV " + ROUND(ev[1]) + " OF " + ROUND(ev[2])).
    RETURN.
  }
  // the TAL: the OMS it needs (the rocket equation on the orbiter after the sep); the contingency: to empty; from the
  // hand-off (the dump's rest to go; HOPREP lights it once ops6q.ks runs a dump on)
  SET asc["oms_st"] TO 3.
  IF md = "TAL" {
    SET asc["abort"] TO "TAL".
    SET asc["oms_rest"] TO asc_3eo_morb(asc_3eo_tanks()) * (1 - CONSTANT:E ^ (-dvt / (ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0))).
    asc_event(asc, "3EO TAL " + ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]] + ": OMS DV " + ROUND(dvt) + " OF " + ROUND(ev[2])).
    RETURN.
  }
  SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 99.
  SET asc["cn"] TO asc_cnt_new(met, SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).
  SET asc["cn"]["ph_cut"] TO "3eo".
  SET asc["cn"]["alpha"] TO asc_s1c_ab(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE)[0].
  IF md = "GREEN" { SET asc["cn"]["site"] TO ev[5]. }
  SET asc["abort"] TO "CONT".
  asc_event(asc, "3EO CONT " + md + " (" + asc["cn"]["site"] + ")").
}

FUNCTION asc_meco {
  // the throttle to zero and the SSMEs off; the attitude held
  SET asc_thr TO 0.
  asc_am_set(0).                              // The AG4 press and the 3 g backup off
  SET asc_am_ag TO asc_ag4().                 // From here kOS watches AG4 (the hand-off's CSS wait)
  SET asc_am_on TO TRUE.
  SET asc["kcmd"] TO 0.
  FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { IF en:IGNITION { en:SHUTDOWN(). } }
  // CSS flies on through MECO; the EO DAP's Law B becomes Law A when asc_eo_steer_off below stops that DAP
  // (ascCssMode); the SSME gimbals locked at once after MECO: set, not toggled, so a gimbal already locked stays locked
  FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { IF en:HASGIMBAL { SET en:GIMBAL:LOCK TO TRUE. } }
  asc_eo_steer_off().                         // the settling times back
  SET asc["t_meco"] TO asc_met().
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms_off(asc["t_meco"]). }
  IF asc["oms_bal"] { asc_oms_bal(). SET asc["oms_bal"] TO FALSE. }   // the last balance before the ET SEP
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_rest"] TO asc["oms_dump"]. SET asc["oms_st"] TO 3. }   // all to go
  // a 3EO in stage 2 (every SSME out, not PEG's cut): its mode (asc_3eo_go) before the events below
  IF asc["why"] = "out" AND ASC_3EO_ON AND asc["s1c"]:LENGTH = 0 { asc_3eo_go(). }
  LOCAL vt IS ASC_VDMAG.
  IF asc["s2_on"] { SET vt TO asc["g"]["peg"]["VDMAG"]. }
  IF asc["rl"]:LENGTH > 0 AND asc["abort"] = "RTLS" {   // not after the contingency took over
    // the RTLS: the relative speed against the MECO line (4.8.5), the range to the site
    LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], TIME:SECONDS).
    LOCAL vl IS asc_rtls_vline(asc["rl"], asc["t_meco"], sm[1], sm[2], 0).
    asc_event(asc, "MECO " + asc["why"]:TOUPPER + "  VREL " + ROUND(vl[0]) + " LINE " + ROUND(vl[3])
      + "  RNG " + ROUND(vl[2] / 1000) + "K  H " + adFx(SHIP:ALTITUDE / 1000, 1) + "K").
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#rtlsmeco," + asc["t_meco"] + "," + vl[0] + "," + vl[1] + "," + vl[2] + "," + vl[3] TO asc["log"]. }
  } ELSE {
    asc_event(asc, "MECO " + asc["why"]:TOUPPER + "  VI " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG) + " TGT "
      + ROUND(vt) + "  H " + adFx(SHIP:ALTITUDE / 1000, 1) + "K").
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#meco," + asc["why"] + "," + asc["t_meco"] + "," + SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG + "," + SHIP:ALTITUDE TO asc["log"]. }
  IF asc["abort"] = "CONT" {                // the contingency's C/O state
    LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
    asc_event(asc, "CONT C/O: ALPHA " + ROUND(cn["alpha"], 1) + "  RATE " + ROUND(cn["rate"], 1) + "  Q "
      + ROUND(SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA * 1000 / 47.880259, 1) + " PSF  SEP IN " + asc_cnt_tsep(cn) + " S").
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cntmeco," + asc["t_meco"] + "," + cn["ph_cut"] + "," + cn["alpha"] + "," + cn["rate"] + ","
      + SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  RETURN "ETSEP".
}

FUNCTION asc_etsep {
  // the ET separation (the craft's next stage, or the next ones: asc_sep_more) ET_SEP_DELAY s after MECO; then the
  // clearing translation (asc_etclr)
  LOCAL dly IS ASC_ET_SEP_DELAY.
  IF asc["abort"] = "CONT" { SET dly TO asc_cnt_tsep(asc["cn"]). }   // the contingency's sep (asc_cnt_tsep)
  IF asc["why"] = "esep" { SET dly TO ASC_RTLS_ES_TSEP. }   // 2EO RED's emergency sep
  // the separation dly s after MECO (a contingency's rate sep: 1 s; its fast sep: 5 s)
  IF asc_met() < asc["t_meco"] + dly OR NOT STAGE:READY { RETURN "ETSEP". }
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("et_in") { SET asc["et_in"] TO asc_sep_in(asc_oms_parts()[1]). }   // the ET's tanks
  LOCAL n0 IS STAGE:NUMBER.
  STAGE.
  IF asc_sep_more(n0, asc["et_in"]) {
    asc_event(asc, "ET SEP: STAGE " + (n0 - 1) + ", STAGING ON").
    RETURN "ETSEP".
  }
  SET asc["t_sep"] TO asc_met().
  SET asc["sep_rcs0"] TO RCS.
  IF asc["abort"] = "RTLS" { SET asc["sep_rt"] TO asc["sep_rt_rtls"]. }
  IF asc["sep_up"] > 0 OR asc["sep_rt"] > 0 {
    RCS ON.
    IF asc["sep_up"] > 0 { SET SHIP:CONTROL:TOP TO 1. }
    IF asc["sep_rt"] > 0 { SET SHIP:CONTROL:STARBOARD TO 1. }
  }
  asc_event(asc, "ET SEP").
  fuiSimPt("ET_SEP", 0).                 // SimSup's decision point (the DLL adds its +20 s); nothing while SIMSUP is not latched
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#etsep," + asc["t_sep"] + "," + asc["sep_up"] + "," + asc["sep_rt"] + "," + asc["sep_rcs0"] TO asc["log"]. }
  RETURN "ETCLR".
}

// The clearing translation for every separation: up for asc["sep_up"] s (default 5) and right for asc["sep_rt"] s
// (1.5; an RTLS's 5), both from the separation, on the RCS (on for it, then back to its state before the sep); up = the control
// part's top (away from the ET), right = its starboard; the attitude held. Then the mode's next step. The log: the
// nearest vessel (the ET) at its first sight and at the end (asc_et_rel: its velocity relative to the orbiter < 0 on
// both axes = clearing).
FUNCTION asc_etclr {
  LOCAL dt IS asc_met() - asc["t_sep"].
  IF asc["sep_v0"]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["sep_v0"] TO asc_et_rel(). }
  IF dt >= asc["sep_rt"] { SET SHIP:CONTROL:STARBOARD TO 0. }
  IF dt >= asc["sep_up"] { SET SHIP:CONTROL:TOP TO 0. }
  IF dt < MAX(asc["sep_up"], asc["sep_rt"]) { RETURN "ETCLR". }
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:NEUTRALIZE TO TRUE.
  LOCAL hof IS asc["abort"] = "TAL" OR asc["abort"] = "RTLS" OR asc["abort"] = "CONT".
  SET RCS TO asc["sep_rcs0"] OR hof.   // a hand-off keeps the RCS on into OPS 6 (else its state before the sep)
  LOCAL r1 IS asc_et_rel().
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#etclr," + asc_met() + "," + asc["sep_v0"]:JOIN(";") + "," + r1:JOIN(";") + "," + RCS TO asc["log"]. }
  // a TAL, an RTLS or a contingency hands over to OPS 6 (ops6q.ks, run at this program's end)
  // after the hand-off's preparation (asc_ho_prep: the hold toward the entry's alpha, the dump again past the OMS
  // line); its ENTRY ARMED and the logger's end there
  IF hof { RETURN "HOPREP". }
  RETURN "OMS2PLAN".
}

// ---- THE GENERIC HAND-OFF: every hand-off keeps the steering and the OMS dump running into OPS 6, not just the
// split-S's: the steering locked to the entry's alpha, a dump MECO stopped continued into the entry. After a TAL's, an
// RTLS's or a contingency's ET separation and translation (HOPREP): the hold (asc_ho_dir) turns alpha about the
// relative wind from the alpha as found toward the entry's (ops6q's: a TAL's TAL_A0 43, the GRTLS's ALPREC 50, a
// contingency's MIDVAL(ALPRS M + ALPRI, ALPRL, ALPREC)), straight there (kOS's steering slews; ASC_HO_RATE > 0: at
// that rate from the alpha as found), wings level heads up; a dump that MECO stopped with propellant to go
// (asc["oms_rest"]; 99 = to empty; a contingency's or a 3EO TAL's only: asc_ho_prep) starts again once its path clears
// the ET (asc_ho_clear; no ET within 2 km: clear); then OPS 6 with the hold and the dump running into it (ASC_HO, the
// contract with ops6q; the dump only when ops6q.ks reads ASC_HO); ASC_HO_T_MAX s at most.
GLOBAL ASC_HO IS LEXICON().          // the hand-off for ops6q (their contract), set just before the RUNPATH
GLOBAL ASC_HO_RATE IS 0.             // deg/s: the hold's alpha rate; 0 = straight to the target
GLOBAL ASC_HO_A_TAL IS 43.           // deg: a TAL's alpha (ops6q TAL_A0, bank 0 heads up)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_A_RTLS IS 50.          // deg: an RTLS's (lib_grtls GR_ALPREC); a contingency's MIDVAL(10 M + 5, 20, 50)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_SOUND IS 300.          // m/s: the speed of sound for a contingency's Mach (lib_grtls GR_ALPRS / _ALPRI)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_T_MAX IS 20.           // s: the preparation at most (then OPS 6 without the dump)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN IS 0.05.      // t: less to go is not started again
GLOBAL ASC_CONT_DUMP_EMPTY IS TRUE.  // a contingency's dump to empty (the full dump for an ECAL; FALSE: 2.5 t)
GLOBAL ASC_TAL2_DUMP_EMPTY IS TRUE.  // a 2EO TAL's dump to empty

// the dump to empty from now (ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY s on when none was armed; a burning one just goes on), or again when it
// is over and the tanks hold more than ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN t
FUNCTION asc_oms_empty {
  PARAMETER met.
  SET asc["oms_need"] TO FALSE.             // a dump to empty ends a TAL's need test
  SET asc["oms_dump"] TO 99.
  LOCAL again IS FALSE.
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 3 { SET again TO asc_oms_mass() > ASC_OMS_DRY + ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN. }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 0 OR again {
    SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met + ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY.
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
  }
}

// a dump waiting for its start (oms_st 1) starts ASC_CNT_DUMP_DELAY after now at the latest: with no crew decision
// needed (a 2EO GREEN) the OMS dump goes with the yaw, pitch and roll at once, for more chance of making a runway
FUNCTION asc_oms_now {
  PARAMETER met.
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_t0"] TO MIN(asc["oms_t0"], met + ASC_CNT_DUMP_DELAY). }
}

// A second SSME out before the abort boundaries are regenerated after the first: from asc_cnt_arm, a second SSME out
// that the boundaries do not cover yet flies the droop (PEG on at the abort throttle with the droop task: MODE SEL 0's
// flight, FSSR 4.3.4) and the OMS dump to empty at once, until the script can tell what to do, and starts the verdict
// (lib_ascent_ard's ard_vd_go: each 2EO mode the selection allows, flown once from the state now on the SSME left;
// asc_ard_work runs it); no thrust to fly it from: "NONE" at once
GLOBAL ASC_2EO_DROOP_ON IS TRUE.
FUNCTION asc_2eo_droop_go {
  PARAMETER g, met, sm.
  LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
  IF NOT g["glim_on"] { SET g["K_CMD"] TO ASC_KMAX. }
  asc_oms_empty(met).
  asc_oms_now(met).
  SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "DROOP".             // the pages' 2EO line until the verdict
  SET cn["vd"] TO "NONE".
  LOCAL n IS asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
  LOCAL fs IS asc_thrust(asc["ssme"]).
  IF n > 0 AND fs[0] > 0 AND fs[1] > 0 {
    LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
    LOCAL et IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]).
    LOCAL o IS LIST().
    IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET o TO LIST(asc["oms_t0"], asc["oms_t0"] + asc_oms_left() / ASC_ARD_MDO). }
    ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { SET o TO LIST(met - 1, met + asc_oms_left() / ASC_ARD_MDO). }
    ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 3 { SET o TO LIST(met - 2, met - 1). }
    LOCAL st IS LIST(p["lamc"], p["lamdc"], p["tlamc"]).
    LOCAL sel IS asc["abort"].
    LOCAL site IS "".
    IF sel = "TAL" { SET site TO ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]. }
    LOCAL tls IS LEXICON().
    FOR x IN ASC_TAL_SITES { SET tls[x] TO asc_tal_lex(x). }
    ard_vd_go(asc["ard"], LEXICON("md", "PRESS", "tl", LEXICON(), "e", n, "K", ASC_KMAX_ABORT, "t", met, "r", sm[1],
      "v", sm[2], "et", et, "mc", SHIP:MASS - et, "res", ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"], "iy", p["IYD"],
      "steer", st, "o", o, "m", LEXICON("f1", fs[0] / n, "vex", fs[1]), "rs", asc_ard_rs()),
      LEXICON("t", met, "r", sm[1], "v", sm[2], "et", et, "om", 0, "iy", p["IYD"], "steer", st, "o", o), sel, site, tls).
    SET cn["vd"] TO "RUN".
  }
  asc_note(asc, "2EO: DROOP + OMS DUMP UNTIL THE VERDICT").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#droop,go," + met + "," + cn["vd"] + "," + asc["oms_st"] + "," + asc["abort"] TO asc["log"]. }
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_tgt {                  // deg: the entry's alpha for mode md at the surface speed spd (m/s), as ops6q's
  PARAMETER md, spd.
  IF md = "TAL" { RETURN ASC_HO_A_TAL. }
  IF md = "CONT" { RETURN MIN(MAX(10 * spd / ASC_HO_SOUND + 5, 20), ASC_HO_A_RTLS). }
  RETURN ASC_HO_A_RTLS.
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_init {                 // the hold from now: alpha a0 toward tgt at rate deg/s; kp: keep the top
  PARAMETER a0, tgt, rate, kp.
  SET asc["ho"] TO LEXICON("t0", TIME:SECONDS, "met0", asc_met(), "a0", a0, "tgt", tgt, "rate", rate, "keep", kp,
    "top", asc_dir:TOPVECTOR, "oms", FALSE).
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_alpha {                // deg: the hold's alpha now (from a0 toward tgt at rate)
  LOCAL h IS asc["ho"].
  LOCAL da IS h["tgt"] - h["a0"].
  LOCAL st IS h["rate"] * (TIME:SECONDS - h["t0"]).
  IF ABS(da) <= st { RETURN h["tgt"]. }
  IF da > 0 { RETURN h["a0"] + st. }
  RETURN h["a0"] - st.
}

// the displays' target (the HUD's diamond and yaw line, the pages' R/P/Y), shown from MECO on: through MECO, ET SEP
// and a hand-off's clearing translation the hand-off's attitude (asc_ho_dir once it is set up, as a split-S's; else
// the hold asc_ho_prep will fly: the entry's alpha, wings level heads up) while the steering keeps the separation's
// attitude (asc_dir); else asc_dir
FUNCTION asc_view_dir {
  LOCAL ph IS asc["phase"].
  IF NOT (ph = "MECO" OR ph = "ETSEP" OR ph = "ETCLR") { RETURN asc_dir. }
  IF NOT (asc["abort"] = "TAL" OR asc["abort"] = "RTLS" OR asc["abort"] = "CONT") { RETURN asc_dir. }
  IF asc["ho"]:LENGTH > 0 { RETURN asc_ho_dir(). }
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  IF vs:MAG < 1 { RETURN asc_dir. }
  LOCAL u IS vs:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL tp IS VXCL(u, UP:VECTOR):NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL a IS asc_ho_tgt(asc["abort"], vs:MAG).
  RETURN LOOKDIRUP(u * COS(a) + tp * SIN(a), tp * COS(a) - u * SIN(a)).
}

// the hold: alpha (asc_ho_alpha) about the relative wind, sideslip 0, wings level heads up (SPLITS: the top as at its
// end); the steering's target in HOPREP and after the main loop (LOCK STEERING TO asc_ho_dir().) into OPS 6
FUNCTION asc_ho_dir {
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL h IS asc["ho"].
  IF vs:MAG < 1 OR h:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN SHIP:FACING. }
  LOCAL u IS vs:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL tp IS VXCL(u, h["top"]):NORMALIZED.
  IF NOT h["keep"] { SET tp TO VXCL(u, UP:VECTOR):NORMALIZED. }
  LOCAL a IS asc_ho_alpha().
  RETURN LOOKDIRUP(u * COS(a) + tp * SIN(a), tp * COS(a) - u * SIN(a)).
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_due {                  // a dump MECO stopped (or never started) with propellant to go
  IF asc["oms_st"] <> 3 OR asc["oms_rest"] <= ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN { RETURN FALSE. }
  IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH < 4 { SET asc["oms_tk"] TO asc_oms_parts(). }
  RETURN asc_oms_mass() > ASC_OMS_DRY + ASC_HO_DUMP_MIN.
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_knows {                // ops6q.ks reads ASC_HO (then a running dump goes on into it)
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("ho_k") {
    SET asc["ho_k"] TO FALSE.
    IF EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") { SET asc["ho_k"] TO OPEN("0:/ops6q.ks"):READALL:STRING:CONTAINS("DEFINED ASC_HO"). }
  }
  RETURN asc["ho_k"].
}

// ops6q runs a TAL / RTLS / CONT dump on into OPS 6 only with the text ASC_HO_DUMP_ON in ops6q.ks; without it ops6q
// ends their dump at the hand-off (the steering hold stays), so HOPREP lights no dump. With it, a CONT's only (and a
// 3EO TAL's: asc_ho_prep)
FUNCTION asc_ho_dumps {
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("ho_d") {
    SET asc["ho_d"] TO FALSE.
    IF EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") { SET asc["ho_d"] TO OPEN("0:/ops6q.ks"):READALL:STRING:CONTAINS("ASC_HO_DUMP_ON"). }
  }
  RETURN asc["ho_d"].
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_az {                   // deg: the ground track's heading (the horizontal surface velocity)
  PARAMETER vs.
  LOCAL vh IS VXCL(UP:VECTOR, vs).
  IF vh:MAG < 0.1 { RETURN 0. }
  RETURN MOD(ARCTAN2(VDOT(vh, VCRS(UP:VECTOR, NORTH:VECTOR)), VDOT(vh, NORTH:VECTOR)) + 360, 360).
}

// deg: a split-S's turn plane at the hand-off, the plane the hold flies (its kept top across the wind: the loft's and
// the sequence's plane), as lib_grtls ssLift builds it (its horizontal part toward az0 while climbing); the ground
// track's when the top is along the wind. (The ground track of the near-vertical path is not the plane flown: on the
// In one FAR flight the loft and the hold flew 68 deg while the track read 63.1 at 46 of 267 m/s, 42-48 in the loft.)
FUNCTION asc_ho_plane {
  PARAMETER h.
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  IF vs:MAG < 1 OR NOT h:HASKEY("top") { RETURN asc_ho_az(vs). }
  LOCAL tp IS VXCL(UP:VECTOR, VXCL(vs:NORMALIZED, h["top"])).
  IF tp:MAG < 0.1 { RETURN asc_ho_az(vs). }
  IF VDOT(UP:VECTOR, vs) < 0 { SET tp TO -tp. }
  RETURN asc_ho_az(tp).
}

// The OMS thrust line clear of the ET, the ET taken as its BOUNDS box (the thrust line against the ET's CoM alone read
// 8.7 deg with the 47 m tank alongside, its CoM forward of the orbiter's, and the hold timed out with no dump): the
// orbiter's CoM flown ASC_HO_T_CHK s ahead on the dump's acceleration (the thrust line ASC_S1C_OMS_EPS below the
// nose) plus the drift now; clear when that path comes no nearer the box than the lesser of now and ASC_HO_D_SAFE
// (less ASC_HO_D_TOL), or no other vessel within 2 km. The thrust line's angle off the ET stays in the log.
GLOBAL ASC_HO_T_CHK IS 30.     // s: the path's horizon (1 s steps)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_D_SAFE IS 30.    // m: the orbiter's half-span (12 m) and its tail, with margin
GLOBAL ASC_HO_D_TOL IS 0.5.    // m
GLOBAL ASC_HO_ACC0 IS 0.5.     // m/s^2: the dump's acceleration when the AJ10s give no thrust figure
FUNCTION asc_ho_clear {
  LOCAL fw IS SHIP:FACING:FOREVECTOR.
  LOCAL td IS fw * COS(ASC_S1C_OMS_EPS) - SHIP:FACING:TOPVECTOR * SIN(ASC_S1C_OMS_EPS).
  LOCAL ef IS asc_ho_et().
  IF NOT ef[0] {
    SET asc["ho"]["ang"] TO -1.
    SET asc["ho"]["clr"] TO LIST(-1, -1).
    RETURN TRUE.
  }
  LOCAL et IS ef[1].
  SET asc["ho"]["ang"] TO VANG(td, et:POSITION).
  LOCAL b IS et:BOUNDS.
  LOCAL qi IS b:FACING:INVERSE.
  LOCAL cl IS asc_ho_clr_path(qi * (V(0, 0, 0) - b:ABSORIGIN), qi * (SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT - et:VELOCITY:ORBIT), asc_ho_acc(),
    qi * td, b:RELMIN, b:RELMAX).
  SET asc["ho"]["clr"] TO cl.
  RETURN cl[1] >= MIN(cl[0], ASC_HO_D_SAFE) - ASC_HO_D_TOL.
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_et {                    // LIST(found, the nearest other vessel within 2 km: the ET)
  LOCAL tl IS LIST().
  LIST TARGETS IN tl.
  LOCAL best IS LIST(FALSE, 0).
  LOCAL dmin IS 2000.
  FOR vs IN tl { IF vs:DISTANCE < dmin { SET dmin TO vs:DISTANCE. SET best TO LIST(TRUE, vs). } }
  RETURN best.
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_acc {                   // m/s^2: the AJ10s' vacuum thrust over the mass
  LOCAL f IS 0.
  FOR en IN SHIP:ENGINES { IF en:NAME:CONTAINS("AJ10") { SET f TO f + en:POSSIBLETHRUSTAT(0). } }
  IF f <= 0 { RETURN ASC_HO_ACC0. }
  RETURN f / SHIP:MASS.
}

// LIST(m now, m least over the path): the orbiter's CoM o (m), drifting rv (m/s), accelerating acc (m/s^2) along the unit
// td, against the box mn..mx, all in the box's frame
FUNCTION asc_ho_clr_path {
  PARAMETER o, rv, acc, td, mn, mx.
  LOCAL d0 IS asc_box_d(o, mn, mx).
  LOCAL dm IS d0.
  FROM { LOCAL k IS 1. } UNTIL k > ASC_HO_T_CHK STEP { SET k TO k + 1. } DO {
    SET dm TO MIN(dm, asc_box_d(o + rv * k + td * (0.5 * acc * k * k), mn, mx)).
  }
  RETURN LIST(d0, dm).
}

FUNCTION asc_box_d {                    // m: a point's distance from a box (0 inside)
  PARAMETER p, mn, mx.
  LOCAL dx IS MAX(0, MAX(mn:X - p:X, p:X - mx:X)).
  LOCAL dy IS MAX(0, MAX(mn:Y - p:Y, p:Y - mx:Y)).
  LOCAL dz IS MAX(0, MAX(mn:Z - p:Z, p:Z - mx:Z)).
  RETURN SQRT(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz).
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_clr_s {                 // the test's figures for the log: "m now;m least"
  IF NOT asc["ho"]:HASKEY("clr") { RETURN "". }
  RETURN ROUND(asc["ho"]["clr"][0], 1) + ";" + ROUND(asc["ho"]["clr"][1], 1).
}

// a dump the hold could not light (ASC_HO dump_wait): OPS 6 calls this (ASC_HO dump_go) once asc_ho_clear (ASC_HO
// dump_clr) holds: ops1q's start (its scope lives through the RUNPATH), the cut by the aft's mass armed; the engines lit
FUNCTION asc_ho_late {
  SET asc["oms_dump"] TO MIN(99, asc["oms_rest"]).
  SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 0.
  asc["oms"]:CLEAR().
  FOR en IN SHIP:ENGINES { IF en:NAME:CONTAINS("AJ10") { asc["oms"]:ADD(en). } }
  SET asc["oms_tk"] TO asc_oms_parts().
  asc_oms_lock(asc_met()).                  // after the sep: none (the mid feeds the fuel cell)
  FOR en IN asc["oms"] { IF NOT en:IGNITION { en:ACTIVATE(). } }
  SET asc["oms_m0"] TO asc_oms_mass().
  SET asc["oms_st"] TO 2.
  SET asc["oms_t0"] TO asc_met().
  asc_oms_cut_arm().
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ho,late," + asc_met() + "," + asc["oms_m0"] + "," + asc["oms_dump"] + "," + ROUND(asc["ho"]["ang"], 2) + ","
    + asc_ho_clr_s() + "," + asc_et_rel():JOIN(";") TO asc["log"]. }
  RETURN asc["oms"]:COPY.
}

GLOBAL ASC_HO_CSS_DEG IS 3.          // deg: CSS's alignment before OPS 6 (the attitude error's whole angle)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_CSS_W IS 0.5.          // deg/s: and the body rate
GLOBAL ASC_HO_CSS_T IS 45.           // s the hand-off waits for the crew's CSS alignment, then OPS 6 flies the hold (0 = no limit, as before)
GLOBAL ASC_HO_CSS_SAY IS 15.         // s between the wait's reminder lines

FUNCTION asc_ho_css_fig {            // LIST(the attitude error's whole angle deg, the body rate deg/s)
  LOCAL f IS SHIP:FACING.
  LOCAL e IS ascCssErr(f:FOREVECTOR, f:TOPVECTOR, f:STARVECTOR, asc_dir):MAG * 57.2958.
  LOCAL w IS SHIP:ANGULARVEL:MAG * 57.2958.
  RETURN LIST(e, w).
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_css_ok {
  LOCAL cf IS asc_ho_css_fig().
  RETURN cf[0] < ASC_HO_CSS_DEG AND cf[1] < ASC_HO_CSS_W.   // no events
}

// The wait for CSS's alignment says what
// it waits for, repeats it every ASC_HO_CSS_SAY s with the figures, and ends after ASC_HO_CSS_T s (OPS 6's DAP then flies the hold).
// ut s, e deg, w deg/s; RETURNS TRUE once the time is up (then hand over), else FALSE (keep waiting). asc["ho"]: cw0 / cws = the start / last line.
FUNCTION asc_ho_css_wait {
  PARAMETER ut, e, w.
  LOCAL h IS asc["ho"].
  IF NOT h:HASKEY("cw0") {
    SET h["cw0"] TO ut.
    SET h["cws"] TO ut.
    SET asc_am_force TO FALSE.                // Only a press while this line is up counts
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  IF asc_am_force {
    SET asc_am_force TO FALSE.
    asc_event(asc, "AG4: OPS 6 TAKES THE ATTITUDE NOW").
    RETURN TRUE.
  }
  IF ASC_HO_CSS_T > 0 AND ut - h["cw0"] >= ASC_HO_CSS_T {
    asc_event(asc, "OPS 6 TAKES THE ATTITUDE: THE ALIGNMENT WAIT IS OVER").
    RETURN TRUE.
  }
  IF ut - h["cws"] >= ASC_HO_CSS_SAY {
    SET h["cws"] TO ut.
    asc_event(asc, "OPS 6 WAITS: ATT ERR " + ROUND(e, 1) + " DEG, RATE " + ROUND(w, 2) + " DEG/S (NEED " + ASC_HO_CSS_DEG + " / " + ASC_HO_CSS_W + ")").
  }
  RETURN FALSE.
}

FUNCTION asc_ho_prep {
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL ab IS asc_s1c_ab(vs).
  IF asc["ho"]:LENGTH = 0 {
    LOCAL tg IS asc_ho_tgt(asc["abort"], vs:MAG).
    asc_ho_init(CHOOSE ab[0] IF ASC_HO_RATE > 0 ELSE tg, tg, ASC_HO_RATE, FALSE).   // straight to tg (ASC_HO_RATE 0)
    SET asc["ho"]["ang"] TO -1.
    asc_ho_clear().
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ho,start," + met + "," + ab[0] + "," + ab[1] + "," + asc["ho"]["tgt"] + "," + asc_oms_mass() + ","
      + asc["oms_rest"] + "," + asc_et_rel():JOIN(";") + "," + ROUND(asc["ho"]["ang"], 2) + "," + asc_ho_clr_s()
      TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  LOCAL h IS asc["ho"].
  SET asc_dir TO asc_ho_dir().
  // the dump relit in the hold for a CONT only (a TAL's and an RTLS's end at the hand-off), and for a 3EO's TAL
  // (the OMS it needs makes up the underspeed)
  LOCAL due IS (asc["abort"] = "CONT" OR (asc["abort"] = "TAL" AND asc["eo3"])) AND asc_ho_due() AND asc_ho_knows()
    AND asc_ho_dumps().   // else ops6q stops it
  IF due AND asc_ho_clear() {               // the dump's path clear of the ET
    SET h["oms"] TO TRUE.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ho,lit," + met + "," + ab[0] + "," + ROUND(h["ang"], 2) + "," + asc_et_rel():JOIN(";") + "," + asc_ho_clr_s()
      TO asc["log"]. }
    SET asc["oms_dump"] TO MIN(99, asc["oms_rest"]).
    SET asc["oms_rest"] TO 0.
    SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met.
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
    SET asc_thr TO 1.
  }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 OR asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms(LEXICON(), met). }   // PEG's S_MECO must not stop it
  IF due AND NOT h["oms"] AND TIME:SECONDS - h["t0"] < ASC_HO_T_MAX { RETURN "HOPREP". }
  IF due AND NOT h["oms"] {                 // not clear in the hold: OPS 6 lights it once clear (asc_ho_set)
    SET asc["ho_wait"] TO TRUE.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ho,wait," + met + "," + ROUND(h["ang"], 2) + "," + asc_ho_clr_s() + "," + asc["oms_rest"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  // with CSS on, no OPS 6 until the pilot has the attitude within ASC_HO_CSS_DEG of the hold's (asc_dir: the HUD's
  // diamond, the pages' R/P/Y) and the body rate under ASC_HO_CSS_W; the wait is announced and ends after ASC_HO_CSS_T s
  IF ascCss["on"] {
    LOCAL cf IS asc_ho_css_fig().
    IF NOT (cf[0] < ASC_HO_CSS_DEG AND cf[1] < ASC_HO_CSS_W) {
      IF NOT asc_ho_css_wait(TIME:SECONDS, cf[0], cf[1]) { RETURN "HOPREP". }
    }
  }
  // ENTRY ARMED: OPS 6 next, run at this program's end; the logger ends now (its trigger must not run
  // on into the entry)
  IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" { asc_event(asc, "TAL ENTRY ARMED"). }
  ELSE IF asc["abort"] = "RTLS" { asc_event(asc, "GRTLS ENTRY ARMED"). }
  ELSE { asc_event(asc, "CONT " + asc["cn"]["site"] + " ENTRY ARMED"). }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ho,end," + met + "," + ab[0] + "," + asc_ho_alpha() + "," + asc["oms_st"] + "," + asc_oms_left() + ","
    + asc_oms_mass() + "," + asc_et_rel():JOIN(";") + "," + ROUND(h["ang"], 2) + "," + asc_ho_clr_s() TO asc["log"]. }
  IF DEFINED LG_END_S { SET LG_END_S TO 0. }
  SET asc["lg_wait"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 10.
  RETURN "DONE".
}

// ASC_HO for ops6q (the contract between the two) just before the RUNPATH: mode, site, ut, met, dump_on, dump_left (t;
// -1 = to empty), fc_lk (asc["oms_lk"]: LIST(resource, ENABLED before)), aj10, surf_on, az0, rate, eo3 (TRUE after a
// stage-2 3EO's pick, asc_3eo_go; ops6q burns a 3EO TAL's dump on for dump_left t only then); css_p, css_r, hud, cam;
// oms_cut, m_cut; meco_ut (MECO's UT for OPS 6's reach test; -1 without a MECO: the split-S); eo2 (asc["eo2_ln"], the
// locked 2EO word: BLUE / GREEN / ORANGE / RED / RTLS / PRESS / TAL / ATO / SPLITS ...; "" without a 2EO line; ops6q:
// "BLUE" in an RTLS = BLUE at once); dump_wait (+ dump_go, dump_clr when set); the hold's alpha_cmd, alpha_tgt,
// ho_rate, a0, t0, top ("UP" / "KEPT"); SPLITS + rate (its own), alpha_max, nz_max, nz, sep_met, sep_ut
FUNCTION asc_ho_set {
  PARAMETER md, site.
  LOCAL h IS asc["ho"].
  LOCAL lit IS asc["oms_st"] = 2.
  LOCAL lf IS 0.
  IF lit { SET lf TO CHOOSE -1 IF asc["oms_dump"] >= 50 ELSE asc_oms_left(). }
  SET ASC_HO TO LEXICON("mode", md, "site", site, "ut", TIME:SECONDS, "met", asc_met(), "dump_on", lit, "dump_left", lf,
    "fc_lk", asc["oms_lk"], "aj10", asc["oms"], "surf_on", md = "SPLITS",
    "az0", CHOOSE asc_ho_plane(h) IF md = "SPLITS" ELSE asc_ho_az(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE),
    "rate", ASC_HO_RATE, "eo3", asc["eo3"]).   // eo3 for ops6q
  // the crew's CSS axes, the HUD and its camera at the hand-off (lib_grdap grdStart, lib_dap dapGuiBuild)
  SET ASC_HO["css_p"] TO asc["css_c"][0].
  SET ASC_HO["css_r"] TO asc["css_c"][1].
  SET ASC_HO["hud"] TO asc["hud_c"][0].
  SET ASC_HO["cam"] TO asc["hud_c"][1].
  SET ASC_HO["oms_cut"] TO asc["oms_ct"].   // ops1q's trigger cuts the AJ10s (the aft's mass, every tick)
  SET ASC_HO["m_cut"] TO ASC_OMS_DRY + ASC_OMS_CUT_M.
  SET ASC_HO["meco_ut"] TO -1.                 // -1: no MECO (the split-S)
  IF asc["t_meco"] >= 0 { SET ASC_HO["meco_ut"] TO TIME:SECONDS - (asc_met() - asc["t_meco"]). }
  SET ASC_HO["eo2"] TO CHOOSE asc["eo2_ln"] IF asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") ELSE "".   // the locked 2EO word
  SET ASC_HO["dump_wait"] TO asc:HASKEY("ho_wait") AND NOT lit.   // the dump OPS 6 lights once the ET is clear
  IF ASC_HO["dump_wait"] {
    SET ASC_HO["dump_left"] TO CHOOSE -1 IF asc["oms_rest"] >= 50 ELSE asc["oms_rest"].
    SET ASC_HO["dump_go"] TO asc_ho_late@.
    SET ASC_HO["dump_clr"] TO asc_ho_clear@.
  }
  IF h:LENGTH > 0 {
    SET ASC_HO["alpha_cmd"] TO asc_ho_alpha().
    SET ASC_HO["alpha_tgt"] TO h["tgt"].
    SET ASC_HO["ho_rate"] TO h["rate"].
    SET ASC_HO["a0"] TO h["a0"].
    SET ASC_HO["t0"] TO h["t0"].
    SET ASC_HO["top"] TO CHOOSE "KEPT" IF h["keep"] ELSE "UP".
  }
  IF md = "SPLITS" {
    LOCAL c IS asc["s1c"].
    SET ASC_HO["rate"] TO c["rate"].
    SET ASC_HO["alpha_max"] TO c["alpha"].
    SET ASC_HO["nz_max"] TO c["nz"].
    SET ASC_HO["nz"] TO c["nzf"].
    SET ASC_HO["sep_met"] TO c["t_sep"].
    SET ASC_HO["sep_ut"] TO TIME:SECONDS - (asc_met() - c["t_sep"]).
  }
}

// The nearest other vessel within 2 km (after the ET separation: the ET): LIST(its distance m, its velocity relative to
// the orbiter along the orbiter's top and starboard m/s); an empty list when there is none
FUNCTION asc_et_rel {
  LOCAL tl IS LIST().
  LIST TARGETS IN tl.
  LOCAL best IS SHIP.
  LOCAL dmin IS 2000.
  FOR vs IN tl { IF vs:DISTANCE < dmin { SET dmin TO vs:DISTANCE. SET best TO vs. } }
  IF dmin >= 2000 { RETURN LIST(). }
  LOCAL rv IS best:VELOCITY:ORBIT - SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT.
  RETURN LIST(ROUND(dmin, 2), ROUND(VDOT(rv, SHIP:FACING:TOPVECTOR), 3), ROUND(VDOT(rv, SHIP:FACING:STARVECTOR), 3)).
}

// The plan files: lib_oms_plan.ks's omsPlanWrite (one writer for ops1q, ops2q (through omsPlanAto) and lib_aoa.ks).

// The OMS-2 plan for ops2q: prograde at the apoapsis to its circle, dv = sqrt(mu / r_a) - v_a.
// Then: RUN ops2q. (it flies the plan written last) or RUN ops2q("0:/oms2_plan.txt"). An ATO writes
// its own (asc_ato_plan).
FUNCTION asc_oms2plan {
  IF asc["abort"] = "ATO" { RETURN asc_ato_plan(). }
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  IF SHIP:ORBIT:ECCENTRICITY >= 1 OR SHIP:APOAPSIS <= 0 OR ETA:APOAPSIS <= 0 {
    asc_event(asc, "NO OMS-2 PLAN: NO APOGEE AHEAD").
    RETURN "DONE".
  }
  LOCAL tap IS ut + ETA:APOAPSIS.
  LOCAL dv IS SQRT(BODY:MU / (BODY:RADIUS + SHIP:APOAPSIS)) - VELOCITYAT(SHIP, tap):ORBIT:MAG.
  omsPlanWrite(asc_oms2_file, ut, tap, dv, 1, "OMS-2").
  asc_event(asc, "OMS-2 PLAN  DV " + ROUND(dv) + "  AT MET " + asc_mmss(tap - asc["t_lo"])).
  IF dv > ASC_OMS2_MAX { asc_event(asc, "OMS-2 DV OVER THE BUDGET " + ROUND(ASC_OMS2_MAX)). }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#oms2," + tap + "," + dv + "," + SHIP:APOAPSIS + "," + SHIP:PERIAPSIS TO asc["log"]. }
  RETURN "DONE".
}

// ---- the ATO's OMS plans (the offline ATO sim's two-burn plan, for ops2q): OMS-1 to an apogee at ATO_H;
// OMS-2 the ATO's circle there with ATO_DV_DEORBIT kept (PRESS TO ORBIT) or lib_aoa's AOA entry perigee (COME BACK).
// Two-body (Kepler) from the state at the writing, mu and R the I-loads'.
// The orbit through a point at r (m), speed v (m/s) and flight path angle gam (deg): LIST(the semi-major axis, e, the
// true anomaly (deg), the semi-latus rectum, the mean anomaly (rad), the mean motion (rad/s)); LIST() when it is not an
// ellipse.
FUNCTION asc_kep {
  PARAMETER rm, vm, gm.
  LOCAL en IS 2 / rm - vm * vm / ASC_MU.
  IF en <= 0 { RETURN LIST(). }
  LOCAL sma IS 1 / en.
  LOCAL hh IS rm * vm * COS(gm).
  LOCAL sl IS hh * hh / ASC_MU.
  LOCAL ec IS SQRT(MAX(0, 1 - sl / sma)).
  LOCAL nu IS 0.
  IF ec > 1e-12 {
    SET nu TO ARCCOS(MAX(-1, MIN(1, (sl / rm - 1) / ec))).
    IF gm < 0 { SET nu TO 360 - nu. }
  }
  LOCAL ea IS 2 * ARCTAN2(SQRT(1 - ec) * SIN(nu / 2), SQRT(1 + ec) * COS(nu / 2)) * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD.
  RETURN LIST(sma, ec, nu, sl, ea - ec * SIN(ea * CONSTANT:RADTODEG), SQRT(ASC_MU / (sma * sma * sma))).
}

// Kepler's equation M = E - e sin E (rad) for E, by Newton
FUNCTION asc_kep_ea {
  PARAMETER mr, ec.
  LOCAL ea IS mr.
  LOCAL dx IS 1.
  LOCAL i IS 0.
  UNTIL ABS(dx) < 1e-12 OR i >= 50 {
    SET dx TO (ea - ec * SIN(ea * CONSTANT:RADTODEG) - mr) / (1 - ec * COS(ea * CONSTANT:RADTODEG)).
    SET ea TO ea - dx.
    SET i TO i + 1.
  }
  RETURN ea.
}

// r (m), v (m/s), gam (deg) on orbit k (asc_kep) dt s after its point
FUNCTION asc_kep_at {
  PARAMETER k, dt.
  LOCAL ec IS k[1].
  LOCAL ed IS asc_kep_ea(k[4] + k[5] * dt, ec) * CONSTANT:RADTODEG.
  LOCAL rm IS k[0] * (1 - ec * COS(ed)).
  LOCAL nu IS 2 * ARCTAN2(SQRT(1 + ec) * SIN(ed / 2), SQRT(1 - ec) * COS(ed / 2)).
  RETURN LIST(rm, SQRT(ASC_MU * (2 / rm - 1 / k[0])), ARCTAN2(ec * SIN(nu), 1 + ec * COS(nu))).
}

// s from orbit k's point to its next apogee
FUNCTION asc_kep_tapo {
  PARAMETER k.
  LOCAL dm IS CONSTANT:PI - k[4].
  IF dm < 0 { SET dm TO dm + 2 * CONSTANT:PI. }
  RETURN dm / k[5].
}

// The speed at radius r (m) and flight path angle gam (deg) whose orbit has its apogee at ra (m, above r): from
// h = r v cos gam = ra va and the energy, v^2 = 2 mu (1/r - 1/ra) / (1 - (r cos gam / ra)^2)
FUNCTION asc_v_apo {
  PARAMETER rm, gm, ra.
  LOCAL cr IS rm * COS(gm) / ra.
  RETURN SQRT(2 * ASC_MU * (1 / rm - 1 / ra) / (1 - cr * cr)).
}

// After the ET separation of an ATO (one ATO button: PRESS TO ORBIT or COME BACK, chosen in a window after OMS-1;
// ops2q plans OMS-2 unless OMS-1 is skipped). OMS-1 only when the apogee is short of ASC_ATO_H: prograde, from
// ABT_OMS1_LEAD s after the writing, centred by its burn time (the rocket equation at OMS_F and OMS_ISP), its dv
// raising the apogee to ATO_H at its centre (impulsive there; the offline sim burns horizontally at the cutoff):
// asc_oms1_file tagged "ATO OMS-1", an old OMS-2 plan deleted; ops2q flies it, asks and plans OMS-2. OMS-1
// skipped: the question here (asc_ato_ask), then asc_oms2_file: the ATO's circle at the apogee ("ATO OMS-2") or
// lib_aoa's aoaPlanOms2 (the AOA's entry perigee, "AOA OMS-2"). The delta-V of the ATO's burns (OMS-2 at the apogee
// of the orbit after OMS-1, ATO_DV_DEORBIT kept) against the OMS on board (the AJ10s' propellant at OMS_ISP).
FUNCTION asc_ato_plan {
  LOCAL hta IS ASC_ATO_H.
  LOCAL keep IS ASC_ATO_DV_DEORBIT.
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut).
  LOCAL rm IS sm[1]:MAG.
  LOCAL vm IS sm[2]:MAG.
  LOCAL gm IS ARCSIN(MAX(-1, MIN(1, VDOT(sm[1], sm[2]) / (rm * vm)))).
  LOCAL k0 IS asc_kep(rm, vm, gm).
  IF k0:LENGTH = 0 { asc_event(asc, "ATO: NO OMS PLAN (NOT AN ELLIPSE)"). RETURN "DONE". }
  IF asc["oms"]:LENGTH = 0 { FOR en IN SHIP:ENGINES { IF en:NAME:CONTAINS("AJ10") { asc["oms"]:ADD(en). } } }
  // the OMS tanks found here when no dump found them: an ATO has no dump, and without them asc_oms_mass reads 0 t
  // ("OVER THE 0 ON BOARD", the AOA window's OMS dV below 0)
  IF asc["oms_tk"]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["oms_tk"] TO asc_oms_parts(). }
  LOCAL mo IS asc_oms_mass().
  asc["oms"]:CLEAR().
  LOCAL ms IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL ve IS ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0.
  LOCAL dvo IS 0.
  IF mo > 0 AND mo < ms { SET dvo TO ve * LN(ms / (ms - mo)). }
  LOCAL dv1 IS 0.
  LOCAL t1 IS ut.
  LOCAL tb IS 0.
  LOCAL k2 IS k0.
  IF k0[0] * (1 + k0[1]) < ASC_R + hta {
    LOCAL s1 IS LIST().
    FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= 4 STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
      SET t1 TO ut + ASC_ABT_OMS1_LEAD + tb / 2.
      SET s1 TO asc_kep_at(k0, t1 - ut).
      SET dv1 TO asc_v_apo(s1[0], s1[2], ASC_R + hta) - s1[1].
      SET tb TO ms * (1 - CONSTANT:E ^ (-dv1 / ve)) * ve / ASC_OMS_F.
    }
    SET k2 TO asc_kep(s1[0], s1[1] + dv1, s1[2]).
  }
  LOCAL tap IS t1 + asc_kep_tapo(k2).
  LOCAL ra IS k2[0] * (1 + k2[1]).
  LOCAL rt IS MIN(ASC_R + hta, ra).
  LOCAL dv2 IS SQRT(ASC_MU * (2 / ra - 2 / (ra + rt))) - SQRT(ASC_MU * (2 / ra - 1 / k2[0])).
  LOCAL need IS dv1 + ABS(dv2) + keep.
  LOCAL bw IS " OF ".
  IF need > dvo { SET bw TO " OVER THE ". }
  LOCAL md IS "ATO".
  IF dv1 > 0 {
    omsPlanWrite(asc_oms1_file, ut, t1, dv1, 1, "ATO OMS-1").
    LOG "site " + ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"] TO asc_oms1_file.   // the launch site (the orbiter's AOA site I-load) for ops2q's AOA
    IF EXISTS(asc_oms2_file) { DELETEPATH(asc_oms2_file). }
    asc_event(asc, "ATO OMS-1 PLAN  DV " + ROUND(dv1) + "  AT MET " + asc_mmss(t1 - asc["t_lo"]) + "  HA "
      + ROUND(hta / 1000) + "K").
    asc_event(asc, "ATO OMS DV " + ROUND(need) + bw + ROUND(dvo) + " ON BOARD").
    asc_note(asc, CHOOSE "OMS-1: OPS2 (ATO / AOA TGT)." IF asc_o2_ho ELSE "OMS-1: RUN SHUTTLE_EXEC.").
  } ELSE {
    IF EXISTS(asc_oms1_file) { DELETEPATH(asc_oms1_file). }
    asc_event(asc, "ATO: NO OMS-1 (HA " + ROUND((ra - ASC_R) / 1000) + "K)  OMS DV " + ROUND(need) + bw
      + ROUND(dvo) + " ON BOARD").
    IF asc_o2_ho { asc_note(asc, "OPS2: ATO / AOA TGT"). }
    ELSE { SET md TO asc_ato_ask(ABS(dv2), keep, dvo). }
    IF asc_o2_ho {                           // ops2q asks and plans OMS-2 for the pick (the hand-off below)
    } ELSE IF md = "AOA" {
      IF aoaPlanOms2() { asc_note(asc, "AOA OMS-2: PLANNED (0:/OMS2_PLAN.TXT)"). }
      ELSE { asc_event(asc, "AOA OMS-2 NO PLAN"). }
    } ELSE {
      omsPlanWrite(asc_oms2_file, ut, tap, ABS(dv2), CHOOSE 1 IF dv2 >= 0 ELSE -1, "ATO OMS-2").
      asc_event(asc, "ATO OMS-2 DV " + ROUND(ABS(dv2)) + "  AT MET "
        + asc_mmss(tap - asc["t_lo"]) + "  HP " + ROUND((rt - ASC_R) / 1000) + "K").
    }
  }
  IF asc_o2_ho { asc_ato_ho(dv1, dv2, keep, dvo, mo, k0, ra, rt, vm). }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#atoplan," + md + "," + ut + "," + rm + "," + vm + "," + gm + "," + ms + "," + mo + "," + dvo + "," + t1 + ","
    + dv1 + "," + tb + "," + tap + "," + dv2 + "," + ra + "," + rt + "," + need TO asc["log"]. }
  RETURN "DONE".
}

// THE HAND-OFF to ops2q: 1:/ops2q_ho.txt, "key value" lines (lib_o2ato.ks o2atHoRead reads it): the abort and why, ops1q's
// own pick (ATO when the OMS left after OMS-1 + OMS-2 covers the deorbit reserve, asc_3eo_go's rule; else AOA), the orbit at MECO
// (ha / hp km, vi m/s, oms kg), the ATO's burns (dv1 / dv2 m/s), the reserve (keep) and the OMS on board (dvo, m/s), whether an
// OMS-1 plan was written, the launch site, and the phase (PRE: OMS-1 still to fly; POST: none). ops1q deletes it at liftoff.
FUNCTION asc_ato_ho {
  PARAMETER dv1, dv2, keep, dvo, mo, k0, ra, rt, vm.
  LOCAL why IS "ATO".
  IF asc["eo3"] { SET why TO "3 ENG OUT". }
  ELSE IF asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") { SET why TO "2 ENG OUT". }
  ELSE IF asc:HASKEY("t_eo1") { SET why TO "ENG OUT". }
  IF asc:HASKEY("t_eo1") { SET why TO why + " " + asc_mmss(asc["t_eo1"]). }
  LOCAL pk IS "ATO".
  IF dvo - dv1 - ABS(dv2) < keep { SET pk TO "AOA". }
  LOCAL f IS "1:/ops2q_ho.txt".
  IF EXISTS(f) { DELETEPATH(f). }
  LOG "abort ATO" TO f.
  LOG "why " + why TO f.
  LOG "pick " + pk TO f.
  LOG "ha " + ROUND((k0[0] * (1 + k0[1]) - ASC_R) / 1000) TO f.
  LOG "hp " + ROUND((k0[0] * (1 - k0[1]) - ASC_R) / 1000) TO f.
  LOG "vi " + ROUND(vm) TO f.
  LOG "oms " + ROUND(mo * 1000) TO f.
  LOG "dv1 " + ROUND(dv1, 2) TO f.
  LOG "dv2 " + ROUND(dv2, 2) TO f.
  LOG "keep " + ROUND(keep, 2) TO f.
  LOG "dvo " + ROUND(dvo, 2) TO f.
  LOG "oms1 " + (CHOOSE 1 IF dv1 > 0 ELSE 0) TO f.
  LOG "site " + ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"] TO f.
  LOG "ph " + (CHOOSE "PRE" IF dv1 > 0 ELSE "POST") TO f.
  SET asc["o2ho"] TO TRUE.
}

// PRESS TO ORBIT ("ATO") or COME BACK ("AOA") with OMS-1 skipped: lib_aoa.ks's aoaAsk window (the ATO's OMS-2 dv,
// the deorbit's reserve, the OMS dV on board, m/s); without lib_aoa.ks "ATO".
FUNCTION asc_ato_ask {
  PARAMETER dva, keep, dvo.
  IF NOT asc_aoa_lib { asc_event(asc, "LIB_AOA.KS: NOT INSTALLED, ATO"). RETURN "ATO". }
  RETURN aoaAsk(LEXICON("dv_ato", dva, "dv_keep", keep, "dv_oms", dvo, "dv_onorb", ASC_OMS_ONORB, "dv_emerg", ASC_OMS_EMERG)).
}

// The fuel cell on: the mid fuselage's ModuleResourceConverter "Fuel Cell" (fed from that part's own LF / Ox,
// NO_FLOW), started through its module, not AG5 (bound to the bay doors too). "start fuel cell" starts, never toggles,
// so a running cell stays on. Returns how many.
FUNCTION asc_fuel_cell {
  LOCAL n IS 0.
  FOR m IN SHIP:MODULESNAMED("ModuleResourceConverter") {
    IF m:HASACTION("start fuel cell") { m:DOACTION("start fuel cell", TRUE). SET n TO n + 1. }
    ELSE IF m:HASEVENT("start fuel cell") { m:DOEVENT("start fuel cell"). SET n TO n + 1. }
  }
  RETURN n.
}

// An SSME fails (a FAIL button or ASC_EO; k = "L" / "C" / "R", the pages' positions): shut down, its gimbal locked and
// dropped from asc["ssme"], so PEG, the throttle and the ET's level go on with the others (in stage 1 the throttle
// at KMAX from now on); nothing else changes (no abort yet). ext: "" for our own failure; from lib_ascent_eo's detector
// the cause of an engine found out from outside ("G" gone, "S" shut down, "F" flame-out, "P" thrust lost): the same
// failure, no SHUTDOWN and no gimbal lock for a part that is gone, one #eo log line.
FUNCTION asc_fail {
  PARAMETER k, ext IS "".
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 {                       // RSLS: on the pad, one of the count's SSMEs (asc["ssme"] is set at liftoff)
    LOCAL cdst IS asc["cd"].
    IF cdst:LENGTH > 0 AND ASC_CD_RSLS { IF cdst["st"] = "HOLD" OR cdst["st"] = "COUNT" {
      LOCAL idp IS adEngIds(cdst["eng"]).
      IF idp:HASKEY(k) { IF asc_cd_fail(cdst, idp[k]) { flNote("MPS 01", k, "", "P", "PAD"). asc_event(asc, "FAIL " + k + " ON THE PAD"). RETURN TRUE. } }
    } }
    asc_event(asc, "FAIL " + k + ": NOT BEFORE IGNITION").
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  LOCAL ids IS adEngIds(asc["ssme"]).
  IF NOT ids:HASKEY(k) { asc_event(asc, "FAIL " + k + ": SSME NOT FOUND"). RETURN FALSE. }
  LOCAL en IS ids[k].
  LOCAL keep IS LIST().
  LOCAL hit IS FALSE.
  FOR eg IN asc["ssme"] { IF eg:UID = en:UID { SET hit TO TRUE. } ELSE { keep:ADD(eg). } }
  IF NOT hit { asc_event(asc, "SSME " + k + " ALREADY OUT"). RETURN FALSE. }
  IF ext <> "G" { en:SHUTDOWN(). }
  // the failed SSME's gimbal locked at once, set, not toggled, as MECO's lock, which runs over asc["ssme"] and so
  // never reaches it; KSP moves an unlocked gimbal with the controls whether its engine runs or not. Nothing unlocks
  // it again (the roll assignment and the DAP work on asc["ssme"] only).
  IF ext <> "G" { IF en:HASGIMBAL { SET en:GIMBAL:LOCK TO TRUE. } }
  SET asc["ssme"] TO keep.
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("t_eo1") {                // the first failure's MET; the 1EO line then (the pages' lock)
    SET asc["eo1_ln"] TO asc_1eo_line(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).
    SET asc["eo1_2ln"] TO asc_2eo_line(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).   // the 2EO line then (asc_cnt_arm's two1)
    SET asc["t_eo1"] TO asc_met().
    SET asc["vi_eo1"] TO SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG.   // the lists' VI from now (asc_ui)
    asc_rk_drop(asc["t_eo1"]).                  // the ranks of an SSME out later than this one go
    IF asc["abort"] = "" AND asc["pg"] { SET asc["auto_st"] TO 1. SET asc["ui_next"] TO 0. }   // the auto pick
  }
  // the 2EO line locked at the second failure (the pages' lock, lib_ascdisp's adLines; on the live VI it would run on
  // and say TAL long after a BLUE contingency had started), MODE SEL then the mode flown (asc_2eo_go, asc_cnt_arm)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 1 AND NOT asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") {
    SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO asc_2eo_line(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).
  }
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 2 { SET asc["ab_auto"] TO FALSE. }   // a 2EO's mode stays (no switch by hand)
  SET adOut[k] TO TRUE.
  flNote("MPS 01", k, "", "P", (CHOOSE "OUT " + ext IF ext <> "" ELSE "CREW")).   // the FAILURES window lists it (a no-op inside its own FAIL / row / RAND)
  IF ext <> "" AND asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#eo," + ROUND(asc_met(), 2) + "," + k + "," + ext TO asc["log"]. }
  asc_event(asc, "SSME " + k + " FAIL  VI " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG)).   // the failure first, then the
  asc_kabort("SSME " + k + " OUT").                                              //   abort throttle-up it causes
  asc_eo_steer().
  // a second (or third) SSME out in stage 1 flies the split-S (the header; asc_s1c_arm; SET ASC_SPLITS TO FALSE.
  // before the run: the 2EO contingency, below); after a 2EO the crew's BAILOUT window (asc_s1c_arm, asc_s1c_bail)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 2 AND NOT asc["s2_on"] AND asc["phase"] = "STAGE1" AND asc["s1c_on"] {
    IF asc["s1c"]:LENGTH = 0 { asc_s1c_arm(). }
    ELSE {
      SET asc["s1c"]["n"] TO asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
      asc_event(asc, (3 - asc["ssme"]:LENGTH) + "EO IN STAGE 1: SPLIT-S").
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1c,eo," + asc_met() + "," + asc["ssme"]:LENGTH TO asc["log"]. }
      IF asc["s1w"] >= 0 { asc_s1c_lock(" (3EO)"). }   // a 3EO in the crew's window keeps the split-S
    }
    // the pages' 3EO line shows the mode flown, SPLITS, not 3EO BLUE
    // (lib_ascdisp adLines: yellow from the third SSME out)
    IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 0 { SET asc["eo3_ln"] TO "SPLITS". }
  }
  // the second failure in stage 2 arms the 2EO contingency (lib_ascent_cnt; its start at the next tick:
  // asc_cnt_arm), in an RTLS the RTLS's own 2EO response: asc_2eo_arm; a failure in stage 1 with no split-S flown arms
  // the same at stage 2's start (asc_s2_start)
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 1 AND asc["cn"]:LENGTH = 0 AND asc["t_meco"] < 0 {
    IF NOT asc["s2_on"] {
      IF asc["s1c"]:LENGTH = 0 {
        asc_note(asc, "2EO IN STAGE 1: " + (CHOOSE "THE RTLS 2EO" IF asc["abort"] = "RTLS" ELSE "THE CONTINGENCY")
          + " AT THE SRB SEP").
      }
    }
    ELSE { asc_2eo_arm(). }
  }
  asc_ard_reset().                            // the ARD on the SSMEs left (off below two)
  RETURN TRUE.
}

// What a second SSME out arms in stage 2 -- in an RTLS its own 2EO response (asc_rtls_2eo), else the 2EO
// contingency (lib_ascent_cnt; MODE SEL and the start at the next tick: asc_cnt_arm) with the roll to
// heads up. From asc_fail at the failure and from asc_s2_start for a failure in stage 1 with no split-S flown (SET
// ASC_SPLITS TO FALSE. before the run, or the failure in the pass at the SRB sep): there t2 = stage 2's start, so
// CREW_DELAY counts from the SRB sep (the FSSR's crew starts a stage-1 2EO's contingency after the SRB sep), as a
// stage-1 3EO's
FUNCTION asc_2eo_arm {
  IF asc["rl"]:LENGTH > 0 { asc_rtls_2eo(). }   // mode 5 or the MECO at once
  ELSE {
    SET asc["cn"] TO asc_cnt_new(asc_met(), SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).
    SET asc["cn"]["two"] TO "".   // the 2EO mode flown instead (asc_2eo_go)
    SET asc["cn"]["now"] TO TRUE.   // asc_cnt_arm on the first tick after the failure (the stage-2 loop)
    // no BLUE / GREEN call here: the pick at the next tick (asc_cnt_arm) posts the mode flown, the contingency with its
    // BLUE / GREEN ("2EO CONT MODE ..."), a 2EO PRESS / ATO / TAL its "2EO VI ..." (a call made here would come first,
    // and before a 3EO's own event)
    // in a 2EO of any kind the roll to heads up starts here, as soon as it can, whatever flies next (the contingency,
    // the 2EO TAL / ATO / PRESS, the droop); the contingency then starts heads up (asc_cnt_start's hu: no man / roll);
    // one SSME: the RCS rolls (roll1)
    IF asc["t_roll"] < 0 {
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#roll," + asc_met() + "," + SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG + ",2eo" TO asc["log"]. }
      SET asc["t_roll"] TO asc_met().
    }
    IF ascDap["on"] { SET ascDap["roll1"] TO TRUE. }
  }
}

// the droop task after a PEG pass in stage 2 (lib_ascent_cnt's asc_drp_pass, FSSR 4.3.4): its inputs from the
// engines now (the SSMEs alone and with the OMS dump: asc_thrust; the throttle at K_CMD as PEG's ATR), the mass at
// the ET's low level, the dump's time left (and for subtask 4's hypothetical the dump a TAL burns: on, its rest;
// selected, from oms_t0; else a 2EO's own, MODE SEL CREW_DELAY after the failure and the dump CNT_DUMP_DELAY
// later; none once done); its messages and its log line (#drp)
FUNCTION asc_drp_go {
  PARAMETER g, met, sm, ft.
  LOCAL D IS asc["drp"].
  LOCAL n IS asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
  IF g["S_MECO"] OR n = 0 OR ft[0] <= 0 OR ft[1] <= 0 OR NOT g["peg"]["S_GDRDY"] { RETURN. }
  LOCAL fs IS asc_thrust(asc["ssme"]).
  IF fs[0] <= 0 OR fs[1] <= 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL M IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL kf IS g["K_CMD"] / 100 * ASC_PL_TO_KSP.
  LOCAL MLL IS MAX(0.05 * M, M - MAX(0, asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]) - ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"])).
  LOCAL mdo IS ASC_OMS_F / (ASC_OMS_ISP * CONSTANT:G0).
  LOCAL ko IS LIST(FALSE, 0, ASC_CNT_CREW_DELAY + ASC_CNT_DUMP_DELAY, ASC_TAL_DUMP / mdo).   // the dump at once
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET ko TO LIST(FALSE, 0, MAX(0, asc["oms_t0"] - met), asc_oms_left() / mdo). }
  ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 {
    SET ko TO LIST(FALSE, 0, 0, 0).
    IF asc["oms"]:LENGTH > 0 {
      LOCAL fo IS asc_thrust(asc["oms"]).
      IF fo[0] > 0 AND fo[1] > 0 {
        LOCAL sl IS asc_oms_left() * fo[1] / fo[0].
        SET ko TO LIST(TRUE, sl, 0, sl).
      }
    }
  } ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 3 { SET ko TO LIST(FALSE, 0, 0, 0). }
  LOCAL was IS LIST(D["S_CDROOP"], D["cmd_on"], D["S_MIN_ALT"]).
  asc_drp_pass(D, g["peg"], met, sm[1], sm[2], M, ft[1], kf * ft[0], kf * fs[0], ASC_PL_TO_KSP * fs[0] / n, fs[1],
    MLL, n, ko).
  // the DROOP lines only on a real droop: none while asc_2eo_droop_go's stopgap droop holds until the verdict (cn["vd"]
  // RUN); still engaged after it, the line then
  LOCAL sg IS FALSE.
  IF asc["cn"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET sg TO asc["cn"]["vd"] = "RUN". }
  IF NOT D["S_CDROOP"] { SET asc["drp_said"] TO FALSE. }
  ELSE IF NOT sg AND NOT asc["drp_said"] {
    SET asc["drp_said"] TO TRUE.
    asc_event(asc, "DROOP ENGAGED " + ROUND(D["rout"] / 1000) + "K").
  }
  IF D["cmd_on"] AND NOT sg {              // a line for each new pitch the droop selects
    LOCAL pa IS ROUND(D["THR_ATT"]).       // (ASC_DRP_ATT_INCR 2 deg a pass)
    IF pa <> asc["drp_pa"] { SET asc["drp_pa"] TO pa. asc_event(asc, "DROOP  PITCH " + pa + " DEG"). }
  }
  IF D["S_MIN_ALT"] AND NOT was[2] {
    IF sg { asc_note(asc, "DROOP COMPLETE"). } ELSE { asc_event(asc, "DROOP COMPLETE"). }
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#drp," + met + "," + n + "," + (sm[1]:MAG - ASC_R) + "," + D["rout"] + "," + D["T1NEW"] + "," + D["THR_ATT"]
    + "," + D["peg_att"] + "," + D["S_CDROOP"] + "," + D["S_DRP_EARLY"] + "," + D["S_MIN_ALT"] + "," + D["cmd_on"]
    + "," + D["hyp"] + "," + D["PRED"] + "," + D["vi_b"] TO asc["log"]. }
}

// MODE SEL at each PEG pass after the second failure; CREW_DELAY after it the start in mode 1 / 2: PEG's thrust
// direction the start's, the SSMEs at KMAX, the OMS dump to empty (ASC_CONT_DUMP_EMPTY; else the TAL's), the abort
// "CONT", the ELS for OPS 6 (asc_abr_site, the pages' BLUE / GREEN), the ascent DAP's roll on (one SSME: the RCS);
// mode 0 (VI above VI_MIN_DROOP): PEG flies on, the droop with it
FUNCTION asc_cnt_arm {
  PARAMETER g, met, sm.
  LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
  SET cn["now"] TO FALSE.
  IF cn["on"] OR g["S_MECO"] { RETURN. }
  SET cn["sel"] TO asc_cnt_sel(sm[1], sm[2]).
  IF met < cn["t2"] + ASC_CNT_CREW_DELAY - 0.000000001 { RETURN. }
  // the 2EO TAL, ATO and PRESS: both SSMEs out together (the second within ASC_CNT_BOTH_S of the first: the case the
  // 2EO marks are made for, both out at t2) at a VI where the pages' 2EO line opens PRESS, ATO or TAL at the second
  // failure: that mode flies on one SSME (PEG), not the contingency. A second failure later than that keeps MODE SEL
  // (the marks are not made for it: offline, staggered 2EO TALs fail far past the both-out mark), unless the ARD has
  // refreshed its 2EO marks on the two SSMEs left (asc["ard"]["ok2"]; ASC_ARD_2EO_STAG): then it flies the mode too
  // the choice through lib_ascent_cnt's asc_cnt_pick, so a 2EO GREEN never presses to MECO: GREEN flies the mode the
  // live sweep scored at vi2, MODE SEL 0 only where the 2EO line opens a mode (PEG then flies that mode), else mode 1
  // a later second failure before that refresh flies the 2EO line at the FIRST failure (asc["eo1_2ln"]) where that
  // one opened a mode already -- the pick's -2 (without it a first failure at VI 1713, past the 2EO ATO's 1700, and a
  // second 7.3 s later flew GREEN to YHZ, not the ATO)
  IF cn["two"] <> "" { RETURN. }
  LOCAL two IS asc_2eo_line(cn["vi2"]).
  LOCAL two1 IS "".
  IF asc:HASKEY("eo1_2ln") { SET two1 TO asc["eo1_2ln"]. }
  LOCAL wm IS 0.
  IF asc["bgl"]["live"] { SET wm TO bgl_md(cn["vi2"]). }
  LOCAL tr IS cn["t2"] - asc["t_eo1"] <= ASC_CNT_BOTH_S + 0.000000001 OR (ASC_ARD_2EO_STAG AND asc["ard"]["ok2"]).
  // asc_2eo_droop_go: a staggered second failure the marks do not cover (not both out together, the ARD not refreshed
  // on 2 SSMEs, the first failure's 2EO line opening no mode) flies the droop and the dump at once while the verdict
  // runs; its line then flies as a trusted 2EO line ("NONE": no mode open -> the contingency, mode 1 where MODE SEL
  // says 0), a TAL to the verdict's site
  IF cn["vd"] = "RUN" {
    IF asc["ard"]["ph"] = 4 { RETURN. }
    SET cn["vd"] TO asc["ard"]["vd_ln"].
    IF cn["vd"] = "" { SET cn["vd"] TO "NONE". }
    asc_note(asc, "2EO VERDICT: " + cn["vd"] + (CHOOSE " " + asc["ard"]["vd_st"] IF asc["ard"]["vd_st"] <> "" ELSE "")).
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#droop,vd," + met + "," + cn["vd"] + "," + asc["ard"]["vd_st"] + "," + asc["ard"]["u"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  IF cn["vd"] = "" AND NOT tr AND NOT asc_cnt_open(two1) AND ASC_2EO_DROOP_ON AND ASC_ARD_ON AND asc["pg"] {
    asc_2eo_droop_go(g, met, sm).
    IF cn["vd"] = "RUN" { RETURN. }
  }
  LOCAL tk IS -1.
  IF cn["vd"] <> "" {
    SET two TO cn["vd"].
    SET tr TO TRUE.
    SET two1 TO "".
    FROM { LOCAL i IS 0. } UNTIL i >= ASC_TAL_SITES:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 1. } DO {
      IF ASC_TAL_SITES[i] = asc["ard"]["vd_st"] { SET tk TO i. }
    }
  }
  LOCAL pk IS asc_cnt_pick(cn["sel"], two, tr, wm, two1).
  IF asc_cnt_m1to2(pk, cn["sel"], cn["vi2"]) {   // a late 2EO's MODE SEL 1 -> mode 2 + its hold
    SET pk TO 2.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#t15,m1to2," + met + "," + ROUND(cn["vi2"]) TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  IF pk = -2 { asc_2eo_go(cn, two1, met, asc["vi_eo1"]). RETURN. }
  IF pk < 0 { asc_2eo_go(cn, two, met, -1, tk). RETURN. }
  SET cn["sel"] TO pk.
  IF cn["sel"] = 0 {                       // the pages' marks unknown (the sidecar not loaded): PEG flies on
    IF NOT cn["said0"] {
      asc_note(asc, "2EO CONT MODE 0 (VI ABOVE " + ROUND(ASC_CNT_VI_MIN_DROOP) + " M/S)").
      SET cn["said0"] TO TRUE.
      SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO CHOOSE "PRESS" IF asc["abort"] = "" ELSE asc["abort"].   // the 2EO line's lock: PEG's target
    }
    RETURN.
  }
  // GREEN's yaw toward its ELS (lib_ascent_cnt's asc_cnt_yaw: mode 1, a second failure below ASC_CNT_VI_YAW_MAX,
  // the side from the site's place): the site first
  SET cn["site"] TO asc_abr_site(2, cn["vi2"]).
  // the early C/O only in a live sweep's window GREEN by its early MECO, i.e. where the early MECO scores better
  // (without a live sweep the site comes from the tables: never)
  SET cn["early_ok"] TO asc["bgl"]["live"] AND bgl_early_ok(cn["vi2"]).
  IF asc["bgl"]["live"] {                // the live BLUE / GREEN: its window's yaw (MODE SEL 1 only, as asc_cnt_yaw)
    IF cn["sel"] = 1 { SET cn["yaw"] TO bgl_yaw(cn["vi2"]). }
  } ELSE IF ASC_CNT_YAW_SITES:HASKEY(cn["site"]) {
    LOCAL ll IS ASC_CNT_YAW_SITES[cn["site"]].
    SET cn["yaw"] TO asc_cnt_yaw(cn["sel"], cn["vi2"], sm[1], asc_to_i(sm[0], SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE),
      asc_to_i(sm[0], LATLNG(ll[0], ll[1]):POSITION - BODY:POSITION)).
  }
  asc_cnt_start(cn, met, asc_peg_dir(g["peg"], met, g["hold"]), cn["sel"], asc["t_roll"] >= 0).
  SET cn["d_site"] TO asc_cnt_dsite(cn["site"]).
  asc_cnt_m2in(cn, sm).                    // mode 2's hold (asc_cnt_m2)
  asc_cnt_cycle(cn, met, sm[1], sm[2], asc_to_i(sm[0], SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE),
    SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA * 1000).
  asc_cnt_early_say(met).
  asc_cnt_law_say(met).
  SET g["K_CMD"] TO ASC_KMAX.
  SET asc["abort"] TO "CONT".
  IF ASC_CONT_DUMP_EMPTY { asc_oms_empty(met). }   // the full dump for an ECAL (to empty)
  ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 0 AND ASC_TAL_DUMP > 0 {
    SET asc["oms_dump"] TO ASC_TAL_DUMP.
    SET asc["oms_t0"] TO met + ASC_TAL_OMS_DELAY.
    SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
  }
  asc_oms_now(met).                        // the dump with the yaw, the pitch and the roll
  IF ascDap["on"] { SET ascDap["roll1"] TO TRUE. }
  LOCAL col IS "GREEN".
  IF cn["site"] = "NONE" { SET col TO "BLUE". }
  SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO col.                  // the 2EO line's lock: the contingency flown
  LOCAL yt IS "".
  IF cn["yaw"] < 0 { SET yt TO ", YAW " + ABS(asc_cnt_psi(cn["yaw"])) + " RIGHT". }   // 45 or 20
  IF cn["yaw"] > 0 { SET yt TO ", YAW " + ABS(asc_cnt_psi(cn["yaw"])) + " LEFT". }
  asc_event(asc, "2EO CONT MODE " + cn["sel"] + " " + col + " (" + cn["site"] + yt + "): " + cn["ph"]:TOUPPER).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt,start," + met + "," + cn["sel"] + "," + cn["site"] + "," + cn["ph"] TO asc["log"]. }
}

// the VI (m/s) from which the pages' 2EO line opens a mode (the lowest of the 2EO PRESS / ATO / TAL marks, the droop's
// floor in them: asc_ard_apply); off the scale while none is known. The live sweep's ASC_BGL_V2.
FUNCTION asc_2eo_vmin {
  LOCAL vm IS ASC_ARD_NEVER.
  FOR k IN LIST("TAL_2EO", "ATO_2EO", "PRESS_2EO") {
    IF asc["abr"]["b"]:HASKEY(k) OR adBnd:HASKEY(k) { SET vm TO MIN(vm, adB(asc, k) * AD_FT). }
  }
  RETURN vm.
}

// the pages' 2EO line (lib_ascdisp's adModes: the abort marks' predictor's, else the sidecar's) at vi (m/s); ""
// when a mark is unknown (the pages off before the sidecar loaded)
FUNCTION asc_2eo_line {
  PARAMETER vi.
  FOR k IN AD_TICKS { IF NOT (asc["abr"]["b"]:HASKEY(k) OR adBnd:HASKEY(k)) { RETURN "". } }
  RETURN adModes(asc, vi / ASC_FT)[1].
}

// the mode the 2EO line opens, best first (PRESS, ATO, TAL), flown on one SSME by PEG at the abort throttle: PRESS
// = PEG on to its target; ATO = the ATO abort (asc_abort) unless one is selected; TAL = the TAL abort, also over an ATO
// selected before (no longer open); a TAL selected before stays (open wherever the ATO is). vk = the VI of the
// line (asc_cnt_arm: the first failure's for the pick's -2, else the second's): the TAL's site at that VI
FUNCTION asc_2eo_go {
  PARAMETER cn, two, met, vk IS -1, tk IS -1.   // tk the verdict's TAL site (its index)
  IF vk < 0 { SET vk TO cn["vi2"]. }
  LOCAL md IS "TAL".
  IF two = "PRESS" { SET md TO "PRESS". } ELSE IF two:CONTAINS("ATO") { SET md TO "ATO". }
  SET cn["two"] TO md.
  IF md <> "TAL" { asc_dtal_unhide("2EO " + md). }   // a 2EO's TAL is declared below (asc_tal_go: the plane change)
  LOCAL vt IS ROUND(cn["vi2"]).
  IF md = "ATO" AND asc["abort"] = "" { asc_abort("ATO"). }
  ELSE IF md = "TAL" AND (asc["abort"] = "" OR asc["abort"] = "ATO") {
    SET asc["abort"] TO "TAL".
    SET asc["tal_k"] TO asc_ard_tal_k(vk).   // the first site the ARD's 2EO marks open (else the first)
    IF tk >= 0 { SET asc["tal_k"] TO tk. }   // the verdict's
    asc_event(asc, "2EO ABORT TAL " + ASC_TAL[ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]]["name"]:TOUPPER + "  VI " + vt).
    asc_tal_go(met).
  }
  // a TAL flying when the second SSME went (selected before, so not re-declared above) takes the low-energy set now
  IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" AND asc_tal_low(ASC_TAL[ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]]) {
    LOCAL tl2 IS asc_tal_lex(ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]).
    IF asc["g"]:HASKEY("peg") { asc_peg_tal(asc["g"]["peg"], tl2). }
    asc_note(asc, "2EO TAL LOW ENERGY TARGETS  " + ROUND((tl2["RDMAG"] - ASC_R) / 1000) + " KM").
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#tallow," + met + "," + ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]] + "," + tl2["RDMAG"] + "," + tl2["GAMD"] + "," + tl2["VMIN"]
      + "," + tl2["CRMAX"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" AND ASC_TAL2_DUMP_EMPTY { asc_oms_empty(met). }   // a 2EO TAL's dump to empty
  asc_oms_now(met).                        // a 2EO's dump at once
  // on one SSME the DAP keeps the roll free unless roll1 -- the RCS then rolls to the attitude (the heads-up roll), as
  // in the contingency (asc_cnt_start)
  IF ascDap["on"] { SET ascDap["roll1"] TO TRUE. }
  SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO CHOOSE "PRESS" IF asc["abort"] = "" ELSE asc["abort"].   // the 2EO line's lock: the mode flown
  LOCAL ab IS asc["abort"].
  IF ab = "" { SET ab TO "PEG ON". }
  asc_note(asc, "2EO VI " + vt + ": " + md + " (" + ab + ")").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#2eo," + met + "," + two + "," + md + "," + asc["abort"] + "," + cn["vi2"] + "," + asc["t_eo1"] + "," + vk
    TO asc["log"]. }
}

// ---- THE ARD (lib/lib_ascent_ard.ks; the header): the search runs in the main loop's passes with the pages
// (asc_ard_work) from a snapshot after a PEG pass (asc_ard_snap), starts again at stage 2, at each SSME out and each
// selection (asc_ard_reset), and puts its marks on the pages' each pass (asc_ard_apply)

// the 1EO line at vi (m/s) as the pages show it ("" while a mark is unknown): asc_fail keeps the first failure's
FUNCTION asc_1eo_line {
  PARAMETER vi.
  FOR k IN AD_TICKS { IF NOT (asc["abr"]["b"]:HASKEY(k) OR adBnd:HASKEY(k)) { RETURN "". } }
  RETURN adModes(asc, vi / ASC_FT)[0].
}

// a new start on the SSMEs running and the selection (off before stage 2, after MECO, below two SSMEs, in an RTLS or
// the contingency: the marks kept)
FUNCTION asc_ard_reset {
  LOCAL sel IS asc["abort"].
  LOCAL site IS "".
  IF sel = "TAL" { SET site TO ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]. }
  LOCAL n IS asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
  IF NOT asc["s2_on"] OR asc["t_meco"] >= 0 { SET n TO 0. }
  LOCAL tls IS LEXICON().
  FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES { SET tls[st] TO asc_tal_lex(st). }
  asc_live_cs_drop("reset").              // the in-flight C# refresh dropped
  SET asc["ardcs_n"] TO 0.
  ard_srch_reset(asc["ard"], n, sel, site, tls).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardr," + asc_met() + "," + n + "," + sel + "," + site + "," + asc["ard"]["ph"] + ard_srch_line(asc["ard"])
    TO asc["log"]. }
}

// the snapshot after a PEG pass when the search waits for one (PEG converged, before the fine count): the path's
// flight from now (the selected mode on the SSMEs running at K_CMD; the OMS dump's schedule: waiting, burning (its
// rest) or done), the SSMEs' thrust and exhaust speed now, the tables' marks as the seeds
FUNCTION asc_ard_snap {
  PARAMETER g, met, sm.
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  IF S["ph"] <> 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL p IS g["peg"].
  IF g["S_MECO"] OR NOT p["SCONV"] { RETURN. }
  LOCAL n IS asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
  IF n <> S["nrun"] { asc_ard_reset(). RETURN. }
  LOCAL fs IS asc_thrust(asc["ssme"]).
  IF fs[0] <= 0 OR fs[1] <= 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL et IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]).
  LOCAL o IS LIST().
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET o TO LIST(asc["oms_t0"], asc["oms_t0"] + asc_oms_left() / ASC_ARD_MDO). }
  ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { SET o TO LIST(met - 1, met + asc_oms_left() / ASC_ARD_MDO). }
  ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 3 { SET o TO LIST(met - 2, met - 1). }
  LOCAL md IS "PRESS".
  LOCAL tl IS LEXICON().
  IF S["sel"] = "ATO" { SET md TO "ATO". }
  IF S["sel"] = "TAL" { SET md TO "TAL". SET tl TO asc_tal_lex(S["site"]). }
  LOCAL sna IS LEXICON("md", md, "tl", tl, "e", n, "K", g["K_CMD"], "t", met, "r", sm[1], "v", sm[2], "et", et,
    "mc", SHIP:MASS - et, "res", ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"], "iy", p["IYD"],
    "steer", LIST(p["lamc"], p["lamdc"], p["tlamc"]), "o", o, "m", LEXICON("f1", fs[0] / n, "vex", fs[1]),
    "rs", asc_ard_rs(), "sh", asc_ard_sh()).
  ard_srch_go(S, sna, asc["abr"]["b"]:COPY).
  asc_live_cs_go(S, sna).                 // the refresh in C# when the addon can
}

// the pad's marks' shift with the vehicle's mass (asc_abr_sh's, as asc_ard_apply shows them) until the first
// refresh in flight replaces them: the ARD then seeds those seeks from the pad's VI + this shift (ard_lv_k0s)
FUNCTION asc_ard_sh {
  LOCAL sh IS LEXICON().
  IF asc["ardp"] = 3 AND asc["ard"]["nref"] = asc["ardp_nr"] AND NOT asc["s1l_la"] {   // a stage-1 refresh's: none
    FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] { IF NOT sh:HASKEY(x["dk"]) { SET sh[x["dk"]] TO asc_abr_sh(x["dk"]). } }
  }
  RETURN sh.
}

// the RTLS site in the PEG frame (asc_rtls_init's ef): the ARD's NEG RTN (its RTLS turnaround test)
FUNCTION asc_ard_rs {
  LOCAL st IS ASC_RTLS_SITE.
  RETURN (ASC_R + st["alt"]) * V(COS(st["lat"]) * COS(st["lng"]), COS(st["lat"]) * SIN(st["lng"]), SIN(st["lat"])).
}

// each pass with the pages: the search's marks into the pages' (after asc_abr_tick's tables); the droop's bound kept
// on the 2EO marks (none before the VI from which a 2EO holds the droop's floor, 67 km)
FUNCTION asc_ard_apply {
  IF NOT ASC_ARD_ON { RETURN. }
  LOCAL b IS asc["abr"]["b"].
  ard_apply_b(asc["ard"], b, asc_met(), SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG).   // the latch by VI
  // the pad's marks, shifted as the tables, only on a level still holding the pad's VI (asc["ardp_vb"], each
  // level's as the pad left it): the first refresh in flight re-solves its levels one by one from the vehicle's own
  // state, and shifting those again would sink PRESS under ATO (~775 / ~785 m/s from 1022 / 886) and freeze them
  // there at the SSME out
  IF asc["ardp"] = 3 AND asc["ard"]["nref"] = asc["ardp_nr"] AND NOT asc["s1l_la"] {   // a stage-1 refresh's: none
    IF asc["phase"] = "PAD" OR NOT asc:HASKEY("ardp_vb") {
      LOCAL pv0 IS LEXICON().
      FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] { SET pv0[x["key"]] TO x["vb"]. }
      SET asc["ardp_vb"] TO pv0.
    }
    LOCAL pv IS asc["ardp_vb"].
    LOCAL tal IS -1.
    FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] {
      IF x["vb"] >= 0 AND x["vb"] < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 {
        LOCAL vk IS x["vb"].
        IF pv:HASKEY(x["key"]) { IF pv[x["key"]] = vk { SET vk TO vk + asc_abr_sh(x["dk"]). } }
        IF x["dk"] = "TAL_2EO" { IF tal < 0 OR vk < tal { SET tal TO vk. } }
        ELSE { SET b[x["dk"]] TO vk. }
      }
    }
    IF tal >= 0 { SET b["TAL_2EO"] TO tal. }
  }
  LOCAL vb IS asc["drp"]["vi_b"].
  IF vb > 0 { FOR k IN LIST("TAL_2EO", "ATO_2EO", "PRESS_2EO") { IF b:HASKEY(k) { SET b[k] TO MAX(b[k], vb). } } }
}

// each pass with the pages (not a PEG pass's): the search's units, the first always, then while the tick has
// ASC_ARD_ROOM opcodes left, ASC_ARD_MAXU at most; off at the fine count or under ASC_ARD_TGO_OFF s of TGO; the log
FUNCTION asc_ard_work {
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  IF asc["phase"] = "PAD" { asc_ard_pad(). RETURN. }   // the pad search
  IF NOT asc["s2_on"] {                   // in stage 1 none (stage 2 starts the ARD); a pad search unfinished stops
    IF asc["ardp"] = 1 OR asc["ardp"] = 2 {
      asc_ard_pad_end(S, "NOT DONE").
      FOR apl IN asc["ardp_log"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG apl TO asc["log"]. } }
      asc["ardp_log"]:CLEAR().
    }
    asc_s1l_work().                       // the stage-1 refreshes in C#
    RETURN.
  }
  IF S["ph"] = 4 {                        // the verdict (its units, as the search's; MECO ends it)
    IF asc["g"]["S_MECO"] { ard_vd_end(S, "NONE", ""). }
    LOCAL nv IS 0.
    UNTIL nv >= ASC_ARD_MAXU OR S["ph"] <> 4 OR (nv > 0 AND OPCODESLEFT < ASC_ARD_ROOM) {
      ard_vd_unit(S).
      SET nv TO nv + 1.
    }
    FOR x IN S["msg"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardv," + asc_met() + "," + x TO asc["log"]. } }
    S["msg"]:CLEAR().
    RETURN.
  }
  IF S["ph"] <> 1 AND S["ph"] <> 2 AND S["ph"] <> 5 { RETURN. }   // 5 the rank
  LOCAL g IS asc["g"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  IF g["S_MECO"] OR (g["peg"]["SCONV"] AND g["peg"]["TGO"] < ASC_ARD_TGO_OFF) {
    SET S["ph"] TO 3.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardo," + met + "," + g["peg"]["TGO"] + ard_srch_line(S) TO asc["log"]. }
    RETURN.
  }
  IF asc["ardcs"] = 1 { IF asc_live_cs_work(S) { RETURN. } }   // the C# on this refresh
  LOCAL nr IS S["nref"].
  LOCAL nu IS 0.
  UNTIL nu >= ASC_ARD_MAXU OR (S["ph"] <> 1 AND S["ph"] <> 2 AND S["ph"] <> 5) OR (nu > 0 AND OPCODESLEFT < ASC_ARD_ROOM) {
    ard_srch_unit(S).
    SET nu TO nu + 1.
  }
  FOR x IN S["msg"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardl," + met + "," + x TO asc["log"]. } }
  S["msg"]:CLEAR().
  IF S["nref"] > nr {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ard," + met + "," + S["nref"] + "," + S["nrun"] + "," + S["sel"] + "," + S["site"] + "," + S["t_ref"] + ","
      + S["u"] + "," + S["ok2"] + ard_srch_line(S) TO asc["log"]. }
  }
}

// THE PAD SEARCH: the abort boundaries are calculated live, first on the pad, then in flight for tuning; the tables are
// the seed and the backup. The count holds at T-30 until the pad search completes. After the E TAL search (its SRBs
// weighed; its frame: epoch now, a liftoff now; PEG's plane), the stage-1 predictor (lib_ascent_etl's ard_s1_*) flies
// the nominal to the SRB separation (+ its bias B: ard_et_sep), and the ARD's search (lib_ascent_ard: the path on three
// SSMEs, the levels for none selected: ATO, PRESS, NEG RTN, the 2EO TAL at each site, 2EO ATO, 2EO PRESS) runs from
// there, PEG cold (the steering along the horizontal speed, as E TAL's TAL flights), the I-loads' masses
// (asc_ard_apply shifts its marks with the tables' mass delta, as E TAL's), the tables' marks its seeds. Its marks are
// the pages' from then on, until the first refresh in flight (stage 2) replaces them (its MET boundaries seed those
// seeks); the BLUE / GREEN sweep runs on its path too (asc_bgl_work). Unfinished at liftoff: stopped (the tables'
// marks). ardp: 0 not begun, 1 the predictor, 2 the search, 3 done, 4 failed / stopped
GLOBAL ASC_ARD_PAD_ON IS TRUE.
GLOBAL ASC_ARD_PAD_MAXU IS 4.       // units a main-loop pass on the pad at most (the first always)
GLOBAL ASC_ARD_PAD_TMAX IS 600.     // s: the count holds at T-30 for the searches this long at most
GLOBAL ASC_PAD_SLICE IS 0.4.        // s of ticks a pad search's pass runs units while the count holds (0: by units)

// ---- THE PAD SEARCH IN C# (lib/lib_ascent_padcs.ks: why, the parts). With ASC_PAD_CS and the KAL/S addon's
// PADSEARCH, the pad's three searches -- E TAL, the ARD's pad search (its stage-1 predictor, path, levels, rank) and the
// BLUE / GREEN sweep -- are ONE addon job started with E TAL (asc_pad_cs_go, the ARD's pad state sampled then too), on
// worker threads (~10 ms instead of ~60 s of kOS): kOS waits (the count holds) and writes the results into asc["etl"],
// asc["ard"], asc["bgl"] and the sweep's globals (asc_pad_cs_apply), the same messages and log lines as its own
// searches, then the pad cache saves. Any addon failure (no addon, an older dll, a bad input, an error on its thread, no
// result within ASC_PAD_CS_TMAX s) and kOS's own searches run from their start, with an event line saying why
// (ASC_PAD_CS_ERR). Checked bit for bit against these libraries in kOS's VM (offline: 3 pad
// snapshots, every value of E TAL, the ARD and the sweep, kOS's write-back too).
GLOBAL ASC_PAD_CS IS TRUE.
GLOBAL ASC_PAD_CS_THREADS IS 0.     // the C#'s worker threads (0: the addon's choice, MIN(4, CPUs - 1))
GLOBAL ASC_PAD_CS_TMAX IS 30.       // s: no C# result by then (a hung thread): kOS's own searches
GLOBAL ASC_PAD_CS_ERR IS "".        // why kOS searched ("" the C# did, or not tried)

// ---- THE IN-FLIGHT REFRESHES IN C# (lib/lib_ascent_ardcs.ks: why, the parts). Each refresh asc_ard_snap
// starts (its snapshot after a PEG pass) goes whole to the pad search's own addon job, ADDONS:KALS:PADSEARCH, with the
// ready snapshot: the path, every level not latched, the rank, and the BLUE / GREEN sweep on the path (when no kOS sweep
// is running), on worker threads; kOS waits for it (no units of its own meanwhile) and writes the results in as its own
// units leave them, with their log lines (#ardl / #ard / #bgl) and #ardcs,done. Fallback on ANY failure (no addon, an
// older dll, a bad input, an error on its thread, no result in ASC_LIVE_CS_TMAX s): kOS's own units run that refresh
// from its start (ard_srch_go's job is untouched), the switch goes off for the flight, the event "ABORT REFRESH: KOS
// (why)" and #ardcs,kos. The event "ABORT REFRESH IN C#: x MS" once per start (stage 2, each SSME out and selection:
// asc_ard_reset). Checked bit for bit against lib_ascent_ard / lib_ascent_bgl in kOS's VM
// (offline). asc["ardcs"]: 0 none, 1 the C# on this refresh
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_LIVE_CS) { GLOBAL ASC_LIVE_CS IS TRUE. }
GLOBAL ASC_LIVE_CS_THREADS IS 0.    // the C#'s worker threads (0: the addon's choice, MIN(4, CPUs - 1))
GLOBAL ASC_LIVE_CS_TMAX IS 5.       // s: no C# result by then (a hung thread): kOS's own units
GLOBAL ASC_LIVE_CS_ERR IS "".       // why kOS refreshes ("" the C# does, or not tried)

// ---- THE STAGE-1 REFRESHES IN C#: the C# refreshes are cheap, so they run continuously in stage 1 too (the pad search's
// C# from the in-flight state). kOS refreshes nothing in stage 1 (the ARD starts at stage 2): without them the pages show
// the pad search's marks shifted with the vehicle's mass (asc_abr_sh, asc_etl_sh). Every ASC_S1LIVE_CS_DT s the pad
// search's own addon job, ADDONS:KALS:PADSEARCH, reruns that whole search from the state in flight: E TAL (until
// passed), the stage-1 predictor from now to the SRB separation (lib_ascent_etl's ard_et_s1 with the tower clear and the
// tail-off tangent the vehicle flies), the ARD's path, levels and rank from there, the BLUE / GREEN sweep on the path;
// with the vehicle's own masses (its core: SHIP:MASS less the ET's propellant and the SRBs, as the stage-2 refreshes
// take SHIP:MASS), so its marks go on the pages unshifted. kOS polls DONE and writes the results where the pad search's
// go (asc_pad_cs_apply's way: asc["etl"], asc["ard"], asc["bgl"], the sweep's globals), one log line a refresh (#s1l,done
// + the levels) and the sweep's #bgl. None after an SSME out, a selection or the split-S, nor once the phase leaves
// STAGE1 (a job then out is dropped). Fallback on ANY failure (no addon, an older dll, a bad input, an error on its
// thread, no result in ASC_S1LIVE_CS_TMAX s): no kOS search (stage 1 has none): the marks stay as they are (the pad's
// with their shift, or the last refresh's), the switch off for the flight, the event "STAGE 1 REFRESH: KOS (why)" and
// #s1l,kos. The event "STAGE 1 REFRESH IN C#: x MS" once. Checked bit
// for bit against lib_ascent_etl / _ard / _bgl in kOS's VM (offline)
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_S1LIVE_CS) { GLOBAL ASC_S1LIVE_CS IS TRUE. }
GLOBAL ASC_S1LIVE_CS_DT IS 2.       // s: a job starts this long after the last one's start at the soonest (none while one is out)
GLOBAL ASC_S1LIVE_CS_THREADS IS 0.  // the C#'s worker threads (0: the addon's choice, MIN(4, CPUs - 1))
GLOBAL ASC_S1LIVE_CS_TMAX IS 5.     // s: no C# result by then (a hung thread): the fallback
GLOBAL ASC_S1LIVE_CS_ERR IS "".     // why the stage-1 refreshes stopped ("" they did not)

// a pad search's pass is over: while the count holds at T-30 once ASC_PAD_SLICE s of ticks are spent (the pages
// refresh between the slices), else by units (maxu units, or the tick's room gone)
FUNCTION asc_pad_full {
  PARAMETER nu, maxu, t0.
  IF asc_pad_slicing() { RETURN TIME:SECONDS - t0 >= ASC_PAD_SLICE. }
  RETURN nu >= maxu OR OPCODESLEFT < ASC_ARD_ROOM.
}

FUNCTION asc_pad_slicing {
  IF ASC_PAD_SLICE <= 0 OR asc["phase"] <> "PAD" OR asc["cd"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN FALSE. }
  RETURN asc["cd"]["st"] = "HOLD".
}

FUNCTION asc_ard_pad {
  IF NOT (ASC_ARD_ON AND ASC_ARD_PAD_ON) OR asc["ardp"] >= 3 { RETURN. }
  IF asc["padcs"] = 1 { RETURN. }           // the C# is on it (asc_pad_cs_work)
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  IF asc["ardp"] = 0 {
    IF NOT SHIP:UNPACKED { RETURN. }
    IF ASC_ETAL_ON { IF asc["etl"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. } IF NOT asc["etl"]["done"] { RETURN. } }
    asc_srb_meas(TRUE).
    asc_core_meas(TRUE).
    LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
    LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc_frame_new(ut), ut).
    SET asc["ardp_t0"] TO ut.
    SET asc["ardp_iy"] TO asc_iyd(sm[1], ASC_TGT_INC, ASC_PLANE_DLNG).
    SET asc["ardp_s1"] TO ard_et_s1(LIST(0, sm[1], sm[2], ASC_S1P_SRB_CAP, asc["et_lo"]), -1,
      LEXICON("mc", ASC_S1P_MC + asc["core_dm"], "sdry", asc["srb_dry"], "ssmd", ASC_S1P_SSMD, "knom", ASC_K_STAGE1, "kabt", ASC_KMAX_ABORT,
        "dpsi", ASC_HDG_DELTA, "south", ASC_LAUNCH_DIR < 0)).
    SET asc["ardp"] TO 1.
    RETURN.
  }
  LOCAL nu IS 0.
  LOCAL t0 IS TIME:SECONDS.
  UNTIL asc["ardp"] >= 3 OR (nu > 0 AND asc_pad_full(nu, ASC_ARD_PAD_MAXU, t0)) {
    SET nu TO nu + 1.
    IF asc["ardp"] = 1 {
      IF ard_s1_step(asc["ardp_s1"]) {
        LOCAL sp IS ard_et_sep(asc["ardp_s1"]).
        LOCAL ru IS sp[1]:NORMALIZED.
        LOCAL hz IS (sp[2] - VDOT(sp[2], ru) * ru):NORMALIZED.
        LOCAL tls IS LEXICON().
        FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES { SET tls[st] TO asc_tal_lex(st). }
        ard_srch_reset(S, 3, "", "", tls).
        ard_srch_go(S, LEXICON("md", "PRESS", "tl", LEXICON(), "e", 3, "K", ASC_KMAX, "t", sp[0], "r", sp[1],
          "v", sp[2], "et", sp[3], "mc", ASC_ABR_MC + asc["core_dm"], "res", ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_lo"],
          "iy", asc["ardp_iy"],
          "steer", LIST(hz, V(0, 0, 0), sp[0]), "o", LIST(), "m", LEXICON("f1", ASC_S1P_F1, "vex", ASC_S1P_VEX),
          "rs", asc_ard_rs()), asc["abr"]["b"]:COPY).
        asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#ardp,sep," + ROUND(sp[0], 2) + "," + ROUND(sp[2]:MAG, 1) + "," + ROUND(sp[1]:MAG - ASC_R)).
        SET asc["ardp"] TO 2.
      }
    } ELSE {
      ard_srch_unit(S).
      IF S["ph"] = 0 { asc_ard_pad_end(S, ""). }
    }
  }
  FOR x IN S["msg"] { asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#ardl,pad," + x). }
  S["msg"]:CLEAR().
}

// the pad search over (S["ph"] 0: done with a refresh, else no path), or stopped (why: its log word); its log line
FUNCTION asc_ard_pad_end {
  PARAMETER S, why.
  LOCAL ts IS ROUND(TIME:SECONDS - asc["ardp_t0"]).
  IF why = "" AND S["nref"] > 0 {
    SET asc["ardp"] TO 3.
    SET asc["ardp_nr"] TO S["nref"].
    asc_note(asc, "PAD ABORT SEARCH COMPLETE IN " + ts + " S").
  } ELSE {
    IF why = "" { SET why TO "NO PATH". }
    SET asc["ardp"] TO 4.
    SET S["ph"] TO 3.
    SET S["lv"] TO LIST().
    IF why <> "NOT DONE" { asc_event(asc, "PAD ABORT SEARCH FAILED"). }
  }
  asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#ardp," + ts + "," + S["u"] + "," + S["nref"] + "," + S["pts"]:LENGTH + "," + why
    + ard_srch_line(S)).
}

// the countdown's hold reasons at T-30 (lib_ascent_cd's hold_x): the E TAL search, the ARD's pad search, the BLUE
// / GREEN sweep on its path; none without the pages (no search runs) or after ASC_ARD_PAD_TMAX s of holding (then the
// count resumes on the marks there are)
FUNCTION asc_pad_hold {
  LOCAL hx IS LIST().
  IF NOT asc["pg"] OR NOT ASC_ARD_ON OR asc["ardp_to"] { RETURN hx. }
  IF asc["ardp_h0"] < 0 { SET asc["ardp_h0"] TO TIME:SECONDS. }
  IF ASC_ETAL_ON { IF asc["etl"]:LENGTH = 0 { hx:ADD("TAL SEARCH"). } ELSE IF NOT asc["etl"]["done"] { hx:ADD("TAL SEARCH"). } }
  IF ASC_ARD_PAD_ON AND asc["ardp"] < 3 { hx:ADD("ABORT SEARCH"). }
  IF ASC_BGL_ON AND asc["bgl"]["ph"] = 1 { hx:ADD("BLUE/GREEN"). }
  IF hx:LENGTH > 0 AND TIME:SECONDS - asc["ardp_h0"] > ASC_ARD_PAD_TMAX {
    SET asc["ardp_to"] TO TRUE.
    asc_event(asc, "PAD SEARCH OVER " + ASC_ARD_PAD_TMAX + " S: RESUME COUNT").
    RETURN LIST().
  }
  RETURN hx.
}

// a table mark's shift with the vehicle's mass (m/s; asc_abr_tick's delta), as asc_etl_sh for E TAL
FUNCTION asc_abr_sh {
  PARAMETER k.
  LOCAL a IS asc["abr"].
  LOCAL tb IS ASC_ABR_SETS[a["k"]][3].
  IF tb:HASKEY(k) {
    LOCAL v1 IS asc_abr_lin(tb[k], a["d"]).
    LOCAL v0 IS asc_abr_lin(tb[k], 0).
    IF v1 < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 AND v0 < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 { RETURN v1 - v0. }
  }
  RETURN 0.
}

// THE LIVE BLUE / GREEN (lib/lib_ascent_bgl.ks): getting inside the footprint decides, and a false GREEN is better
// than a false BLUE. A sweep of the footprint over the ARD's path each time the search has a new one (in its levels'
// phase), the sweep before it finished first; one unit a pass when the tick has ASC_BGL_ROOM opcodes left (else after
// ASC_BGL_SKIP passes without: the ARD's own units come first); at its end its windows are ASC_ABR_CONT's 2EO list
// (the pages' BLUE / GREEN, the contingency's site) with their yaws; none once in the contingency
FUNCTION asc_bgl_work {
  IF NOT ASC_BGL_ON OR asc["abort"] = "CONT" { RETURN. }
  LOCAL bg IS asc["bgl"].
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  LOCAL sph IS S["ph"] = 2 OR (asc["phase"] = "PAD" AND S["ph"] = 0).   // on the pad also a finished search's path
  IF bg["ph"] = 0 AND sph AND S["t_ref"] <> bg["t_ref"] AND S["pts"]:LENGTH >= 2 {
    SET ASC_BGL_V2 TO asc_2eo_vmin().      // MODE SEL 0 scored as mode 1 below it (asc_cnt_pick)
    bgl_start(bg, S["pts"], S["t_ref"]).
  }
  IF bg["ph"] <> 1 { RETURN. }
  IF asc_pad_slicing() {                    // the count held: a slice of units
    LOCAL t0 IS TIME:SECONDS.
    LOCAL nu IS 0.
    UNTIL bg["ph"] <> 1 OR (nu > 0 AND TIME:SECONDS - t0 >= ASC_PAD_SLICE) {
      asc_bgl_one(bg).
      SET nu TO nu + 1.
    }
    RETURN.
  }
  IF OPCODESLEFT < ASC_BGL_ROOM AND bg["skip"] < ASC_BGL_SKIP { SET bg["skip"] TO bg["skip"] + 1. RETURN. }
  SET bg["skip"] TO 0.
  asc_bgl_one(bg).
}

// one unit of the sweep; at its end its log line
FUNCTION asc_bgl_one {
  PARAMETER bg.
  IF bgl_unit(bg) {
    LOCAL bgln IS "#bgl," + asc_met() + "," + bg["nsw"] + "," + bg["u"] + "," + bg["t_ref"] + "," + bg["pts"]:LENGTH
      + bgl_line().
    IF asc["log"] = "" { asc["ardp_log"]:ADD(bgln). } ELSE { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG bgln TO asc["log"]. } }   // on the pad, at liftoff
  }
}

// ---- THE PAD SEARCH CACHE (lib/lib_ascent_padc.ks: why, the file, the means)
// the inputs the searches read at run time: the pad (its site's I-loads follow from it), the SRBs as measured, the
// target box (lib_ascent_gui), the RTLS site, the TAL sites, the switches
FUNCTION padc_key {
  LOCAL gp IS SHIP:GEOPOSITION.
  RETURN LIST(ROUND(gp:LAT, 4), ROUND(gp:LNG, 4), ROUND(asc["srb_dry"], 4), ROUND(asc["core_dm"], 2),
    ROUND(asc["et_lo"], 2), ASC_TGT_INC, ASC_LAUNCH_DIR, ASC_PLANE_DLNG,
    ASC_HDG_DELTA, ASC_VDMAG, ASC_TGT_AP, ASC_GAMD, ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"], ASC_TAL_SITES:JOIN(" "), ASC_ETAL_ON,
    ASC_ARD_PAD_ON, ASC_BGL_ON):JOIN("|").
}

// the first pass on the pad (unpacked, before the searches start): the cached states for this key, TRUE on a hit
FUNCTION asc_padc_load {
  SET asc["padc"] TO 1.
  IF NOT ASC_PADC_ON { RETURN FALSE. }
  asc_srb_meas(TRUE).                       // the key's SRBs (as E TAL's start weighs them)
  asc_core_meas(TRUE).                      // and its core
  SET asc["padc_key"] TO padc_key().
  LOCAL why IS "".
  LOCAL C IS LEXICON().
  IF NOT EXISTS(ASC_PADC_FILE) { SET why TO "no file". }
  ELSE {
    SET C TO READJSON(ASC_PADC_FILE).
    IF NOT C:HASKEY(asc["padc_key"]) { SET why TO "no key". }
    ELSE IF NOT padc_same() { SET why TO "code changed". }
  }
  IF why <> "" {
    asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padc,miss," + why + "," + asc["padc_key"]).
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  LOCAL e IS C[asc["padc_key"]].
  SET asc["etl"] TO padc_dec(e["etl"]).
  SET asc["ard"] TO padc_dec(e["ard"]).
  SET asc["bgl"] TO padc_dec(e["bgl"]).
  IF asc["ard"]["pj"]:HASKEY("pts") { SET asc["ard"]["pts"] TO asc["ard"]["pj"]["pts"]. }   // one list, as the search left it
  IF asc["bgl"]["t_ref"] = asc["ard"]["t_ref"] { SET asc["bgl"]["pts"] TO asc["ard"]["pts"]. }
  LOCAL g IS padc_dec(e["g"]).
  SET ASC_ABR_CONT[0] TO g["cont0"].
  SET ASC_BGL_YAW TO g["yaw"].
  SET ASC_BGL_EARLY TO g["early"].
  SET ASC_BGL_MD TO g["md"].
  SET ASC_BGL_V2 TO g["v2"].
  SET asc["ardp"] TO e["ardp"].
  SET asc["ardp_nr"] TO e["ardp_nr"].
  FOR x IN e["log"] { asc["ardp_log"]:ADD(x). }
  asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padc,hit," + asc["padc_key"]).
  SET asc["padc"] TO 2.
  asc_note(asc, "TAL " + asc_etl_txt(asc["etl"])).
  asc_event(asc, "PAD SEARCH LOADED FROM CACHE").
  RETURN TRUE.
}

// once all three are done on the pad after a miss: the states under the key (a changed code: the file starts over)
FUNCTION asc_padc_save {
  SET asc["padc"] TO 3.
  IF NOT ASC_PADC_ON { RETURN. }
  IF asc["padc_key"] = "" { SET asc["padc_key"] TO padc_key(). }
  SET padc_bad TO "".
  LOCAL lg IS LIST().
  FOR x IN asc["ardp_log"] { IF NOT x:STARTSWITH("#padc,") { lg:ADD(x). } }
  LOCAL e IS LEXICON("etl", padc_enc(asc["etl"]), "ard", padc_enc(asc["ard"]), "bgl", padc_enc(asc["bgl"]),
    "g", padc_enc(LEXICON("cont0", ASC_ABR_CONT[0], "yaw", ASC_BGL_YAW, "early", ASC_BGL_EARLY, "md", ASC_BGL_MD,
      "v2", ASC_BGL_V2)), "ardp", asc["ardp"], "ardp_nr", asc["ardp_nr"], "log", lg).
  IF padc_bad <> "" {
    asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padc,skip," + padc_bad).
    RETURN.
  }
  LOCAL C IS LEXICON().
  IF EXISTS(ASC_PADC_FILE) AND padc_same() { SET C TO READJSON(ASC_PADC_FILE). }
  ELSE {
    IF NOT EXISTS(ASC_PADC_DIR) { CREATEDIR(ASC_PADC_DIR). }
    FOR f IN ASC_PADC_SRC {
      IF EXISTS(padc_copy_of(f)) { DELETEPATH(padc_copy_of(f)). }
      COPYPATH("0:/" + f, padc_copy_of(f)).
    }
  }
  IF C:HASKEY(asc["padc_key"]) { C:REMOVE(asc["padc_key"]). }
  UNTIL C:LENGTH < ASC_PADC_MAXN { C:REMOVE(C:KEYS[0]). }
  SET C[asc["padc_key"]] TO e.
  WRITEJSON(C, ASC_PADC_FILE).
  asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padc,save," + C:LENGTH + "," + asc["padc_key"]).
}

// each pass with the pages, ON THE PAD ONLY: the first unpacked pass tries the file; after a miss the save once E TAL,
// the ARD's pad search and the sweep are all done (a failed or unfinished one: no save)
FUNCTION asc_padc_work {
  IF NOT ASC_PADC_ON OR asc["phase"] <> "PAD" OR NOT ASC_ARD_ON { RETURN. }
  IF asc["padc"] = 0 {
    IF SHIP:UNPACKED AND asc["etl"]:LENGTH = 0 AND asc["ardp"] = 0 { asc_padc_load(). }
    RETURN.
  }
  IF asc["padc"] <> 1 { RETURN. }
  IF ASC_ETAL_ON { IF asc["etl"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. } IF NOT asc["etl"]["done"] { RETURN. } }
  IF ASC_ARD_PAD_ON AND asc["ardp"] <> 3 { RETURN. }
  IF ASC_BGL_ON { IF asc["bgl"]["ph"] <> 0 OR NOT asc["bgl"]["live"] { RETURN. } }
  asc_padc_save().
}

// ---- THE SRBs MEASURED live: one SRB's mass less its own SolidFuel, from the vessel on the pad, for the E TAL search
// and the stage-1 marks, so a lighter case (the FWC: B9PartSwitch's "Motor case", 3.25 t) flies as it is. Per solid
// motor (asc_srbs' throttle-locked engines with SolidFuel of their own: the SRBs and their noses' separation motors, not
// the pad's tail service masts) the decoupler it hangs from; under each such decoupler every part, itself included
// (what separates with that SRB: in all 14 craft the decoupler, the SRB, its nose), their MASS (kOS: the part's
// rigidbody, 0 on a packed vessel; a physicsless part's mass is in its parent's) less the biggest SolidFuel there (the
// SRB's own, which the predictor flies from ASC_S1P_SRB_CAP; the nose's stays in, as in the offline stack's 21.83 t);
// the mean over the SRBs.
GLOBAL ASC_SRB_DBAND IS 0.01.   // t: measured within this of ASC_S1P_SDRY = the I-load itself (steel: the I-load exactly)

FUNCTION asc_is_dec {                       // a part that decouples (a radial or a stack decoupler)
  PARAMETER pt.
  RETURN pt:MODULES:CONTAINS("ModuleAnchoredDecoupler") OR pt:MODULES:CONTAINS("ModuleDecouple").
}

// the vessel's side: per decoupler that a solid motor of engs hangs from, LIST(its MASS, LIST(LIST(MASS, SolidFuel t)
// of every part under it, itself included))
FUNCTION asc_srb_rows {
  PARAMETER engs.
  LOCAL dcs IS LEXICON().
  FOR en IN engs {
    LOCAL sol IS FALSE.
    FOR rs IN en:RESOURCES { IF rs:NAME = "SolidFuel" AND rs:CAPACITY > 0 { SET sol TO TRUE. } }
    IF sol {
      LOCAL pt IS en.
      UNTIL asc_is_dec(pt) OR NOT pt:HASPARENT { SET pt TO pt:PARENT. }
      IF asc_is_dec(pt) AND NOT dcs:HASKEY(pt:UID) { SET dcs[pt:UID] TO pt. }
    }
  }
  LOCAL rows IS LIST().
  FOR k IN dcs:KEYS {
    LOCAL ps IS LIST().
    LOCAL stk IS LIST(dcs[k]).
    UNTIL stk:LENGTH = 0 {
      LOCAL pt IS stk[stk:LENGTH - 1].
      stk:REMOVE(stk:LENGTH - 1).
      LOCAL sfm IS 0.
      FOR rs IN pt:RESOURCES { IF rs:NAME = "SolidFuel" { SET sfm TO sfm + rs:AMOUNT * rs:DENSITY. } }
      ps:ADD(LIST(pt:MASS, sfm)).
      FOR ch IN pt:CHILDREN { stk:ADD(ch). }
    }
    rows:ADD(LIST(dcs[k]:MASS, ps)).
  }
  RETURN rows.
}

// one SRB's dry mass (t) from asc_srb_rows' rows: per decoupler the MASS under it less the biggest SolidFuel there,
// the mean; -1 unless exactly ASC_S1P_NSRB decouplers, each with a mass of its own (a physicsless one's sits in the
// tank's, outside) and more mass under it than SolidFuel (a packed vessel's parts read 0)
FUNCTION asc_srb_dry_of {
  PARAMETER rows.
  IF rows:LENGTH <> ASC_S1P_NSRB { RETURN -1. }
  LOCAL tot IS 0.
  FOR rw IN rows {
    IF rw[0] <= 0 { RETURN -1. }
    LOCAL mm IS 0.
    LOCAL sfm IS 0.
    FOR pq IN rw[1] {
      SET mm TO mm + pq[0].
      SET sfm TO MAX(sfm, pq[1]).
    }
    IF mm <= sfm { RETURN -1. }
    SET tot TO tot + mm - sfm.
  }
  RETURN tot / rows:LENGTH.
}

// asc["srb_dry"] / asc["srb_dd"], once: each pass with the pages until then (first in the pass, before asc_abr_tick),
// measured with the vessel unpacked; still unmeasured when last (the E TAL's set-up, or off the pad: before MET 1 s,
// the stage-1 delta's): the I-load from then on. The pad message.
FUNCTION asc_srb_meas {
  PARAMETER last.
  IF asc["srb_dry"] > 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL sd IS -1.
  IF SHIP:UNPACKED { SET sd TO asc_srb_dry_of(asc_srb_rows(asc_srbs())). }
  IF sd > 0 {
    IF ABS(sd - ASC_S1P_SDRY) <= ASC_SRB_DBAND { SET sd TO ASC_S1P_SDRY. }
    SET asc["srb_dry"] TO sd.
    SET asc["srb_dd"] TO ASC_S1P_NSRB * (sd - ASC_S1P_SDRY).
    asc_note(asc, "SRBS: " + ROUND(sd, 2) + " T DRY EACH").
  } ELSE IF last {
    SET asc["srb_dry"] TO ASC_S1P_SDRY.
    asc_note(asc, "SRBS: " + ROUND(ASC_S1P_SDRY, 2) + " T DRY EACH (I-LOAD)").
  }
}

// ---- THE CORE MEASURED on the pad, as the SRBs are: with the I-load's stack (ASC_S1P_MC, the ET full at liftoff) the
// pad searches flew a vehicle 4-7 t heavier than the craft flown -> late pad ticks. The core (the stack less the ET's
// propellant after the SRB sep: stage 2's MASS_MIN) from the launch box's weighing (lib_ascent_gui's asc_gui_orb: the
// parts, the pad and the SRBs left out; PEG's MASS_MIN at the sep within 0.01 t on five flights) and the ET's
// propellant at liftoff: on the pad less what the SSMEs burn in the countdown before liftoff (ASC_AST_PRE_B0; the
// I-load's stack burned none). Weighed once, before main engine start, as asc_srb_meas; still unweighed when last:
// the I-loads. asc["core_dm"] t over ASC_S1P_MC (0 within the dead band), asc["et_lo"] t.
GLOBAL ASC_CORE_DBAND IS 0.1.   // t: within this of ASC_S1P_MC = the I-load itself
GLOBAL ASC_CORE_DMAX IS 15.     // t: a core further off than this is a misread (the I-loads)

FUNCTION asc_core_meas {
  PARAMETER last.
  IF asc["core_ok"] { RETURN. }
  LOCAL ob IS LIST(-1).
  IF SHIP:UNPACKED AND asc["phase"] = "PAD" AND asc_liquids():LENGTH = 0 {
    SET ob TO asc_gui_orb(SHIP:PARTS, SHIP:ENGINES, SHIP:MASS, TRUE).
  }
  LOCAL pb IS 0.                            // the countdown's burn before liftoff (none without the countdown)
  IF ASC_CD_ON { SET pb TO ASC_AST_PRE_B0. }
  IF asc["cd"]:LENGTH > 0 { IF asc["cd"]["st"] = "OFF" { SET pb TO 0. } }
  IF ob:LENGTH >= 4 {
    LOCAL dm IS ob[2] - ob[3] - ASC_S1P_MC.
    IF ob[3] > pb AND ABS(dm) <= ASC_CORE_DMAX {
      IF ABS(dm) <= ASC_CORE_DBAND { SET dm TO 0. }
      SET asc["core_dm"] TO dm.
      SET asc["et_lo"] TO ob[3] - pb.
      SET asc["core_ok"] TO TRUE.
      asc_note(asc, "CORE: " + (CHOOSE "+" IF dm >= 0 ELSE "") + ROUND(dm, 2) + " T OVER THE I-LOAD; ET "
        + ROUND(asc["et_lo"], 1) + " T AT LIFTOFF").
      asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#core,meas," + ROUND(ob[2] - ob[3], 4) + "," + ROUND(dm, 4) + "," + ROUND(ob[3], 4) + "," + pb).
      RETURN.
    }
  }
  IF last {
    SET asc["core_dm"] TO 0.
    SET asc["et_lo"] TO ASC_S1P_ET.
    SET asc["core_ok"] TO TRUE.
    asc_note(asc, "CORE: " + ROUND(ASC_S1P_MC, 2) + " T (I-LOAD)").
    LOCAL mc IS -1.
    IF ob:LENGTH >= 4 { SET mc TO ROUND(ob[2] - ob[3], 4). }
    asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#core,iload," + ob:LENGTH + "," + mc).
  }
}

// ---- E TAL LIVE (lib/lib_ascent_etl.ks): E TAL computed on the pad, not read from the tables: the search from the pad
// state in a frame of its own (its epoch = now: the sites turn from it as for a liftoff now, the same geometry as any
// later liftoff), the stack's I-loads (ASC_S1P_*: the masses its bias B is calibrated on) but the SRBs, the core and the
// ET at liftoff as measured (asc_srb_meas, asc_core_meas; B stays as calibrated, with steel SRBs), PEG's plane (as
// asc_pad's), stage 1's heading (asc_s1_att's: the target box's ASC_HDG_DELTA, mirrored for a southbound launch), the
// TAL sites, the throttles
FUNCTION asc_etl_new {
  asc_srb_meas(TRUE).                       // the SRBs as measured (unmeasured by now: the I-load)
  asc_core_meas(TRUE).                      // the core and the ET at liftoff as weighed (unweighed by now: the I-loads)
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc_frame_new(ut), ut).
  LOCAL tls IS LEXICON().
  FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES { SET tls[st] TO asc_tal_lex(st). }
  LOCAL ej IS ard_et_new(LIST(0, sm[1], sm[2], ASC_S1P_SRB_CAP, asc["et_lo"]),
    LEXICON("mc", ASC_S1P_MC + asc["core_dm"], "sdry", asc["srb_dry"], "ssmd", ASC_S1P_SSMD, "knom", ASC_K_STAGE1, "kabt", ASC_KMAX_ABORT,
      "dpsi", ASC_HDG_DELTA, "south", ASC_LAUNCH_DIR < 0),
    LEXICON("mc", ASC_S1P_MC + asc["core_dm"], "res", ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_lo"],
      "m", LEXICON("f1", ASC_S1P_F1, "vex", ASC_S1P_VEX)),
    tls, asc_iyd(sm[1], ASC_TGT_INC, ASC_PLANE_DLNG)).
  IF asc["abr"]["b"]:HASKEY("E_TAL") {      // the tables' mark (m/s, delta 0 on the pad) seeds the search
    IF asc["abr"]["b"]["E_TAL"] < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 { SET ej["sv"] TO asc["abr"]["b"]["E_TAL"]. }
  }
  IF tls:LENGTH = 0 {                       // no TAL site (all NO WX in the target box): done at once, never
    SET ej["etal"] TO ASC_ARD_NEVER.
    SET ej["vi"] TO ASC_ARD_NEVER.
    SET ej["done"] TO TRUE.
  }
  RETURN ej.
}

// E TAL as the messages show it: the VI (m/s) and the SSME-out time
FUNCTION asc_etl_txt {
  PARAMETER ej.
  IF ej["vi"] >= ASC_ARD_NEVER { RETURN "NONE". }
  RETURN ROUND(ej["vi"]) + " M/S (" + ROUND(ej["etal"], 1) + " S)".
}

// each pass with the pages: the search's units ON THE PAD ONLY (the first always, then while the tick has ASC_ARD_ROOM
// opcodes left, ASC_ETAL_MAXU at most; none in flight: the stage-1 loop keeps its rate, and unfinished at liftoff the
// tables' mark stays); once done two messages; its line in the PEG log once that exists (liftoff), in every case
// (asc_etl_log: the result, NOT DONE or NOT STARTED)
FUNCTION asc_etl_work {
  IF NOT (ASC_ARD_ON AND ASC_ETAL_ON) { RETURN. }
  LOCAL ph IS asc["phase"].
  IF asc["etl"]:LENGTH = 0 {
    IF ph = "PAD" AND SHIP:UNPACKED {                                     // unpacked: the SRBs weighed first
      SET asc["etl_t0"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
      SET asc["etl"] TO asc_etl_new().
      asc_pad_cs_go().                      // the three pad searches in C#, when the addon can
    }
    ELSE IF ph <> "PAD" { asc_etl_log(asc["etl"]). }                      // never begun: NOT STARTED
    RETURN.
  }
  asc_pad_cs_work().                        // the C#'s results in (or kOS's fallback)
  LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
  IF NOT ej["done"] {
    IF ph <> "PAD" { asc_etl_log(ej). RETURN. }                            // unfinished at liftoff: NOT DONE
    IF asc["padcs"] = 1 { RETURN. }         // the C# is on it
    LOCAL nu IS 0.
    LOCAL t0 IS TIME:SECONDS.
    UNTIL ej["done"] OR (nu > 0 AND asc_pad_full(nu, ASC_ETAL_MAXU, t0)) {
      ard_et_unit(ej).
      SET nu TO nu + 1.
    }
    IF ej["done"] {
      asc_note(asc, "TAL " + asc_etl_txt(ej)).   // "TAL", not "E TAL", as the other pad messages
      // the search's end, noted after the result so that it shows on top of the MESSAGES (newest first)
      asc_note(asc, "PAD TAL SEARCH COMPLETE IN " + ROUND(TIME:SECONDS - asc["etl_t0"]) + " S").
    }
  }
  IF ej["done"] { asc_etl_log(ej). }
}

// ---- THE ABORT REFRESH IN C# (ASC_LIVE_CS): its side here (the block above ASC_LIVE_CS; lib_ascent_ardcs: the input,
// the write-back) with ard_srch_go (asc_ard_snap): the job (sna: the snapshot), or why kOS refreshes
FUNCTION asc_live_cs_go {
  PARAMETER S, sna.
  SET asc["ardcs"] TO 0.
  IF NOT ASC_LIVE_CS OR S["ph"] <> 1 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL why IS padcs_why().
  IF why <> "" { asc_live_cs_kos(why). RETURN. }
  LOCAL inp IS LEXICON("c", 0, "threads", ASC_LIVE_CS_THREADS, "ard", ardcs_in(S, sna, S["seed"])).
  LOCAL bg IS asc["bgl"].
  SET asc["ardcs_bgl"] TO FALSE.
  IF ASC_BGL_ON AND asc["abort"] <> "CONT" AND bg["ph"] = 0 AND S["t_ref"] <> bg["t_ref"] {
    SET ASC_BGL_V2 TO asc_2eo_vmin().     // as asc_bgl_work at its sweep's start
    SET inp["bgl"] TO TRUE.
    SET asc["ardcs_bgl"] TO TRUE.
  }
  SET inp["c"] TO padcs_consts().
  LOCAL h IS ADDONS:KALS:PADSEARCH(inp).
  IF h:DONE AND h:ERROR <> "" { asc_live_cs_kos("PADSEARCH: " + h:ERROR). RETURN. }
  SET asc["ardcs_h"] TO h.
  SET asc["ardcs_t0"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  SET asc["ardcs_t"] TO S["t_ref"].
  SET asc["ardcs_l0"] TO ardcs_lat(S).
  SET asc["ardcs"] TO 1.
  IF asc["ardcs_n"] = 0 {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardcs,go," + asc_met() + "," + ASC_LIVE_CS + "," + h:THREADS + "," + inp:HASKEY("bgl")
      TO asc["log"]. }
  }
}

FUNCTION asc_live_cs_kos {                  // kOS's own refreshes from here, for the flight (why: the event's)
  PARAMETER why.
  SET ASC_LIVE_CS_ERR TO why.
  SET ASC_LIVE_CS TO FALSE.
  SET asc["ardcs"] TO 0.
  asc_event(asc, "ABORT REFRESH: KOS (" + why + ")").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardcs,kos," + asc_met() + "," + why TO asc["log"]. }
}

FUNCTION asc_live_cs_drop {                 // the job's result unwanted (a new start, the phase moved on): its thread ends alone
  PARAMETER why.
  IF asc["ardcs"] > 0 { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardcs,drop," + asc_met() + "," + why TO asc["log"]. } }
  SET asc["ardcs"] TO 0.
}

// each pass of asc_ard_work on a refresh (its phases 1, 2, 5): TRUE while the C# is on it (kOS runs no units), its result in
// when done; FALSE: kOS's own units (none running, or the fallback: from the refresh's start)
FUNCTION asc_live_cs_work {
  PARAMETER S.
  IF asc["ardcs"] <> 1 { RETURN FALSE. }
  IF S["ph"] <> 1 OR S["t_ref"] <> asc["ardcs_t"] { asc_live_cs_drop("phase " + S["ph"]). RETURN FALSE. }
  LOCAL h IS asc["ardcs_h"].
  IF NOT h:DONE {
    IF TIME:SECONDS - asc["ardcs_t0"] > ASC_LIVE_CS_TMAX {
      asc_live_cs_kos("no result in " + ASC_LIVE_CS_TMAX + " s").
      RETURN FALSE.
    }
    RETURN TRUE.
  }
  IF h:ERROR <> "" { asc_live_cs_kos(h:ERROR). RETURN FALSE. }
  asc_live_cs_apply(S, h).
  RETURN TRUE.
}

// the result into S (ardcs_apply: padcs_apply_ard, the levels the pages latched meanwhile kept), the log lines as
// asc_ard_work's, the sweep (padcs_apply_bgl) and its line as asc_bgl_one's
FUNCTION asc_live_cs_apply {
  PARAMETER S, h.
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL nr IS S["nref"].
  LOCAL kp IS ardcs_apply(S, h:ARD, asc["ardcs_l0"]).
  SET asc["ardcs"] TO 0.
  FOR x IN S["msg"] { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardl," + met + "," + x TO asc["log"]. } }
  S["msg"]:CLEAR().
  IF S["nref"] > nr {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ard," + met + "," + S["nref"] + "," + S["nrun"] + "," + S["sel"] + "," + S["site"] + "," + S["t_ref"] + ","
      + S["u"] + "," + S["ok2"] + ard_srch_line(S) TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  LOCAL nb IS 0.
  IF asc["ardcs_bgl"] AND asc["bgl"]["ph"] = 0 AND h:BGL:HASKEY("gp") {
    LOCAL bg IS asc["bgl"].
    padcs_apply_bgl(bg, S["pts"], S["t_ref"], h:BGL).
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#bgl," + met + "," + bg["nsw"] + "," + bg["u"] + "," + bg["t_ref"] + "," + bg["pts"]:LENGTH + bgl_line()
      TO asc["log"]. }
    SET nb TO 1.
  }
  SET asc["ardcs_n"] TO asc["ardcs_n"] + 1.
  IF asc["ardcs_n"] = 1 { asc_note(asc, "ABORT REFRESH IN C#: " + ROUND(h:MS, 1) + " MS"). }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ardcs,done," + met + "," + ROUND(h:MS, 2) + "," + ROUND(h:MSARD, 2) + "," + ROUND(h:MSBGL, 2) + "," + h:THREADS
    + "," + nb + "," + kp + "," + ROUND(TIME:SECONDS - asc["ardcs_t0"], 2) TO asc["log"]. }
}

// ---- THE STAGE-1 REFRESHES IN C# (ASC_S1LIVE_CS): their side here (the block above ASC_S1LIVE_CS; lib_ascent_padcs:
// the constants, the ARD's input, the write-back)
// each pass with the pages before stage 2 (asc_ard_work): a job's result in (or its drop, or the fallback), the next job
FUNCTION asc_s1l_work {
  IF asc["s1l"] = 9 { RETURN. }
  IF NOT ASC_S1LIVE_CS OR NOT (ASC_ARD_ON AND ASC_ARD_PAD_ON) {
    asc_s1l_drop("off").
    SET asc["s1l"] TO 9.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1l,off," + asc_met() TO asc["log"]. }
    RETURN.
  }
  LOCAL why IS asc_s1l_cond().
  IF asc["s1l"] = 1 {
    IF why <> "" { asc_s1l_drop(why). }
    ELSE {
      LOCAL h IS asc["s1l_h"].
      IF NOT h:DONE {
        IF TIME:SECONDS - asc["s1l_t0"] > ASC_S1LIVE_CS_TMAX { asc_s1l_kos("no result in " + ASC_S1LIVE_CS_TMAX + " s"). }
        RETURN.
      }
      IF h:ERROR <> "" { asc_s1l_kos(h:ERROR). RETURN. }
      LOCAL rsl IS h:ARD.
      IF NOT rsl:HASKEY("s1po") { asc_s1l_kos("the KAL/S dll has no in-flight stage 1"). RETURN. }   // an older PadRun.cs
      SET asc["s1l"] TO 0.
      asc_s1l_apply(h, rsl).
      RETURN.                               // the next job on a later pass
    }
  }
  IF asc["phase"] <> "STAGE1" { SET asc["s1l"] TO 9. RETURN. }   // stage 1 over
  IF why <> "" OR TIME:SECONDS - asc["s1l_t0"] < ASC_S1LIVE_CS_DT { RETURN. }
  asc_s1l_go().
}

// "" when a stage-1 refresh may run (and its result go on the pages), else why not
FUNCTION asc_s1l_cond {
  IF asc["phase"] <> "STAGE1" { RETURN "phase " + asc["phase"]. }
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH <> 3 { RETURN "SSME out". }
  IF asc["abort"] <> "" { RETURN "abort " + asc["abort"]. }
  IF asc["s1c"]:LENGTH > 0 { RETURN "split-S". }
  IF asc["ardp"] < 3 { RETURN "pad search". }
  RETURN "".
}

// one SRB's SolidFuel (t; the predictor's sf): the mean over the SRBs lit (asc["srbs"]); -1 not ASC_S1P_NSRB of them
FUNCTION asc_s1l_srb {
  IF asc["srbs"]:LENGTH <> ASC_S1P_NSRB { RETURN -1. }
  LOCAL m IS 0.
  FOR en IN asc["srbs"] { FOR rs IN en:RESOURCES { IF rs:NAME = "SolidFuel" { SET m TO m + rs:AMOUNT * rs:DENSITY. } } }
  RETURN m / ASC_S1P_NSRB.
}

// a job from the state now (the vehicle's own masses), or why not (the fallback); as asc_pad_cs_go's pad start, but the
// state in flight: p0 = LIST(MET, r, v, SolidFuel, the ET's propellant, past the tower clear, the tail-off tangent)
FUNCTION asc_s1l_go {
  LOCAL why IS padcs_why().
  IF why <> "" { asc_s1l_kos(why). RETURN. }
  IF asc["srbs"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }     // not listed yet (asc_stage1's first pass, after this one): the next pass
  LOCAL srb IS asc_s1l_srb().
  IF srb < 0 { asc_s1l_kos(asc["srbs"]:LENGTH + " SRBS LIT"). RETURN. }
  IF srb <= 0 { RETURN. }                   // burnt out: the separation's next
  LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc["fr"], ut).
  LOCAL et IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]).
  LOCAL dm IS SHIP:MASS - et - ASC_S1P_NSRB * (asc["srb_dry"] + srb) - ASC_S1P_MC.   // the core over the I-load's (t)
  LOCAL po IS asc["s1"]["clear"] OR ard_s1_vrel(LIST(sm[1], sm[2])) >= ASC_PPOLY[1].
  LOCAL p0 IS LIST(met, sm[1], sm[2], srb, et, po, asc["s1"]["thetc_cns"]).
  LOCAL vh IS LEXICON("mc", ASC_S1P_MC + dm, "sdry", asc["srb_dry"], "ssmd", ASC_S1P_SSMD, "knom", ASC_K_STAGE1,
    "kabt", ASC_KMAX_ABORT, "dpsi", ASC_HDG_DELTA, "south", ASC_LAUNCH_DIR < 0).
  LOCAL res IS ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"].
  LOCAL mf IS LEXICON("f1", ASC_S1P_F1, "vex", ASC_S1P_VEX).
  LOCAL tls IS LEXICON().
  FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES { SET tls[st] TO asc_tal_lex(st). }
  LOCAL b IS asc["abr"]["b"].
  LOCAL inp IS LEXICON("c", 0, "threads", ASC_S1LIVE_CS_THREADS).
  IF ASC_ETAL_ON AND asc["etl"]:LENGTH > 0 AND NOT asc["s1l_etp"] AND tls:LENGTH > 0 {   // E TAL until passed
    LOCAL sv IS -1.                         // the pages' mark: the seed (asc_etl_new's)
    IF b:HASKEY("E_TAL") { IF b["E_TAL"] < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 { SET sv TO b["E_TAL"]. } }
    LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
    IF ej["done"] AND ej["vi"] < ASC_ARD_NEVER AND sv > 0 AND sm[2]:MAG >= sv { SET asc["s1l_etp"] TO TRUE. }   // the search's mark passed
    ELSE {
      SET inp["etl"] TO LEXICON("p0", p0, "vh", vh, "sn", LEXICON("mc", ASC_S1P_MC + dm, "res", res, "m", mf), "tls", tls,
        "iy", asc["iyd"], "sv", sv).
    }
  }
  LOCAL S0 IS ard_srch_new().
  ard_srch_reset(S0, 3, "", "", tls).
  LOCAL seed IS b:COPY.
  SET inp["ard"] TO padcs_in_ard(S0, p0, vh, LEXICON("md", "PRESS", "tl", LEXICON(), "e", 3, "K", ASC_KMAX,
    "mc", ASC_ABR_MC + dm, "res", res, "iy", asc["iyd"], "o", LIST(), "m", mf, "rs", asc_ard_rs()), seed).
  SET asc["s1l_bgl"] TO FALSE.
  IF ASC_BGL_ON AND asc["bgl"]["ph"] = 0 {
    SET ASC_BGL_V2 TO asc_2eo_vmin().       // as asc_bgl_work at its sweep's start
    SET inp["bgl"] TO TRUE.
    SET asc["s1l_bgl"] TO TRUE.
  }
  SET inp["c"] TO padcs_consts().
  LOCAL h IS ADDONS:KALS:PADSEARCH(inp).
  IF h:DONE AND h:ERROR <> "" { asc_s1l_kos("PADSEARCH: " + h:ERROR). RETURN. }
  SET asc["s1l_h"] TO h.
  SET asc["s1l_t0"] TO ut.
  SET asc["s1l_cx"] TO LEXICON("met", met, "tls", tls, "seed", seed, "mc", ASC_ABR_MC + dm, "res", res, "m", mf,
    "etl", inp:HASKEY("etl")).
  SET asc["s1l"] TO 1.
  SET asc["s1l_j"] TO asc["s1l_j"] + 1.
  IF asc["s1l_j"] = 1 {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1l,go," + met + "," + ASC_S1LIVE_CS + "," + h:THREADS + "," + inp:HASKEY("etl") + ","
      + inp:HASKEY("bgl") + "," + ROUND(dm, 3) + "," + po + "," + ROUND(srb, 3) TO asc["log"]. }
  }
}

FUNCTION asc_s1l_kos {                      // the stage-1 refreshes off for the flight, the marks as they are (why: the event's)
  PARAMETER why.
  SET ASC_S1LIVE_CS_ERR TO why.
  SET ASC_S1LIVE_CS TO FALSE.
  SET asc["s1l"] TO 9.
  asc_event(asc, "STAGE 1 REFRESH: KOS (" + why + ")").
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1l,kos," + asc_met() + "," + why TO asc["log"]. }
}

FUNCTION asc_s1l_drop {                     // the job's result unwanted (the phase moved on): its thread ends alone
  PARAMETER why.
  IF asc["s1l"] = 1 { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1l,drop," + asc_met() + "," + why TO asc["log"]. } }
  SET asc["s1l"] TO 0.
}

// the job's results where the pad search's go (asc_pad_cs_apply's way, without its pad messages), unshifted from now on;
// E TAL open at the state (a site's tb at or before its MET: ard_et_site would extrapolate the VI back to MET 0) = passed
// there (its MET, its VI), and no more E TAL in the jobs
FUNCTION asc_s1l_apply {
  PARAMETER h, rsl.
  LOCAL cx IS asc["s1l_cx"].
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  LOCAL etx IS "-".
  IF cx["etl"] {
    LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
    padcs_apply_etl(ej, h:ETL).
    IF ej["etal"] < ASC_ARD_NEVER AND ej["etal"] <= cx["met"] {
      FOR k IN ej["tb"]:KEYS { IF ej["tb"][k] <= cx["met"] { SET ej["tb"][k] TO ej["vt"][0]. } }
      SET ej["etal"] TO ej["vt"][0].
      SET ej["vi"] TO ej["vt"][1].
      SET asc["s1l_etp"] TO TRUE.
    }
    SET asc["st_et"] TO LEXICON().          // asc_site_etal's cache
    SET asc["s1l_le"] TO TRUE.
    SET etx TO ROUND(ej["etal"], 2) + ":" + ROUND(ej["vi"], 1).
  }
  IF rsl["nopath"] {                        // no path (no thrust): the levels as they are
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1l,nopath," + met + "," + cx["met"] TO asc["log"]. }
    RETURN.
  }
  SET asc["ard"] TO ard_srch_new().         // a new search, as the pad's (asc_pad_cs_apply)
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  LOCAL sp IS rsl["sp"].
  LOCAL ru IS sp[1]:NORMALIZED.
  LOCAL hz IS (sp[2] - VDOT(sp[2], ru) * ru):NORMALIZED.
  ard_srch_reset(S, 3, "", "", cx["tls"]).
  ard_srch_go(S, LEXICON("md", "PRESS", "tl", LEXICON(), "e", 3, "K", ASC_KMAX, "t", sp[0], "r", sp[1], "v", sp[2],
    "et", sp[3], "mc", cx["mc"], "res", cx["res"], "iy", asc["iyd"], "steer", LIST(hz, V(0, 0, 0), sp[0]), "o", LIST(),
    "m", cx["m"], "rs", asc_ard_rs()), cx["seed"]).
  padcs_apply_ard(S, rsl).
  S["msg"]:CLEAR().
  SET asc["ardp"] TO 3.
  SET asc["ardp_nr"] TO S["nref"].
  SET asc["s1l_la"] TO TRUE.
  LOCAL nb IS 0.
  IF asc["s1l_bgl"] AND asc["bgl"]["ph"] = 0 {
    LOCAL rb IS h:BGL.
    IF rb:HASKEY("gp") {
      LOCAL bg IS asc["bgl"].
      padcs_apply_bgl(bg, S["pts"], S["t_ref"], rb).
      IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#bgl," + met + "," + bg["nsw"] + "," + bg["u"] + "," + bg["t_ref"] + "," + bg["pts"]:LENGTH + bgl_line()
        TO asc["log"]. }
      SET nb TO 1.
    }
  }
  SET asc["s1l_n"] TO asc["s1l_n"] + 1.
  IF asc["s1l_n"] = 1 { asc_note(asc, "STAGE 1 REFRESH IN C#: " + ROUND(h:MS, 1) + " MS"). }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#s1l,done," + met + "," + cx["met"] + "," + ROUND(h:MS, 2) + "," + ROUND(h:MSETL, 2) + "," + ROUND(h:MSARD, 2) + ","
    + ROUND(h:MSBGL, 2) + "," + h:THREADS + "," + etx + "," + nb + "," + ROUND(TIME:SECONDS - asc["s1l_t0"], 2)
    + ard_srch_line(S) TO asc["log"]. }
}

// ---- THE PAD SEARCH IN C# (ASC_PAD_CS): its side here (lib_ascent_padcs: the constants, the inputs, the write-back).
// asc["padcs"]: 0 not started, 1 the C# running (kOS waits), 2 its results in, 3 kOS searches (off, no addon, a
// failure)
FUNCTION asc_pad_cs_go {                    // with E TAL's start (asc_etl_work): the job, or why kOS searches
  SET asc["padcs"] TO 3.
  IF NOT ASC_PAD_CS {
    asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padcs,off").
    RETURN.
  }
  LOCAL why IS padcs_why().
  IF why <> "" { asc_pad_cs_kos(why). RETURN. }
  LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
  LOCAL inp IS LEXICON("c", 0, "threads", ASC_PAD_CS_THREADS).
  IF NOT ej["done"] { SET inp["etl"] TO padcs_in_etl(ej). }
  IF ASC_ARD_PAD_ON AND asc["ardp"] = 0 {   // the ARD's pad start (asc_ard_pad's), in E TAL's job
    LOCAL ut IS TIME:SECONDS.
    LOCAL sm IS asc_sample(asc_frame_new(ut), ut).
    LOCAL iy IS asc_iyd(sm[1], ASC_TGT_INC, ASC_PLANE_DLNG).
    LOCAL tls IS LEXICON().
    FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES { SET tls[st] TO asc_tal_lex(st). }
    LOCAL S0 IS ard_srch_new().
    ard_srch_reset(S0, 3, "", "", tls).
    LOCAL seed IS asc["abr"]["b"]:COPY.
    SET inp["ard"] TO padcs_in_ard(S0, LIST(0, sm[1], sm[2], ASC_S1P_SRB_CAP, asc["et_lo"]),
      LEXICON("mc", ASC_S1P_MC + asc["core_dm"], "sdry", asc["srb_dry"], "ssmd", ASC_S1P_SSMD, "knom", ASC_K_STAGE1, "kabt", ASC_KMAX_ABORT,
        "dpsi", ASC_HDG_DELTA, "south", ASC_LAUNCH_DIR < 0),
      LEXICON("md", "PRESS", "tl", LEXICON(), "e", 3, "K", ASC_KMAX, "mc", ASC_ABR_MC + asc["core_dm"],
        "res", ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_lo"], "iy", iy, "o", LIST(), "m", LEXICON("f1", ASC_S1P_F1, "vex", ASC_S1P_VEX), "rs", asc_ard_rs()), seed).
    SET asc["padcs_ard"] TO LEXICON("ut", ut, "iy", iy, "tls", tls, "seed", seed).
    IF ASC_BGL_ON AND asc["abort"] <> "CONT" {
      SET ASC_BGL_V2 TO asc_2eo_vmin().     // as asc_bgl_work at its sweep's start (the tables' 2EO marks: no level in yet)
      SET inp["bgl"] TO TRUE.
    }
  }
  IF NOT (inp:HASKEY("etl") OR inp:HASKEY("ard")) { RETURN. }
  SET inp["c"] TO padcs_consts().
  LOCAL h IS ADDONS:KALS:PADSEARCH(inp).
  IF h:DONE AND h:ERROR <> "" { asc_pad_cs_kos("PADSEARCH: " + h:ERROR). RETURN. }
  SET asc["padcs_h"] TO h.
  SET asc["padcs_in"] TO inp.
  SET asc["padcs_t0"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  SET asc["padcs"] TO 1.
  asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padcs,go," + ASC_PAD_CS + "," + h:THREADS + "," + inp:HASKEY("etl") + ","
    + inp:HASKEY("ard") + "," + inp:HASKEY("bgl")).
}

FUNCTION asc_pad_cs_kos {                   // kOS's own searches from here (why: the event's)
  PARAMETER why.
  SET ASC_PAD_CS_ERR TO why.
  SET asc["padcs"] TO 3.
  asc_event(asc, "PAD SEARCH: KOS (" + why + ")").
  asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padcs,kos," + why).
}

// each pass (asc_etl_work's first): the job's result in, a failure's fallback
FUNCTION asc_pad_cs_work {
  LOCAL st IS asc["padcs"].
  IF st = 1 {
    LOCAL h IS asc["padcs_h"].
    IF NOT h:DONE {
      IF TIME:SECONDS - asc["padcs_t0"] > ASC_PAD_CS_TMAX { asc_pad_cs_kos("no result in " + ASC_PAD_CS_TMAX + " s"). }
      RETURN.
    }
    IF h:ERROR <> "" { asc_pad_cs_kos(h:ERROR). RETURN. }
    IF asc["phase"] <> "PAD" { asc_pad_cs_kos("lifted off before its result"). RETURN. }
    asc_pad_cs_apply(h).
  }
}

// the job's results into kOS's structures, as kOS's own searches leave them: E TAL (its two messages), the ARD's pad search
// (ard_srch_reset + ard_srch_go with the separation's snapshot, as asc_ard_pad; its log lines; asc_ard_pad_end), the sweep
FUNCTION asc_pad_cs_apply {
  PARAMETER h.
  LOCAL inp IS asc["padcs_in"].
  IF inp:HASKEY("etl") {
    LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
    padcs_apply_etl(ej, h:ETL).
    asc_note(asc, "TAL " + asc_etl_txt(ej)).
    asc_note(asc, "PAD TAL SEARCH COMPLETE IN " + ROUND(TIME:SECONDS - asc["etl_t0"]) + " S").
  }
  IF inp:HASKEY("ard") {
    LOCAL pa IS asc["padcs_ard"].
    LOCAL rsl IS h:ARD.
    LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
    LOCAL sp IS rsl["sp"].
    SET asc["ardp_t0"] TO pa["ut"].
    SET asc["ardp_iy"] TO pa["iy"].
    LOCAL ru IS sp[1]:NORMALIZED.
    LOCAL hz IS (sp[2] - VDOT(sp[2], ru) * ru):NORMALIZED.
    ard_srch_reset(S, 3, "", "", pa["tls"]).
    ard_srch_go(S, LEXICON("md", "PRESS", "tl", LEXICON(), "e", 3, "K", ASC_KMAX, "t", sp[0], "r", sp[1],
      "v", sp[2], "et", sp[3], "mc", ASC_ABR_MC + asc["core_dm"], "res", ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_lo"],
          "iy", asc["ardp_iy"],
      "steer", LIST(hz, V(0, 0, 0), sp[0]), "o", LIST(), "m", LEXICON("f1", ASC_S1P_F1, "vex", ASC_S1P_VEX),
      "rs", asc_ard_rs()), pa["seed"]).
    asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#ardp,sep," + ROUND(sp[0], 2) + "," + ROUND(sp[2]:MAG, 1) + "," + ROUND(sp[1]:MAG - ASC_R)).
    SET asc["ardp"] TO 2.
    padcs_apply_ard(S, rsl).
    FOR x IN S["msg"] { asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#ardl,pad," + x). }
    S["msg"]:CLEAR().
    asc_ard_pad_end(S, "").
    IF inp:HASKEY("bgl") AND asc["ardp"] = 3 AND h:BGL:HASKEY("gp") {
      LOCAL bg IS asc["bgl"].
      padcs_apply_bgl(bg, S["pts"], S["t_ref"], h:BGL).
      LOCAL bgln IS "#bgl," + asc_met() + "," + bg["nsw"] + "," + bg["u"] + "," + bg["t_ref"] + "," + bg["pts"]:LENGTH
        + bgl_line().
      IF asc["log"] = "" { asc["ardp_log"]:ADD(bgln). } ELSE { IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG bgln TO asc["log"]. } }
    }
  }
  SET asc["padcs"] TO 2.
  asc_note(asc, "PAD SEARCH IN C#: " + ROUND(h:MS, 1) + " MS, " + h:THREADS + " THREADS").
  asc["ardp_log"]:ADD("#padcs,done," + h:MS + "," + h:MSETL + "," + h:MSARD + "," + h:MSBGL + "," + h:THREADS).
}

// the pad search's line in the PEG log, once and only once that log exists: done = #etl,met,E TAL (s),VI (m/s),
// units[,site,t...]; unfinished at liftoff #etl,met,-1,-1,units,NOT DONE,site index,phase,SSME-out time tried[,site,
// t...] (the sites found); never begun #etl,met,-1,-1,0,NOT STARTED
FUNCTION asc_etl_log {
  PARAMETER ej.
  IF asc["etl_lg"] OR asc["log"] = "" { RETURN. }
  LOCAL s IS ",-1,-1,0,NOT STARTED".
  IF ej:LENGTH > 0 {
    LOCAL x IS "".
    FOR k IN ej["tb"]:KEYS { SET x TO x + "," + k + "," + ej["tb"][k]. }
    IF ej["done"] { SET s TO "," + ej["etal"] + "," + ej["vi"] + "," + ej["n"] + x. }
    ELSE { SET s TO ",-1,-1," + ej["n"] + ",NOT DONE," + ej["si"] + "," + ej["ph"] + "," + ej["tf"] + x. }
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#etl," + asc_met() + s TO asc["log"]. }
  SET asc["etl_lg"] TO TRUE.
}

// each pass with the pages, after asc_abr_tick: the search's E TAL mark (VI, m/s) over the tables', shifted as the
// tables shift with the vehicle's mass (asc_abr_tick's delta from MET 1 s; the search flies the I-loads' masses but the
// SRBs as measured, and that delta leaves the SRBs out)
FUNCTION asc_etl_apply {
  IF NOT (ASC_ARD_ON AND ASC_ETAL_ON) { RETURN. }
  LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
  IF ej:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN. }
  IF (NOT ej["done"]) OR ej["vi"] >= ASC_ARD_NEVER { RETURN. }
  IF asc["s1l_le"] { SET asc["abr"]["b"]["E_TAL"] TO ej["vi"]. RETURN. }   // a stage-1 refresh's, unshifted
  SET asc["abr"]["b"]["E_TAL"] TO ej["vi"] + asc_etl_sh().
}

// THE TAL WEATHER BANS (the target box's GUI, lib_ascent_gui; pre-launch only): every TAL site banned in the target box
// (ASC_TAL_SITES empty) = no TAL that flight: the pages' TAL marks (E TAL, 2EO TAL) off the scale each pass after the
// tables' and the searches' (no site's search replaces the tables' marks), so the 1EO / 2EO lines, the marks and the
// 2EO automatics never open a TAL (the Mode list has none already: no site in the list); a TAL by hand refused
// (asc_abort). A banned site is gone from every list.
FUNCTION asc_ban_b {
  IF ASC_TAL_SITES:LENGTH > 0 OR NOT asc:HASKEY("abr") { RETURN. }
  SET asc["abr"]["b"]["E_TAL"] TO ASC_ARD_NEVER.
  SET asc["abr"]["b"]["TAL_2EO"] TO ASC_ARD_NEVER.
}

// the tables' E TAL shift with the vehicle's mass (m/s; asc_etl_apply's and per site): asc_abr_tick's delta
FUNCTION asc_etl_sh {
  LOCAL a IS asc["abr"].
  LOCAL tb IS ASC_ABR_SETS[a["k"]][3].
  IF tb:HASKEY("E_TAL") {
    LOCAL v1 IS asc_abr_lin(tb["E_TAL"], a["d"]).
    LOCAL v0 IS asc_abr_lin(tb["E_TAL"], 0).
    IF v1 < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 AND v0 < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 { RETURN v1 - v0. }
  }
  RETURN 0.
}

// the first TAL site (its index in ASC_TAL_SITES) whose 2EO mark the ARD has at or below vi (m/s), else 0; the
// sites in the rank's order (asc_sites_sort: the least dV first)
FUNCTION asc_ard_tal_k {
  PARAMETER vi.
  FOR st IN asc_sites_sort(ASC_TAL_SITES) {
    FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] {
      IF x["key"] = "TAL_2EO_" + st AND x["vb"] >= 0 AND vi >= x["vb"] { RETURN ASC_TAL_SITES:INDEXOF(st). }
    }
  }
  RETURN 0.
}

// THE EARLY C/O: the 2EO guidance may cut off early to reach a pocket it would otherwise overshoot. The ground distance
// (km) to the contingency's site, an ELS of the live BLUE / GREEN's list (ASC_BGL_SITES), for lib_ascent_cnt's mode 2
// (ASC_CNT_DCO; -1: no site), and its message once (asc_cnt_early_say)
FUNCTION asc_cnt_dsite {
  PARAMETER st.
  FOR s IN ASC_BGL_SITES {
    IF s[0] = st { RETURN bgl_gc(SHIP:GEOPOSITION:LAT, SHIP:GEOPOSITION:LNG, s[1], s[2])[0]. }
  }
  RETURN -1.
}

FUNCTION asc_cnt_early_say {
  PARAMETER met.
  LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
  IF cn["early"] >= 0 AND NOT cn["early_said"] {
    SET cn["early_said"] TO TRUE.
    asc_event(asc, "2EO CONT EARLY C/O: " + cn["site"] + " " + ROUND(cn["d_site"]) + " KM").
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt,early," + met + "," + cn["site"] + "," + cn["d_site"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
}

// mode 2's hold inputs before a contingency pass (lib_ascent_cnt's asc_cnt_m2): the thrust over the mass now (the
// SSMEs at K_CMD as PEG's ATR, + the OMS dump's, as the offline sim's), the same at the ET's low level (the flat
// thrust's gate; asc_drp_go's MLL) and the cut law's ends (inertial, from the body's centre, as the sample's r)
FUNCTION asc_cnt_m2in {
  PARAMETER cn, sm.
  IF NOT ASC_CNT_M2H OR cn["mode"] <> 2 OR cn["ph"] <> "hold" { RETURN. }
  LOCAL M IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL f IS asc["g"]["K_CMD"] / 100 * ASC_PL_TO_KSP * asc_thrust(asc["ssme"])[0].
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 AND asc["oms"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET f TO f + asc_thrust(asc["oms"])[0]. }
  SET cn["acc"] TO f / M.
  IF ASC_CNT_M2_FLAT {
    SET cn["abo"] TO f / MAX(0.05 * M, M - MAX(0, asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]) - ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"])).
  }
  IF ASC_CNT_LAW {
    LOCAL ps IS LIST().
    FOR en IN ASC_CNT_LAW_ENDS { ps:ADD(asc_to_i(sm[0], LATLNG(en[1], en[2]):POSITION - BODY:POSITION)). }
    SET cn["eps"] TO ps.
  }
}

// the cut law's C/O, once: its end's site becomes the contingency's (OPS 6 lands there; a BLUE turns GREEN); before
// it, the hold's aim at each new site
FUNCTION asc_cnt_law_say {
  PARAMETER met.
  LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
  IF cn["law_gated"] > 0 AND NOT cn["gate_said"] {   // the load gate holds the law's C/O, once
    SET cn["gate_said"] TO TRUE.
    asc_note(asc, "CONT LOAD GATE: C/O HELD  H " + adFx(SHIP:ALTITUDE / 1000, 1) + "K").
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt,gate," + met + "," + SHIP:ALTITUDE + "," + cn["law_x"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  IF cn["law_k"] < 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL en IS ASC_CNT_LAW_ENDS[cn["law_k"]][0].
  LOCAL st IS en:SUBSTRING(0, 3).
  IF cn["law_cut"] >= 0 {
    IF cn["law_said"] { RETURN. }
    SET cn["law_said"] TO TRUE.
    LOCAL was IS cn["site"].
    SET cn["site"] TO st.
    IF asc["eo2_ln"] = "BLUE" OR asc["eo2_ln"] = "YELLOW" { SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "GREEN". }   // YELLOW too
    LOCAL wt IS "".
    IF was <> st { SET wt TO " (WAS " + was + ")". }
    asc_note(asc, "2EO CONT C/O FOR " + en + " (" + ROUND(cn["law_d"]) + " KM): TAEM AT " + ROUND(cn["law_x"]) + " KM" + wt).
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt,law," + met + "," + en + "," + cn["law_d"] + "," + cn["law_x"] + "," + was TO asc["log"]. }
  } ELSE IF st <> cn["law_site"] AND cn["ph"] = "hold" {
    SET cn["law_site"] TO st.
    asc_note(asc, "CONT HOLD AIMS AT " + st + " (TAEM AT " + ROUND(cn["law_x"]) + " KM)").
  }
}

// the contingency's pass (lib_ascent_cnt's asc_cnt_cycle on the sampled state); the C/O -> PEG's T_MECO (MECO "cut")
FUNCTION asc_cnt_pass {
  PARAMETER met, sm.
  LOCAL cn IS asc["cn"].
  LOCAL ph IS cn["ph"].
  asc_cnt_phi(cn, met, asc_cnt_roll_now(cn, sm[0])).
  SET cn["d_site"] TO asc_cnt_dsite(cn["site"]).
  asc_cnt_m2in(cn, sm).                    // mode 2's hold
  asc_cnt_cycle(cn, met, sm[1], sm[2], asc_to_i(sm[0], SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE),
    SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA * 1000).
  asc_cnt_early_say(met).
  asc_cnt_law_say(met).
  SET cn["t_next"] TO cn["t_next"] + ASC_DTGD.
  IF cn["ph"] <> ph {
    asc_note(asc, "CONT " + cn["ph"]:TOUPPER + "  H " + adFx(SHIP:ALTITUDE / 1000, 1) + "K" + "  HDOT "
      + ROUND(SHIP:VERTICALSPEED)).
  }
  IF cn["t_cut"] >= 0 AND asc["g"]["T_MECO"] < 0 { SET asc["g"]["T_MECO"] TO cn["t_cut"]. }
  IF cn["t_cut"] >= 0 AND cn["law_cut"] < 0 AND asc["eo2_ln"] = "YELLOW" {   // C/O without the law: no end in reach
    SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "BLUE".
    asc_event(asc, "RTLS 2EO " + asc_col_word("BLUE") + ": NO RUNWAY END IN REACH").
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt," + met + "," + cn["ph"] + "," + cn["phi"] + "," + cn["k_al"] + "," + SHIP:VERTICALSPEED + ","
    + SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE TO asc["log"]. }
  IF ASC_CNT_M2H AND cn["mode"] = 2 AND ph = "hold" {   // the hold's pass (elevation, thrust, the law's best end)
    LOCAL en IS "".
    IF cn["law_k"] >= 0 { SET en TO ASC_CNT_LAW_ENDS[cn["law_k"]][0]. }
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#cnt2," + met + "," + cn["e2"] + "," + SHIP:VERTICALSPEED + "," + cn["acc"] + "," + en + "," + cn["law_d"] + ","
      + cn["law_x"] + "," + cn["law_rel"] + "," + cn["ph"] TO asc["log"]. }
  }
}

// the stack's own roll (deg) in the contingency's roll (0 heads down, 180 heads up about its xb): -its top on nb, sb
FUNCTION asc_cnt_roll_now {
  PARAMETER cn, ax.
  IF cn["ph"] <> "roll" { RETURN 0. }
  LOCAL zt IS -asc_to_i(ax, SHIP:FACING:TOPVECTOR).
  LOCAL pa IS ARCTAN2(VDOT(zt, cn["sb"]), VDOT(zt, cn["nb"])).
  IF pa < -90 { SET pa TO pa + 360. }
  RETURN pa.
}

// does ops6q.ks fly mode md (its text tests talMode = "md")? It flies the TAL logic for a mode it does not know
FUNCTION asc_o6_knows {
  PARAMETER md.
  IF NOT EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") { RETURN FALSE. }
  RETURN OPEN("0:/ops6q.ks"):READALL:STRING:CONTAINS("talMode = " + CHAR(34) + md + CHAR(34)).
}

// AN SSME OUT IN STAGE 2 (the SRBs' gimbals gone): the roll on one SSME gimbal only -- the centre one while it runs,
// else the first of the others; with one SSME left no gimbal rolls: the RCS does, roll only (its pitch and yaw off, the
// RCS on), as on the real Shuttle; with no RCS part the last SSME keeps the roll. Flown by the ascent DAP
// (asc["eo_dap"]), else by kOS's cooked steering with its roll and yaw torque loops slower (ROLLTS and YAWTS
// asc["eo_ts"] s; kOS's default 2 s): that steering oscillated on 2 SSMEs, and the roll on one gimbal only helped. All
// back at MECO (asc_eo_steer_off).
FUNCTION asc_eo_steer {
  LOCAL n IS asc["ssme"]:LENGTH.
  IF NOT asc["s2_on"] OR n = 0 OR n > 2 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL rl IS asc["ssme"][0].
  IF adIds:HASKEY("C") { FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { IF en:UID = adIds["C"]:UID { SET rl TO en. } } }
  LOCAL k IS "?".
  FOR kk IN LIST("C", "L", "R") { IF adIds:HASKEY(kk) { IF adIds[kk]:UID = rl:UID { SET k TO kk. } } }
  IF n = 1 AND asc["eo_rcs"]:LENGTH = 0 {
    LOCAL rx IS LIST().
    LIST RCS IN rx.
    FOR th IN rx {
      asc["eo_rcs"]:ADD(LIST(th, th:PITCHENABLED, th:YAWENABLED, th:ROLLENABLED)).
      SET th:PITCHENABLED TO FALSE.
      SET th:YAWENABLED TO FALSE.
      SET th:ROLLENABLED TO TRUE.
    }
    IF rx:LENGTH > 0 {
      SET asc["eo_rcs0"] TO RCS.
      RCS ON.
    }
  }
  IF asc["eo_rcs"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET k TO "RCS". }   // the RCS rolls, set up now or by an earlier call (an RTLS picked)
  FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { IF en:HASGIMBAL { SET en:GIMBAL:ROLL TO (k <> "RCS" AND en:UID = rl:UID). } }
  IF NOT asc["eo_st"] {
    SET asc["eo_ts0"] TO LIST(STEERINGMANAGER:ROLLTS, STEERINGMANAGER:YAWTS).
    SET asc["eo_st"] TO TRUE.
  }
  // the DAP flies unless A is asked for (ASC_EO_DAP FALSE), an RTLS too unless ASC_RTLS_DAP is FALSE
  LOCAL bd IS asc["eo_dap"] AND (asc["abort"] <> "RTLS" OR asc["rtls_dap"]).
  IF asc["csd"] {                            // the C# DAP hands over to this path
    asc_csd_off().
    IF NOT bd { SET asc["relock"] TO TRUE. }
  }
  IF bd {
    // the ascent DAP in place of kOS's steering, to MECO (one SSME: the RCS rolls, the roll attitude free)
    IF NOT ascDap["on"] { UNLOCK STEERING. }
    SET ascDap["tgt"] TO asc_dir.
    ascDapStart(asc["ssme"], k = "RCS").
    asc_note(asc, "EO DAP: ROLL ON " + k + ", " + ascDap["n"] + " SSME").
  } ELSE {
    // kOS's steering, its roll / yaw loops slower; an RTLS selected while the DAP flies: the DAP off, kOS's steering
    // locked again (the main loop's relock)
    IF ascDap["on"] {
      ascDapStop().
      SET asc["relock"] TO TRUE.
    }
    SET STEERINGMANAGER:ROLLTS TO asc["eo_ts"].
    SET STEERINGMANAGER:YAWTS TO asc["eo_ts"].
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#eo,steer," + asc_met() + "," + k + "," + n + "," + asc["eo_ts"] + "," + bd TO asc["log"]. }
}

// the roll and yaw torque loops' settling times, the RCS parts' axes and the RCS back to their state before the
// failure (MECO: the SSMEs off)
FUNCTION asc_eo_steer_off {
  IF ascDap["on"] {
    ascDapStop().
    SET asc["relock"] TO TRUE.
  }
  IF asc["csd"] {
    asc_csd_off().
    SET asc["relock"] TO TRUE.
  }
  IF NOT asc["eo_st"] { RETURN. }
  SET STEERINGMANAGER:ROLLTS TO asc["eo_ts0"][0].
  SET STEERINGMANAGER:YAWTS TO asc["eo_ts0"][1].
  FOR it IN asc["eo_rcs"] {
    SET it[0]:PITCHENABLED TO it[1].
    SET it[0]:YAWENABLED TO it[2].
    SET it[0]:ROLLENABLED TO it[3].
  }
  IF asc["eo_rcs"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET RCS TO asc["eo_rcs0"]. }
  asc["eo_rcs"]:CLEAR().
  SET asc["eo_st"] TO FALSE.
}

// THE C# DAP (ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAP, KalsAddon.AscDap.cs: lib_ascent_dap's DAP flown in the fly-by-wire handler, its
// B-hat from every lit engine's gimbals, the SRBs' too). Wanted from liftoff to MECO unless an SSME out in stage 2
// took the engine-out path (asc_eo_steer), lib_ascent_dap flies, CSS Law A flies, or it failed; in the split-S only
// its loft in stage 1, with ASC_SPLITS_DAP (its sep and sequence fly CSS's Law A: the RCS, the surfaces). The
// stage-1 set (ASC_DAP_S1_WN, the stage-1 I-hat) to SRB sep, then the stage-2 set (ASC_DAP_WN, ASC_DAP_IXX ..).
FUNCTION asc_sw1 {                            // SW 01 AUTO DAP LOST (ASCENT) is active: the C# DAP stays off, kOS's steering is NOT locked in its place (the stick flies)
  IF DEFINED FLFX_SWPROG { RETURN flfxSwAutoLost("ASCENT", "ASCENT"). }   // SW 01 ASCENT, or SW 02 ASCENT held DAP_GD_LOST_S (the last command is flown that long, then CSS)
  RETURN FALSE.
}

FUNCTION asc_crewAuto {                       // The crew re-selects AUTO after RESTART SW healed SW 01 / SW 02 (lib_flfx flfxTick, only while the automated test flight has the vessel: no pilot)
  IF NOT adCssBtnP:ISTYPE("Scalar") { SET adCssBtnP:PRESSED TO FALSE. SET adCssBtnR:PRESSED TO FALSE. }   // their ONTOGGLE clears the wish
  SET adCssReqP TO FALSE.
  SET adCssReqR TO FALSE.
  // past MECO the CSS pass no longer follows the wish (the phase is DONE): the state the hand-off carries is set here, as ascCssMode's transition does
  IF ascCss["cp"] { SET ascCss["cp"] TO FALSE. SET ascCss["hpOn"] TO FALSE. asc_note(asc, "CSS PITCH AUTO"). }
  IF ascCss["cr"] { SET ascCss["cr"] TO FALSE. SET ascCss["hrOn"] TO FALSE. SET ascCss["hyOn"] TO FALSE. asc_note(asc, "CSS ROLL/YAW AUTO"). }
  asc_event(asc, "AUTO DAP LOST: RESTART SW DONE, THE CREW RE-SELECTS AUTO").
}

FUNCTION asc_csd_want {
  LOCAL ph IS asc["phase"].
  RETURN asc["csd_on"] AND NOT asc["csd_bad"] AND NOT asc_sw1() AND (ph = "STAGE1" OR ph = "SRBSEP" OR ph = "STAGE2") AND asc["t_meco"] < 0
    AND (asc["s1c"]:LENGTH = 0 OR (ph = "STAGE1" AND asc["s1c_dap"])) AND NOT asc["eo_st"] AND NOT ascDap["on"]
    AND ascCss["law"] <> "A".
}

// LIST(the parameters, the 12 I-hat coefficients) of stage 1 or 2
FUNCTION asc_csd_set {
  PARAMETER s2.
  LOCAL ih IS LIST(ASC_DAP_S1_IXX, ASC_DAP_S1_IYY, ASC_DAP_S1_IZZ, ASC_DAP_S1_IYZ).
  IF s2 { SET ih TO LIST(ASC_DAP_IXX, ASC_DAP_IYY, ASC_DAP_IZZ, ASC_DAP_IYZ). }
  LOCAL co IS LIST().
  FOR l IN ih { FOR x IN l { co:ADD(x). } }
  RETURN LIST(LIST(CHOOSE ASC_DAP_WN IF s2 ELSE ASC_DAP_S1_WN, ASC_DAP_ZETA, ASC_DAP_WMAX, ASC_DAP_KI, ASC_DAP_BDT, 0,
    ASC_DAP_CS_TMAX), co).
}

// armed (the steering already unlocked by the caller); FALSE: refused, kOS's steering to MECO
FUNCTION asc_csd_arm {
  LOCAL s2 IS asc["phase"] = "STAGE2".
  LOCAL c IS asc_csd_set(s2).
  LOCAL csdTag IS "".   // The flight's id (ascent_peg_<id>.csv) = the C# log's (ascdap_<id>.csv); "" = the DLL picks its own first free
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { SET csdTag TO asc["log"]:REPLACE("0:/logs/ascent_peg_", ""):REPLACE(".csv", ""). }
  LOCAL res IS ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAP(LIST(c[0], c[1], asc["log"] <> "", csdTag)).
  IF res <> "" {
    asc_event(asc, "C# DAP NOT ARMED: " + res).
    SET asc["csd_bad"] TO TRUE.
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  SET asc["csd"] TO TRUE.
  SET asc["csd_s2"] TO s2.
  SET asc["csd_dir"] TO asc_dir.
  SET asc["csd_t"] TO TIME:SECONDS.
  SET asc["csd_wff"] TO V(0, 0, 0).
  asc_note(asc, "C# DAP ON (STAGE " + (CHOOSE 2 IF s2 ELSE 1) + ")").
  RETURN TRUE.
}

FUNCTION asc_csd_off {
  IF NOT asc["csd"] { RETURN. }
  ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAPOFF().
  SET asc["csd"] TO FALSE.
  asc_note(asc, "C# DAP OFF (" + asc["phase"] + ")").
}

// each pass while it flies: the stage-2 set past SRB sep (its state kept), the target and its rate (asc_dir's turn
// since the last pass, raw, rad/s: VCRS's sense, the DAP's own), the log's #csd line each second
FUNCTION asc_csd_pass {
  IF asc["phase"] = "STAGE2" AND NOT asc["csd_s2"] {
    LOCAL c IS asc_csd_set(TRUE).
    LOCAL res IS ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAP(LIST(c[0], c[1], FALSE)).
    SET asc["csd_s2"] TO TRUE.
    asc_note(asc, "C# DAP STAGE 2" + (CHOOSE "" IF res = "" ELSE ": " + res)).
  }
  LOCAL t IS TIME:SECONDS.
  LOCAL dt IS t - asc["csd_t"].
  IF dt > 0.001 {
    LOCAL o IS asc["csd_dir"].
    LOCAL wf IS (VCRS(o:STARVECTOR, asc_dir:STARVECTOR) + VCRS(o:FOREVECTOR, asc_dir:FOREVECTOR)
      + VCRS(o:TOPVECTOR, asc_dir:TOPVECTOR)) * (0.5 / dt).
    IF wf:MAG > asc_csd_wmax * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD { SET wf TO V(0, 0, 0). }
    SET asc["csd_wff"] TO wf.
    SET asc["csd_dir"] TO asc_dir.
    SET asc["csd_t"] TO t.
  }
  ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAPTGT(asc_dir, LIST(asc["csd_wff"], V(0, 0, 0), V(0, 0, 0))).
  IF asc["log"] <> "" AND t >= asc["dap_log"] {
    SET asc["dap_log"] TO t + 1.
    LOCAL s IS ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAPSTATE.
    LOG "#csd," + asc_met() + "," + s[1] + "," + s[2] + "," + ROUND(s[3]:X, 3) + "," + ROUND(s[3]:Y, 3) + "," + ROUND(s[3]:Z, 3)
      + "," + ROUND(s[4]:X, 3) + "," + ROUND(s[4]:Y, 3) + "," + ROUND(s[4]:Z, 3) + "," + ROUND(s[5]:X, 3) + ","
      + ROUND(s[5]:Y, 3) + "," + ROUND(s[5]:Z, 3) + "," + ROUND(asc["csd_wff"]:MAG * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 2) + "," + ROUND(s[8], 1)
      TO asc["log"].
  }
}

// An abort selected (the Mode list + ABORT, ASC_AB, or the 1EO automatic): TAL, RTLS or ATO, from liftoff, one per
// flight, but a TAL may replace an ATO by hand (the real software allows ATO -> TAL, both MM 103 aborts; asc_2eo_go
// does it at a second failure), and after an automatic one (ab_auto) the crew may switch ATO <-> TAL, or to RTLS while
// it is open, by hand. A TAL flies to site (the TAL site list's pick; "": the least-dV site, asc_site_best_k); in a
// TAL, ABORT with another site picked switches the site (asc_tal_switch). In stage 1 it waits for PEG's start (at the
// SRB separation, as the offline sims fly it). TAL and RTLS until PEG's fine count; an RTLS once the roll to heads up
// has started is refused: past negative return (NEG RTN ~4900 ft/s VI on the nominal; the pages' mark computed in
// flight, below the roll's VREL 1700 m/s), and the RTLS's attitude starts heads down. ATO until its OMS plans are
// written (they come after the ET separation; past the fine count PEG keeps its target); from a TAL until the fine
// count (asc_tal_off).
FUNCTION asc_abort {
  PARAMETER md, site IS "", auto IS FALSE.
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + ": NOT BEFORE LIFTOFF"). RETURN. }
  LOCAL was IS asc["abort"].
  IF was = "TAL" AND md = "TAL" AND ASC_TAL_SITES:CONTAINS(site) {   // a TAL's site switch
    IF site <> ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]] { asc_tal_switch(site). RETURN. }
  }
  LOCAL sw IS was = "ATO" AND md = "TAL".
  IF asc["ab_auto"] AND (was = "ATO" OR was = "TAL") AND md <> was { SET sw TO TRUE. }
  IF was <> "" AND NOT sw { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + was + " ALREADY SELECTED"). RETURN. }
  LOCAL mds IS LIST("TAL", "RTLS", "ATO").   // one ATO button; the AOA is chosen after OMS-1
  IF NOT mds:CONTAINS(md) { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + ": NO SUCH MODE"). RETURN. }
  LOCAL tag IS "".                           // the automatic's selection, a switch
  // the ABORT line carries no " (AUTO)" / " (WAS ...)" tag (tag stays "")
  LOCAL late IS asc_late().
  IF md = "ATO" {
    IF asc["phase"] = "DONE" { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + ": TOO LATE"). RETURN. }
    asc_dtal_unhide("ATO").                  // a hidden TAL's targets back
    IF was = "TAL" {
      IF late { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + ": TOO LATE"). RETURN. }
      asc_tal_off().
    }
    SET asc["abort"] TO md.
    SET asc["ab_auto"] TO auto.
    SET adSel TO md.
    asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + "  VI " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG) + tag).
    IF was = "TAL" AND asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") { IF asc["eo2_ln"] = "TAL" { SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "ATO". } }
    IF asc["s2_on"] AND asc["t_meco"] < 0 { asc_ato_go(asc_met()). }
    asc_ard_reset().                          // the ARD on the ATO's path
    RETURN.
  }
  IF late { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + ": TOO LATE"). RETURN. }
  IF md = "RTLS" {
    IF asc["t_roll"] >= 0 {
      asc_event(asc, "ABORT RTLS FAIL: PAST NEGATIVE RETURN").
      RETURN.
    }
    asc_dtal_unhide("RTLS").                 // a hidden TAL's targets back
    // from a TAL whose OMS dump is over, the RTLS's own dump less what that one burned (else asc_rtls_init's)
    LOCAL dn IS -1.
    IF was = "TAL" AND asc["oms_st"] = 3 { SET dn TO asc["oms_m0"] - asc_oms_mass(). }
    SET asc["abort"] TO "RTLS".
    SET asc["ab_auto"] TO FALSE.
    SET adSel TO "RTLS".
    asc_event(asc, "ABORT RTLS " + ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"] + "  VI " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG) + tag).
    IF asc["s2_on"] {
      asc_rtls_go(TIME:SECONDS, asc_met()).
      IF dn >= 0 AND asc["oms_dump"] - dn > 0.05 {
        SET asc["oms_dump"] TO asc["oms_dump"] - dn.
        SET asc["oms_t0"] TO asc_met().
        SET asc["oms_st"] TO 1.
      }
      IF ascDap["on"] AND NOT asc["rtls_dap"] { asc_eo_steer(). }
    }
    asc_ard_reset().                          // off in an RTLS (the marks kept)
    RETURN.
  }
  IF ASC_TAL_SITES:LENGTH = 0 {             // all banned for weather, or a launch site with none (Vandenberg)
    asc_event(asc, "ABORT TAL: NO TAL SITE" + (CHOOSE " (ALL NO WX)" IF ASC_TAL_BAN:LENGTH > 0 ELSE "")).
    RETURN.
  }
  LOCAL k IS ASC_TAL_SITES:INDEXOF(site).
  IF k < 0 { SET k TO asc_site_best_k(). }   // no pick: the least-dV site
  SET asc["tal_hand"] TO adSiteHand AND site <> "" AND site = adSite.   // the crew's own pick
  SET asc["abort"] TO "TAL".
  SET asc["tal_k"] TO k.
  SET asc["tal_chk"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["ab_auto"] TO auto.
  SET adSel TO "TAL".
  SET adSite TO ASC_TAL_SITES[k].
  asc_event(asc, "ABORT TAL " + ASC_TAL[ASC_TAL_SITES[k]]["name"]:TOUPPER + "  VI "
    + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG) + tag).
  IF was = "ATO" AND asc:HASKEY("eo2_ln") { IF asc["eo2_ln"] = "ATO" { SET asc["eo2_ln"] TO "TAL". } }   // the lock: the mode flown
  IF asc["s2_on"] { asc_tal_go(asc_met()). }
  asc_ard_reset().                            // the ARD on the TAL's path
}

// past PEG's fine count or MECO: no TAL / RTLS selection, no ATO from a TAL (asc_abort; the Mode list)
FUNCTION asc_late {
  IF asc["t_meco"] >= 0 { RETURN TRUE. }
  IF asc["s2_on"] { RETURN asc["g"]["S_MECO"]. }
  RETURN FALSE.
}

// a TAL left for an ATO (after an automatic TAL): PEG's TAL target off (asc_tal_vel no longer moves VDMAG and the
// plane; the plane stays where the TAL turned it; no re-init: PEG's hold is stage 2's first direction), RDMAG and GAMD
// the nominal's (asc_ato_go then VDMAG); the OMS dump not started dropped, a burning one stopped
FUNCTION asc_tal_off {
  IF asc["s2_on"] {
    LOCAL p IS asc["g"]["peg"].
    SET p["TAL"] TO LEXICON().
    SET p["RDMAG"] TO ASC_R + ASC_MECO_H.
    SET p["GAMD"] TO ASC_GAMD.
    IF p:HASKEY("tal_rth") { p:REMOVE("tal_rth"). }
  }
  IF asc["oms_st"] = 1 { SET asc["oms_st"] TO 0. }
  ELSE IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms_off(asc_met()). }
}

// SimSup's decision points: the abort marks' crossings (the TAL / ATO / RTLS boundaries: the mark's VI over the vehicle's, at its
// thrust acceleration: the predicted UT) and MECO (the target speed), each once (fuiSimPt). Nothing while SIMSUP is not latched.
LOCAL asc_srDone IS FALSE.              // SIMREACH told the DLL once
LOCAL asc_gos IS -1.                    // The same for GREEN_OPEN: the qualifying window's TRUE start (m/s of VI), the last listed start seen while it was still ahead of the vehicle
GLOBAL ASC_SIM_GREEN_MINW IS 60.         // A window ahead is a GREEN for SimSup only with this much of it (m/s of VI) still ahead
GLOBAL ASC_SIM_GREEN_IN IS 10.           // And the mark is fed once VI is this far (m/s) inside it
GLOBAL ASC_SIM_GREEN3_KM IS 5.          // The 3EO GREEN's mark (GREEN3_OPEN) = the pages' 3EO line GREEN by at least this margin (km)
GLOBAL ASC_SIM_LATE_TGO IS 100.          // S2_LATE (SimSup's no-pilot late-ascent guard) once a TAL's PEG TGO is this low (s; the sim: a 38-45 s outage fails from ~85 s)
FUNCTION asc_simPts {
  IF NOT fuiSimOn() OR asc["t_lo"] < 0 OR asc["t_meco"] >= 0 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL vi IS SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG.
  LOCAL ac IS 0.
  IF SHIP:MASS > 0 { SET ac TO SHIP:AVAILABLETHRUST / SHIP:MASS. }
  IF ac < 1 { RETURN. }
  LOCAL bm IS asc["abr"]["b"].
  // SIMREACH first (the DLL plans the moment a mark arrives, so the reachable list must be in before the marks): once, which outcomes this
  // flight can reach. The 3EO / 2EO BLUE modes need the SRB sep + the abort marks; 3EO TAL / ATO also the 2EO TAL boundary (no TAL site on a VBG launch: none)
  IF NOT asc_srDone {
    SET asc_srDone TO TRUE.
    LOCAL rch IS "RTLS;AOA;2EO BLUE;3EO BLUE;3EO RTLS;3EO SPLITS;RTLS 2EO GREEN;RTLS 2EO BLUE".   // The RTLS variants of the 2EO outcomes (the RTLS is open from any launch site)
    IF asc_site[0]["name"] <> "VBG" { SET rch TO rch + ";1EO TAL;2EO TAL;3EO TAL;3EO ATO". }
    IF ASC_ABR_CONT[0]:LENGTH >= 3 { SET rch TO rch + ";2EO GREEN;3EO GREEN". }
    IF fuiSimHas() { IF ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("SIMREACH") { ADDONS:KALS:SIMREACH(rch). } }   // an older DLL has none
  }
  FOR mk IN LIST(LIST("E_TAL", "ABORT_TAL"), LIST("ATO", "ABORT_ATO"), LIST("NEG_RTN", "ABORT_RTLS")) {
    IF bm:HASKEY(mk[0]) { IF bm[mk[0]] < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 AND bm[mk[0]] > vi { fuiSimPt(mk[1], TIME:SECONDS + (bm[mk[0]] - vi) / ac). } }
  }
  // The stage 1 / 2 boundary (the SRB sep: the burnout cue ~3 s before the time backup), once, from liftoff
  IF asc_met() < ASC_SRB_SEP_BKUP { fuiSimPt("SRB_SEP", TIME:SECONDS + MAX(1, ASC_SRB_SEP_BKUP - 3 - asc_met())). }
  // A prediction (mark - vi) / ac from
  // the pad or from the climb is 3-5x too early (ac = thrust / mass is mostly vertical; the speed gain along the path is far smaller), so these marks are fed at the ACTUAL crossing
  // (the VI passes the mark; the edge is now): TAL_OPEN / ATO_OPEN (the 1st out of a 3EO TAL / ATO waits for it), TAL_2EO (the 2nd), V3_TAL / V3_ATO (VI 2750 / 3500: the 3rd).
  // SimSup releases each waiting out at the crossing + a few s.
  FOR mk IN LIST(LIST("TAL_OPEN", "E_TAL", -1), LIST("ATO_OPEN", "ATO", -1), LIST("TAL_2EO", "TAL_2EO", -1), LIST("V3_TAL", "", ASC_3EO_VI_TAL), LIST("V3_ATO", "", ASC_3EO_VI_ATO)) {
    LOCAL vm IS mk[2].
    IF mk[1] <> "" { IF bm:HASKEY(mk[1]) { SET vm TO bm[mk[1]]. } }
    IF vm > 0 AND vm < ASC_ARD_NEVER / 2 AND vi >= vm { fuiSimPt(mk[0], TIME:SECONDS). }
  }
  // The widest upcoming window of ASC_ABR_CONT[0] (flat (lo, hi m/s, site) triples:
  // the static KSC one or the live sweep's) as two points, its start and its end UT (a window already open starts now); and, once, which outcomes
  // this flight can reach (SIMREACH): no GREEN window = no 2EO GREEN, a Vandenberg launch (VBG) has no TAL site
  // (SIMREACH: above the marks)
  LOCAL gw IS -1.
  LOCAL gwid IS 0.
  LOCAL gl IS ASC_ABR_CONT[0].
  FROM { LOCAL gi IS 0. } UNTIL gi + 2 >= gl:LENGTH STEP { SET gi TO gi + 3. } DO {
    IF gl[gi + 1] > vi AND gl[gi + 1] - MAX(gl[gi], vi) > gwid { SET gw TO gi. SET gwid TO gl[gi + 1] - MAX(gl[gi], vi). }
  }
  IF gw >= 0 {
    fuiSimPt("GREEN_2EO", TIME:SECONDS + MAX(0, gl[gw] - vi) / ac).
    fuiSimPt("GREEN_2EO_END", TIME:SECONDS + (gl[gw + 1] - vi) / ac).
  }
  // The REAL crossing of a window's start (GREEN_OPEN, once): the 2nd out of a 2EO GREEN and the 3rd of a 3EO GREEN wait for it (GREEN_2EO above is the pad's early prediction,
  // 3-5x too early like the other abort marks)
  // The live sweep's list has one-point SLIVERS (866-867, 873-875: a window a few m/s wide at the very VI the vehicle
  // is at) next to the real windows (1011-1177, 1177-1409); the old test (vi inside ANY window) fed GREEN_OPEN inside a sliver at MET 94.3, out 2 fired +9.2 s later at VI 877,
  // between the slivers: asc_abr_site(2, 877) = NONE, the guidance flew '2EO CONT BLUE (no site)'. Now the mark is the crossing of the FIRST window that holds an out: at least
  // ASC_SIM_GREEN_MINW m/s of it still ahead (the 2nd out comes 5..10+ s after the mark at 1..3 m/s2, the list moves ~15 m/s between sweeps), and the mark waits for VI to be
  // ASC_SIM_GREEN_IN m/s inside it, so the out lands inside the window and not on its edge
  LOCAL gq IS 0.
  UNTIL gq + 2 >= gl:LENGTH {
    IF gl[gq + 1] - MAX(gl[gq], vi) >= ASC_SIM_GREEN_MINW {
      // The live sweep's list is CLIPPED to the vehicle's VI, so inside the window its listed start is the vehicle's own VI and 'vi >= start + IN' never held on a
      // fresh list (it fired only on a STALE one, 1..8 s old, 10..30 m/s late). The window's TRUE start is the last listed start seen while it was still ahead of the vehicle (asc_gos);
      // with none seen (the vehicle was already inside at the first sweep) the mark is fed at once, as GREEN3_OPEN's.
      LOCAL gos IS gl[gq].
      IF gl[gq] > vi { SET asc_gos TO gl[gq]. }
      ELSE IF asc_gos >= 0 { SET gos TO asc_gos. }
      ELSE { SET gos TO vi - ASC_SIM_GREEN_IN. }
      IF vi >= gos + ASC_SIM_GREEN_IN AND vi < gl[gq + 1] { fuiSimPt("GREEN_OPEN", TIME:SECONDS). }
      BREAK.   // the first window that qualifies is the one waited for (a later one opens later)
    }
    SET gq TO gq + 3.
  }
  // replaces the early-MECO window + 65 m/s: GREEN3_OPEN = the pages' 3EO line (asc_3eo_work, every ASC_3EO_LN_DT s: a 3EO
  // cut NOW, its CONT pick by the 3EO footprint bgl_point3) GREEN by ASC_SIM_GREEN3_KM km or more. The 2EO list's early-MECO window is the 2EO
  // footprint's, not the 3EO's: the 4 forced 3EO GREENs of 11-14 flown by it (VI 1090 .. 1282) all landed short of BDA10. SimSup's 3EO GREEN waits for it
  // (its 2EO GREEN keeps GREEN_OPEN); no GREEN on the path = no mark.
  IF asc["eo3_ln"] = "GREEN" AND asc["eo3_mg"] >= ASC_SIM_GREEN3_KM { fuiSimPt("GREEN3_OPEN", TIME:SECONDS). }
  // The RTLS 2EO line's colour windows, fed at their TRUE start (the first tick of the colour, once): the
  // live word asc["rl2_ln"] (asc_rtls_step: what a second SSME out would fly NOW, asc_rtls_2eo_word) and the RTLS phase. GREEN (a runway is made) = the pitcharound's YELLOW (the contingency's mode 2
  // from the near side) and the flyback (ORANGE: PEG on one SSME to the site, RED: mode 5); BLUE (no runway end in reach) = the fuel dissipation's YELLOW (mode 2 from the far side, the law's gate
  // holds the C/O) and any BLUE word (ASC_RTLS_2EO_M2 FALSE: the cut at once). The marks are PHASE PROXIES for the runway test (no sim sweep exists for the RTLS 2EO yet): a forced RTLS 2EO
  // GREEN / BLUE reads the real colour at the law's C/O (the #cnt,law / 'RTLS 2EO BLUE: NO RUNWAY END IN REACH' lines) and the windows are tuned here. SimSup's out 2 waits for its mark (+2..10 s).
  IF asc["rl"]:LENGTH > 0 {
    LOCAL r2w IS asc["rl2_ln"].
    LOCAL r2m IS asc["rl"]["mode"].
    IF r2w = "BLUE" OR (r2w = "YELLOW" AND r2m = "fd") { fuiSimPt("RTLS_2EO_BLUE", TIME:SECONDS). }
    ELSE IF (r2w = "YELLOW" AND r2m = "turn") OR r2w = "ORANGE" OR r2w = "RED" { fuiSimPt("RTLS_2EO_GREEN", TIME:SECONDS). }
  }
  // The MECO point's target = the PEG's own (asc_meco's TGT, as MECO_NEAR below): an abort's (TAL / ATO) is not ASC_VDMAG, so the nominal target put the point at the wrong VI
  LOCAL vt IS ASC_ABR_VD.
  IF DEFINED ASC_VDMAG { SET vt TO ASC_VDMAG. }
  IF asc["s2_on"] { LOCAL vtp IS asc["g"]["peg"]["VDMAG"]. IF vtp > 2000 { SET vt TO vtp. } }
  IF vi > vt - 500 AND vi < vt { fuiSimPt("MECO", TIME:SECONDS + (vt - vi) / ac). }
  // MECO_NEAR = the VI is within 40 m/s of the
  // PEG's CURRENT target (asc_meco's TGT: the abort's, not ASC_VDMAG), fed once at the crossing (~2.5 s of burn before the cut); the ATO's third out waits for it as for V3_ATO
  IF asc["s2_on"] {
    LOCAL vpt IS asc["g"]["peg"]["VDMAG"].
    IF vpt > 2000 AND vi >= vpt - 40 { fuiSimPt("MECO_NEAR", TIME:SECONDS). }
  }
  // S2_LATE = the late stage 2 of an ascent that lands from its MECO (a TAL, declared or hidden), PEG's TGO <= ASC_SIM_LATE_TGO,
  // fed once; SimSup (NO PILOT only) then draws, schedules and fires no SW 01 / SW 02 / DPS 04 / DPS 05 to the end of OPS 1 (the final-approach guard). An older DLL ignores the name
  IF asc["s2_on"] AND (asc["abort"] = "TAL" OR asc_dtal_hid()) {
    LOCAL lp IS asc["g"]["peg"].
    IF lp["npass"] > 2 AND lp["TGO"] > 0 AND lp["TGO"] <= ASC_SIM_LATE_TGO { fuiSimPt("S2_LATE", TIME:SECONDS). }
  }
}
// The buttons' requests (one per tick), the FAILURES window's keys, rows (ASC_EO's among them) and RAND (fuiTick) and
// the abort (ASC_AB); with the pages first: the lists, the automatic (asc_ui)
FUNCTION asc_req {
  IF asc["pg"] { asc_ui(). }
  fuiTick(asc_fmet(), FL_NOTIG, asc["t_lo"] >= 0 AND asc["t_meco"] < 0).   // the FAILURES window's keys, its MET rows (and ASC_EO's), RAND from liftoff to MECO
  asc_simPts().                          // SimSup's decision points (once each, only while latched)
  FOR ab IN asc_ab_due {
    IF NOT ab[2] AND asc["t_lo"] >= 0 AND ab[1] >= 0 AND asc_met() >= ab[1] {
      SET ab[2] TO TRUE.
      IF asc_dtal_crew(ab[0]) { asc_abort(ab[0], adSite). }   // TAL or RTLS only while a TAL is hidden
    }
  }
  LOCAL rq IS adTake().
  IF rq = "" { RETURN. }
  IF rq = "ABORT" {
    IF asc["s1w"] >= 0 {                     // the crew's pick in the window
      IF adSel = "BAILOUT" { asc_s1c_bail(). } ELSE { asc_s1c_lock(""). }
    }
    ELSE IF adSel = "" { asc_event(asc, "ABORT: SELECT A MODE FIRST"). }
    ELSE IF asc_dtal_crew(adSel) { asc_abort(adSel, adSite). }   // TAL or RTLS only while hidden
  }
}

// ---- THE MODE SELECTION AND THE FAILURES (the pages): the Mode button brings up a selector with only the modes open
// now, the TAL site selector only the sites in reach; the SSME per failure row, RAND off by default, FAIL in the
// failure window, the 1EO automatic. Another kOS Shuttle script's behaviour, rebuilt (not copied) on this vehicle's
// own marks.

// with the pages, each tick (the FAILURES window's schedule and RAND are asc_req's fuiTick); twice a second on a tick without a PEG pass: the
// TAL site list, the 1EO automatic, the Mode list (lib_ascdisp's adSetSites / adSetModes). The marks are for a failure
// at a VI: once an SSME is out the lists take the first failure's VI (vi_eo1); RTLS and a site's reach the VI now
FUNCTION asc_ui {
  IF asc["busy"] OR TIME:SECONDS < asc["ui_next"] { RETURN. }
  SET asc["ui_next"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 0.5.
  LOCAL vnow IS SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG.
  LOCAL viref IS vnow.
  IF asc:HASKEY("vi_eo1") { SET viref TO asc["vi_eo1"]. }
  LOCAL st IS asc_sites_open(viref, vnow).
  adSetSites(st, asc_site_labels(st), asc["abort"] <> "TAL").   // the labels; the pick follows the best
  LOCAL op IS asc_modes_open(viref, vnow, st).
  asc_auto_1eo(op).
  adSetModes(asc_modes_list(op)).
}

// the modes a first SSME out opens, as the pages' 1EO line (the pages' marks, ft/s): "PRESS" alone at or above the
// PRESS mark; else RTLS below NEG RTN (the VI now) before the roll to heads up, TAL with a site in the list (st), ATO
// from the ATO mark; past the fine count no TAL / RTLS, no ATO once its OMS plans are written; none on the pad or while
// a mark is unknown
FUNCTION asc_modes_open {
  PARAMETER viref, vnow, st.
  LOCAL L IS LIST().
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 { RETURN L. }
  FOR k IN AD_TICKS { IF NOT (asc["abr"]["b"]:HASKEY(k) OR adBnd:HASKEY(k)) { RETURN L. } }
  LOCAL vf IS viref / ASC_FT.
  IF vf >= adB(asc, "PRESS") { L:ADD("PRESS"). RETURN L. }
  LOCAL late IS asc_late().
  IF NOT late AND vnow / ASC_FT < adB(asc, "NEG_RTN") AND asc["t_roll"] < 0 { L:ADD("RTLS"). }
  IF NOT late AND st:LENGTH > 0 { L:ADD("TAL"). }
  IF vf >= adB(asc, "ATO") AND asc["phase"] <> "DONE" { L:ADD("ATO"). }
  RETURN L.
}

// the Mode list from the modes open (op), in the order RTLS, TAL, ATO: none selected -- op without PRESS (with fewer than
// two SSMEs none: the 2EO automatics fly it); an ATO or a TAL flown on two SSMEs or more -- that mode, after an automatic
// one (ab_auto) also the others open, after an ATO a TAL open; else the abort flown alone
FUNCTION asc_modes_list {
  PARAMETER op.
  IF asc["s1w"] >= 0 { RETURN LIST("SPLITS", "BAILOUT"). }   // the crew's window after a stage-1 2EO
  LOCAL ab IS asc["abort"].
  LOCAL L IS LIST().
  IF ab = "" {
    IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 2 { RETURN L. }
    FOR m IN op { IF m <> "PRESS" AND NOT (m = "ATO" AND asc_dtal_hid()) { L:ADD(m). } }   // TAL / RTLS while hidden
    RETURN L.
  }
  IF NOT (ab = "ATO" OR ab = "TAL") OR asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 2 { L:ADD(ab). RETURN L. }
  FOR m IN LIST("RTLS", "TAL", "ATO") {
    IF m = ab { L:ADD(m). }
    ELSE IF op:CONTAINS(m) AND (asc["ab_auto"] OR (ab = "ATO" AND m = "TAL")) { L:ADD(m). }
  }
  RETURN L.
}

// the TAL site list (only the sites in reach): a TAL flown -- its site, and while it may switch (asc_tal_sw_ok) every
// other site the rank reaches; none for an RTLS or a contingency, on the pad, past the fine count, or with fewer than
// two SSMEs and nothing selected; else each site the rank reaches (a short site hidden; a TAL from now on MIN(SSMEs,
// 2), asc_rk_ok / asc_rk_m), and a site the rank has not flown yet by the marks: its own E TAL at or below viref or its
// 2EO TAL mark passed by the VI now (a TAL on one SSME reaches it); less a site whose TAL MECO speed the VI now has
// passed (out of reach). Best first (asc_sites_sort).
FUNCTION asc_sites_open {
  PARAMETER viref, vnow.
  LOCAL L IS LIST().
  LOCAL ab IS asc["abort"].
  LOCAL rr IS V(0, 0, 0).
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  IF ab = "TAL" {
    LOCAL cur IS ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]].
    IF NOT asc_tal_sw_ok() { L:ADD(cur). RETURN L. }
    SET rr TO asc_sample(asc["fr"], TIME:SECONDS)[1].
    FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES {
      LOCAL op IS st = cur.
      IF NOT op AND asc_rk_ok(st) { SET op TO asc_rk_m(st) >= 0 AND vnow < asc_tal_reach(st, rr, met). }
      IF op { L:ADD(st). }
    }
    RETURN asc_sites_sort(L).
  }
  IF ab = "RTLS" OR ab = "CONT" OR asc["t_lo"] < 0 OR asc_late() { RETURN L. }
  IF asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 2 { RETURN L. }
  SET rr TO asc_sample(asc["fr"], TIME:SECONDS)[1].
  FOR st IN ASC_TAL_SITES {
    LOCAL op IS FALSE.
    IF asc_rk_ok(st) { SET op TO asc_rk_m(st) >= 0. }
    ELSE {
      SET op TO viref >= asc_site_etal(st).
      IF NOT op {
        FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] {
          IF x["key"] = "TAL_2EO_" + st AND x["vb"] >= 0 AND vnow >= x["vb"] { SET op TO TRUE. }
        }
      }
    }
    IF op { IF vnow >= asc_tal_reach(st, rr, met) { SET op TO FALSE. } }
    IF op { L:ADD(st). }
  }
  RETURN asc_sites_sort(L).
}

// ---- THE TAL SITE SELECTION: any TAL site may be picked, the least-dV site by default, and the site may be switched
// after the abort is called; a site is listed only when in reach (a short site hidden).
// THE RANK (lib_ascent_ard's phase 5: each site flown from the snapshot as a TAL on MIN(SSMEs, 2), its margin = the ET
// left at MECO as dV, plus ASC_ARD_TAL_VGO_TOL; >= 0 reached) orders the lists and picks the default; a site the rank
// has not flown (none yet, or its snapshot over ASC_TAL_RK_AGE s old) after the ranked ones, by the crossrange (the
// backup order). A TAL's site may be switched by hand until ASC_TAL_SW_TGO s of TGO.
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_RK_AGE IS 120.   // s: a rank this old (from its snapshot's MET) is not used
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_SW_TGO IS 40.    // s of PEG's TGO: no switch of a TAL's site from here

FUNCTION asc_rk_ok {             // the rank has site st, fresh
  PARAMETER st.
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  IF NOT S:HASKEY("rk") { RETURN FALSE. }
  IF NOT S["rk"]:HASKEY(st) { RETURN FALSE. }
  // a rank is an SSME out at its snapshot's MET; before a failure the lists show an SSME out NOW, so a rank from a
  // later snapshot (the pad's: the predicted separation) waits for that MET (until then the E TAL marks list the
  // sites: no TAL is offered before the 1EO TAL line); after a failure asc_rk_drop has left only the ranks that apply
  IF ASC_TAL_RK_EO AND NOT asc:HASKEY("t_eo1") AND S["rk"][st][1] > asc_met() { RETURN FALSE. }
  RETURN asc_met() - S["rk"][st][1] <= ASC_TAL_RK_AGE.
}

// ASC_TAL_RK_EO: a rank is a TAL flown from its snapshot, i.e. an SSME out at the snapshot's MET, and the pad's
// snapshot is the PREDICTED separation (three SSMEs to ~80 s), so after an SSME out before it that rank is a flight
// that will not happen (a flight out at 19 s: the pad's rank +362 m/s for SNN from 79.5 s listed the site; the TAL
// flown topped at 65.6 km and cut at 60.6 km, under ASC_DRP_MIN_ALT, and the ET broke up). At the first failure (tf,
// its MET) the ranks whose snapshot is later go; the lists then use the E TAL marks (asc_site_etal) until the
// flight's own rank (on the SSMEs left, from the separation). A rank from before the failure stays (it flew an SSME
// out earlier: harder). ASC_TAL_RK_EO FALSE: every rank kept.
GLOBAL ASC_TAL_RK_EO IS TRUE.

FUNCTION asc_rk_drop {
  PARAMETER tf.
  IF NOT ASC_TAL_RK_EO { RETURN. }
  LOCAL S IS asc["ard"].
  IF NOT S:HASKEY("rk") { RETURN. }
  FOR st IN S["rk"]:KEYS { IF S["rk"][st][1] > tf { S["rk"]:REMOVE(st). } }
}

FUNCTION asc_rk_m {              // its margin (m/s); asc_rk_ok first
  PARAMETER st.
  RETURN asc["ard"]["rk"][st][0].
}

// the backup order: site st's angle off the plane flown (the sine; PEG's IYD in stage 2, before it the pad search's,
// else the orbit's plane now as asc_3eo_tal_k)
FUNCTION asc_site_xr {
  PARAMETER st.
  LOCAL iy IS V(0, 0, 0).
  IF asc["s2_on"] { SET iy TO asc["g"]["peg"]["IYD"]. } ELSE { SET iy TO asc["ardp_iy"]. }
  IF iy:MAG < 0.5 {
    LOCAL nv IS VCRS(-BODY:POSITION, SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT):NORMALIZED.
    LOCAL s IS ASC_TAL[st].
    RETURN ABS(VDOT((LATLNG(s["lat"], s["lng"]):POSITION - BODY:POSITION):NORMALIZED, nv)).
  }
  LOCAL tl IS asc_tal_lex(st).
  RETURN ABS(VDOT(asc_rotz(tl["ef"], tl["w"] * asc_met()):NORMALIZED, iy:NORMALIZED)).
}

// the sites L best first: the ranked ones by their margin (the most first), then the rest by asc_site_xr (the nearest
// first); equal keys keep L's order
FUNCTION asc_sites_sort {
  PARAMETER L.
  LOCAL out IS LIST().
  LOCAL ky IS LIST().
  FOR st IN L {
    LOCAL qk IS 0.
    IF asc_rk_ok(st) { SET qk TO -asc_rk_m(st). } ELSE { SET qk TO 1E9 + asc_site_xr(st). }
    LOCAL i IS 0.
    UNTIL i >= ky:LENGTH { IF ky[i] > qk { BREAK. } SET i TO i + 1. }
    out:INSERT(i, st).
    ky:INSERT(i, qk).
  }
  RETURN out.
}

// the list's labels: the key and, ranked, the margin (m/s, to 10, as all the ascent's velocities)
FUNCTION asc_site_labels {
  PARAMETER L.
  LOCAL out IS LIST().
  FOR st IN L {
    IF asc_rk_ok(st) {
      LOCAL m IS ROUND(asc_rk_m(st) / 10) * 10.
      LOCAL sg IS "".
      IF m >= 0 { SET sg TO "+". }
      out:ADD(st + " " + sg + m).
    } ELSE { out:ADD(st). }
  }
  RETURN out.
}

// the default site (no pick): the first of the list now, else the best of all (an index in ASC_TAL_SITES)
FUNCTION asc_site_best_k {
  LOCAL vnow IS SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG.
  LOCAL viref IS vnow.
  IF asc:HASKEY("vi_eo1") { SET viref TO asc["vi_eo1"]. }
  LOCAL L IS asc_sites_open(viref, vnow).
  IF L:LENGTH = 0 { SET L TO asc_sites_sort(ASC_TAL_SITES). }
  RETURN ASC_TAL_SITES:INDEXOF(L[0]).
}

// the propellant check's other site: the best-ranked one in reach but cur; else the next after cur in ASC_TAL_SITES'
// order that the rank has not flown and whose E TAL is not never; "": none
FUNCTION asc_tal_next_site {
  PARAMETER cur.
  FOR st IN asc_sites_sort(ASC_TAL_SITES) {
    IF st <> cur AND asc_rk_ok(st) { IF asc_rk_m(st) >= 0 { RETURN st. } }
  }
  LOCAL k IS ASC_TAL_SITES:INDEXOF(cur) + 1.
  UNTIL k >= ASC_TAL_SITES:LENGTH {
    LOCAL st IS ASC_TAL_SITES[k].
    IF NOT asc_rk_ok(st) AND asc_site_etal(st) < ASC_ARD_NEVER { RETURN st. }
    SET k TO k + 1.
  }
  RETURN "".
}

// a TAL's site may still be switched: on two SSMEs or more, before the fine count, in stage 1 or PEG's TGO over
// ASC_TAL_SW_TGO s
FUNCTION asc_tal_sw_ok {
  IF asc["abort"] <> "TAL" OR asc_late() OR asc["ssme"]:LENGTH < 2 { RETURN FALSE. }
  IF NOT asc["s2_on"] { RETURN TRUE. }
  LOCAL p IS asc["g"]["peg"].
  IF p["S_INIT"] { RETURN TRUE. }
  RETURN p["TGO"] > ASC_TAL_SW_TGO.
}

// the switch (ABORT with another site picked in a TAL): PEG's target to it from its next pass (stage 1: PEG's start
// takes it), the site picked by hand from now (the propellant check keeps it), the ARD on the new site's path
FUNCTION asc_tal_switch {
  PARAMETER st.
  LOCAL nm IS ASC_TAL[st]["name"]:TOUPPER.
  IF NOT asc_tal_sw_ok() { asc_event(asc, "TAL SITE " + nm + ": TOO LATE"). RETURN. }
  LOCAL was IS ASC_TAL[ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]]]["name"]:TOUPPER.
  SET asc["tal_k"] TO ASC_TAL_SITES:INDEXOF(st).
  SET asc["tal_hand"] TO TRUE.
  SET adSite TO st.
  LOCAL met IS asc_met().
  IF asc["s2_on"] {
    LOCAL tl IS asc_tal_lex(st).
    asc_peg_tal(asc["g"]["peg"], tl).
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#tal," + met + "," + st + "," + tl["RDMAG"] + "," + tl["GAMD"] + asc_csv_v(tl["ef"]) + "," + tl["w"]
      TO asc["log"]. }
  }
  asc_event(asc, "TAL SITE " + nm + " (WAS " + was + ")  VI " + ROUND(SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG)).
  asc_ard_reset().
}

// site st's E TAL (VI, m/s): the pad search's for that site (its SSME-out MET on the search's nominal path, the tables'
// mass shift as asc_etl_apply's), else (no search, not done) the pages' E TAL mark; ASC_ARD_NEVER: never
FUNCTION asc_site_etal {
  PARAMETER st.
  LOCAL ej IS asc["etl"].
  LOCAL ok IS ej:LENGTH > 0.
  IF ok { SET ok TO ej["done"]. }
  IF ok { SET ok TO ej["tb"]:HASKEY(st). }
  IF NOT ok { RETURN adB(asc, "E_TAL") * ASC_FT. }
  IF NOT asc["st_et"]:HASKEY(st) { SET asc["st_et"][st] TO asc_etl_vi(ej["vt"], ej["tb"][st]). }
  LOCAL vx IS asc["st_et"][st].
  IF vx >= ASC_ARD_NEVER { RETURN vx. }
  IF asc["s1l_le"] { RETURN vx. }        // a stage-1 refresh's (asc_s1l_apply), unshifted
  RETURN vx + asc_etl_sh().
}

// the VI (m/s) at MET tb on the E TAL search's nominal path (vt: its (MET, VI) pairs; lib_ascent_etl's ard_et_site
// interpolation); ASC_ARD_NEVER for never
FUNCTION asc_etl_vi {
  PARAMETER vt, tb.
  IF tb >= ASC_ARD_NEVER OR vt:LENGTH < 2 { RETURN ASC_ARD_NEVER. }
  LOCAL vx IS vt[1].
  FROM { LOCAL i IS 2. } UNTIL i >= vt:LENGTH STEP { SET i TO i + 2. } DO {
    IF tb <= vt[i] { RETURN vt[i - 1] + (tb - vt[i - 2]) / (vt[i] - vt[i - 2]) * (vt[i + 1] - vt[i - 1]). }
    SET vx TO vt[i + 1].
  }
  RETURN vx.
}

// the TAL MECO speed (m/s) to site st from the inertial position rr at MET met: asc_tal_vel's cubic and limits on the
// range to the site now (at MECO the range is shorter and the speed lower: past it the site is out of reach)
FUNCTION asc_tal_reach {
  PARAMETER st, rr, met.
  LOCAL il IS ASC_TAL[st].
  LOCAL rm IS ASC_R + il["alt"].
  LOCAL ef IS rm * V(COS(il["lat"]) * COS(il["lng"]), COS(il["lat"]) * SIN(il["lng"]), SIN(il["lat"])).
  LOCAL rth IS rm * VANG(rr, asc_rotz(ef, asc["fr"]["w"] * met)) * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD.
  LOCAL lw IS asc_tal_low(il).               // the 2EO low-energy set
  LOCAL ca IS CHOOSE il["A_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["A"].
  RETURN asc_mid(CHOOSE il["VMIN_LOW"] IF lw ELSE il["VMIN"], ca[0] + rth * (ca[1] + rth * (ca[2] + rth * ca[3])), il["VMAX"]).
}

// the SSME a failure stops: k itself ("L" / "C" / "R"), for "ANY" a random running one (the centre one too); ""
// when none runs
FUNCTION asc_eo_k {
  PARAMETER k.
  IF k <> "ANY" { RETURN k. }
  LOCAL ids IS adEngIds(asc["ssme"]).
  LOCAL ks IS LIST().
  FOR kk IN LIST("L", "C", "R") {
    IF ids:HASKEY(kk) { FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { IF en:UID = ids[kk]:UID { ks:ADD(kk). } } }
  }
  IF ks:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN "". }
  RETURN ks[MIN(ks:LENGTH - 1, FLOOR(RANDOM() * ks:LENGTH))].
}

// ---- THE FAILURES WINDOW (lib_failui.ks / lib_fail.ks; was lib_ascdisp's ENGINE FAILURE window, asc_rand and asc_sched_new).
// The window's FAIL, its MET rows and RAND all reach the SSMEs through ONE handler (asc_flSsme, registered for "MPS 01"), which
// resolves ANY and flies asc_fail. RAND (off by default, the window's RAND key): lib_fail's hazard table, 0.08 % per second per SSME
// from liftoff to MECO at the chosen scale (was: one SSME at 0.08 %, two together 0.02 %, three 0.01 %, each doubled per SSME out).
// Rows: MET s from liftoff, or before it (the count, RSLS: a negative time = s before T-0) -- asc_fmet is their time base.
FUNCTION asc_fmet {                          // the rows' MET: after liftoff the MET, in the count s from its T-0, else none
  IF asc["t_lo"] >= 0 { RETURN asc_met(). }
  IF asc["cd"]:LENGTH > 0 { IF asc["cd"]["st"] = "COUNT" { RETURN TIME:SECONDS - asc["cd"]["t0"]. } }
  RETURN -1E9.
}
FUNCTION asc_flSsme {                        // the window's MPS 01 handler: target L / C / R / ANY; why CREW / MET ROW / RAND
  PARAMETER tg, vl, why.
  LOCAL k IS tg.
  IF tg = "ANY" {                            // a random running SSME (asc_eo_k), on the pad one of L, C, R (as the rows' ANY in the count)
    IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 { LOCAL kl IS LIST("L", "C", "R"). SET k TO kl[MIN(2, FLOOR(RANDOM() * 3))]. }
    ELSE { SET k TO asc_eo_k("ANY"). }
    IF k = "" { RETURN "REFUSE: NO SSME RUNNING". }
  }
  IF NOT asc_fail(k) { RETURN "REFUSE: SSME " + k + " NOT FAILED". }   // asc_fail's own message says why (not before ignition, not found, already out)
  RETURN "OK:" + k.
}
FUNCTION asc_flEng {                         // lib_flfx's SSME resolver (MPS 02 / 03): the RUNNING engine of position k (L / C / R), "" when there is none (before liftoff, out, gone)
  PARAMETER k.
  IF asc["t_lo"] < 0 { RETURN "". }
  LOCAL ids IS adEngIds(asc["ssme"]).
  IF NOT ids:HASKEY(k) { RETURN "". }
  FOR eg IN asc["ssme"] { IF eg:UID = ids[k]:UID { RETURN eg. } }
  RETURN "".
}
FUNCTION asc_flBind {                        // lib_flfx's SSME binder: the part of position k (L / C / R) for the DLL, also once it is out (adIds keeps the engines)
  PARAMETER k.
  IF adIds:HASKEY(k) { RETURN LIST("" + adIds[k]:UID). }
  RETURN LIST().
}
FUNCTION asc_gpcRestart {                    // lib_gpc's RESTART guard: the crew cannot reach the GPC switches before MECO (the real constraint)
  IF asc["t_meco"] >= 0 { RETURN "". }
  RETURN "AFTER MECO".
}
FUNCTION asc_flSwPage {                     // SW 03's page on the ascent = the main display TOP (a constant: design choice, lib_flfx)
  RETURN "TOP".
}
FUNCTION asc_failInit {                      // at the start: the handler, the window's message line, a new ascent (nothing failed), ASC_EO's rows
  flInit().
  flReg("MPS 01", asc_flSsme@).
  flfxRegSw("ASCENT", asc_flSwPage@).      // SW 03 DISPLAY SOFTWARE (lib_flfx)
  flfxRegAuto("ASC", asc_crewAuto@).      // A crew re-selects AUTO after RESTART SW (lib_flfx); the automated test flight does the same
  flfxRegGuid(LIST("ASCENT")).             // SW 02 GUIDANCE LOST (the ascent guidance halts: asc_gdl; the C# DAP lets go to CSS 3 s later)
  IF DEFINED FLFX_PH { SET FLFX_PH TO "ASCENT". }   // The phase lib_hudg's hdgGdLost reads (the diamond, the yaw line, the phase word blank under SW 02), as ops3q's "ENTRY"
  flfxRegMps(asc_flEng@, asc_flBind@).                    // MPS 02 THRUST LOW / MPS 03 GIMBAL LOCKED (lib_flfx)
  flSimHost("OPS1").                        // The DLL's SimSup / RAND table for this program's codes
  gpcInit("OPS1", asc_gpcRestart@).          // DPS 01 / DPS 02 (a GPC fails: its window freezes, then the big X), RESTART only after MECO
  fuiBoot(TRUE).
  gpcReset().
  LOCAL nrows IS 0.
  FOR eo IN asc_eo_due { IF eo[1] <> -1 { IF flAddRow("MET", eo[1], "MPS 01", eo[0], "", "P") = "OK" { SET nrows TO nrows + 1. } } }
  IF nrows > 0 { SET FUI_SCHED TO TRUE. }   // ASC_EO's failures run (as before: the pages' TIME mode on with one)
}

// ---- THE DELAYED TAL (ASC_DTAL_ON): the automatic TAL held until the 2EO TAL mark when it would steer away from the
// ECAL sites. The offline sim's four tests (the onboard ARD's path ahead + the BLUE / GREEN at its points) on the live
// data, each guidance pass from asc_auto_wait s after the first failure. The automatic's TAL is HELD (PEG flies on,
// the pick shown) while ALL:
//   (1) a second SSME out now would be GREEN: the live BLUE / GREEN's 2EO window holding VI names an ECAL site S
//       (asc_abr_site(2, VI));
//   (2) the TAL steers away from S: S and the TAL site on opposite sides of the ground track, S more than ASC_DTAL_DEAD
//       deg off it (10: keeps Bermuda, 5-6 deg off the 36.25-deg track, "ahead", so one rule serves both inclinations);
//   (3) the 2EO TAL mark is not reached (the ARD's TAL_2EO_<site>: VI below its boundary);
//   (4) this vehicle's addition, a safety deadline: the TAL on two SSMEs keeps ASC_DTAL_MMIN m/s of margin (the rank's,
//       asc_rk_m: the ET left at MECO as dV) ASC_DTAL_LEAD s ahead at its present rate (270 m/s and 10 s from the
//       offline sim's latest TAL), and the rank is fresh -- else an early 1EO (the 2EO TAL mark never comes) would hold
//       the TAL away. After a stage-1 failure no rank is fresh at the SRB separation (asc_rk_drop took the pad's: its
//       snapshot is the predicted separation, a flight that did not happen) and the first stage-2 rank lands 4 - 8 s
//       later (83.96 s and 87.74 s in two flown cases, the separation 80 s): the hold waits for it (ASC_DTAL_RK_WAIT s from
//       its first pass at most, then released as NO RANK), not released at the first pass.
// The first pass any test fails selects the TAL. Events: the hold's start and its end (why). The hold gates only the
// automatic (asc_auto_1eo): the crew can always select early, and their ABORT pick ends it at once. The four tests
// alone, offline at 51.6 deg: 414 of 801 second failures land, against 455 of 805 without the hold (36.25 deg: equal).
// ASC_DTAL_ALL skips tests (1) and (2): the hold needs no GREEN ECAL site the TAL turns away from (at 36.25 deg a
// stage-1 failure found none and selected the TAL at the SRB sep); it holds every automatic TAL until (3) the 2EO TAL
// mark or (4) the latest TAL, whichever comes first.
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_ON IS TRUE.      // TRUE = the hold (above)
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_ALL IS TRUE.    // TRUE = hold every automatic TAL (tests 3-4 only); FALSE = all four tests
// ASC_DTAL_HIDDEN: the held TAL flown hidden from its selection (asc_dtal_hide), under the guise of the nominal guidance
// until the switch point: PEG flies the site's MECO altitude and flight path angle and its speed on the range
// (asc_tal_vel's), in the ascent's plane; no abort declared, no OMS dump; the Mode list and the crew's ABORT offer only
// TAL (declared at once: the plane change) or RTLS. At the switch point (the hold's end) the TAL is declared (asc_tal_go:
// the plane change, the OMS dump). PRESS, ATO, RTLS or a 2EO's PRESS / ATO put the nominal targets back
// (asc_dtal_unhide). A DEVIATION from the FSSR: the real TAL turns to its site at the selection. Offline at 51.6 deg 860
// of 1610 second failures land, against 747 with the four tests and 735 with ASC_DTAL_ALL alone.
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_HIDDEN IS TRUE.   // TRUE = the held TAL flown hidden in plane; FALSE = PRESS while held
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_DEAD IS 10.     // deg: S within this of the track counts as ahead, not away
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_MMIN IS 270.    // m/s: the TAL-on-2 margin the hold must leave
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_LEAD IS 10.     // s: how far ahead the margin is projected
// 15 -> 45. While no fresh rank exists the DEADLINE below cannot run (it needs the rank's margin), so only the 2EO TAL mark and this wait can release.
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_RK_WAIT IS 45.  // s: how long the hold waits for the first fresh rank (from its first pass), then NO RANK
// With no fresh rank the DEADLINE above had no margin to test, so the hold could fly on blind up to
// ASC_DTAL_RK_WAIT. The FALLBACK deadline needs no rank: while the hold is flown hidden (PEG on the TAL site's target) the TAL's margin is asc_tal_check's own, the ET's dV
// less PEG's VGO to the site (asc_dtal_fm), each fresh converged PEG pass, projected ASC_DTAL_LEAD s ahead at its own falling rate, against the same ASC_DTAL_MMIN. In one flown case
// that margin (111 m/s at 110.9 s) equals the rank's (111). Once a fresh rank exists the rank's deadline takes over as before.
// test (1)'s "2EO BLUE" release (the live 2EO line has no GREEN site: asc_abr_site(2, VI) = "NONE") waits for the BLUE to hold this many seconds; a BLUE that
// goes GREEN again inside it releases nothing, and the next BLUE restarts the clock. Only that test: the 2EO TAL mark, the safety deadline and NO RANK release at once.
// (With ASC_DTAL_ALL TRUE, as shipped, tests (1) and (2) are skipped, so this grace is not in the flown path.)
GLOBAL ASC_DTAL_BLUE_GRACE IS 10.  // s: how long the 2EO line must stay BLUE before the held TAL is released
FUNCTION asc_dtal_hold {
  IF NOT ASC_DTAL_ON { RETURN FALSE. }
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("dtal") {
    SET asc["dtal"] TO LEXICON("on", FALSE, "done", FALSE, "tk", -1, "mk", 0, "rate", 0, "hid", FALSE, "hx", FALSE, "rw", -1, "bt", -1, "fn", -1, "fk", -1, "fm", 0, "fr", 0).
  }
  IF asc["dtal"]["done"] { RETURN FALSE. }
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL nv IS SHIP:NORTH:VECTOR.
  RETURN asc_dtal_step(adSite, SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG, SHIP:GEOPOSITION:LAT, SHIP:GEOPOSITION:LNG,
    ARCTAN2(VDOT(vs, VCRS(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, nv)), VDOT(vs, nv)), asc_met()).
}
// one pass of the tests: the TAL site st, VI vi (m/s), the position la / lo and ground heading hd (deg), MET met; TRUE = hold
FUNCTION asc_dtal_step {
  PARAMETER st, vi, la, lo, hd, met.
  LOCAL D IS asc["dtal"].
  LOCAL why IS "".
  IF D["rw"] < 0 { SET D["rw"] TO met. }   // the hold's first pass (the rank wait below)
  LOCAL gs IS asc_abr_site(2, vi).
  IF gs <> "NONE" { SET D["bt"] TO -1. }    // T1002: the 2EO BLUE clock restarts at each new BLUE
  LOCAL rt IS 0.
  LOCAL rg IS 0.
  IF NOT ASC_TAL:HASKEY(st) { SET why TO "NO SITE". }
  ELSE IF ASC_DTAL_ALL { }             // tests (1) and (2) skipped
  ELSE IF gs = "NONE" {
    IF D["bt"] < 0 { SET D["bt"] TO met. }
    IF met - D["bt"] >= ASC_DTAL_BLUE_GRACE { SET why TO "2EO BLUE". }   // T1002: only a BLUE that has lasted ASC_DTAL_BLUE_GRACE s
  }
  ELSE {
    SET rt TO asc_dtal_wrap(asc_dtal_brg(la, lo, ASC_TAL[st]["lat"], ASC_TAL[st]["lng"]) - hd).
    FOR bs IN ASC_BGL_SITES { IF bs[0] = gs { SET rg TO asc_dtal_wrap(asc_dtal_brg(la, lo, bs[1], bs[2]) - hd). } }
    IF ABS(rg) <= ASC_DTAL_DEAD OR (rt > 0) = (rg > 0) {
      SET why TO "NOT AWAY (" + gs + " " + ROUND(rg) + ", " + st + " " + ROUND(rt) + " DEG)".
    }
  }
  IF why = "" {
    FOR x IN asc["ard"]["lv"] {
      IF x["key"] = "TAL_2EO_" + st AND x["vb"] >= 0 AND vi >= x["vb"] { SET why TO "2EO TAL MARK". }
    }
  }
  IF why = "" {
    IF NOT asc_rk_ok(st) {
      // no fresh rank (a stage-1 failure: the pad's went at the failure, the first stage-2 one lands a few s after the
      // separation): keep holding until it lands, at most ASC_DTAL_RK_WAIT s from the first pass; T1002c: the FALLBACK deadline
      // (the ET's dV less PEG's VGO to the site) meanwhile, the same threshold as the rank's
      LOCAL fm IS asc_dtal_fm().
      IF fm > -1E8 {
        IF asc["g"]["peg"]["npass"] <> D["fn"] {
          IF D["fk"] >= 0 AND met - D["fk"] >= 1.5 { SET D["fr"] TO (fm - D["fm"]) / (met - D["fk"]). }
          IF D["fk"] < 0 OR met - D["fk"] >= 1.5 { SET D["fk"] TO met. SET D["fm"] TO fm. }
          SET D["fn"] TO asc["g"]["peg"]["npass"].
        }
        IF fm + MIN(D["fr"], 0) * ASC_DTAL_LEAD < ASC_DTAL_MMIN { SET why TO "FALLBACK DEADLINE (TAL MARGIN " + ROUND(fm) + ")". }
      }
      IF why = "" AND met - D["rw"] >= ASC_DTAL_RK_WAIT { SET why TO "NO RANK (" + ROUND(met - D["rw"]) + " S)". }
    }
    ELSE {
      LOCAL m IS asc_rk_m(st).
      LOCAL tk IS asc["ard"]["rk"][st][1].
      IF D["tk"] >= 0 AND tk > D["tk"] + 0.5 { SET D["rate"] TO (m - D["mk"]) / (tk - D["tk"]). }
      IF tk <> D["tk"] { SET D["tk"] TO tk. SET D["mk"] TO m. }
      IF m + MIN(D["rate"], 0) * (met - tk + ASC_DTAL_LEAD) < ASC_DTAL_MMIN {
        SET why TO "DEADLINE (TAL MARGIN " + ROUND(m) + ")".
      }
    }
  }
  IF why <> "" {
    SET D["done"] TO TRUE.
    asc_note(asc, "DELAYED TAL: " + (CHOOSE "RELEASED, " IF D["on"] ELSE "NOT HELD, ") + why).
    RETURN FALSE.
  }
  IF NOT D["on"] {
    SET D["on"] TO TRUE.
    IF ASC_DTAL_ALL { asc_note(asc, "DELAYED TAL: HELD (TAL " + st + " AT THE 2EO TAL MARK OR THE LAST TAL)"). }
    ELSE { asc_note(asc, "DELAYED TAL: HELD (2EO GREEN " + gs + " " + ROUND(rg) + " DEG, TAL " + st + " " + ROUND(rt) + " DEG)"). }
  }
  RETURN TRUE.
}
// T1002c: the TAL's margin with no rank (m/s): asc_tal_check's quantity, the ET's dV (the SSMEs' vacuum exhaust speed, the burnable load less the reserve, the OMS
// left out) less PEG's VGO, valid only while the held TAL is flown hidden (PEG's target = the site's) and PEG has converged on it; -1E9 = no valid margin
FUNCTION asc_dtal_fm {
  IF NOT asc["dtal"]["hid"] OR NOT asc["s2_on"] OR asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 0 { RETURN -1E9. }
  LOCAL p IS asc["g"]["peg"].
  IF p["S_INIT"] OR NOT p["SCONV"] { RETURN -1E9. }
  LOCAL ms IS SHIP:MASS.
  LOCAL prop IS asc_burnable(asc["ssme"]) - ASC_ET_RESERVE_FRAC * asc["et_full"].
  IF prop <= 0 OR prop >= ms { RETURN -1E9. }
  RETURN asc["ssme"][0]:VISP * CONSTANT:G0 * LN(ms / (ms - prop)) - p["vgo"]:MAG.
}
FUNCTION asc_dtal_wrap { PARAMETER a. RETURN MOD(MOD(a + 180, 360) + 360, 360) - 180. }
// the hidden TAL flying (held, no abort declared)
FUNCTION asc_dtal_hid {
  IF NOT asc:HASKEY("dtal") { RETURN FALSE. }
  RETURN asc["dtal"]["hid"] AND asc["abort"] = "".
}
// the held TAL's hidden start (once, in stage 2): PEG's target to the site's, its plane held (asc_tal_vel)
FUNCTION asc_dtal_hide {
  IF NOT ASC_DTAL_HIDDEN OR NOT asc["s2_on"] OR asc["dtal"]["hx"] OR NOT ASC_TAL:HASKEY(adSite) { RETURN. }
  LOCAL tl IS asc_tal_lex(adSite).
  LOCAL pg IS asc["g"]["peg"].
  IF pg["rnow"]:MAG = 0 { RETURN. }       // no PEG pass yet: the next loop
  // the plane held: the great circle through the position and the SURFACE velocity now (the inertial velocity less the
  // body's rotation x position), kept in the liftoff axes so that it turns with the body
  LOCAL wr IS V(0, 0, tl["w"] * CONSTANT:DEGTORAD).
  LOCAL iys IS VCRS(pg["vnow"] - VCRS(wr, pg["rnow"]), pg["rnow"]):NORMALIZED.
  SET tl["hold"] TO TRUE.
  SET tl["iyef"] TO asc_rotz(iys, -tl["w"] * pg["tnow"]).
  asc_peg_tal(pg, tl).
  SET asc["dtal"]["hid"] TO TRUE.
  SET asc["dtal"]["hx"] TO TRUE.
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#taldh," + asc_met() + ",on," + adSite + "," + tl["RDMAG"] + "," + tl["GAMD"] + asc_csv_v(tl["iyef"]) TO asc["log"]. }
}
// the nominal targets back (PRESS, ATO, RTLS, a 2EO's PRESS / ATO); the plane is still the ascent's
FUNCTION asc_dtal_unhide {
  PARAMETER why.
  IF NOT asc_dtal_hid() { RETURN. }
  SET asc["dtal"]["hid"] TO FALSE.
  IF asc["s2_on"] {
    LOCAL p IS asc["g"]["peg"].
    SET p["TAL"] TO LEXICON().
    SET p["iy"] TO p["IYD"].
    SET p["RDMAG"] TO ASC_R + ASC_MECO_H.
    SET p["GAMD"] TO ASC_GAMD.
    SET p["VDMAG"] TO ASC_VDMAG.
  }
  IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#taldh," + asc_met() + ",off," + why TO asc["log"]. }
}
// the crew's ABORT while the TAL is hidden: TAL or RTLS only
FUNCTION asc_dtal_crew {
  PARAMETER md.
  IF asc_dtal_hid() AND md <> "TAL" AND md <> "RTLS" { asc_event(asc, "ABORT " + md + ": NOT AVAILABLE"). RETURN FALSE. }
  RETURN TRUE.
}
FUNCTION asc_dtal_brg {           // the great-circle bearing (deg) from (la, lo) to (la2, lo2)
  PARAMETER la, lo, la2, lo2.
  LOCAL dl IS lo2 - lo.
  RETURN ARCTAN2(SIN(dl) * COS(la2), COS(la) * SIN(la2) - SIN(la) * COS(la2) * COS(dl)).
}

// THE 1EO AUTOMATIC: a first SSME out with no abort selected (auto_st 1, asc_fail) selects the best mode open by itself
// -- ATO, else TAL (to the site list's pick), else RTLS -- shown in the Mode list at once, selected from stage 2 (a
// stage-1 failure: at the SRB separation), with TAL open asc_auto_wait s after the failure (the crew's own pick first:
// ABORT) and the delayed TAL's hold (asc_dtal_hold); none at or above PRESS (PEG flies on); over at the crew's
// selection, a second SSME out or MECO. After it the crew may switch by hand (asc_abort: ATO <-> TAL, or RTLS while
// open)
FUNCTION asc_auto_1eo {
  PARAMETER op.
  LOCAL sa IS asc["auto_st"].
  IF sa <> 1 AND sa <> 3 { RETURN. }
  IF asc["abort"] <> "" OR asc["ssme"]:LENGTH <> 2 OR asc["t_meco"] >= 0 OR op:CONTAINS("PRESS") {
    IF asc["abort"] = "" AND asc["ssme"]:LENGTH = 2 { asc_dtal_unhide("PRESS"). }   // a hidden TAL's targets back
    SET asc["auto_st"] TO 2.
    RETURN.
  }
  LOCAL best IS "".
  FOR m IN LIST("RTLS", "TAL", "ATO") { IF op:CONTAINS(m) { SET best TO m. } }
  IF best = "" { RETURN. }
  IF sa = 1 { SET adSel TO best. SET asc["auto_st"] TO 3. }
  IF NOT asc["s2_on"] { RETURN. }
  IF op:CONTAINS("TAL") AND asc_met() < asc["t_eo1"] + asc_auto_wait { RETURN. }
  IF best = "TAL" AND asc_dtal_hold() { asc_dtal_hide(). RETURN. }   // the delayed TAL, flown hidden
  SET asc["auto_st"] TO 2.
  asc_abort(best, adSite, TRUE).
}

// With the logs on (ASC_LGON) RUN ops1q. starts its own logger -- ascent_log.ks set up in the background (its rows
// by a trigger: 0:/logs/ascent_<n>.csv + .txt), its end awaited after the main loop; under RUN
// ascent_log("ops1q.ks"). its logger runs already (LG_DONE defined and FALSE)
LOCAL asc_slog IS ASC_LGON.
IF DEFINED LG_DONE { IF NOT LG_DONE { SET asc_slog TO FALSE. } }
IF asc_slog AND asc_gui_ok { RUNPATH("0:/ascent_log.ks", "ops1q.ks", TRUE). }

// THE HUD IN OPS 1, each pass of the main loop (lib_hud, as hud.ks: no runway, the heights from the ground below): the
// crew's HUD (shown / hidden) and HUD CAM (the camera to the HUD's eye) from the OMS/MPS page's row; AUTO / CSS / CSS P
// / CSS R from the CSS axes (ascCss)
FUNCTION ascHudPass {
  PARAMETER asc.
  SET hdVis TO adHudOn.
  IF adCamReq <> asc["hcam"] {
    IF NOT adCamReq {
      hdCamRelease().
      SET asc["hcam"] TO FALSE.
    } ELSE IF hdCamSnap() {
      SET asc["hcam"] TO TRUE.
    } ELSE {
      adHudCamOff().
      asc_note(asc, "HUD CAM: NO FREE CAMERA").
    }
  }
  SET hdCtlTxt TO CHOOSE "CSS" IF (ascCss["cp"] AND ascCss["cr"]) ELSE (CHOOSE "CSS P" IF ascCss["cp"]
    ELSE (CHOOSE "CSS R" IF ascCss["cr"] ELSE "AUTO")).
  SET hdSb TO 0.
  SET hdSbc TO 0.
  SET hdAltAsc TO TRUE.                  // ALT MODE RDR / BARO (lib_hud hdAltPick; the button follows its switch)
  adAltSet(hdAltMode = "BARO").
  IF hdVis {
    SET hdElev TO MAX(SHIP:GEOPOSITION:TERRAINHEIGHT, 0).
    SET hdElevFar TO hdElev.
    ascHudRec(asc).
    ascHudQa(asc).
  }
  hdTick().
  IF asc["hudg"] { hdgTick(). }
}

// the ascent's end: the camera back, the HUD hidden (OPS 6 takes it over as loaded: lib_dap / lib_grdap, hdOK; its
// runway its own), the row grey
FUNCTION ascHudEnd {
  PARAMETER asc.
  IF DEFINED FLFX_PH { SET FLFX_PH TO "". }   // The ascent's guidance phase ends with the ascent (ops3q / ops6q set their own)
  // the CSS / HUD / HUD CAM states carried across scripts: a prepared hand-off (HOPREP ran) keeps the camera and the
  // HUD shown for OPS 6 (ASC_HO hud / cam); hdClose releases them when OPS 6 does not follow
  IF NOT (asc["t_sep"] > 0 AND asc["ho"]:LENGTH > 0) {
    hdCamRelease().
    SET asc["hcam"] TO FALSE.
    SET hdVis TO FALSE.
  }
  // lib_hud and lib_hudg as OPS 6 expects them: the speedbrake's scale, the KEAS tape, no ascent keys; through the
  // hand-off's gap no velocity vector and no diamond (no guidance flies it: lib_grdap / landRun set both again)
  hdgRec:CLEAR().
  SET hdFdMode TO TRUE.
  SET hgDiaOff TO TRUE.
  SET hdAzOn TO FALSE.                   // the launch-azimuth horizon off
  SET hgFdPlain TO FALSE.                // the FD square's wings and tail back
  SET hdSpdMode TO 0.
  SET hdTapeKK TO -99999.
  IF hdSpr:HASKEY("sb_scale") { SET SP_SBSCALE TO hdSpr["sb_scale"]. }
  SET hdStaticOn TO FALSE.
  SET hdAltAsc TO FALSE.                 // ALT MODE as OPS 6's: RDR / RWY (BARO back to RDR, blended)
  IF hdAltMode = "BARO" { SET hdAltMode TO "RDR". }
  hdTick().
  SET hdRwyOn TO TRUE.
  adHudSet(FALSE).
}

// THE HUD's GUIDANCE SYMBOLS IN OPS 1, the FD box-and-diamond with tapes as in entry and TAEM before PRFNL: the
// diamond off the FD square by the errors to the guidance's attitude (asc_hud_dir: asc_view_dir = asc_dir, from MECO the
// hand-off's, smoothed in stage 2; the pages' R/P/Y, adRpyErr, fly-to): pitch ASC_HUD_DIA_PIT deg per deg (up), roll
// ASC_HUD_DIA_ROLL deg per deg (right; the entry's bank scale); the yaw error as the yaw line; the G-meter the thrust's g (the pages' g); the phase word
// STG 1 / STG 2 or the abort; the speed tape (ascHudRec: KEAS, VI or VHH). The speedbrake's slider shows the SSME
// throttle: its pointers the SSMEs' power level, actual above, commanded below, 0 .. ASC_HUD_PL_FULL % (pl_scale's
// ticks at 0, 67 and 100 %)
GLOBAL ASC_HUD_DIA_ROLL IS 0.1.
GLOBAL ASC_HUD_DIA_PIT IS 0.5.            // the diamond's HUD degrees per degree of pitch error (was 1; OPS 1's only)
GLOBAL ASC_HUD_PL_FULL IS 110.

// THE DRAWN COMMAND (display only: the steering, the DAP and the pages' R/P/Y keep asc_dir / asc_view_dir). PEG's command
// steps at each pass; in STAGE2 the HUD's diamond and yaw line take asc_view_dir through a first-order lag, its nose and top
// vectors low-passed by a = 1 - e^(-dt / ASC_HUD_SM_TAU) per call (a light touch: 0.5 s; 0 = off, the raw command). Any other
// phase, or a gap of over 1 s between calls (the HUD was hidden), takes the raw command and seeds the lag from it. The same
// tick's second call (the check mode, the kOS fallback after the addon's) returns the same attitude.
GLOBAL ASC_HUD_SM_TAU IS 0.5.
GLOBAL asc_hud_sf IS V(0, 0, 1).
GLOBAL asc_hud_sp IS V(0, 1, 0).
GLOBAL asc_hud_st IS -1.
GLOBAL asc_hud_sd IS LOOKDIRUP(V(0, 0, 1), V(0, 1, 0)).

FUNCTION asc_hud_dir {
  LOCAL now IS TIME:SECONDS.
  IF now = asc_hud_st { RETURN asc_hud_sd. }
  LOCAL vd IS asc_view_dir().
  LOCAL dt IS now - asc_hud_st.
  SET asc_hud_st TO now.
  IF ASC_HUD_SM_TAU > 0 AND asc["phase"] = "STAGE2" AND dt > 0 AND dt <= 1 {
    LOCAL a IS 1 - CONSTANT:E ^ (-dt / ASC_HUD_SM_TAU).
    LOCAL nf IS asc_hud_sf + a * (vd:FOREVECTOR - asc_hud_sf).
    LOCAL nt IS VXCL(nf, asc_hud_sp + a * (vd:TOPVECTOR - asc_hud_sp)).
    IF nf:MAG > 0.01 AND nt:MAG > 0.01 {
      SET asc_hud_sf TO nf:NORMALIZED.
      SET asc_hud_sp TO nt:NORMALIZED.
      SET asc_hud_sd TO LOOKDIRUP(asc_hud_sf, asc_hud_sp).
      RETURN asc_hud_sd.
    }
  }
  SET asc_hud_sf TO vd:FOREVECTOR.
  SET asc_hud_sp TO vd:TOPVECTOR.
  SET asc_hud_sd TO vd.
  RETURN vd.
}

// ascHudRec's maths in the coprocessor (coproc AscHud.cs: ADDONS:KALS:ASCHUD) while ASC_HUD_CS (TRUE): kOS gives it the
// guidance's attitude (asc_view_dir), the game reads and asc_hud_pll's engines, and turns the horizon's heading it
// returns into hdAzN (HEADING). Any failure: kOS's own (ascHudRecK) the same tick and for the rest of the flight
// (ASC_HUD_CS_ERR says why; asc_cs_say's event).
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_HUD_CS) { GLOBAL ASC_HUD_CS IS TRUE. }
GLOBAL ASC_HUD_CS_ERR IS "".
GLOBAL asc_hud_cs_ok IS -1.              // -1: the addon not looked for yet (ascHudCsOk)

// deg, stage 1's heading on the HUD: the I-loaded table (ASC_PSI) at the point asc_hud_pit last read, turned by
// ASC_HDG_DELTA and mirrored for a southbound launch, as asc_s1_att's
FUNCTION asc_hud_az {
  LOCAL ps IS asc_tab(ASC_PPOLY, ASC_PSI, asc_hud_pi, asc_hud_x) + ASC_HDG_DELTA.
  IF ASC_LAUNCH_DIR < 0 { SET ps TO 180 - ps. }
  RETURN ps.
}

// deg, the pitch to fly on stage 1's HUD line: the I-loaded table (ASC_THET) at VREL_AERO_REF, as asc_s1_att's but
// without the guidance's tail-off or the split-S, so it shows the plan, not the command
GLOBAL asc_hud_pi IS 0.
GLOBAL asc_hud_x IS 0.
FUNCTION asc_hud_pit {
  SET asc_hud_x TO asc_vref(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE:MAG, SHIP:ALTITUDE).
  SET asc_hud_pi TO asc_seg(ASC_PPOLY, asc_hud_pi, asc_hud_x).
  RETURN asc_tab(ASC_PPOLY, ASC_THET, asc_hud_pi, asc_hud_x).
}

// THE q x ALPHA CUE (lib_hudg's qaAct / qaCmd, kPa deg; the braking cue's slider, CSS and AUTO alike): from SRB sep (STAGE2)
// while q is at least ASC_QA_Q_MIN kPa, hidden after ASC_QA_HOLD s below it (qaAct -1). The actual: q times the nose's angle
// to the surface wind in the nose's pitch plane (lib_ascent_s2 asc_qa_alpha); the demanded: the same off asc_dir, the steering
// target (PEG's command with the thrust-axis correction: what AUTO flies, and the CSS pilot's fly-to), which asc_qa_limit
// keeps at HDG_QA_LIM or under. The cue itself limits nothing.
GLOBAL ASC_QA_Q_MIN IS 0.5.
GLOBAL ASC_QA_HOLD IS 2.
GLOBAL asc_qa_lo IS -1.                  // UT q first fell under ASC_QA_Q_MIN (-1: it has not)
GLOBAL asc_qa_sm IS -1.                  // the demanded pointer after the HUD's lag (the diamond's ASC_HUD_SM_TAU; -1: none)
GLOBAL asc_qa_smt IS 0.                  //   and the UT it was made

FUNCTION ascHudQa {
  PARAMETER asc.
  LOCAL vs IS SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE.
  LOCAL qk IS SHIP:DYNAMICPRESSURE * CONSTANT:ATMTOKPA.
  LOCAL qs IS asc["phase"] = "STAGE2" AND vs:MAG > 1.
  IF NOT qs { SET asc_qa_lo TO -1. }
  ELSE IF qk >= ASC_QA_Q_MIN { SET asc_qa_lo TO -1. }
  ELSE IF asc_qa_lo < 0 { SET asc_qa_lo TO TIME:SECONDS. }
  ELSE IF TIME:SECONDS - asc_qa_lo >= ASC_QA_HOLD { SET qs TO FALSE. }
  IF qs {
    LOCAL w IS vs:NORMALIZED.
    SET hdgRec["qaAct"] TO qk * asc_qa_alpha(SHIP:FACING, w).
    LOCAL qcn IS TIME:SECONDS.
    SET asc_qa_sm TO asc_qa_lag(asc_qa_sm, qcn - asc_qa_smt, ASC_HUD_SM_TAU, qk * asc_qa_alpha(asc_dir, w)).
    SET asc_qa_smt TO qcn.
    SET hdgRec["qaCmd"] TO asc_qa_sm.
    IF asc_gdl() { SET hdgRec["qaCmd"] TO -1. }      // T1001 part B: no steering target, the HUD hides the commanded pointer (lib_hudg / Hud.cs: qaCmd < 0)
  } ELSE {
    SET hdgRec["qaAct"] TO -1.
    SET asc_qa_sm TO -1.
  }
}

FUNCTION ascHudRec {
  PARAMETER asc.
  IF ASC_HUD_CS {
    IF ascHudCsOk() {
      LOCAL inp IS ascHudIn(asc).
      LOCAL hcz IS ADDONS:KALS:ASCHUD(inp).
      IF NOT hcz:ISTYPE("String") {
        IF hdAzOn { SET hdAzN TO VCRS(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, HEADING(hcz, 0):VECTOR). }
        RETURN.
      }
      ascHudCsOff("ASCHUD: " + hcz).        // nothing was written: kOS's own this tick
    }
  }
  ascHudRecK(asc).
}

FUNCTION ascHudCsOk {
  IF asc_hud_cs_ok < 0 {
    SET asc_hud_cs_ok TO 1.
    IF NOT ADDONS:HASSUFFIX("KALS") { ascHudCsOff("no KAL/S addon"). }
    ELSE IF NOT ADDONS:KALS:AVAILABLE { ascHudCsOff("the KAL/S addon is not available"). }
    ELSE IF NOT ADDONS:KALS:HASSUFFIX("ASCHUD") { ascHudCsOff("the KAL/S addon has no ASCHUD (an older DLL)"). }
  }
  RETURN ASC_HUD_CS.
}

FUNCTION ascHudCsOff {
  PARAMETER why.
  SET ASC_HUD_CS_ERR TO why.
  SET ASC_HUD_CS TO FALSE.
}

// ASCHUD's list (AscHud.cs): the facing, the guidance's attitude, the ups, north, the velocities, the altitude, the mass,
// G0, the VHH site's position (asc_rtls_vhh's cached geoposition; 0 without the VHH tape: stage 1, no RTLS or no RTLS
// state) and asc_hud_pl's engines
FUNCTION ascHudIn {
  PARAMETER asc.
  LOCAL fc IS SHIP:FACING.
  LOCAL vd IS asc_hud_dir().
  LOCAL ph IS asc["phase"].
  LOCAL sp IS 0.
  IF asc["abort"] = "RTLS" AND asc["rl"]:LENGTH > 0 AND NOT (ph = "PAD" OR ph = "STAGE1" OR ph = "SRBSEP") {
    IF NOT asc:HASKEY("vhh_geo") { SET asc["vhh_geo"] TO LATLNG(ASC_RTLS_SITE["lat"], ASC_RTLS_SITE["lng"]). }
    SET sp TO asc["vhh_geo"]:POSITION.
  }
  RETURN LIST(asc, fc:FOREVECTOR, fc:TOPVECTOR, fc:STARVECTOR, vd:FOREVECTOR, vd:TOPVECTOR, SHIP:UP:VECTOR, UP:VECTOR,
    NORTH:VECTOR, SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE, SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG, SHIP:ALTITUDE, SHIP:MASS, CONSTANT:G0, sp, asc_hud_pll(asc)).
}

FUNCTION ascHudRecK {
  PARAMETER asc.
  LOCAL fc IS SHIP:FACING.
  LOCAL vd IS asc_hud_dir().             // the hand-off's attitude from MECO, smoothed in stage 2
  LOCAL er IS adRpyErr(fc:FOREVECTOR, fc:TOPVECTOR, fc:STARVECTOR, vd:FOREVECTOR, vd:TOPVECTOR).
  SET hdgRec["diaDx"] TO ASC_HUD_DIA_ROLL * er[0].
  SET hdgRec["diaDy"] TO ASC_HUD_DIA_PIT * er[1].
  SET hdgRec["yaw"] TO er[2].
  LOCAL ph IS asc["phase"].
  LOCAL s1 IS ph = "PAD" OR ph = "STAGE1" OR ph = "SRBSEP".
  // stage 1's horizon lines aligned to the launch azimuth and always shown: lib_hud's horizon on the plane of the
  // launch azimuth at the table's pitch (hdAzLine), its gap under the cross once the roll program is done (the
  // pages' ROLL PGM ends: hdAzRoll, latched); a split-S's ladder in the plane its loft flies (the table's heading,
  // asc_s1c_dir's), its line the horizon
  LOCAL ss IS asc["abort"] = "SPLITS".
  SET hdAzOn TO s1 OR ss.
  IF ss {
    asc_hud_pit().                        // the table's segment, for asc_hud_az
    SET hdAzPit TO 0.
    SET hdAzN TO VCRS(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, HEADING(asc_hud_az(), 0):VECTOR).
    SET hdAzRoll TO TRUE.
  } ELSE IF s1 {
    IF NOT hdAzRoll AND asc["s1"]["clear"] AND NOT asc["slew"] { SET hdAzRoll TO TRUE. }
    SET hdAzPit TO asc_hud_pit().
    SET hdAzN TO VCRS(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, HEADING(asc_hud_az(), 0):VECTOR).
  }
  LOCAL f IS 0.
  FOR en IN asc["ssme"] { SET f TO f + en:THRUST. }
  IF ph = "PAD" OR ph = "STAGE1" { FOR en IN asc["srbs"] { SET f TO f + en:THRUST. } }
  IF asc:HASKEY("oms") { FOR en IN asc["oms"] { SET f TO f + en:THRUST. } }
  SET hdgRec["nzm"] TO f / (SHIP:MASS * CONSTANT:G0).
  LOCAL ab IS asc["abort"].
  SET hdgRec["phase"] TO CHOOSE "SPLIT-S" IF ab = "SPLITS" ELSE (CHOOSE ab IF ab <> "" ELSE
    (CHOOSE "" IF ph = "PAD" ELSE (CHOOSE "STG 1" IF s1 ELSE "STG 2"))).
  // the speed tape: KEAS in stage 1 and a contingency (CONT, SPLITS: q matters for the sep), VHH in an RTLS
  // (asc_rtls_vhh, the events' VHH), else VI
  LOCAL m IS 1.
  IF s1 OR ab = "CONT" OR ab = "SPLITS" { SET m TO 0. }
  ELSE IF ab = "RTLS" AND asc["rl"]:LENGTH > 0 { SET m TO 2. }
  IF m <> hdSpdMode {
    SET hdSpdMode TO m.
    SET hdTapeKK TO -99999.
  }
  IF m = 2 {                            // asc_rtls_vhh's VHH in KSP's frame (the site's cached geoposition), + downrange
    IF NOT asc:HASKEY("vhh_geo") { SET asc["vhh_geo"] TO LATLNG(ASC_RTLS_SITE["lat"], ASC_RTLS_SITE["lng"]). }
    SET hdSpdV TO -VDOT(SHIP:VELOCITY:SURFACE, VXCL(SHIP:UP:VECTOR, asc["vhh_geo"]:POSITION):NORMALIZED).
  } ELSE {
    SET hdSpdV TO SHIP:VELOCITY:ORBIT:MAG.
  }
  LOCAL pl IS asc_hud_pl(asc).
  SET hdSb TO H_SB_FULL * pl[0] / ASC_HUD_PL_FULL.
  SET hdSbc TO H_SB_FULL * pl[1] / ASC_HUD_PL_FULL.
}

FUNCTION asc_hud_pl {                     // LIST(actual, commanded) SSME power level, % (the running ones' mean)
  PARAMETER asc.
  LOCAL s IS 0.
  LOCAL n IS 0.
  FOR en IN asc_hud_pll(asc) {
    IF en:IGNITION AND NOT en:FLAMEOUT AND en:AVAILABLETHRUST > 0 {
      SET s TO s + en:THRUST / en:AVAILABLETHRUST.
      SET n TO n + 1.
    }
  }
  IF n = 0 { RETURN LIST(0, 0). }
  RETURN LIST(s / n * 100 / ASC_PL_TO_KSP, asc_thr * 100 / ASC_PL_TO_KSP).
}

FUNCTION asc_hud_pll {                    // the SSMEs asc_hud_pl averages; on the pad (the throttle up shown) the
  PARAMETER asc.                          // liftoff's list is not made yet: the lit engines, read each second
  IF asc["phase"] = "PAD" {               // (asc_liquids)
    IF NOT asc:HASKEY("hud_pt") { SET asc["hud_pt"] TO 0. }
    IF TIME:SECONDS >= asc["hud_pt"] {
      SET asc["hud_pt"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 1.
      SET asc["hud_pe"] TO asc_liquids().
    }
    RETURN asc["hud_pe"].
  }
  RETURN asc["ssme"].
}

// ---- the main loop
CLEARSCREEN.
LOCAL asc_go IS asc_gui_ok.
IF asc_go { SET asc_go TO asc_body_ok(). }
IF asc_go { SET asc_go TO asc_plane_ok(). }
IF asc_go {
  SET asc["pg"] TO adInit().
  IF NOT asc["pg"] { asc_con_init(). }
  asc_failInit().                          // the FAILURES window's handler and rows (ASC_EO's failures as its MET rows, SCHEDULE on)
  // the HUD loaded here on the pad, hidden until the crew's HUD (off by default, as the entry's and the GRTLS's); no
  // runway (lib_hud draws none and never switches ends)
  SET asc["hud"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["hcam"] TO FALSE.
  SET asc["hudg"] TO FALSE.
  IF asc["pg"] {
    SET hdVis TO FALSE.
    SET asc["hud"] TO hdInit().
    IF asc["hud"] {
      SET hdRwyIx TO -1.
      SET hdRwyOn TO FALSE.
      SET hdRwyAuto TO FALSE.
      SET hdFinalOn TO FALSE.
      // the FD box-and-diamond with tapes, as in entry and TAEM before PRFNL: the FD square fixed, no velocity
      // vector (TAEM's before PRFNL), lib_hudg's diamond and yaw line (ascHudRec); the SSME throttle on the
      // speedbrake's slider (the HUD sprites' pl_scale)
      SET hdFdMode TO TRUE.
      SET hgFdPlain TO TRUE.                 // the FD square without its wings and tail
      SET hgDiaOff TO FALSE.
      SET asc["hudg"] TO hdgInit().
      IF hdSpr:HASKEY("pl_scale") {
        SET SP_SBSCALE TO hdSpr["pl_scale"].
        SET hdStaticOn TO FALSE.
      }
    } ELSE { asc_note(asc, "HUD NOT LOADED"). }
    adHudSet(asc["hud"]).
  }
  SET asc["fc"] TO asc_fuel_cell() > 0.
  IF NOT asc["fc"] { asc_event(asc, "NO FUEL CELL FOUND"). }
  asc_note(asc, "RTLS SITE " + ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"] + "  " + ROUND(asc_site[1] / 1000, 1) + " KM FROM THE PAD").
  IF ASC_TAL_BAN:LENGTH > 0 {             // the target box's weather bans
    asc_note(asc, "TAL NO WX " + ASC_TAL_BAN:JOIN(" ") + (CHOOSE ": NO TAL" IF ASC_TAL_SITES:LENGTH = 0 ELSE "")).
  }
  asc_note(asc, "OPS1 READY").
  STEERINGMANAGER:RESETTODEFAULT().        // not a stopped run's PITCHTS / ROLLTS / YAWTS (read back as the 'before')
  LOCK STEERING TO asc_dir.
  LOCK THROTTLE TO asc_thr.
  asc_am_set(3).                               // idle (a press before the SRB sep only gets a message)
  UNTIL asc["phase"] = "DONE" {
    LOCAL ph IS asc["phase"].
    IF AOP_ON { SET AOP_O TO CONFIG:IPU. SET AOP_T TO TIME:SECONDS. aop_k(0). }   // The pass's first checkpoint (0 = the tick's triggers)
    // an SSME found out from outside (lib_ascent_eo) fails like our own, before the phase's work reads the engines
    FOR eo IN asc_eo_watch(asc, asc_thr) { asc_fail(eo[0], eo[1]). }
    asc_am_poll().                         // An AG4 press
    asc_am_trk().                          // An AG4 press after MECO
    IF ph = "PAD" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_pad(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "STAGE1" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_stage1(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "SRBSEP" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_srbsep(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "S1CSEP" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_s1c_sep(). }   // the split-S's sep, then its sequence
    ELSE IF ph = "S1CSEQ" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_s1c_seq(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "STAGE2" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_stage2(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "MECO" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_meco(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "ETSEP" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_etsep(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "ETCLR" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_etclr(). }
    ELSE IF ph = "HOPREP" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_ho_prep(). }   // the hand-off's preparation
    ELSE IF ph = "OMS2PLAN" { SET asc["phase"] TO asc_oms2plan(). }
    ELSE { asc_event(asc, "UNKNOWN PHASE " + ph). SET asc["phase"] TO "DONE". }
    IF AOP_ON { aop_k(CHOOSE 21 IF asc["busy"] ELSE 1). }
    IF asc["phase"] <> ph {                  // on the screen only the phase changes AD_REN names (LIFTOFF, SRB SEP,
      LOCAL tx IS ph + " -> " + asc["phase"].  // ET SEP); every change in the log
      LOCAL sh IS FALSE.
      IF AD_REN:HASKEY(tx) { SET sh TO AD_REN[tx] <> "". }
      IF sh { asc_event(asc, tx). } ELSE { asc_note(asc, tx). }
    }
    asc_cs_say().                               // which C# parts ran, and any fall back to kOS
    IF AOP_ON { aop_k(2). }
    // the ascent DAP's target each pass, its log line each second; the steering locked again after it (MECO)
    IF ascDap["on"] {
      SET ascDap["tgt"] TO asc_dir.
      SET ascDap["wff"] TO asc["wff"].
      SET ascDap["eff"] TO asc["eff"].
      SET ascDap["aff"] TO asc["aff"].
      IF ascDap["ihs"] <> asc["ihs"] {          // which I-hat flies, at each change
        SET asc["ihs"] TO ascDap["ihs"].
        LOCAL ih IS ascDap["I"].
        IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ihat,kos," + ascDap["ihs"] + "," + ROUND(ih[0], 1) + "," + ROUND(ih[1], 1) + "," + ROUND(ih[2], 1) + ","
          + ROUND(ih[3], 1) + "," + asc_met() + "," + ROUND(SHIP:MASS, 2) TO asc["log"]. }
      }
      IF TIME:SECONDS >= asc["dap_log"] {
        SET asc["dap_log"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 1.
        IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#dap," + asc_met() + "," + ascDap["n"] + "," + ascDap["sat"] + "," + ROUND(ascDap["e"]:X * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 3) + ","
          + ROUND(ascDap["e"]:Y * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 3) + "," + ROUND(ascDap["e"]:Z * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 3) + ","
          + ROUND(ascDap["w"]:X * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 3) + "," + ROUND(ascDap["w"]:Y * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 3) + ","
          + ROUND(ascDap["w"]:Z * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 3) + "," + ROUND(ascDap["u"]:X, 3) + "," + ROUND(ascDap["u"]:Y, 3) + ","
          + ROUND(ascDap["u"]:Z, 3) + "," + ROUND(ascDap["wff"]:MAG * CONSTANT:RADTODEG, 2) TO asc["log"]. }
      }
    }
    // the pages' R/P/Y errors (deg, fly-to, unrounded) to asc["dir"], as the TRAJ pages show them, each second whoever
    // flies (the C# DAP, kOS's, the steering)
    IF asc["log"] <> "" AND asc:HASKEY("dir") AND TIME:SECONDS >= asc["rpy_log"] {
      SET asc["rpy_log"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 1.
      LOCAL pf IS SHIP:FACING.
      LOCAL pe IS adRpyErr(pf:FOREVECTOR, pf:TOPVECTOR, pf:STARVECTOR, asc["dir"]:FOREVECTOR, asc["dir"]:TOPVECTOR).
      LOG "#rpy," + asc_met() + "," + ROUND(pe[0], 3) + "," + ROUND(pe[1], 3) + "," + ROUND(pe[2], 3) TO asc["log"].
    }
    IF AOP_ON { aop_k(3). }
    // CSS, liftoff to MECO: the guidance's target and the crew's toggles each pass; while CSS flies kOS's
    // steering (Law A) the relock waits for its return
    IF asc["pg"] {
      ascCssTgt(asc_dir).
      LOCAL cwp IS adCssReqP.
      LOCAL cwr IS adCssReqR.
      LOCAL cs IS ascCssMode(asc, cwp, cwr).
      adCssSet(cs[0], cwp AND NOT cs[1], cwr AND NOT cs[2]).
      // SW 01 AUTO DAP LOST (ASCENT): the loss presses both CSS toggles and they STAY pressed after RESTART SW heals it:
      // the crew re-selects AUTO (the arbiter forced the axes CSS but the crew's wish stayed AUTO, so the heal returned both axes
      // to AUTO and the C# DAP re-armed by itself 20 s later)
      IF asc_sw1() AND adCssEn AND (NOT adCssReqP OR NOT adCssReqR) {
        IF adCssBtnP:ISTYPE("Scalar") { SET adCssReqP TO TRUE. SET adCssReqR TO TRUE. }
        ELSE { SET adCssBtnP:PRESSED TO TRUE. SET adCssBtnR:PRESSED TO TRUE. }
        asc_event(asc, "AUTO DAP LOST: CSS HELD, THE CREW RE-SELECTS AUTO").
      }
      IF AOP_ON { aop_k(4). IF asc["hud"] { SET AOP_HN TO hdNextUpd. SET AOP_HT TO hdReal(). } }
      IF asc["hud"] { ascHudPass(asc). }   // the ascent's HUD
      IF AOP_ON { aop_k(5). IF asc["hud"] { IF hdNextUpd <> AOP_HN { aop_iv(0, AOP_HT, 1 / HD_MAX_HZ). } } }
    }
    // the C# DAP armed at liftoff (and again on CSS's return), stopped where it is not wanted (asc_csd_want), fed
    // each pass; kOS's steering locked in its place when it stops here, or when it let go itself (its target too old)
    IF asc["csd_ok"] {
      IF asc["csd"] {
        LOCAL dps IS ADDONS:KALS:ASCDAPSTATE.
        IF NOT dps[0] {                        // released in C#: CSS's FBW3, or its own timeout
          SET asc["csd"] TO FALSE.
          IF asc_sw1() { asc_note(asc, "C# DAP RELEASED: " + dps[7]). }   // SW 01, not a fault: no csd_bad, no cooked steering
          ELSE IF ascCss["law"] <> "A" {
            asc_event(asc, "C# DAP LET GO: " + dps[7]).
            SET asc["csd_bad"] TO TRUE.
            IF NOT ascDap["on"] { LOCK STEERING TO asc_dir. }
          }
        }
      }
      LOCAL cw IS asc_csd_want().
      IF cw AND NOT asc["csd"] {
        UNLOCK STEERING.
        IF NOT asc_csd_arm() { LOCK STEERING TO asc_dir. }
      } ELSE IF asc["csd"] AND NOT cw {
        asc_csd_off().
        IF ascCss["law"] <> "A" AND NOT ascDap["on"] AND NOT asc_sw1() { LOCK STEERING TO asc_dir. }   // Not under SW 01
      }
      IF asc["csd"] { asc_csd_pass(). }
    }
    IF asc["relock"] AND ascCss["law"] <> "A" {
      IF NOT asc["csd"] { LOCK STEERING TO asc_dir. }
      SET asc["relock"] TO FALSE.
    }
    IF AOP_ON { aop_k(6). }
    SET asc["dir"] TO asc_view_dir().      // the steering target, for the pages' R/P/Y errors (from MECO the hand-off's)
    asc_req().
    IF AOP_ON { aop_k(7). }
    IF asc["busy"] { SET asc["busy"] TO FALSE. }
    ELSE IF asc["pg"] {                  // the ARD; E TAL live
      asc_srb_meas(asc["phase"] <> "PAD").   // the SRBs weighed (before the stage-1 delta's MET 1 s)
      asc_core_meas(asc["phase"] <> "PAD").  // the core and the ET at liftoff weighed (the pad's, before main engine start)
      IF AOP_ON { aop_k(8). }
      asc_padc_work(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(9). }
      asc_abr_tick(asc). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(10). }
      asc_etl_apply(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(11). }
      asc_ard_apply(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(12). }
      asc_ban_b(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(13). SET AOP_AC TO adCyc. SET AOP_AT TO uiRt(). }
      adTick(asc). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(14). IF adCyc <> AOP_AC { aop_iv(CHOOSE 2 IF MOD(adCyc, 2) = 0 ELSE 1, AOP_AT,
        CHOOSE AD_DT_CS IF adCsOn AND AD_CS ELSE AD_DT). } }
      asc_ard_work(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(15). }
      asc_bgl_work(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(16). }
      asc_etl_work(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(17). }
      asc_3eo_work(). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(18). }
    }
    ELSE { asc_con(asc, asc_dir). IF AOP_ON { aop_k(19). } }
    asc_oms_full(TRUE).
    IF AOP_ON { aop_k(20). aop_log(). }
    WAIT 0.
  }
  asc_oms_full(FALSE).                     // the OMS engines back on the vessel's throttle
  // the crew's CSS axes, the HUD and its camera, for OPS 6 (asc_ho_set: ASC_HO css_p / css_r / hud / cam)
  SET asc["css_c"] TO LIST(ascCss["on"] AND ascCss["cp"], ascCss["on"] AND ascCss["cr"]).
  SET asc["hud_c"] TO LIST(asc["hud"] AND hdVis, asc["hud"] AND asc["hcam"]).
  ascCssStop(asc, "END").                  // CSS off before the controls are handed on
  IF asc["hud"] { ascHudEnd(asc). }        // the camera back, the HUD hidden, its row grey
  // the end: the throttle to zero, then both controls released (to the pilot, or to ops2q); a last update (the
  // pages without their buttons; the messages also go to the terminal), then the pages closed (below)
  // a hand-off to OPS 6 keeps the hold (LOCK STEERING TO asc_ho_dir(): the entry's alpha) and, when ops6q.ks reads
  // ASC_HO, a running dump at throttle 1 (ops6q's WHEN on hoDumpDue ends it); else both released, the dump stopped
  LOCAL ho_go IS asc["t_sep"] > 0 AND asc["ho"]:LENGTH > 0 AND (((asc["abort"] = "TAL" OR asc["abort"] = "RTLS")
    AND EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks")) OR ((asc["abort"] = "CONT" OR asc["abort"] = "SPLITS") AND asc_o6_knows(asc["abort"]))).
  IF NOT (ho_go AND asc["oms_st"] = 2 AND asc_ho_knows()) {
    IF asc["oms_st"] = 2 { asc_oms_off(asc_met()). }
    SET asc_thr TO 0.
    SET SHIP:CONTROL:PILOTMAINTHROTTLE TO 0.
    UNLOCK THROTTLE.
  }
  // A nominal ascent (and an ATO) that goes on to OPS 2 keeps flying the attitude it has at this moment
  // (kOS cooked steering on a direction captured ONCE, RCS on) through the OPS 2 PRO wait and ops2q's compile, instead of UNLOCK STEERING; ops2q UNLOCKs it right before its DAP ON (o2qDapStart); no press (the wait ends) = released below. TAL / RTLS / CONT / SPLITS (ho_go) untouched.
  // Revert = ASC_OPS2_COOKED FALSE.
  IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_COOKED) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_COOKED IS TRUE. }
  IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_AUTO) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_AUTO IS FALSE. }   // read by o2ck below (declared again, unchanged, at the hand-off blocks)
  GLOBAL ASC_O2_HOLD IS FALSE.
  GLOBAL ASC_O2_DIR IS SHIP:FACING.
  GLOBAL ASC_O2_HOLD_T IS 0.
  LOCAL o2ck IS ASC_OPS2_COOKED AND NOT ho_go AND asc_go AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 AND asc["t_meco"] >= 0 AND EXISTS("0:/ops2q.ks")
    AND ((asc["abort"] = "" AND (asc["pg"] OR ASC_OPS2_AUTO)) OR (asc["abort"] = "ATO" AND asc["o2ho"] AND (asc["pg"] OR ASC_OPS2_AUTO))).
  IF ho_go { LOCK STEERING TO asc_ho_dir(). }
  ELSE IF o2ck {
    SET ASC_O2_DIR TO SHIP:FACING.
    SET ASC_O2_HOLD TO TRUE.
    SET ASC_O2_HOLD_T TO TIME:SECONDS.
    RCS ON.
    LOCK STEERING TO ASC_O2_DIR.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#ho," + asc_met() + ",COOKED HOLD to ops2q" TO asc["log"]. }
  } ELSE { UNLOCK STEERING. }
  asc_eo_steer_off().
  IF ho_go { RCS ON. }                 // the hand-off's RCS (asc_eo_steer_off: the RCS of before a 2EO)
  asc_event(asc, "OPS1 COMPLETE").
  IF asc["pg"] {
    adEnd(asc).                          // the terminal stays blank (the list: the log's #ev rows)
  } ELSE {
    SET asc["con_next"] TO 0.
    asc_con(asc, asc_dir).
  }
}

// THE PAGES HANDED ON (ASC_PG_KEEP): the OPS 1 pages turn straight into the GRTLS pages. In an RTLS, a contingency or a
// split-S hand-off that ops6q flies (the tests of the blocks below) the pages stay up, frozen at adEnd's last update,
// while ops6q compiles and sets up (no CLEARGUIS(): no other window is left by then); ops6q closes them right after its
// own pages open where these were (tdGrStart; at once if they fail); a TAL's likewise (below). FALSE: closed here
GLOBAL ASC_PG_KEEP IS TRUE.
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_END_HOLD) { GLOBAL ASC_END_HOLD IS 5. }
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_WAIT) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_WAIT IS 180. }   // s an ATO's pages wait for OPS2's press   // s the pages stay up after the end (no hand-off)
GLOBAL ASC_PG_KEEP_UP IS FALSE.          // this flight's hand-off keeps them up
IF ASC_PG_KEEP AND asc_go {
  IF asc["pg"] AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 {
    IF asc["abort"] = "RTLS" { SET ASC_PG_KEEP_UP TO EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks"). }
    ELSE IF asc["abort"] = "CONT" OR asc["abort"] = "SPLITS" { SET ASC_PG_KEEP_UP TO asc_o6_knows(asc["abort"]). }
    ELSE IF asc["abort"] = "TAL" {   // a TAL's pages stay up too, once ops6q
      IF EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") {      // opens its deck before closing these (ASC_PG_KEEP_TAL)
        SET ASC_PG_KEEP_UP TO OPEN("0:/ops6q.ks"):READALL:STRING:CONTAINS("ASC_PG_KEEP_TAL").
      }
    }
  }
}

// the log ops1q started ends with this program (its trigger flushes and stops), then the pages closed and
// CLEARGUIS() (before a TAL's, an RTLS's or a contingency's OPS 6 below)
IF asc_slog AND asc_go {
  IF NOT LG_DONE { SET LG_DONE TO TRUE. WAIT 0.2. }
}
// AN ATO'S HAND-OFF TO OPS 2: with the hand-off file written (asc_ato_ho) OPS2 replaces HUD CAM on the OMS/MPS page and
// the pages wait ASC_OPS2_WAIT s for its press; then they close and ops2q runs (its ATO / AOA TGT page asks the pick before OMS-1
// and flies OMS-1 from it). Without a press the program ends as before: RUN ops2q. by hand does the same.
LOCAL asc_o2_go IS FALSE.
// ASC_OPS2_AUTO (automated test flight: no crew) makes the press for an ATO too, ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S s after the end, as the nominal block below does. A crew flight (AUTO FALSE) is unchanged: the button, 180 s.
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_AUTO) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_AUTO IS FALSE. }
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S IS 15. }
IF asc_go AND asc["abort"] = "ATO" AND asc["o2ho"] AND (asc["pg"] OR ASC_OPS2_AUTO) AND EXISTS("0:/ops2q.ks") {
  adOps2Arm().
  LOCAL o2t IS TIME:SECONDS + ASC_OPS2_WAIT.
  LOCAL o2a IS TIME:SECONDS + ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S.
  WAIT UNTIL adOps2Req OR TIME:SECONDS > o2t OR (ASC_OPS2_AUTO AND TIME:SECONDS > o2a).
  IF ASC_OPS2_AUTO AND NOT adOps2Req AND TIME:SECONDS > o2a { SET adOps2Req TO TRUE. asc_event(asc, "OPS 2 PRO: AUTO"). }
  SET asc_o2_go TO adOps2Req.
}
// A NOMINAL ASCENT'S HAND-OFF TO OPS 2 (the Shuttle's MM 106 -> OPS 2 transition by the crew): MECO and the ET sep flown, no
// abort: the OMS/MPS page's HUD CAM button becomes "OPS 2 PRO" and the pages wait ASC_OPS2_WAIT s for its press, then close and
// ops2q runs (it reads 0:/oms2_plan.txt itself; no hand-off file: it opens nominal without one). ASC_OPS2_AUTO TRUE = the press is
// made for the crew ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S s after the end (the OMS-2 plan line readable; with AUTO the pages are not needed: the automated runs
// without them). Neither: the program ends as before (RUN ops2q.).
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_AUTO) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_AUTO IS FALSE. }
IF NOT (DEFINED ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S) { GLOBAL ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S IS 15. }
IF NOT asc_o2_go AND asc_go AND asc["abort"] = "" AND asc["t_meco"] >= 0 AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 AND (asc["pg"] OR ASC_OPS2_AUTO) AND EXISTS("0:/ops2q.ks") {
  IF EXISTS("1:/ops2q_ho.txt") { DELETEPATH("1:/ops2q_ho.txt"). }   // a stale ATO hand-off would open ops2q's ATO page
  adOps2Arm("OPS 2 PRO").
  IF ASC_OPS2_AUTO OR NOT adOps2Btn:ISTYPE("Scalar") {
    LOCAL o2t IS TIME:SECONDS + ASC_OPS2_WAIT.
    LOCAL o2a IS TIME:SECONDS + ASC_OPS2_AUTO_S.
    WAIT UNTIL adOps2Req OR TIME:SECONDS > o2t OR (ASC_OPS2_AUTO AND TIME:SECONDS > o2a).
    IF ASC_OPS2_AUTO AND NOT adOps2Req AND TIME:SECONDS > o2a { SET adOps2Req TO TRUE. asc_event(asc, "OPS 2 PRO: AUTO"). }
    SET asc_o2_go TO adOps2Req.
  }
}
IF DEFINED ASC_O2_HOLD {                  // (declared only when the end block above ran)
  IF ASC_O2_HOLD AND NOT asc_o2_go {       // no OPS 2 press (the wait ended, or ops2q is not coming): the controls back to the crew
    UNLOCK STEERING.
    SET RCS TO asc["sep_rcs0"].
    SET ASC_O2_HOLD TO FALSE.
    PRINT "COOKED HOLD released: no OPS 2".
  }
}
IF asc_go AND NOT ASC_PG_KEEP_UP {         // else ops6q closes the pages
  // the pages stay up ASC_END_HOLD s more before they close, so that the last line (the OMS-2 PLAN) can be read
  IF asc["pg"] { IF NOT asc_o2_go { WAIT ASC_END_HOLD. } adClose(). }
  IF asc["hud"] { hdClose(). }           // before CLEARGUIS (an OPS 6 after it loads its own)
  cwuiClose().                          // CLEARGUIS disposes the C&W window; cwuiMade must go FALSE or cwuiInit never rebuilds it
  CLEARGUIS().
}

// THE TAL's HAND-OFF: after a TAL's ET separation and its translation ops1q runs OPS 6 as its last action --
// RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "TAL", site) (ops6q.ks or its compiled ksm), site a TAL site's key ("ZZA", "MRN", "SNN"). Before it: no
// trigger of ops1q left (the logger ended at the separation; an outer one waited for), the pages closed unless ops6q takes them
// (ASC_PG_KEEP_UP), the raw controls neutral, SAS off, the RCS on. The craft's next stage is the drag chute; the ET separation's
// stage also lit the two OMS engines (at throttle 0). The steering stays on the hand-off's hold and a running dump on into OPS 6
// (asc_ho_prep, ASC_HO: see there); else steering and throttle are released at the main loop's end (throttle 0). Without the
// file: TAL INITIALIZATION FAILED.
IF asc_go AND asc["abort"] = "TAL" AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 {
  LOCAL o6site IS ASC_TAL_SITES[asc["tal_k"]].
  IF DEFINED LG_DONE {
    IF asc["lg_wait"] < 0 { SET asc["lg_wait"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 10. }
    WAIT UNTIL LG_DONE OR TIME:SECONDS > asc["lg_wait"].
    IF NOT LG_DONE {
      SET LG_DONE TO TRUE.
      WAIT 0.2.
    }
  }
  IF asc["pg"] AND NOT ASC_PG_KEEP_UP { adClose(). }   // else ops6q closes them
  SAS OFF.
  RCS ON.                              // the hand-off's RCS on
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:NEUTRALIZE TO TRUE.
  IF EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#o6," + asc_met() + ",INITIATING TAL " + o6site + " ENTRY" TO asc["log"]. }   // not printed
    asc_ho_set("TAL", o6site).
    RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "TAL", o6site).
  } ELSE {
    PRINT "TAL INITIALIZATION FAILED".
  }
}

// THE RTLS's HAND-OFF: after an RTLS's ET separation and its translation ops1q runs OPS 6 as its last action --
// RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "RTLS", site), site the launch site's RTLS runway (ASC_RTLS_SITE's name: "SLF" from KSC, "VBG"
// from Vandenberg): OPS 6's GRTLS to it (the SLF's end SLF33 unless a third argument forces one; RUN ops6q("RTLS",
// "SLF", "SLF15").). Before it, as the TAL's: the logger ended (the 10 s guard), the pages closed unless ops6q takes
// them, the raw controls neutral, SAS off, the RCS on. The RTLS separates heads up (its top = u x n turned through the
// vertical on the flyback). Without the file: GRTLS INITIALIZATION FAILED.
IF asc_go AND asc["abort"] = "RTLS" AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 {
  IF DEFINED LG_DONE {
    IF asc["lg_wait"] < 0 { SET asc["lg_wait"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 10. }
    WAIT UNTIL LG_DONE OR TIME:SECONDS > asc["lg_wait"].
    IF NOT LG_DONE {
      SET LG_DONE TO TRUE.
      WAIT 0.2.
    }
  }
  IF asc["pg"] AND NOT ASC_PG_KEEP_UP { adClose(). }   // else ops6q closes them
  SAS OFF.
  RCS ON.                              // the hand-off's RCS on
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:NEUTRALIZE TO TRUE.
  IF EXISTS("0:/ops6q.ks") {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#o6," + asc_met() + ",INITIATING GRTLS " + ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"] + " ENTRY" TO asc["log"]. }
    asc_ho_set("RTLS", ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"]).
    RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "RTLS", ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"]).
  } ELSE {
    PRINT "GRTLS INITIALIZATION FAILED".
  }
}

// THE 2EO CONTINGENCY's HAND-OFF: after the contingency's fast ET separation and its translation ops1q runs OPS 6 as
// its last action -- RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "CONT", site), site the ELS key (asc_abr_site: GREEN) or "NONE" (BLUE); OPS
// 6 checks its own reach. Before it, as the TAL's. Only once ops6q.ks flies the mode (asc_o6_knows; else nothing).
IF asc_go AND asc["abort"] = "CONT" AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 {
  IF DEFINED LG_DONE {
    IF asc["lg_wait"] < 0 { SET asc["lg_wait"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 10. }
    WAIT UNTIL LG_DONE OR TIME:SECONDS > asc["lg_wait"].
    IF NOT LG_DONE {
      SET LG_DONE TO TRUE.
      WAIT 0.2.
    }
  }
  IF asc["pg"] AND NOT ASC_PG_KEEP_UP { adClose(). }   // else ops6q closes them
  SAS OFF.
  RCS ON.                              // the hand-off's RCS on
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:NEUTRALIZE TO TRUE.
  LOCAL o6c IS asc["cn"]["site"].
  IF asc_o6_knows("CONT") {
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#o6," + asc_met() + ",INITIATING CONT " + o6c + " ENTRY" TO asc["log"]. }
    asc_ho_set("CONT", o6c).
    RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "CONT", o6c).
  }
}

// THE SPLIT-S's HAND-OFF (the header): after its sequence (asc_s1c_seq) ops1q runs OPS 6 as its last action --
// RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "SPLITS", site), site the launch site's RTLS runway (ASC_RTLS_SITE's name: "SLF" / "VBG"), only
// once ops6q.ks flies the mode (asc_o6_knows); before it as the TAL's / RTLS's (the logger ended, the pages closed, the
// raw controls neutral; the steering and the throttle released at the main loop's end, the OMS dump stopped there and
// the fuel cell's tanks unlocked; both kept running when ops6q.ks reads ASC_HO). Else the controls are the crew's: SAS
// on (it holds the attitude), the RCS on.
IF asc_go AND asc["abort"] = "SPLITS" AND asc["t_sep"] > 0 {
  IF DEFINED LG_DONE {
    IF asc["lg_wait"] < 0 { SET asc["lg_wait"] TO TIME:SECONDS + 10. }
    WAIT UNTIL LG_DONE OR TIME:SECONDS > asc["lg_wait"].
    IF NOT LG_DONE {
      SET LG_DONE TO TRUE.
      WAIT 0.2.
    }
  }
  IF asc["pg"] AND NOT ASC_PG_KEEP_UP { adClose(). }   // else ops6q closes them
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:NEUTRALIZE TO TRUE.
  RCS ON.                              // the hand-off's RCS on (OPS 6 or the crew's controls)
  IF asc_o6_knows("SPLITS") {
    SAS OFF.
    IF asc["log"] <> "" { LOG "#o6," + asc_met() + ",INITIATING SPLIT-S " + ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"] + " ENTRY" TO asc["log"]. }
    asc_ho_set("SPLITS", ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"]).
    RUNPATH(asc_o6_path(), "SPLITS", ASC_RTLS_SITE["name"]).
  } ELSE {
    SAS ON.
    PRINT "SPLIT-S ENTRY NOT BUILT (OPS 6): YOUR CONTROLS (SAS ON)".
  }
}

// AN ATO'S HAND-OFF TO OPS 2 (above): OPS2 was pressed, the pages and the HUD are closed: ops2q runs now (the hand-off file
// 1:/ops2q_ho.txt carries the abort, the ATO's burns and the OMS on board; typed `RUN ops2q.` does the same).
IF asc_go AND asc_o2_go {
  SET SHIP:CONTROL:NEUTRALIZE TO TRUE.
  RUNPATH("0:/ops2q.ks").
}
progReset().   // No hook of this program outlives it (lib_progreset)
